    <stringTable>
      <string id="SUPPORTED_WIN7">Support for Microsoft Windows 7 and later</string>
      <string id="SUPPORTED_WIN7_ONLY">Support only Microsoft Windows 7</string>
      <string id="yandex">Yandex</string>
      <string id="yandexbrowser_mandatory">Yandex Browser</string>
      <string id="yandexbrowser_recommended">Yandex Browser: default settings (users can change)</string>
      <string id="AudioAndVideo_group">Audio and video</string>
      <string id="YandexOowVideoDisable">Manage video output to a separate window</string>
      <string id="YandexOowVideoDisable_Explain">YandexOowVideoDisable

The policy allows or prohibits taking videos to a separate Browser window.

Values

- Not Configured: users can control the video output in the Browser settings.
- Enabled: the video is not displayed, it cannot be changed in the settings.
- Disabled: the video is being taken out, it cannot be changed in the settings.</string>
      <string id="AudioCaptureAllowed">Allow audio capture</string>
      <string id="AudioCaptureAllowed_Explain">AudioCaptureAllowed

The policy allows sites from capturing audio from audio recording devices on the user's computer.

The AudioCaptureAllowedUrls policy takes precedence over the AudioCaptureAllowed policy.

It applies to all devices (not just the built-in microphone).

Features

- This is an increased security policy. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/deployment/windows/setting-policy#advanced
- Available in the mobile version of the Browser for organizations. More details: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html

Values

- Not Configured, Enabled: Users see the access request. URLs from the AudioCaptureAllowedUrls policy get access without a request.
- Disabled: users see a message about audio recording being banned. URLs from the AudioCaptureAllowedUrls policy get access without a request.

Safety recommendations

Value: Disabled. Disable audio capture to prevent possible data leakage.

Possible problems. Users won't be able to connect to video conferencing sites. To allow audio capture on such sites, use the AudioCaptureAllowedUrls policy.</string>
      <string id="AudioCaptureAllowedUrls">Set a list of URLs that are allowed to capture audio</string>
      <string id="AudioCaptureAllowedUrls_Explain">AudioCaptureAllowedUrls

The policy sets a list of URLs that can capture audio automatically, even if it's restricted by the AudioCaptureAllowed policy.

The policy takes precedence over the AudioCaptureAllowed policy.

Features

- Available in the mobile version of the Browser for organizations. More details: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: Users determine for each URL whether to allow access to audio recording devices.
- Enabled: The administrator sets the list of URLs that have access to audio recording devices without a request. 

You can use URL templates. For more information about URL templates, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/policy/url-patterns.html

Convert non-Latin URLs (for example, яндекс.рф) via punycode: https://www.reg.ru/web-tools/punycode

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example value:

https://www.example.com/
https://[*.]example.edu/</string>
      <string id="AudioCaptureAllowedUrlsDesc">URLs that access audio recording devices without a request</string>
      <string id="AudioSandboxEnabled">Allow audio sandboxing</string>
      <string id="AudioSandboxEnabled_Explain">AudioSandboxEnabled

The policy controls audio processing in the sandbox. If the software security settings interfere with the sandbox, you can disable it.

Features

- This is a basic security policy. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support2/browser-corporate/ru/deployment/windows/setting-policy#basic

Values

- Not Configured: The default settings are used.
- Enabled: Audio is always processed in the sandbox.
- Disabled: Audio processing in the sandbox is disabled. Audio processing will be performed outside of the sandbox, and the WebRTC audio processing module will be launched at the rendering stage. This may cause security risks due to running the audio subsystem outside of the sandbox.

Safety recommendations

Value: Enabled. Enable audio processing in the sandbox. This will prevent possible data leakage if the site misuses audio.</string>
      <string id="AutoplayAllowed">Allow video autoplay</string>
      <string id="AutoplayAllowed_Explain">AutoplayAllowed

The policy allows automatic video playback in Yandex Browser.

The policy supersedes AutoplayAllowlist.

If the policy is changed when Yandex Browser is running, it will only apply to new tabs.

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: auto-playback of videos is prohibited, but it is allowed for URLs from the AutoplayAllowlist policy. Some sites control autoplay themselves.
- Enabled: Videos are played automatically in Yandex Browser. Some sites manage autoplay themselves.</string>
      <string id="AutoplayAllowlist">Set a list of URLs where videos are played automatically</string>
      <string id="AutoplayAllowlist_Explain">AutoplayAllowlist

The policy sets a list of URLs that allow video autoplay.

The AutoplayAllowed policy supersedes AutoplayAllowlist.

If the policy is changed when Yandex Browser is running, it will only apply to new tabs.

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: Autoplay is managed by the AutoplayAllowed policy if it is set.
- Enabled: The administrator sets the list of URLs that play videos automatically. 

You can use URL templates. For more information about URL templates, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/policy/url-patterns.html

Convert non-Latin URLs (for example, яндекс.рф) via punycode: https://www.reg.ru/web-tools/punycode

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example value:

https://www.example.com
[*.]example.edu</string>
      <string id="AutoplayAllowlistDesc">Allow video autoplay on pages from the URL templates whitelist</string>
      <string id="VideoCaptureAllowed">Enable video capture</string>
      <string id="VideoCaptureAllowed_Explain">VideoCaptureAllowed

The policy allows or restricts sites to capture video from devices on the user's computer.

Features

- This is an increased security policy. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support2/browser-corporate/ru/deployment/windows/setting-policy#advanced
- Available in the mobile version of the Browser for organizations. More details: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html

Values

- Not Configured, Enabled: Users see the access request. URLs from the VideoCaptureAllowedUrls policy have access to video devices without a request.
- Available in the mobile version of the Browser for organizations. More details: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html
- Disabled: Only URLs from the VideoCaptureAllowedUrls policy can capture video. These sites get access automatically, without a request.

Safety recommendations

Value: Disabled. Disable video capture to prevent possible data leakage.

Possible problems. Users won't be able to connect to video conferencing sites. To allow audio capture on such sites, use the VideoCaptureAllowedUrls policy.</string>
      <string id="VideoCaptureAllowedUrls">Set a list of URLs that are allowed to capture video</string>
      <string id="VideoCaptureAllowedUrls_Explain">VideoCaptureAllowedUrls

The policy sets a list of URLs with automatic access to video capture, even if it is restricted by the VideoCaptureAllowed policy.

Features

- Available in the mobile version of the Browser for organizations. More details: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: Users determine for each URL whether to allow access to video devices.
- Enabled: The administrator sets the list of URLs that have access without a request. You can use URL templates. The "*" wildcard is only used for subdomains in this form: "[*.]".

For more information about URL templates, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/policy/url-patterns.html

Convert non-Latin URLs (for example, яндекс.рф) via punycode: https://www.reg.ru/web-tools/punycode

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example value:

https://www.example.com/
https://[*.]example.edu/</string>
      <string id="VideoCaptureAllowedUrlsDesc">List of URLs that access video recording devices without a request</string>
      <string id="Behavior_group">Behavior</string>
      <string id="DefaultPageSaveSettings">Configure saving pages</string>
      <string id="DefaultPageSaveSettings_Explain">DefaultPageSaveSettings

The policy controls the "Save as..." function in the context menu.

The PageSaveAllowedForUrls and PageSaveBlockedForUrls policies supersede DefaultPageSaveSettings.

Features

- Available in the mobile version of the Browser for organizations. More details: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html
- Works only in the extended version of Yandex Browser for organizations. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: Saving pages and their elements is allowed.
- Enabled: The administrator sets the mode for saving pages and their elements:
     - Allowed.
     - Prohibited.</string>
      <string id="DefaultPageSaveSettings_AllowPageSave">Allowed</string>
      <string id="DefaultPageSaveSettings_BlockPageSave">Prohibited</string>
      <string id="DefaultUploadSetting">Configure uploading files to sites</string>
      <string id="DefaultUploadSetting_Explain">DefaultUploadSetting

The policy allows or prohibits uploading files to sites.

The UploadAllowedForUrls and UploadBlockedForUrls policies take precedence over the DefaultUploadSetting policy.

Features

- This is an increased security policy. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support2/browser-corporate/ru/deployment/windows/setting-policy#advanced
- Available in the mobile version of the Browser for organizations. More details: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html
- Works only in the extended version of Yandex Browser for organizations. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: Upload is allowed.
- Enabled: The administrator determines the upload mode:
     - Allowed.
     - Prohibited.

Security recommendations

Value: Enabled (Prohibited). Prevent uploading files to websites to protect against data breaches.</string>
      <string id="DefaultUploadSetting_AllowFilesUpload">Allowed</string>
      <string id="DefaultUploadSetting_BlockFilesUpload">Not allowed</string>
      <string id="DisableInformationDragAllowedUrls">Set a list of URLs from which data can be dragged</string>
      <string id="DisableInformationDragAllowedUrls_Explain">DisableInformationDragAllowedUrls

The policy sets a list of URLs from which data can be dragged. The URL of each iframe inside the page is taken into account, not the URL of the entire page.

The policy only works when the DisableInformationDragAndDrop policy is enabled.

Features

- This is an increased security policy. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support2/browser-corporate/ru/deployment/windows/setting-policy#advanced
- Works only in the extended version of Yandex Browser for organizations. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: The policy is not set.
- Enabled: The administrator sets a list of URLs. You can use the "internal_urls" keyword to designate all single-domain sites. For example, the rule will apply to "https://example" but not to "https://example.com". You can use URL templates. 

For more information about URL templates, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/policy/url-patterns.html

Convert non-Latin URLs (for example, яндекс.рф) via punycode: https://www.reg.ru/web-tools/punycode

Example value: testserver.example.com;[*.]example.org

Security recommendations

Value: Enabled

testserver.example.com;[*.]example.org

Enable the DisableInformationDragAndDrop policy. Block the use of developer tools for all URLs with the DisableInformationDragBlockedUrls policy to protect against data leakage. Set exceptions for the URLs you want to allow.</string>
      <string id="DisableInformationDragAndDrop">Disable Drag and Drop</string>
      <string id="DisableInformationDragAndDrop_Explain">DisableInformationDragAndDrop

The policy disables drag-and-drop within the Yandex Browser window, including dragging and dropping from other applications.

Features

- This is an increased security policy. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support2/browser-corporate/ru/deployment/windows/setting-policy#advanced
- Works only in the extended version of Yandex Browser for organizations. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: Drag and drop is enabled.
- Enabled: Drag and drop is disabled.

Security recommendations

Value: Enabled. Disable drag-and-drop data transfer to protect against data leakage.</string>
      <string id="DisableInformationDragBlockedUrls">Set a list of URLs from which data can't be dragged</string>
      <string id="DisableInformationDragBlockedUrls_Explain">DisableInformationDragBlockedUrls

The policy sets a list of URLs from which it is forbidden to drag data. The URL of each iframe inside the page is taken into account, not the URL of the entire page.

The policy only works when the DisableInformationDragAndDrop policy is enabled.

Features

- This is an increased security policy. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support2/browser-corporate/ru/deployment/windows/setting-policy#advanced
- Works only in the extended version of Yandex Browser for organizations. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: The policy is not set.
- Enabled: The administrator sets a list of URLs. You can use the "internal_urls" keyword to designate all single-domain sites. For example, the rule will apply to "https://example" but not to "https://example.com". You can use URL templates.

For more information about URL templates, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/policy/url-patterns.html

Convert non-Latin URLs (for example, яндекс.рф) via punycode: https://www.reg.ru/web-tools/punycode

Example value: testserver.example.com;[*.]example.org

Security recommendations

Value: Enabled *

Enable the DisableInformationDragAndDrop policy. Prevent drag-and-drop data transfer for all URLs to protect against data leakage. Set exceptions with the DisableInformationDragAllowedUrls policy.</string>
      <string id="DisableInformationDropAllowedUrls">Set a list of URLs to which data can be dropped</string>
      <string id="DisableInformationDropAllowedUrls_Explain">DisableInformationDropAllowedUrls

The policy sets a list of URLs to which data can be dragged and dropped. The URL of each iframe inside the page is taken into account, not the URL of the entire page.

The policy only works when the DisableInformationDragAndDrop policy is enabled.

Features

- Works only in the extended version of Yandex Browser for organizations. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: The policy is not set.
- Enabled: The administrator sets a list of URLs. You can use the "internal_urls" keyword to designate all single-domain sites. For example, the rule will apply to "https://example" but not to "https://example.com". You can use URL templates.

For more information about URL templates, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/policy/url-patterns.html

Convert non-Latin URLs (for example, яндекс.рф) via punycode: https://www.reg.ru/web-tools/punycode

Example value: testserver.example.com;[*.]example.org

Security recommendations

Value: Enabled

testserver.example.com;[*.]example.org

Enable the DisableInformationDragAndDrop policy. Block the use of developer tools for all URLs with the DisableInformationDropBlockedUrls policy to protect against data leakage. Set exceptions for the URLs you want to allow.</string>
      <string id="DisableInformationDropBlockedUrls">Set a list of URLs to which data can't be dropped</string>
      <string id="DisableInformationDropBlockedUrls_Explain">DisableInformationDropBlockedUrls

The policy sets a list of URLs to which it is forbidden to drag and drop data. The URL of each iframe inside the page is taken into account, not the URL of the entire page.

The policy only works when the DisableInformationDragAndDrop policy is enabled.

Features

- Works only in the extended version of Yandex Browser for organizations. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: The policy is not set.
- Enabled: The administrator sets a list of URLs. You can use the "internal_urls" keyword to designate all single-domain sites. For example, the rule will apply to "https://example" but not to "https://example.com". You can use URL templates.

For more information about URL templates, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/policy/url-patterns.html

Convert non-Latin URLs (for example, яндекс.рф) via punycode: https://www.reg.ru/web-tools/punycode

Example value: testserver.example.com;[*.]example.org

Security recommendations

Value: Enabled *

Enable the DisableInformationDragAndDrop policy. Prevent drag-and-drop data transfer for all URLs to protect against data leakage. Set exceptions with the DisableInformationDropAllowedUrls policy.</string>
      <string id="NewTabSessionOnStartup">Open the new tab page when the browser is restarted</string>
      <string id="NewTabSessionOnStartup_Explain">NewTabSessionOnStartup

When restarting, Yandex Browser can restore tabs and open the new tab page at the same time. The policy controls this setting.

The new tab page opens:
- When Yandex Browser is first started.
- If there are no tabs open in Yandex Browser.
- When you click the button to open a new tab.

Values

- Not Configured: After restarting, Yandex Browser restores all tabs and opens the new tab page. Users can change this setting. 
- Enabled: After restarting, Yandex Browser restores all tabs and opens the new tab page. Users can't change this parameter.
- Disabled: After restarting, Yandex Browser restores all tabs and opens the last active tab. Users can't change this setting.</string>
      <string id="PageSaveAllowedForUrls">Allow saving pages for URLs from the list</string>
      <string id="PageSaveAllowedForUrls_Explain">PageSaveAllowedForUrls

The policy sets a list of URLs where the "Save as..." function is available in the context menu.

The PageSaveBlockedForUrls policy supersedes DefaultPageSaveSettings and PageSaveAllowedForUrls. The PageSaveAllowedForUrls policy supersedes DefaultPageSaveSettings.

Features

- Available in the mobile version of the Browser for organizations. More details: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html
- Works only in the extended version of Yandex Browser for organizations. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: The value of the DefaultPageSaveSetting policy is used (if it is set).
- Enabled: The administrator sets a list of URLs. You can use URL patterns. The "*" wildcard is only used for subdomains in this form: "[*.]".

For more information about URL patterns, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/policy/url-patterns.html

Convert non-Latin URLs (for example, яндекс.рф) to punycode: https://www.reg.ru/web-tools/punycode

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example value:

https://www.example.com
[*.]example.edu</string>
      <string id="PageSaveAllowedForUrlsDesc">Allow saving pages for URLs from the list</string>
      <string id="PageSaveBlockedForUrls">Prohibit saving pages and their URL elements from the list</string>
      <string id="PageSaveBlockedForUrls_Explain">PageSaveBlockedForUrls

Attention. The policy is outdated and it is not recommended to use it. To manage the saving of pages, use the policies of the YandexDownloadRestrictions group.

The policy sets a list of URLs that prohibit using:
- Save functions in the context menu for pages and their elements: audio, videos, images, files, and other objects.
- The "Save" function in the SmartBox.

The PageSaveBlockedForUrls policy supersedes DefaultPageSaveSettings and PageSaveAllowedForUrls. The PageSaveAllowedForUrls policy supersedes DefaultPageSaveSettings.

Features

- Available in the mobile version of the Browser for organizations. More details: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html
- Works only in the extended version of Yandex Browser for organizations. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: The value of the DefaultPageSaveSetting policy is used (if it is set).
- Enabled: The administrator sets a list of URLs. You can use URL patterns. The "*" wildcard is only used for subdomains in this form: "[*.]".

For more information about URL patterns, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/policy/url-patterns.html

Convert non-Latin URLs (for example, яндекс.рф) to punycode: https://www.reg.ru/web-tools/punycode

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example value:

https://www.example.com
[*.]example.edu</string>
      <string id="PageSaveBlockedForUrlsDesc">Prohibit saving pages for URLs from the list</string>
      <string id="PrivateNetworkAccessRespectPreflightResultsEnabled">Check preflight request to hosts from a private network before the main request</string>
      <string id="PrivateNetworkAccessRespectPreflightResultsEnabled_Explain">PrivateNetworkAccessRespectPreflightResultsEnabled

The policy enables checking preflight requests (OPTIONS) to hosts from a private network before main requests (GET). The preflight request should be successful, otherwise the corresponding main request is not sent. 

For more information about preflight requests, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/security/protection-private-networks.html

Features

- Works only in the extended version of Yandex Browser for organizations. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: Checking preflight requests is disabled.
- Enabled: Yandex Browser checks the preflight request before executing the main request to hosts from a private network. If the preflight request is not successful, the main request is not sent.</string>
      <string id="UploadAllowedForUrls">Allow uploading files to URLs from the list</string>
      <string id="UploadAllowedForUrls_Explain">UploadAllowedForUrls

The policy sets a list of URLs to which users can upload files.

The policy works if uploading from the desired paths is allowed by the UploadAllowedFromLocations and UploadBlockedFromLocations policies.

The policy supersedes DefaultUploadSetting and UploadBlockedForUrls.

Features

- This is an increased security policy. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support2/browser-corporate/ru/deployment/windows/setting-policy#advanced
- Available in the mobile version of the Browser for organizations. More details: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html
- Works only in the extended version of Yandex Browser for organizations. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: The value of the DefaultUploadSetting policy is used (if it is set).
- Enabled: The administrator sets the list of URLs. You can use URL templates.

For more information about URL templates, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/policy/url-patterns.html

Convert non-Latin URLs (for example, яндекс.рф) via punycode: https://www.reg.ru/web-tools/punycode

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example value:

https://www.example.com
[*.]example.edu

Security recommendations

Value: Enabled

https://www.example.com
[*.]example.edu

Block uploading files to all sites with the DefaultUploadSetting and UploadBlockedForURLs policies. Set exceptions for trusted sites with the UploadAllowedForUrls policy.</string>
      <string id="UploadAllowedForUrlsDesc">Allow uploading files to the URLs from the list</string>
      <string id="UploadAllowedFromLocations">Allow uploading files from the location list</string>
      <string id="UploadAllowedFromLocations_Explain">UploadAllowedFromLocations

The policy allows uploading files over the path list.

The policy works if uploading to the desired URLs allowed by the DefaultUploadSetting, UploadAllowedForUrls and UploadBlockedForUrls policies.

The policy takes precedence over the UploadBlockedFromLocations policy.

Features

- Available in the mobile version of the Browser for organizations. More details: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html
- Works only in the extended version of Yandex Browser for organizations. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: The value of the DefaultUploadSetting policy is used (if it is set).
- Enabled: The administrator sets the list of paths. You can use supported variables. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/policy/supported-variables.html

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example value:

C:\Windows\path
//network/path
/unix/path
${program_files}\folder
${documents}\folder</string>
      <string id="UploadAllowedFromLocationsDesc">Alow uploading files from the location list</string>
      <string id="UploadBlockedForUrls">Prohibit uploading files to the URLs from the list</string>
      <string id="UploadBlockedForUrls_Explain">UploadBlockedForUrls

The policy sets a list of URLs to which users can't upload files.

The policy supersedes the DefaultUploadSetting policy. The UploadAllowedForUrls policy supersedes UploadBlockedForUrls.

Features

- This is an increased security policy. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support2/browser-corporate/ru/deployment/windows/setting-policy#advanced
- Available in the mobile version of the Browser for organizations. More details: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html
- Works only in the extended version of Yandex Browser for organizations. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: The value of the DefaultUploadSetting policy is used (if it is set).
- Enabled: The administrator sets the list of URLs. You can use URL templates.

For more information about URL templates, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/policy/url-patterns.html

Convert non-Latin URLs (for example, яндекс.рф) via punycode: https://www.reg.ru/web-tools/punycode

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example value:

https://www.example.com
[*.]example.edu

Security recommendations

Value: Enabled

https://www.example.com
[*.]example.edu

Enable the policy and configure restrictions for uploading files on URLs to reduce the risk of data leakage through uploading files to untrusted resources.</string>
      <string id="UploadBlockedForUrlsDesc">Don't allow uploading files to the URLs from the list</string>
      <string id="UploadBlockedFromLocations">Don't allow uploading files from the location list</string>
      <string id="UploadBlockedFromLocations_Explain">UploadBlockedFromLocations

The policy saves uploading files from the list of paths.

The UploadAllowedFromLocations policy takes precedence over the UploadBlockedFromLocations policy.

Features

- Available in the mobile version of the Browser for organizations. More details: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html
- Works only in the extended version of Yandex Browser for organizations. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: The value of the DefaultUploadSetting policy is used (if it is set).
- Enabled: The administrator sets the list of paths. You can use supported variables. The value "*" restricts uploading over all local and network paths.

For more information about setting up paths, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/policy/supported-variables.html

For more information about supported variables, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/policy/supported-variables.html

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example value:

C:\windows\path
//network/path
/unix/path
${program_files}\folder
${documents}\folder</string>
      <string id="UploadBlockedFromLocationsDesc">Don't allow uploading files from the location list</string>
      <string id="YandexAutoLaunchMode">Configure Browser autorun when you turn on your computer</string>
      <string id="YandexAutoLaunchMode_Explain">YandexAutoLaunchMode

The policy sets up Yandex Browser autorun when the computer is turned on.

The policy controls the "Open Yandex Browser at Windows startup" setting. To go to the settings, in Yandex Browser, click "Main Menu" → "Settings" → "System" → "Autorun and background mode" and select the mode:

- "Always" — Yandex Browser starts automatically after the computer is turned on.
- "If it was open at computer shutdown" — Yandex Browser starts automatically if it was opened when the computer was turned off.
- "Never" — Yandex Browser does not start automatically after turning on the computer.

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: Yandex Browser starts automatically after the computer is turned on. Users can change the mode.
- Enabled — the administrator sets Yandex Browser startup mode. Users cannot change the mode.</string>
      <string id="YandexAutoLaunchMode_Never">Never</string>
      <string id="YandexAutoLaunchMode_Always">Always</string>
      <string id="YandexAutoLaunchMode_Restart">If it was opened when the computer was turned off</string>
      <string id="YandexBackgroundModeDisableRestart">Disable Browser restarting in background mode</string>
      <string id="YandexBackgroundModeDisableRestart_Explain">YandexBackgroundModeDisableRestart

The policy disables Yandex Browser restarts in the background.

Restart is disabled, even if it is set in Yandex Browser settings:

- In the "Open Yandex Browser at Windows startup" setting, the "Always" or "If it was open at computer shutdown" mode is enabled.
- The "Allow background work" setting is enabled.

To go to the settings, in Yandex Browser, click "Main Menu" → "Settings" → "System" → "Autorun and background mode".

The policy is available for Browsers version 24.6.1 and higher.

Features

- Works only on Windows and Linux.

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled — restarting Yandex Browser in the background is enabled.
- Enabled — restarting Yandex Browser in the background is disabled.</string>
      <string id="YandexClipboardAccessByPolicyEnabled">Enable copy and paste management policies</string>
      <string id="YandexClipboardAccessByPolicyEnabled_Explain">YandexClipboardAccessByPolicyEnabled

The policy enables policies for managing copy and paste functionality: 

- YandexPasteExt
- YandexCopyAllowlist
- YandexCopyBlocklist
- YandexPasteAllowlist
- YandexPasteBlocklist

The policy is available for Browsers version 23.9.5 and higher.

Features

- This is an increased security policy. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support2/browser-corporate/ru/deployment/windows/setting-policy#advanced
- Available in the mobile version of the Browser for organizations. More details: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html
- Works only in the extended version of Yandex Browser for organizations. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: The policies are disabled.
- Enabled: The policies are enabled.

Security recommendations

Value: Enabled. Enable the policy. Block copying and pasting to the clipboard on all URLs with the YandexCopyBlocklist and YandexPasteBlocklist policies to reduce the risk of data leakage through clipboard paste. Set exceptions for trusted URLs with the YandexCopyAllowlist and YandexPasteAllowlist policies.</string>
      <string id="YandexClipboardEventsReporting">Specify lists of URLs to send security events for clipboard operations</string>
      <string id="YandexClipboardEventsReporting_Explain">YandexClipboardEventsReporting

The policy defines lists of URLs for which the ClipboardRestrictionViolation security event is sent during clipboard operations.

If a clipboard operation is prohibited by other policies, the security event is sent regardless of the settings of this policy.

The policy works only when the YandexClipboardAccessByPolicyEnabled policy is enabled, along with one of the following policies: YandexSecurityEventConnectorUrl or YandexSecurityEventConnectors.

The policy is available for Browsers version 25.10.3 and higher.

Features

- Available in the mobile version of the Browser for organizations. More details: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html
- It only works in the extended version of the Browser for organizations. Learn more: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled — no security event is generated.
- Enabled — the administrator sets the parameters:
     - copy — a list for copy operations;
          - report — URLs, for which the generation of a security event is enabled;
          - ignore — URLs, for which the generation of a security event is disabled.
     - paste — a list for paste operations;
          - report — URLs, for which the generation of a security event is enabled;
          - ignore — URLs, for which the generation of a security event is disabled.

For more information about URL patterns: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/policy/url-patterns.html

You can also use the keyword "internal_urls" to denote all same‑domain sites. For example, in this case, https://example will match the rule, while https://example.com will not.

Convert non‑Latin URLs (e.g., яндекс.рф) using Punycode: https://www.reg.ru/web-tools/punycode

You can configure via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config


Example of a value:

{
  "copy": {
    "report": [
      "internal_urls",
      "yandex.ru"
    ],
    "ignore": [
      "example.org",
      "yandex.com"
    ]
  },
  "paste": {
    "report": [
      "*"
    ],
    "ignore": [
      "example.org",
      "yandex.ru"
    ]
  }
}</string>
      <string id="YandexClipboardSizeRestriction">Limit the size of the clipboard</string>
      <string id="YandexClipboardSizeRestriction_Explain">YandexClipboardSizeRestriction

The policy limits the maximum size of the clipboard when copying and pasting text and images for specified URLs.

The YandexClipboardSizeRestriction policy takes precedence over the YandexClipboardMaxTextSize and YandexClipboardMaxImageSize policies.

Buffer sizes are set separately during operations.
- image copying;
- copy text;
- inserting images;
- text insertion.
At the same time, for copy and paste operations, URLs for which restrictions apply and URLs for which they do not apply are set separately.

The policy is available for Browsers version 25.2.4 and higher.

Features

- Available in the mobile version of the Browser for organizations. More details: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html
- It only works in the extended version of the Browser for organizations. Learn more: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled — the size is limited by the OS settings.
- Enabled — the administrator sets a list of URLs for clipboard restrictions during copy and paste operations. You can use the "internal_urls" keyword to designate all single-domain sites. For example, the rule will apply to "https://example" but not to "https://example.com". After disabling the policy, the previously set list of URLs is not saved.

Learn more about URL templates: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/policy/url-patterns.html 

Convert URLs without Latin letters (for example, яндекс.рф) via punycode: https://www.reg.ru/web-tools/punycode

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example of a value:

{
    "copy": {
        "apply": [
            "[*.]badssl.com",
            "http://192.168.56.1"
        ],
        "not_apply": [
            "*"
        ],
        "max_image_size": 150000,
        "max_text_size": 100
    },
    "paste": {
        "apply": [
            "file:///*",
            "internal_urls"
        ],
        "not_apply": [
            "*"
        ],
        "max_image_size": 150000,
        "max_text_size": 100
    }
}</string>
      <string id="YandexCopyAllowlist">Allow copying on URLs from the list</string>
      <string id="YandexCopyAllowlist_Explain">YandexCopyAllowlist

The policy sets a list of URLs where copying to the clipboard is allowed.

The policy takes precedence over the YandexCopyBlocklist policy.

The policy only works when the YandexClipboardAccessByPolicyEnabled policy is enabled.

The policy is available for Browsers version 23.9.5 and higher.

Features

- This is an increased security policy. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support2/browser-corporate/ru/deployment/windows/setting-policy#advanced
- Available in the mobile Browser version for organizations. Learn more: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html
- It only works in the extended version of the Browser for organizations. Learn more: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: The list is empty.
- Enabled: The administrator sets a list of URLs.
You can't set the same rules in the YandexCopyAllowlist and YandexCopyBlocklist policies.
You can use URL templates: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/policy/url-patterns.html
You can use the keyword "internal_urls" to designate all single-domain sites. For example, the rule will apply to "https://example" but not to "https://example.com".

Convert URLs without Latin letters (e.g., яндекс.рф) via punycode: https://www.reg.ru/web-tools/punycode

Example of the value:

test.ru;[*.]example.com;192.168.0.1;internal_urls;browser://policy/

Security recommendations

Value: Enabled

"test.ru;[*.]example.com;192.168.0.1;internal_urls;browser://policy/"

Enable the YandexClipboardAccessByPolicyEnabled policy. Block copying and pasting on all URLs using the YandexCopyBlocklist and YandexPasteBlocklist policies to reduce the risk of data leakage through clipboard paste. Set exceptions for trusted URLs using the YandexCopyAllowlist and YandexPasteAllowlist policies.</string>
      <string id="YandexCopyBlocklist">Prohibit copying for URLs from the list</string>
      <string id="YandexCopyBlocklist_Explain">YandexCopyBlocklist

The policy sets a list of URLs where copying to the clipboard is restricted.

The YandexCopyAllowlist policy supersedes YandexCopyBlocklist.

The policy only works when the YandexClipboardAccessByPolicyEnabled policy is enabled.

The policy is available for Browsers version 23.9.5 and higher.

Features

- This is an increased security policy. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support2/browser-corporate/ru/deployment/windows/setting-policy#advanced
- Available in the mobile version of the Browser for organizations. More details: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html
- Works only in the extended version of Yandex Browser for organizations. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: The list is empty.
- Enabled: The administrator sets a list of URLs.
A blank value or the wildcard character «*» prohibits copying on all websites.
You can't set the same rules in the YandexCopyAllowlist and YandexCopyBlocklist policies.
You can use URL templates: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/policy/url-patterns.html
You can use the keyword "internal_urls" to designate all single-domain sites. For example, the rule will apply to "https://example" but not to "https://example.com".

Convert URLs without Latin letters (e.g., яндекс.рф) via punycode: https://www.reg.ru/web-tools/punycode

Example of the value:

test.ru;[*.]example.com;192.168.0.1;internal_urls;browser://policy/

Security recommendations

Value: Enabled *

Enable the YandexClipboardAccessByPolicyEnabled policy. Block copying and pasting to the clipboard on all URLs using the YandexCopyBlocklist and YandexPasteBlocklist policies to reduce the risk of data leakage through clipboard paste. Set exceptions for trusted URLs using the YandexCopyAllowlist and YandexPasteAllowlist policies.</string>
      <string id="YandexDownloadRestrictionsAllowedTypes">Set a list of MIME file types allowed for download</string>
      <string id="YandexDownloadRestrictionsAllowedTypes_Explain">YandexDownloadRestrictionsAllowedTypes

The policy sets a list of MIME file types allowed for downloading. Downloading is prohibited for all other MIME file types.

Downloading is prohibited for file types not from the list:

- using the "Save" button in the Smart bar;
- using the keyboard shortcuts Ctrl + S;
- using the options "Save image as ..." and "Save page" in the context menu.

For more information about MIME types, see https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Media_type

The policy supersedes YandexDownloadRestrictionsBlockedTypes.

The policy only works when the YandexDownloadRestrictionsEnabled policy is enabled.

The policy is available for Browsers version 24.1.3 and higher.

Features

- This is an increased security policy. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support2/browser-corporate/ru/deployment/windows/setting-policy#advanced
- Available in the mobile version of Yandex Browser for organizations. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html
- Works only in the extended version of Yandex Browser for organizations. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: The policy is not set.
- Enabled: The administrator sets the list of types. You can use the wildcard "*". For example, "*" or "*/*".

Example value:

text/html;*/*;image/png

Security recommendations

Value: Enabled

text/html;*/*;image/png

Enable the YandexDownloadRestrictionsEnabled policy. Block all file types and URLs with the YandexDownloadRestrictionsBlockedUrls and YandexDownloadRestrictionsBlockedTypes policies to reduce the risk of data leakage through file downloads from untrusted sites. Set exceptions for trusted sites with the YandexDownloadRestrictionsAllowedUrls and YandexDownloadRestrictionsAllowedTypes policies.</string>
      <string id="YandexDownloadRestrictionsAllowedUrls">Set a list of URLs from which users can download files.</string>
      <string id="YandexDownloadRestrictionsAllowedUrls_Explain">YandexDownloadRestrictionsAllowedUrls

The policy sets a list of URLs from which files can be downloaded. Downloading is prohibited for all other URLs.

On some pages, the download button redirects to a different URL. The policy does not protect against redirects. To allow downloading, add the end URL to the list of policy values.

Downloading is prohibited for URLs not from the list:

- using the "Save" button in the Smart bar;
- using the keyboard shortcuts Ctrl + S;
- using the options "Save image as ..." and "Save page" in the context menu.

The policy supersedes YandexDownloadRestrictionsBlockedUrls.

The policy only works if the YandexDownloadRestrictionsEnabled policy is enabled.

Features

- This is an increased security policy. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support2/browser-corporate/ru/deployment/windows/setting-policy#advanced
- Available in the mobile version of Yandex Browser for organizations. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html
- Works only in the extended version of Yandex Browser for organizations. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: The policy isn't set.
- Enabled: The administrator sets the list of URLs. You can use the "internal_urls" keyword to designate all single-domain sites. For example, the rule will apply to "https://example" but not to "https://example.com". You can use URL templates. 

For more information about URL templates, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/policy/url-patterns.html

Convert non-Latin URLs (for example, яндекс.рф) via punycode: https://www.reg.ru/web-tools/punycode

Example value: testserver.example.com;[*.]example.org

Security recommendations

Value: Enabled

testserver.example.com;
[*.]example.org

Enable the YandexDownloadRestrictionsEnabled policy. Block all types of files and all URLs with the YandexDownloadRestrictionsBlockedUrls and YandexDownloadRestrictionsBlockedTypes policies to reduce the risk of data leakage through file downloads from untrusted sites. Set exceptions for trusted sites with the YandexDownloadRestrictionsAllowedUrls and YandexDownloadRestrictionsAllowedTypes policies.</string>
      <string id="YandexDownloadRestrictionsBlockedTypes">Set a list of MIME file types that can't be downloaded</string>
      <string id="YandexDownloadRestrictionsBlockedTypes_Explain">YandexDownloadRestrictionsBlockedTypes

The policy sets a list of MIME file types restricted for downloading.

Downloading is prohibited for file types from the list:

- using the "Save" button in the Smart bar;
- using the keyboard shortcuts Ctrl + S;
- using the options "Save image as ..." and "Save page" in the context menu.

For more information about MIME types, see https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Media_type

The YandexDownloadRestrictionsAllowedTypes policy supersedes YandexDownloadRestrictionsBlockedTypes.

The policy only works when the YandexDownloadRestrictionsEnabled policy is enabled.

The policy is available for Browsers version 24.1.3 and higher.

Features

- This is an increased security policy. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support2/browser-corporate/ru/deployment/windows/setting-policy#advanced
- Available in the mobile version of Yandex Browser for organizations. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html
- Works only in the extended version of Yandex Browser for organizations. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: The policy is not set.
- Enabled: The administrator sets the list of types. You can use the wildcard "*". For example, "*" or "*/*".

Example value:

text/html;*/*;image/png

Security recommendations

Value: Enabled */*

Enable the YandexDownloadRestrictionsEnabled policy. Block all types of files and all URLs using the YandexDownloadRestrictionsBlockedUrls and YandexDownloadRestrictionsBlockedTypes policies to reduce the risk of data leakage through file downloads from untrusted sites. Set exceptions for trusted sites using the YandexDownloadRestrictionsAllowedUrls and YandexDownloadRestrictionsAllowedTypes policies.</string>
      <string id="YandexDownloadRestrictionsBlockedUrls">Set a list of URLs from which users can't download files.</string>
      <string id="YandexDownloadRestrictionsBlockedUrls_Explain">YandexDownloadRestrictionsBlockedUrls

The policy sets a list of URLs from which files can't be downloaded.

On some pages, the download button redirects to a different URL. The policy does not protect against redirects. To allow downloading, add the end URL to the list of policy values.

Downloading is prohibited for URLs from the list:

- using the "Save" button in the Smart bar;
- using the keyboard shortcuts Ctrl + S;
- using the options "Save image as ..." and "Save page" in the context menu.

The YandexDownloadRestrictionsAllowedUrls policy supersedes YandexDownloadRestrictionsBlockedUrls.

The policy only works if the YandexDownloadRestrictionsEnabled policy is enabled.

Features

- This is an increased security policy. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support2/browser-corporate/ru/deployment/windows/setting-policy#advanced
- Available in the mobile version of Yandex Browser for organizations. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html
- Works only in the extended version of Yandex Browser for organizations. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: The policy isn't set.
- Enabled: The administrator sets a list of URLs. You can use the "internal_urls" keyword to designate all single-domain sites. For example, the rule will apply to "https://example" but not to "https://example.com". You can use URL templates. 

For more information about URL templates, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/policy/url-patterns.html

Convert non-Latin URLs (for example, яндекс.рф) via punycode: https://www.reg.ru/web-tools/punycode

Example value: 

testserver.example.com;[*.]example.org

Security recommendations

Value: Enabled *

Enable the YandexDownloadRestrictionsEnabled policy. Block downloading of all file types and from all URLs using the YandexDownloadRestrictionsBlockedUrls and YandexDownloadRestrictionsBlockedTypes policies to reduce the risk of data leakage through downloading files from untrusted sites. Set exceptions for trusted sites using the YandexDownloadRestrictionsAllowedUrls and YandexDownloadRestrictionsAllowedTypes policies.</string>
      <string id="YandexDownloadRestrictionsEnabled">Enable file download policies</string>
      <string id="YandexDownloadRestrictionsEnabled_Explain">YandexDownloadRestrictionsEnabled

Policy enables download policies:

* YandexDownloadRestrictionsAllowedUrls
* YandexDownloadRestrictionsBlockedUrls
* YandexDownloadRestrictionsAllowedTypes
* YandexDownloadRestrictionsBlockedTypes

Features

- This is an increased security policy. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support2/browser-corporate/ru/deployment/windows/setting-policy#advanced
- Available in the mobile version of Yandex Browser for organizations. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html
- Works only in the extended version of Yandex Browser for organizations. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: The policies are disabled.
- Enabled: The policies are enabled.

Security recommendations

Value: Enabled. Enable the policy. Block downloading of all types of files and from all URLs by YandexDownloadRestrictionsBlockedUrls and YandexDownloadRestrictionsBlockedTypes policies to reduce the risks of data leakage through downloading of files from untrusted sites. Set exceptions for trusted sites by YandexDownloadRestrictionsAllowedUrls and YandexDownloadRestrictionsAllowedTypes policies.</string>
      <string id="YandexPasteExt">Allow or prohibit URLs from pasting from the clipboard</string>
      <string id="YandexPasteExt_Explain">YandexPasteExt

The policy sets lists of URLs where it is allowed or prohibited to paste data from the clipboard.

The policy only works when the YandexClipboardAccessByPolicyEnabled policy is enabled.

The policy is available for Browsers version 24.7.6 and higher.

Features

- This is an increased security policy. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support2/browser-corporate/ru/deployment/windows/setting-policy#advanced
- Available in the mobile version of the Browser for organizations. More details: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html
- Works only in the extended version of the Browser for organizations. More details: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: pasting data from the clipboard is allowed on any sites.
- Enabled: the administrator sets the parameters:
     - allow: a list of allowed URLs to paste from the clipboard;
     - deny: a list of forbidden URLs to paste from the clipboard.

If the list of prohibited URLs is not specified or a wildcard "*" is specified, the policy prohibits pasting from the buffer on all sites except those allowed.
You can use URL templates: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/policy/url-patterns

You can use the keyword "internal_urls" to designate all single-domain sites. For example, then https://example it will fall under the rule, and https://example.com — No, it's not.
Convert URLs with non‑Latin characters (e.g., яндекс.рф) to punycode: https://www.reg.ru/web-tools/punycode
In the Local Group Policy Editor and Registry Editor, only single‑line values can be set.  To convert multi‑line values into a single line, use a JSON Beautifier: https://jsonbeautifier.org/
Paste the value into the left pane of the tool and click Minify.

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example of a value:

{
    "allow": [
      "test.ru",
      "192.168.0.1",
      "$(foo)",
      "internal_urls"
    ],
    "deny": [
      "[*.]example.com",
      "browser://policy/"
    ]
}

Security recommendations

Value: Enabled

"YandexPasteExt": {
  "allow": [
    "test.ru",
    "192.168.0.1",
    "internal_urls"
  ],
  "deny": [
    "*"
  ]
}

Enable the YandexClipboardAccessByPolicyEnabled policy. Disable clipboard paste on all sites to reduce the risks of data leakage through clipboard paste. Set exceptions for trusted URLs.</string>
      <string id="YandexTextWatermarkDataSettings">Configure data for text watermarks</string>
      <string id="YandexTextWatermarkDataSettings_Explain">YandexTextWatermarkDataSettings

The policy sets up a list of user data that is displayed in a text watermark.

The policy only works when the YandexWatermark policy is enabled and the YandexWatermarkSettings policy is disabled.

You can customize the style of text watermarks in the YandexTextWatermarkStyleSettings policy.


Features

- Available in the mobile version of the Browser for organizations. More details: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html
- It only works in the extended version of the Browser for organizations. Learn more: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled — watermarks contain default data:
      - Prefix is an empty string.
      - AddUserId is the user's name.
      - AddDeviceHostName is the name of the device.
- Enabled — The administrator sets a dictionary with user data that is displayed in a text watermark. All fields are optional:
     - Prefix is an arbitrary string.
     - AddUserId — add a username (true or false).
     - AddDeviceHostName — add the device name (true or false).
     - AddBrowserSessionId — add session number (true or false).
     - AddDateTime — add date and time (true or false).
     - AddIPv4s — add IPv4 (true or false).
     - AddIPv6s — add IPv6 (true or false).


You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example of a value:

{
  "Prefix": "Test string"
  "AddUserId": true,
  "AddDeviceHostName": false,
  "AddBrowserSessionId": true,
  "AddPartnerIdHash": true,
  "AddDateTime": true,
  "AddIPv4s": false,
  "AddIPv6s": true,
}</string>
      <string id="YandexTextWatermarkStyleSettings">Customize the style of text watermarks</string>
      <string id="YandexTextWatermarkStyleSettings_Explain">YandexTextWatermarkStyleSettings

The policy adjusts the appearance settings for the text watermark.

The policy only works when the YandexWatermark, YandexTextWatermarkDataSettings policies are enabled and the YandexWatermarkSettings policy is disabled.

Features

- Available in the mobile version of the Browser for organizations. More details: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html
- It only works in the extended version of the Browser for organizations. Learn more: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled — text watermarks have default settings:

    - Positions — the location of the watermarks on the page is "Random".
    - WatermarksCount — the number of text watermarks: 8.
    - WatermarksOpacity — transparency: 30.
    - FontSize — the size of the text in millimeters: 4.
    - WatermarkRotation — the angle of rotation of the watermark in degrees: 30.
    - TextColor — the color of the watermark text: #000000.
    - TextStrokeColor — the outline color of the watermark text: #FFFFFF.

- Enabled — the administrator sets a dictionary with appearance parameters for the watermark. All fields are optional:

    - Positions — the location of watermarks on the page.

    To set up a random location, set the parameters:
        - "Type": "Random" — type "random";
        - WatermarksCount — the number of text watermarks. Range of values: from 0 to 100.
        
    To arrange the grid, set the parameters:
        - "Type": "Grid" — type "by grid";
        - SpacingX — the X-axis distance between watermarks in millimeters;
        - SpacingX — Y-axis distance between watermarks in millimeters;
        - HasShift — whether to shift every even row (true/false);
        - IsCheckered — whether to skip every even watermark in the row (true/false).

    - WatermarksCount — the number of text watermarks. Ignored for grid layout. Range of values: from 0 to 100. Deprecated parameter, use a similar parameter inside Positions.
    - WatermarksOpacity — transparency (integer from 0 to 100).
    - FontSize — the size of the text in millimeters (integer from 0 to 100).
    - WatermarkRotation — the angle of rotation of the watermark in degrees (an integer from 0 to 90).
- textColor — the color of the watermark text in the format #RRGGBBAA or #RRGGBB.
    - TextStrokeColor — the outline color of the watermark text in the format #RRGGBBAA or #RRGGBB.

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example of a value:

{
  "Positions": {
    "Type": "Grid",
    "SpacingX": 20,
    "SpacingY": 20,
    "HasShift": true,
    "IsCheckered": true
  },
  "WatermarksCount": 8,
  "WatermarksOpacity": 30,
  "FontSize": 4,
  "WatermarkRotation": 30,
  "TextColor": "#80808080",
  "TextStrokeColor": "#FFFFFF80"
}</string>
      <string id="YandexWatermark">Set a list of URLs where watermarks will be displayed</string>
      <string id="YandexWatermark_Explain">YandexWatermark

The policy sets a list of URLs where the watermark will be displayed.

To configure watermark settings, use the YandexWatermarkSettings policy.

The policy is available for Browsers version 24.1.3 and higher.

Features

- Available in the mobile version of Yandex Browser for organizations. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html
- Works only in the extended version of Yandex Browser for organizations. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: Watermarks are not displayed.
- Enabled: The administrator sets the list of URLs. You can use URL patterns. The "*" wildcard is only used for subdomains in this form: "[*.]". You can use the "internal_urls" keyword to designate all single-domain sites. For example, then https://example will fall under the rule, and https://example.com will not.
By default, watermarks have the following parameters:
     - Size: 30 mm.
     - Quantity: 8.
     - Transparency: 30%.
     - User name and device name added.
     - Session number not added.
  
For more information about URL templates, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/policy/url-patterns.html

Convert non-Latin URLs (for example, яндекс.рф) via punycode: https://www.reg.ru/web-tools/punycode

Example value: testserver.example.com;[*.]example.org

Security Recommendations

Value: Enabled *

Enable watermarks on all URLs to prevent data leakage and identify the source of the leak.</string>
      <string id="YandexWatermarkSettings">Customize the watermark in the form of QR codes</string>
      <string id="YandexWatermarkSettings_Explain">YandexWatermarkSettings

The policy sets the watermark parameters in the form of QR codes.

The policy only works when the YandexWatermark policy is enabled and the YandexTextWatermarkStyleSettings and YandexTextWatermarkDataSettings policies are disabled.

The policy is available for Browsers version 24.1.3 and higher.

Features

- This is an increased security policy. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support2/browser-corporate/ru/deployment/windows/setting-policy#advanced
- Available in the mobile version of Yandex Browser for organizations. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html
- Works only in the extended version of Yandex Browser for organizations. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: Default settings are used for watermarks:

    - the location of the watermarks on the page is "Random";
    - size in millimeters — 30;
    - quantity — 8;
    - percentage transparency — 30;
    - user name and device name added;
    - the prefix is empty.

- Enabled: The administrator sets the watermark parameters. All fields are optional:

    - Positions — the location of watermarks on the page.

    To set up a random location, set the parameters:
        - "Type": "Random" — type "random";
        - WatermarksCount — the number of watermarks. Range of values: from 0 to 100.
        
    To arrange the grid, set the parameters:
        - "Type": "Grid" — type "by grid";
        - SpacingX — the X-axis distance between watermarks in millimeters;
        - SpacingX — Y-axis distance between watermarks in millimeters;
        - HasShift — whether to shift every even row (true/false);
        - IsCheckered — whether to skip every even watermark in the row (true/false).

    - QRCodeSize — size in millimeters. The range of values is from 1 to 10,000.
    - WatermarksCount — the number of watermarks. Ignored for grid layout. Range of values: from 0 to 100. Deprecated parameter, use a similar parameter inside Positions.
    - WatermarksOpacity — transparency in percentage. The range of values is from 0 to 100, where 0 is full transparency.
    - AddUserId —  add the username (true/false).
    - AddDeviceHostName —  add the device name (true/false).
    - AddBrowserSessionId — add the session number (true/false).

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example value:

{
  "Positions": {
    "Type": "Grid",
    "SpacingX": number,
    "SpacingY": number,
    "HasShift": true,
    "IsCheckered": true
  },
  "QRCodeSize": 100,
  "WatermarksCount": 10,
  "WatermarksOpacity": 50,
  "AddUserId": true,
  "AddDeviceHostName": false,
  "AddBrowserSessionId": true
}

Security recommendations

Value: Enabled

{
 "Positions": {
 "Type": "Grid",
 "SpacingX": 20,
 "SpacingY": 20,
 "HasShift": true,
 "IsCheckered": true
 },
 "QRCodeSize": 100,
 "WatermarksCount": 10,
 "WatermarksOpacity": 50,
 "AddUserId": true,
 "AddDeviceHostName": false,
 "AddBrowserSessionId": true,
 "AddPartnerIdHash": true,
 "Prefix": "Test string"
}

Enable the YandexWatermark policy to prevent data leakage and identify the source of the leak. Configure the watermarks with the YandexWatermarkSettings policy.</string>
      <string id="BrowserNetworkTimeQueriesEnabled">Enable requests to the Google time service</string>
      <string id="BrowserNetworkTimeQueriesEnabled_Explain">BrowserNetworkTimeQueriesEnabled

The policy enables requests to the Google server to obtain accurate timestamps.

Features

- Refers to the basic security level. Learn more: https://yandex.ru/support2/browser-corporate/ru/deployment/windows/setting-policy#basic

Values

- Not Configured, Enabled: requests are enabled.
- Disabled: requests are disabled.

Safety recommendations

Value: Enabled. Enable queries in the Google Time service. This will allow the Browser to verify the validity and authenticity of the certificates.</string>
      <string id="DefaultBrowserSettingEnabled">Enable browser verification by default when launching Yandex Browser</string>
      <string id="DefaultBrowserSettingEnabled_Explain">DefaultBrowserSettingEnabled

The policy includes browser verification by default when launching Yandex Browser.

Values

- Not Configured: users can prohibit checking whether Yandex Browser is the default browser. In this case, notifications that Yandex Browser is not the default browser will no longer be displayed.
- Enabled: Yandex Browser is registered in the OS as the default browser. At startup, the Browser checks each time whether it remains the default browser. Users cannot disable this check.
- Disabled: Yandex Browser does not check at startup whether it is the default browser. Users cannot enable this check.</string>
      <string id="ForcedLanguages">Set up language preferences</string>
      <string id="ForcedLanguages_Explain">ForcedLanguages

The policy sets the order of preferred languages in the Browser. With its help, the administrator controls the language version of the content, regardless of the site settings. 

The list and order of languages can be viewed on the regional settings page: browser://settings/regionalSettings

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled — language preferences are disabled, users can customize them.
- Enabled — Language preferences are enabled. The administrator determines their order.  Users can't change it, but they can add new languages to the end of the list.

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example of a policy value:

en-US</string>
      <string id="ForcedLanguagesDesc">Set up language preferences</string>
      <string id="FullscreenAllowed">Allow fullscreen mode</string>
      <string id="FullscreenAllowed_Explain">FullscreenAllowed

The policy allows fullscreen mode. In this mode, all Yandex Browser interface elements are hidden and only the site content is displayed on the screen.

Features

- It works only on Windows and Linux.

Values

- Not Configured, Enabled: Users can activate fullscreen mode by pressing F11. Fullscreen mode can be activated by applications and extensions if they have permission.
- Disabled: Fullscreen mode is disabled for all users, applications, and extensions.</string>
      <string id="SafeSitesFilterBehavior">Configure adult content blocking</string>
      <string id="SafeSitesFilterBehavior_Explain">SafeSitesFilterBehavior

The policy sets up blocking pornographic sites.

Features

- This is an increased security policy. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support2/browser-corporate/ru/deployment/windows/setting-policy#advanced

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: Blocking is disabled.
- Enabled: The administrator sets the blocking mode:
     - Disabled.
     - Enabled for all sites except those loaded via iframe.

Safety recommendations

Value: Enabled → Enabled for all sites except those loaded via iframe. Activate the "Enabled for all sites except those loaded via iframe" mode. Users shouldn't accidentally visit sites that are more likely to have malicious content.

Possible problems. Using the Safe Search API can leak information that was entered in the SmartBox, such as passwords, internal web services, and folder structures.</string>
      <string id="SafeSitesFilterBehavior_SafeSitesFilterDisabled">Disabled</string>
      <string id="SafeSitesFilterBehavior_SafeSitesFilterEnabled">Enabled for all sites except those loaded via iframe.</string>
      <string id="InsecurePrivateNetworkRequestsAllowedForUrls">Set exceptions for the PrivateNetworkAccessRespectPreflightResultsEnabled policy</string>
      <string id="InsecurePrivateNetworkRequestsAllowedForUrls_Explain">InsecurePrivateNetworkRequestsAllowedForUrls

The policy sets exceptions for the PrivateNetworkAccessRespectPreflightResultsEnabled policy. No preliminary requests are sent to the specified list of URLs.

The policy only works when the PrivateNetworkAccessRespectPreflightResultsEnabled policy is enabled.

Features

- Works only in the extended version of Yandex Browser for organizations. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: No exceptions are set.
- Enabled: The administrator sets the list of URLs. You can use URL patterns. The «*» wildcard is only used for subdomains in this form: «[*.]». You can use the «internal_urls» keyword to designate all single-domain sites. Then, for example, https://example will fall under the rule, but https://example.com won't.

For more information about URL templates, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/policy/url-patterns.html

Convert non-Latin URLs (for example, яндекс.рф) via punycode: https://www.reg.ru/web-tools/punycode

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example value:

http://www.example.com:8080
[*.]example.edu</string>
      <string id="InsecurePrivateNetworkRequestsAllowedForUrlsDesc">Set exceptions for the PrivateNetworkAccessRespectPreflightResultsEnabled policy</string>
      <string id="HomepageLocation">Set the home page URL</string>
      <string id="HomepageLocation_Explain">HomepageLocation

The policy sets the home page URL. If a New Tab Page is set as the home page, the policy will not work.

Features

- In Windows and macOS it only works within the domain.
- Can be configured as a recommendation. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/deployment/setting-policy.html#recommend-policy

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: Users can set the URL of the home page in Yandex Browser settings.
- Enabled: The URL of the home page is set in Yandex Browser. The URL should have a standard form (http://example.com or https://example.com ). The home page will open if Yandex Browser was closed last time without tabs or using the Alt + Home key combination. Users can't change the home page in Yandex Browser.

Convert non-Latin URLs (for example, яндекс.рф) via punycode: https://www.reg.ru/web-tools/punycode

Example value:

https://ya.ru</string>
      <string id="NewTabPageLocation">Set the URL of the page to open with new tabs and windows</string>
      <string id="NewTabPageLocation_Explain">NewTabPageLocation

The policy sets the URL of the page that opens with new tabs and windows. You can set a URL or local address, for example file:///C:/Users/Alice/Downloads/example_doc. pdf.

The specified page will open when:
- Pressing the button to open a new tab.
- Opening a new window.
- Closing all tabs.

Applying the policy:
- Creating groups is not blocked.
- The policy doesn't affect the recovery of tabs after an error (the administrator can restrict opening a new tab when recovering with the NewTabSessionOnStartup policy).
- Doesn't apply to Incognito mode.

Features

- In Windows and macOS only works within the domain.

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: A new tab or window opens.
- Enabled: The administrator sets the URL of the page that opens instead of a new tab or window. Users can't change this URL.

Convert non-Latin URLs (for example, яндекс.рф) via punycode: https://www.reg.ru/web-tools/punycode

Example value: 

https://ya.ru</string>
      <string id="RestoreOnStartup">Actions on startup</string>
      <string id="RestoreOnStartup_Explain">RestoreOnStartup

The policy determines what opens upon Yandex Browser launch and restricts users from changing these settings.

Features

- On Windows and macOS only works within the domain.
- Can be configured as a recommendation. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/deployment/setting-policy.html#recommend-policy

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: Users define in the settings what opens upon Yandex Browser launch.
- Enabled: The administrator specifies one of the values:
     - Restore the last session.
     - Open the URL list. This list is set in the RestoreOnStartupURLs policy.
     - Open the URL list and restore the last session. This list is set in the RestoreOnStartupURLs policy.
     - Open the new tab page. For more information about the new tab page, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser/personalization/ntp.html</string>
      <string id="RestoreOnStartup_RestoreOnStartupIsNewTabPage">Open a new tab</string>
      <string id="RestoreOnStartup_RestoreOnStartupIsLastSession">Restore the last session</string>
      <string id="RestoreOnStartup_RestoreOnStartupIsURLs">Open one or more pages</string>
      <string id="RestoreOnStartup_RestoreOnStartupIsLastSessionAndURLs">Open the URL list and restore the last session</string>
      <string id="RestoreOnStartupURLs">Set a list of URLs that open at startup</string>
      <string id="RestoreOnStartupURLs_Explain">RestoreOnStartupURLs

The policy sets a list of URLs that open when Yandex Browser launches. The policy only works if the RestoreOnStartup policy is set to certain values.

Features

- Only works within the domain in Windows and macOS.

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: Users define in the settings which URLs open upon Yandex Browser launch.
- Enabled: The administrator sets the list of URLs to open when Yandex Browser launches. 

Convert non-Latin URLs (for example, яндекс.рф) via punycode: https://www.reg.ru/web-tools/punycode

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example value:

https://www.ya.ru
https://example.com</string>
      <string id="RestoreOnStartupURLsDesc">Set a list of URLs that open at startup</string>
      <string id="BlockingByURL_group">Blocking by URL</string>
      <string id="URLAllowlist">Set exceptions for the URLBlocklist policy</string>
      <string id="URLAllowlist_Explain">URLAllowlist

The policy sets exceptions for the URLBlocklist policy and takes priority over it. 

To allow files to be printed from Yandex Browser when "*" is set in the URLBlocklist policy, add the following values to the URLAllowlist.

For versions 23.3.2 and higher:

- browser-untrusted://*print
- browser://print
- browser-untrusted://print

For versions 23.3.1 and below:

- browser-untrusted://*print
- browser://print
- chrome-untrusted://*print

The policy allows:

- Exceptions for specific protocols, subdomains, individual domains, ports, or paths. You can specify a maximum of 1000 URLs.
- Automatic Yandex Browser call to external apps registered as handlers of protocols specified in the list (for example, tel: or ssh:).
- Exceptions for pages with Yandex Browser settings (for example, browser://settings).

Features

- Available in the mobile version of Yandex Browser for organizations. For more information, see: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: There are no exceptions to the URLBlocklist policy.
- Enabled: The administrator sets exceptions for the URLBlocklist policy. You can use URL templates. You can use the "internal_urls" keyword to designate all single-domain sites. For example, the rule will apply to "https://example" but not to "https://example.com". After disabling the policy, the previously set list of URLs is not saved.

For more information about URL templates, see: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/policy/url-patterns.html 

Convert non-Latin URLs (for example, яндекс.рф) using Punycode: https://www.reg.ru/web-tools/punycode

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example value:

example.com
https://ssl.server.com
hosting.com/good_path
https://server:8080/path
.exact.hostname.com
mailto://*

Security recommendations

Value: Enabled

example.com
https://ssl.server.com
hosting.com/good_path
https://server:8080/path
.exact.hostname.com
mailto://*

Block all URLs with the URLBlocklist policy to filter web resources with exceptions for trusted sites. Set exceptions for trusted sites using the URLAllowlist policy.</string>
      <string id="URLAllowlistDesc">Allow access to the URL list</string>
      <string id="URLBlocklist">Block URL from the specified list</string>
      <string id="URLBlocklist_Explain">URLBlocklist

The policy blocks URLs from the specified list. You can specify no more than 1000 URLs. Exceptions to this policy are set in the URLAllowlist policy.

The policy does not apply to URLs's with embedded JavaScript code and dynamically loaded data. For example, if the administrator blocks the address example.com/abc , website example.com It will still be able to load the page. example.com/abc using XMLHttpRequest.

The administrator can add pages with Browser settings to the list (for example, browser://settings). You cannot block only certain settings (for example, blocking the browser://settings/content subpage will block the entire browser://settings page).

The wildcard "*" does not block the internal pages of the Browser. To block such a page, specify its exact address, for example browser://policy.

Features

- Available in the mobile Browser version for organizations. Learn more: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled — The browser does not block URLs. 
- Enabled — the administrator sets a list of URLs. You can use URL templates. You can use the "internal_urls" keyword to designate all single-domain sites. For example, the rule will apply to "https://example" but not to "https://example.com".

After disabling the policy, the previously set list of URLs is not saved.

Learn more about URL templates: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/policy/url-patterns.html 

Convert URLs without Latin letters (for example, яндекс.рф) via punycode: https://www.reg.ru/web-tools/punycode

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example of a value:

example.com
https://ssl.server.com
hosting.com/bad_path
https://server:8080/path
.exact.hostname.com
file://*
custom_scheme:*
browser://history
browser://settings
*

Security recommendations

Value: Enabled *

Block all URLs with the URLBlocklist policy to filter web resources with exceptions for trusted sites. Set exceptions for trusted sites using the URLAllowlist policy.</string>
      <string id="URLBlocklistDesc">Blocking access to the URL list</string>
      <string id="YandexContentFiltering">Set a list of categories for blocking sites</string>
      <string id="YandexContentFiltering_Explain">YandexContentFiltering

The policy sets a list of categories of sites that will be blocked from loading. Sites are checked for belonging to categories through Yandex servers. 

The URLAllowlist policy supersedes YandexContentFiltering.

The policy is available for browsers version 23.9.5 and above.

Features

- Available in the mobile version of the Browser for organizations. More details: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html
- Works only in the extended version of Yandex Browser for organizations. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: Sites are not blocked.
- Enabled: The administrator sets the list of site categories. 

For more information about Yandex Safe Browsing technology, see https://yandex.ru/dev/safebrowsing/doc/quickstart/concepts/about.html

List of categories:

- ads: Advertising.
- armor: Weapons.
- bank: Banks.
- blogs: Blogs.
- chat: Chats.
- dating: Dating sites.
- download: File sharing.
- finance: Finance.
- forum: Forums.
- funny: Entertainment.
- games: Games.
- job: Job search.
- lottery: Gambling, lotteries, sweepstakes.
- mail: Mail.
- music: Music.
- news: News.
- porn: Pornography.
- religion: Religion.
- shop: Stores.
- soft: Software.
- video: Video.

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example value:

porn
games</string>
      <string id="YandexContentFilteringDesc">Set a list of categories for blocking sites</string>
      <string id="Bookmarks_group">Bookmarks</string>
      <string id="BookmarkBarEnabled">Enable the bookmarks bar</string>
      <string id="BookmarkBarEnabled_Explain">BookmarkBarEnabled

The policy enables a bookmarks bar in the Browser.

The policy controls the "Show the bookmarks bar" setting. To proceed to the settings, in the Browser, click "Main Menu" → "Settings" → "Interface" → "Bookmarks bar" and select it.

Features

- Can be configured as a recommendation page. Learn more: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/deployment/setting-policy.html#recommend-policy

Values

- Not Configured: the bookmarks bar is displayed. Users manage the settings.
- Enabled: the bookmarks bar is displayed. The setting is enabled, users cannot disable it.
- Disabled: the bookmarks bar is not displayed. The setting is disabled, users cannot enable it.</string>
      <string id="EditBookmarksEnabled">Configure bookmark editing</string>
      <string id="EditBookmarksEnabled_Explain">EditBookmarksEnabled

The policy enables or disables the ability to change bookmarks.

The YandexImportBookmarksPath and ImportBookmarks policies take precedence over the EditBookmarksEnabled policy.

Features

- Available in the mobile version of Yandex Browser for organizations. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html

Values

- Not Configured, Enabled: Users can add, change, and delete bookmarks.
- Disabled: Users can't add, change, or delete bookmarks. User bookmarks created before the policy was disabled remain available.</string>
      <string id="ManagedBookmarks">Set managed bookmarks</string>
      <string id="ManagedBookmarks_Explain">ManagedBookmarks

The policy sets a list of managed bookmarks.

Users cannot change this list, but they can hide bookmarks in the toolbar. Managed bookmarks are not synchronized with the user's account, and extensions cannot change them.

Features

- Available in the mobile Browser version for organizations. Learn more: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled — the list of managed bookmarks is empty.
- Enabled — the administrator sets a list of bookmarks. Each bookmark is a dictionary with the keys name and url, which correspond to the name and URL of the bookmark. 
The administrator can also set a subfolder for bookmarks. To do this, instead of the url key, set the children key with a list of nested bookmarks or folders as the value.
By default, the folder is called "Managed Bookmarks". To change the name, add a dictionary to the policy with a single toplevel_name key and the folder name as the value. 
The browser complements incomplete URLs in the same way as when they are entered in the address bar, for example, ya.ru will be converted to https://ya.ru /.

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example of a value:

[
{
"toplevel_name": "Corporate bookmarks"
},
  {
"name": "Yandex",
"url": "ya.ru "
},
  {
"name": "Public services",
"url": "gosuslugi.ru "
},
  {
"name": "My organization",
"children": [
{
"name": "News",
"url": "news.my-org-site.ru "
},
      {
"name": "HR Department",
        "url": "hr.my-org-site.ru"
      }
    ]
  }
]</string>
      <string id="Cache_group">Cache</string>
      <string id="DiskCacheDir">Select the cache folder on the disk</string>
      <string id="DiskCacheDir_Explain">DiskCacheDir

The policy sets the cache folder on the disk.

The browser manages the contents of the cache folder, so do not specify the root folder or a folder that is used for other purposes in the policy. This will avoid data loss and protect you from other errors.

Attention. Browser profiles are not backward compatible. If you use a roaming profile and access it from different Browser versions, this can lead to fault and data loss. To prevent this from happening, we recommend using variables or synchronization.

More information about the roaming-profile: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/deployment/roaming-profile.html

About supported variables: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/policy/supported-variables.html

About synchronization: https://yandex.ru/support/browser/device/sync.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: Yandex Browser uses the default folder. Users can change it with the --disk-cache-dir parameter.
- Enabled: The administrator sets the folder for storing cache. Users can't change it with the --disk-cache-dir parameter.

Example value:

C:\yandex_cache</string>
      <string id="DiskCacheSize">Set the cache size in bytes</string>
      <string id="DiskCacheSize_Explain">DiskCacheSize

The policy sets the cache size in bytes. 
The value is used by various subsystems in Yandex Browser as a reference. This means that the actual amount of disk space used may exceed the specified value, but would be within the same order of magnitude.

Features

- This is a basic security policy. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/deployment/windows/setting-policy#basic

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: Yandex Browser uses the default cache size. Users can change the cache size using the --disk-cache-size parameter.
- Enabled: The administrator sets the maximum cache size in bytes. Users can't change the cache size using the --disk-cache-size parameter.

Safety recommendations

Value: Enabled → 250609664. Set the maximum cache size to 250609664 bytes or more. It is important to have sufficient space for the Yandex Browser cache to successfully investigate cybercrimes.</string>
      <string id="CloudManagement_group">Yandex Browser management from the cloud</string>
      <string id="YandexCMURLAllowlistIfNotEnrolled">Set a list of URLs that are available without a license or linking to a Management Console.</string>
      <string id="YandexCMURLAllowlistIfNotEnrolled_Explain">YandexCMURLAllowlistIfNotEnrolled

The policy sets a list of URLs that are available without a license or linking Yandex Browser to a Management Console.

The policy takes priority over YandexCMURLBlocklistIfNotEnrolled.

The policy is available for Browsers version 23.9.5 and higher.

Features

- Available in the mobile Browser version for organizations. Learn more: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html
- Works only in the extended version of Yandex Browser for organizations. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: No policy set.
- Enabled: The administrator sets a list of no more than 1000 URLs. You can use URL patterns. After disabling the policy, the previously set list of URLs is not saved.

For more information about URL templates, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/policy/url-patterns.html

Convert non-Latin URLs (for example, яндекс.рф) via punycode: https://www.reg.ru/web-tools/punycode

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example value:

example.com
https://ssl.server.com
hosting.com/bad_path
https://server:8080/path
.exact.hostname.com
file://*
custom_scheme:*
*</string>
      <string id="YandexCMURLAllowlistIfNotEnrolledDesc">Set a list of URLs that are available without linking the extended version of Yandex Browser to the Management Console.</string>
      <string id="YandexCMURLBlocklistIfNotEnrolled">Set a list of URLs that aren't available without a license or linking to a Management Console.</string>
      <string id="YandexCMURLBlocklistIfNotEnrolled_Explain">YandexCMURLBlocklistIfNotEnrolled

The policy sets a list of URLs that aren't available without a license or linking Yandex Browser to a Management Console.

The policy doesn't apply to URLs with built-in JavaScript code and dynamically loaded data. For example, if the administrator blocks the example.com/abc address, the example.com site will still be able to load the example.com/abc page using XMLHttpRequest.

The administrator can add pages with Yandex Browser settings to the list (for example, browser://settings). You can't block only the Yandex Browser registration page or some settings (for example, blocking the browser://settings/content subpage will block the entire browser://settings page).

The YandexCMURLAllowlistIfNotEnrolled policy supersedes YandexCMURLBlocklistIfNotEnrolled.

The policy is available for Browsers version 23.9.5 and higher.

Features 

- Available in the mobile Browser version for organizations. Learn more: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html
- Only works in the extended version of Yandex Browser for organizations. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: Policy isn't set.
- Enabled: The administrator sets a list of no more than 1000 URLs. You can use URL templates. After disabling the policy, the previously set list of URLs is not saved.

For more information about URL templates, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/policy/url-patterns.html

Convert non-Latin URLs (for example, яндекс.рф) via punycode: https://www.reg.ru/web-tools/punycode

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example value:

example.com
https://ssl.server.com
hosting.com/bad_path
https://server:8080/path
.exact.hostname.com
file://*
custom_scheme:*
*</string>
      <string id="YandexCMURLBlocklistIfNotEnrolledDesc">Set a list of URLs that aren't available without linking Yandex Browser to the Management Console.</string>
      <string id="YandexCloudEnrollment">Set a token for Browser registration in the Management Console</string>
      <string id="YandexCloudEnrollment_Explain">YandexCloudEnrollment

The policy sets a token for Browser registration for organizations in the Management Console. 

The browser will register on the first launch or when the policy is changed. If you have active licenses, the browser will be added to management.

You can create an assembly with a preset policy in the Console:
1. Get a token to register Yandex Browser. Learn more: https://browser .yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/constructor/management-settings#browsers
2. Set up a policy for the desired entity.
3. In the Browser Constructor, link the entity with the configured policy to the assembly.
4. Install the assembly on the user's computer.
5. Open Yandex Browser. It will be registered in the Management Console.

For more information, see the Control Settings section: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/constructor/management-settings#browsers

Features

- Available in the mobile Browser version for organizations. Learn more: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html
- It only works in the extended version of the Browser for organizations. Learn more: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled — the token is not set.
- Enabled — the administrator sets the parameter enrollment_token— the token for registration.

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example of a value:

{
  "enrollment_token": "ab1c2d34-e5fg-6789-h0iq-12345678k90m"
}</string>
      <string id="CloudPolicyOverridesPlatformPolicy">Set the priority of policies from your Management Console over policies on your device</string>
      <string id="CloudPolicyOverridesPlatformPolicy_Explain">CloudPolicyOverridesPlatformPolicy

The policy sets the priority of policies set in the Management Console over policies set on the device.

The policy is available for Browsers version 23.9.5 and higher.

Features

- Available in the mobile Browser version for organizations. Learn more: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: Policies on the device take priority over policies from the Management Console.
- Enabled: Policies from the Management Console have priority over policies on the device.</string>
      <string id="PolicyRefreshRate">Set the frequency of user policy updates (backup mechanism)</string>
      <string id="PolicyRefreshRate_Explain">PolicyRefreshRate

The policy sets the interval between checks for policy updates from the Management Console. Policy polling works regardless of the PolicyRefreshRate value:

- On Windows, macOS, Linux and iOS — 5–7 minutes after the change in the Management Console;
- On Android — every 3 hours.

PolicyRefreshRate serves as an optional backup mechanism for automatic update errors.

You can select a value in milliseconds from 1,800,000 (30 minutes) to 86,400,000 (1 day). If a number outside the range is specified, the nearest limit value will be used.

Features

- Available in the mobile version of the Browser for organizations. Learn more: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: Yandex Browser requests user policy updates: at launch, 5–7 minutes after changing the values in the Management Console, and after pressing the "Reload policies" button on the browser://policy page.
- Enabled: The administrator sets the interval.

Security recommendations

Value: Enabled. Set the policy update interval to apply security policy changes in a timely manner.</string>
      <string id="DataExchangeWithYandex_group">Data Exchange with Yandex</string>
      <string id="BackgroundUpdateAllowed">Enable background updating of browser</string>
      <string id="BackgroundUpdateAllowed_Explain">BackgroundUpdateAllowed

The policy allows background Browser updates.

The policy controls the "Update the browser, even if it is not running" setting. To go to the setting, in the Browser click  "Main menu" → "Settings" → "System" → "Performance" and select it.

The policy only works if the UpdateAllowed policy is not set or enabled.

The policy is available for Browsers version 23.3.1 and higher.

Values

- Not Configured — background updates are allowed, users manage the settings.
- Enabled — Background updates are allowed. The setting is enabled, users cannot disable it.
- Disabled — background updates are prohibited. The setting is disabled, users cannot enable it.</string>
      <string id="CrashesReporting">Enable sending Yandex Browser crash reports</string>
      <string id="CrashesReporting_Explain">CrashesReporting

The policy allows or restricts anonymous sending of crash reports to Yandex.

To allow or restrict sending crash reports to Yandex, use the option: Main menu icon → "Settings" → "System" → "Personal data settings" → "Send crash reports to Yandex".

Features

- In Windows and macOS only works within the domain.

Values

- Not Configured: Sending reports to Yandex is allowed, users can restrict sending reports in Yandex Browser settings.
- Enabled: Sending reports to Yandex is allowed, users can't restrict sending reports. Crash records appear on the browser://crashes page and in the file C:\Users\LOGIN\AppData\Local\Yandex\YandexBrowser\User Data\Crashpad\uploads.log.
- Disabled: Sending reports to Yandex is restricted, users can't allow sending reports.</string>
      <string id="StatisticsReporting">Send anonymous statistics to Yandex</string>
      <string id="StatisticsReporting_Explain">StatisticsReporting

The policy allows or restricts sending anonymous statistics to Yandex.

You can allow or restrict sending statistics in Yandex Browser settings: Main menu icon → "Settings" → "System" → "Personal data settings" → "Send usage statistics to Yandex".

Features

- On Windows and macOS only works within the domain.
- Can be configured as a recommendation. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/deployment/setting-policy.html#recommend-policy
- Available in the mobile version of Yandex Browser for organizations. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html

Values

- Not Configured: Statistics are sent to Yandex, users can disable this option.
- Enabled: Statistics are sent to Yandex, users can't disable this option.
- Disabled: Statistics are not sent to Yandex, users can't enable this option.</string>
      <string id="UpdateAllowed">Allow updates</string>
      <string id="UpdateAllowed_Explain">UpdateAllowed

The policy allows automatic Browser updates.

The policy doesn't affect Yandex Browser updates by the network administrator. The administrator can update the Yandex Browser version at any time by rolling out an update package to local network.

Values

- Not Configured, Enabled — automatic updates are allowed, users cannot prohibit it. 
- Disabled — Automatic updates are prohibited, users cannot allow it.</string>
      <string id="YandexUserFeedbackMode">Set up sending data in feedback forms</string>
      <string id="YandexUserFeedbackMode_Explain">YandexUserFeedbackMode

The policy configures the transfer of data through feedback forms.

 The policy controls the "Feedback" button. To access the button, in the Browser click "Main Menu" → "Help" → "Feedback".

 Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: The button is enabled. All data is transferred to Yandex.
- Enabled: The administrator determines which data will be transferred to Yandex:
     - "Disable" — the button is disabled. Users cannot fill out feedback forms.
     - "Send everything" - the button is enabled. Users can send all data along with a screenshot.
    - "Send without screenshot" - the button is enabled. Users can send all data, but the screenshot is not automatically attached.
    - "Save in archive on disk" - the button is enabled. When users click on the "Feedback" button, they can save the data in an archive on disk to check for personal information. If the YandexUserFeedbackPath policy is set, the archive is saved at the specified path. If the YandexUserFeedbackPath policy is not set or disabled, the user chooses the path for saving the archive.</string>
      <string id="YandexUserFeedbackMode_Disabled">Disable</string>
      <string id="YandexUserFeedbackMode_SendAll">Send all</string>
      <string id="YandexUserFeedbackMode_SendWithoutScreenshot">Send without screenshot</string>
      <string id="YandexUserFeedbackMode_SaveLocalArchive">Save to disk archive</string>
      <string id="YandexUserFeedbackPath">Set the path to the archive for the Browser support service</string>
      <string id="YandexUserFeedbackPath_Explain">YandexUserFeedbackPath

The policy sets the path to the archive for the Browser support service.

The policy works only if the YandexUserFeedbackMode policy is set to 3 "Archive on disk".

The policy is available for Browsers version 24.7.6 and higher.

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: The path to save the archive is chosen by the user.

- Enabled: The archive is saved according to the specified path.

Example of a value:

C:/some/path</string>
      <string id="ComponentUpdatesEnabled">Enable Browser component updates</string>
      <string id="ComponentUpdatesEnabled_Explain">ComponentUpdatesEnabled

The policy manages the update of Yandex Browser components.

You can see the list of components on the browser://components page

Features

- This is a basic security policy. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/deployment/windows/setting-policy#basic

Values

- Not Configured, Enabled: All components are updated.
- Disabled: Only components without executable code that are responsible for security are updated. For example, certificate revocation lists and the Subresource Filter Rules component.

Safety recommendations

Value: Enabled. Enable the policy or don't set it to keep Yandex Browser components up to date — this affects security.</string>
      <string id="SpellCheckServiceEnabled">Set up sending unfamiliar words to Yandex for spell checking</string>
      <string id="SpellCheckServiceEnabled_Explain">SpellCheckServiceEnabled

The policy controls the "Send unfamiliar words to Yandex to check spelling" setting.

Features

- This is a basic security policy. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support2/browser-corporate/ru/deployment/windows/setting-policy#basic
- Can be configured as a recommendation. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/deployment/setting-policy.html#recommend-policy

Values

- Not Configured: The setting is enabled, users can disable it.
- Enabled: The setting is enabled, users can't disable it.
- Disabled: The setting is disabled, users can't enable it.

Safety recommendations

Value: Disabled. Disable sending unfamiliar words to Yandex to avoid possible data leakage.

You can still use the downloaded dictionary to check spelling.</string>
      <string id="SpellcheckLanguage">Set a list of languages with forced spell checking</string>
      <string id="SpellcheckLanguage_Explain">SpellcheckLanguage

The policy sets a list of languages for which spell checking is enforced.

The policy does not work if the SpellCheckServiceEnabled policy is enabled.

Values:

- Not Configured, Disabled — users set the spelling check parameters themselves.
- Enabled — the administrator sets the languages for which spell checking is forcibly enabled. If the user has selected the languages for forced spell checking, the languages specified by the policy will be added to this list.

Supported languages: AF, BG, CA, CS, DA, de, EL, en-AU, en-CA, en-GB, en-US, ES, ES-419, ES-AR, ES-ES, ES-MX, ES-US, et, FA, fo, fr, he, hi, hr, hu, id, it, ko, lt, lv, nb, nl, pl, pt-BR, pt-PT, ro, ru, sh, sk, sl, sq, sr, sv, ta, tg, tr, uk, vi.

Unknown languages are ignored.

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example of a value:

fr
es</string>
      <string id="SpellcheckLanguageDesc">Set a list of languages with forced spell checking</string>
      <string id="ExtensionsAndWebApplications_group">Extensions and web applications</string>
      <string id="BlockExternalExtensions">Block external extensions from being installed in the Browser</string>
      <string id="BlockExternalExtensions_Explain">BlockExternalExtensions

The policy blocks the installation of external extensions in the Browser.

The policy is available for Browsers version 22.9.1 and higher.

Features

- This is a basic security policy. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/deployment/windows/setting-policy#basic
- Available in the mobile version of Yandex Browser for organizations. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: the installation of external extensions is allowed.
- Enabled: the installation of external extensions is prohibited.

Safety recommendations

Value: Enabled. Prohibit the installation of external extensions. Users may accidentally or intentionally install malicious extensions.

Possible problems. The installation of external extensions is not available.</string>
      <string id="ExtensionInstallAllowlist">Set a list of allowed extensions</string>
      <string id="ExtensionInstallAllowlist_Explain">ExtensionInstallAllowlist

The policy sets exceptions to the extension blocklist from the ExtensionInstallBlocklist policy.

The policy is valid if the extension blocklist of the ExtensionInstallBlocklist policy contains a wildcard «*». The IDs of extensions in the allowed list are separated by commas.

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: The extension allow list is empty, the administrator can't add an extension to the allow list.
- Enabled: The administrator sets the extension allow list.

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example value:

mbniclmhobmnbdlbpiphghaielnnpgdp
bfbmjmiodbnnpllbbbfblcplfjjepjdn</string>
      <string id="ExtensionInstallAllowlistDesc">Configuring the list of allowed extensions</string>
      <string id="ExtensionInstallBlocklist">Set a list of forbidden extensions</string>
      <string id="ExtensionInstallBlocklist_Explain">ExtensionInstallBlocklist

The policy sets a list of extensions that can't be installed.

Features

- This is a basic security policy. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/deployment/windows/setting-policy#basic

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: Users can install any extensions.
- Enabled: The administrator sets the extension blocklist, users can't install extensions from this list. When you activate this policy, previously installed extensions that are now in the blocklist get disabled. If the extension is installed by the ExtensionSettings policy, it gets removed. After removing extensions from the blocklist, they are enabled automatically. The «*» wildcard disables all extensions except those allowed by the ExtensionInstallAllowlist policy.

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example value:

extension_id1
extension_id2

Safety recommendations

Value: Enabled→«*». Disable the installation of all extensions using «*». There may be extensions that can manage the system remotely.

Possible problems.	All installed extensions will be deleted if they are not specified in the ExtensionInstallAllowlist policy. If your organization uses password managers as extensions, add them to the ExtensionInstallAllowlist policy.</string>
      <string id="ExtensionInstallBlocklistDesc">Setting up a blacklist of extensions</string>
      <string id="ExtensionInstallForcelist">Set a list of forced web applications and extensions</string>
      <string id="ExtensionInstallForcelist_Explain">ExtensionInstallForcelist

The policy sets a list of extensions that are force-installed without user interaction. Users cannot delete or disable forcibly installed extensions. The extension can also be installed in a closed loop. Learn more: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/deployment/closed-contour.html

Policy features

- The policy doesn't apply to Incognito mode.  To disable Incognito mode, use the IncognitoModeAvailability policy.
     - The "browser://tune/" and "browser://extensions/" extension pages are unavailable in Incognito mode: when you try to open them, Yandex Browser exits the mode, even if it is enabled by the IncognitoModeAvailability policy.
- After enabling the policy, permissions are granted for the API extensions (enterprise.deviceAttributes and enterprise.platformKeys). These APIs are only available for extensions that are force-installed.
- The policy takes priority over ExtensionInstallBlocklist. If you remove a force-installed extension from the ExtensionInstallForcelist policy list, Yandex Browser will automatically delete it (if it's in the ExtensionInstallBlocklist policy list).
- If the DeveloperToolsAvailability policy allows the use of developer tools, users can change the code for force-installed extensions. This may cause Yandex Browser crashes.
- Extensions are installed at the URL specified in the policy. 
    - If the URL is not specified, the default is the URL of the Chrome online store https://clients2.google.com/service/update2/crx .
    - If the extension is hosted in the Opera online store, specify https://extension-updates.opera.com/api/omaha/update /.
    - You can use an XML file. Local and network paths are supported.
  For all subsequent updates to the extension, the URL specified in the extension manifest will be used.
- Each line specified in the policy sets the extension ID and may contain the URL for installing the extension (the path to the CRX file) separated by a semicolon. Example: extension_id1; update_url.

Features

- Only works within the domain in Windows and macOS.

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: Extensions are not added automatically, and users can remove all extensions.
- Enabled: The administrator specifies a list of mandatory extensions to be added, and users can't remove or disable them.

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example value:

mbniclmhobmnbdlbpiphghaielnnpgdp;https://example.com/update_url
bfbmjmiodbnnpllbbbfblcplfjjepjdn</string>
      <string id="ExtensionInstallForcelistDesc">Create a list of forced applications and extensions</string>
      <string id="ExtensionSettings">Manage extension settings</string>
      <string id="ExtensionSettings_Explain">ExtensionSettings

The policy controls the settings for Yandex Browser extensions. Replaces any other policies for extension configuration.

Features

- In Windows and macOS, works only within the domain.
- Available in the mobile version of Yandex Browser for organizations. For more information, see: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html

Values

 - Not Configured, Disabled: Users can configure extensions themselves.
- Enabled: The administrator uses the code specified in the policy settings to configure extension settings.
     - The extension ID or update URL is linked to one setting only. 
     - The «*» wildcard is valid for all extensions for which a separate configuration is not specified in the policy. 
     - If the update URL is set, the specified configuration applies to all extensions whose manifest contains this URL.
     - If the experimental override_update_url parameter is set to "True", the extension will be installed and updated using the update URL in the ExtensionInstallForcelist policy or in the update_url field of the ExtensionSettings policy. If the value is set to «False», the URL from the extension manifest will be used for updating.

Learn more about the policy fields in Help: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/policy/extension-settings.html

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config
 
Example value:

{
  "abcdefghijklmnopabcdefghijklmnop": {
    "installation_mode": "allowed",
    "blocked_permissions": [
      "history"
    ],
    "minimum_version_required": "1.0.1",
    "toolbar_pin": "force_pinned"
  },
  "bcdefghijklmnopabcdefghijklmnopa": {
    "installation_mode": "force_installed",
    "update_url": "https://example.com/update_url",
    "allowed_permissions": [
      "downloads"
    ],
    "runtime_blocked_hosts": [
      "*://*.example.com"
    ],
    "runtime_allowed_hosts": [
      "*://good.example.com"
    ]
  },
  "cdefghijklmnopabcdefghijklmnopab": {
    "installation_mode": "blocked",
    "blocked_install_message": "Custom error message."
  },
  "defghijklmnopabcdefghijklmnopabc,efghijklmnopabcdefghijklmnopabcd": {
    "installation_mode": "blocked",
    "blocked_install_message": "Custom error message."
  },
  "update_url:https://www.example.com/update.xml": {
    "blocked_permissions": [
      "wallpaper"
    ],
    "allowed_permissions": [
      "downloads"
    ],
    "installation_mode": "allowed"
  },
  "fghijklmnopabcdefghijklmnopabcde": {
    "installation_mode": "removed",
    "blocked_install_message": "Custom removal message."
  },
  "ghijklmnopabcdefghijklmnopabcdef": {
    "installation_mode": "force_installed",
    "update_url": "https://example.com/update_url",
    "override_update_url": true
  },
  "*": {
    "installation_mode": "blocked",
    "blocked_permissions": [
      "downloads",
      "bookmarks"
    ],
    "install_sources": [
      "https://company-intranet/chromeapps"
    ],
    "allowed_types": [
      "hosted_app"
    ],
    "runtime_blocked_hosts": [
      "*://*.example.com"
    ],
    "runtime_allowed_hosts": [
      "*://good.example.com"
    ],
    "blocked_install_message": "Custom error message."
  }
}</string>
      <string id="YandexExtensionsStoreURL">Set the URL of the extension directory</string>
      <string id="YandexExtensionsStoreURL_Explain">YandexExtensionsStoreURL

The policy sets the URL of the extensions directory on the browser://tune page.

The policy is available for Browsers version 23.9.1 and higher.

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: The standard extension directory is used.
- Enabled: The administrator sets the extension directory URL that is used on the "browser://tune" page.

Convert non-Latin URLs (for example, яндекс.рф) via punycode: https://www.reg.ru/web-tools/punycode

Example value: 

https://www.example.com</string>
      <string id="DefaultWebAppsPlainTextPolicy">Set a list of pre-installed web applications</string>
      <string id="DefaultWebAppsPlainTextPolicy_Explain">DefaultWebAppsPlainTextPolicy

The policy sets the list of pre-installed web applications.

The DefaultWebAppsPolicy policy supersedes DefaultWebAppsPlainTextPolicy.

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: The policy is not set.
- Enabled: The administrator sets the list of pre-installed web applications. Web applications that are not in the list are removed.

A web application is a website that you can open in a separate window and work with it as a program. Viewing a site as a web application is convenient for messengers, email services, and video conferences. For more information, see Help: https://yandex.ru/support/browser/personalization/web-app.html.

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example value:

{
  "default_apps": [
    {
      "install": "all",
      "scope": "https://mail.yandex.ru",
      "is_pinned": true,
      "create_desktop_shortcut": true,
      "launch_after_install": true
    }
  ]
}</string>
      <string id="DefaultWebAppsPolicy">Set the path to the file with a list of pre-installed web applications</string>
      <string id="DefaultWebAppsPolicy_Explain">DefaultWebAppsPolicy

The policy sets the path to the file with a list of pre-installed web applications.

The DefaultWebAppsPolicy policy supersedes DefaultWebAppsPlainTextPolicy.

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: The policy is not set.
- Enabled: The administrator sets the path to the file located on a separate server with a list of pre-installed web applications. Web applications that are not in the list are removed.

A web application is a website that you can open in a separate window and work with it as a program. Viewing a site as a web application is convenient for messengers, email services, and video conferences. For more information, see Help: https://yandex.ru/support/browser/personalization/web-app.html.

You can see an example of JSON with web applications in Help: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/policy/default-web-apps-policy.html#default-web-apps-policy__json-example

Example value:

https://domain.example/path/to/web_app/config/config.json</string>
      <string id="WebAppStorePlainTextPolicy">Set a list of web applications available in the store</string>
      <string id="WebAppStorePlainTextPolicy_Explain">WebAppStorePlainTextPolicy

The policy sets the list of web applications available in the store. A web application is a website that can be opened in a separate window and operated as a separate program. It is convenient for messengers, mail services, and video conferences. Learn more: https://yandex.ru/support/browser/ru/personalization/web-app.html

In the list, you can specify both web applications from the Browser's built-in catalog, and custom web applications that are not in the catalog. For custom web applications, you need to set the name and icon (icon_url) so that they are displayed correctly in the store. If the web application is in the embedded directory, it is enough to specify only its address (scope) — the name and icon will be substituted automatically.

The WebAppStorePolicy policy takes precedence over the WebAppStorePlainTextPolicy policy.

The policy is available for Browsers version 23.9.1 and higher.

Parameters:

- "apps_store": The JSON array contains web applications available for installation. They are located in the sidebar and are installed without going to external sites. The array can contain several sections with different names and the number of web applications.

- "name": The name of the section in the web application store. For custom web applications that are not included in the built-in directory, this field also specifies the name of the application itself.

- "apps": An array of web applications.

- "scope": The unique website address of the web application.

- "icon_url": A link to the icon of an arbitrary web application that is missing from the embedded directory. It is used so that the app is displayed in the store with the correct icon. For applications from the built-in catalog, the field is not required — the icon is inserted automatically.

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: All web applications are available in the store.
- Enabled: The administrator sets the list of web applications available in the store.

A web application is a website that you can open in a separate window and work with it as a program. Viewing a site as a web application is convenient for messengers, email services, and video conferences. For more information, see Help: https://yandex.ru/support/browser/personalization/web-app.html .

Convert non-Latin URLs (for example, яндекс.рф) via punycode: https://www.reg.ru/web-tools/punycode

You can only set single-line values in the Local Group Policy Editor and Registry Editor. To convert multi-line values to a single line, use JSON Beautifier: https://jsonbeautifier.org/
On the left side of the page, paste the value and click Minify.

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example of a value:

{
  "apps_store": [
    {
      "apps": [
        {
          "scope": "https://telemost.yandex.ru/"
        }
      ],
      "name": "Yandex 360"
    },
    {
      "apps": [
        {
          "scope": "https://translate.yandex.ru/"
        },
        {
          "icon_url": "https://example.com/favicon.icon",
          "name": "Облако",
          "scope": "https://example.com/"
        },
        {
          "icon_url": "https://example.org/favicon.icon",
          "name": "Банк",
          "scope": "https://example.org/"
        },
        {
          "icon_url": "https://example.net/favicon.icon",
          "name": "Новости",
          "scope": "https://example.net/"
        }
      ],
      "name": "Сервисы"
    }
  ]
}</string>
      <string id="WebAppStorePolicy">Set the path to the file with the list of web applications available in the store</string>
      <string id="WebAppStorePolicy_Explain">WebAppStorePolicy

The policy sets the path to the file with the list of web applications available in the store.

The WebAppStorePolicy policy supersedes WebAppStorePlainTextPolicy.

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: All web applications are available in the store.
- Enabled: The administrator sets the path to the file with the list of web applications available in the store. The file is stored on a separate server.

A web application is a website that you can open in a separate window and work with it as a program. Viewing a site as a web application is convenient for messengers, email services, and video conferences. For more information, see Help: https://yandex.ru/support/browser/personalization/web-app.html.

Convert non-Latin URLs (for example, яндекс.рф) via punycode: https://www.reg.ru/web-tools/punycode

You can see an example of JSON with web applications in Help: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/policy/web-app-store-policy.html#web-app-store-policy__json-example

Example value: 

https://domain.example/path/to/web_app/config/config.json</string>
      <string id="YandexAdblock">Block obtrusive ads</string>
      <string id="YandexAdblock_Explain">YandexAdblock

The policy blocks obtrusive ads. Learn more: https://yandex.ru/support/browser/security/undesired-ad-blocking.html#what-blocked

The policy controls the "Block obtrusive ads" setting. To go to the settings, in the Browser, click "Main Menu" → "Settings" → "Tools" → "Ad Blocker" and select it.

Features

- Available in the mobile version of Yandex Browser for organizations. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html

Values

- Not Configured: Blocking is enabled. Users manage the setting.
- Enabled: Blocking is enabled. The setting is enabled, users cannot disable it.
- Disabled: Blocking is disabled. The setting is disabled, users cannot enable it.</string>
      <string id="YandexAntishock">Enable Antishock</string>
      <string id="YandexAntishock_Explain">YandexAntishock

The policy blocks offensive ads. Learn more: https://yandex.ru/support/browser/security/antishock.html#what-blocked

The policy controls the "Block offensive ads" setting. To go to the settings, in the Browser, click "Main Menu" → "Settings" → "Tools" → "Ad Blocker" and select it.

Features

- Available in the mobile version of Yandex Browser for organizations. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html

Values

- Not Configured: Blocking is disabled. Users manage the setting.
- Enabled: Blocking is enabled. The setting is enabled, users cannot disable it.
- Disabled: Blocking is disabled. The setting is disabled, users cannot enable it.</string>
      <string id="EnterpriseHardwarePlatformAPIEnabled">Allow extensions to collect computer data</string>
      <string id="EnterpriseHardwarePlatformAPIEnabled_Explain">EnterpriseHardwarePlatformAPIEnabled

The policy allows or restricts collecting computer manufacturer and model data by extensions using the Enterprise Hardware Platform API.

Features

- This is a basic security policy. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support2/browser-corporate/ru/deployment/windows/setting-policy#basic

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: Data collection is restricted.
- Enabled: Data collection is allowed.

Safety recommendations

Value: Disabled. Restrict collecting data about your computer.</string>
      <string id="Files_group">Working with files</string>
      <string id="CloudDocumentsDisabled">Prohibit opening office format files in the Browser</string>
      <string id="CloudDocumentsDisabled_Explain">CloudDocumentsDisabled

The policy prohibits users from opening office files in the Browser.

The policy controls the "Open files in Office format in the browser" setting. To go to the setting, in the Browser click "Main Menu" → "Settings" → "Tools" → "File viewer" and select it.

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: office format files are opened in the Browser. Users manage the setting.
- Enabled: office format files do not open in the Browser. Users cannot manage the setting.</string>
      <string id="AllowFileSelectionDialogs">Allow calling the file selection window</string>
      <string id="AllowFileSelectionDialogs_Explain">AllowFileSelectionDialogs

The policy allows or restricts displaying the file selection window in Yandex Browser.

Features

- This is an increased security policy. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/deployment/windows/setting-policy#advanced

Values

- Not Configured, Enabled: Users can open a file selection window (import bookmarks or passwords, upload files, save links, etc.) and save a file using the context menu.
- Disabled: The file selection window is not displayed, users can't save a file from the context menu. Files are downloaded to the default folder.

Safety recommendations

Value: Disabled. Disable the file selection window. Importing favorites, downloading files, and saving links can lead to data leakage or malware infections.

Possible problems. Users won't be able to download files.</string>
      <string id="AlwaysOpenPdfExternally">Open PDF files outside Yandex Browser</string>
      <string id="AlwaysOpenPdfExternally_Explain">AlwaysOpenPdfExternally

The policy sets up the opening of PDF files outside the Browser.

The policy controls the "Open PDF files in the browser" setting. To go to the setting, in the Browser click  "Main Menu" → "Settings" → "Tools" → "File Viewer" and select it.

The policy is available for Browsers version 22.11.0 and higher.

Features

- Can be configured as a recommendation page. Learn more: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/deployment/setting-policy.html#recommend-policy

Values

- Not Configured — downloaded PDF files open in the Browser. Users manage the settings.
- Enabled — The default application is used to open downloaded PDF files. The setting is disabled, users cannot enable it.
- Disabled — downloaded PDF files open in the Browser. The setting is enabled, users cannot disable it.</string>
      <string id="AutoOpenAllowedForURLs">Set a list of allowed URLs for the AutoOpenFileTypes policy</string>
      <string id="AutoOpenAllowedForURLs_Explain">AutoOpenAllowedForURLs

The policy sets a list of URLs for AutoOpenFileTypes. The policy doesn't apply to automatic opening parameters set by users.

The policy is available for Browsers version 22.11.0 and higher.

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: AutoOpenFileTypes files open automatically on all websites.
- Enabled: Administrator sets a list of URLs for AutoOpenFileTypes. Downloaded files open automatically if the URL is in the list and the file type is in AutoOpenFileTypes.

Convert non-Latin URLs (for example, яндекс.рф) via punycode: https://www.reg.ru/web-tools/punycode

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example value:

example.com
https://ssl.server.com
hosting.com/good_path
https://server:8080/path
.exact.hostname.com</string>
      <string id="AutoOpenAllowedForURLsDesc">Set a list of allowed URLs for the AutoOpenFileTypes policy</string>
      <string id="AutoOpenFileTypes">Set a list of file formats that will open automatically after downloading</string>
      <string id="AutoOpenFileTypes_Explain">AutoOpenFileTypes

The policy sets a list of file formats that will be automatically opened after downloading.

If Safe Browsing is enabled, files will be checked for malware during the download process, regardless of whether the policy is enabled. Files that have not been checked will not be opened.

Learn more about Safe Browsing: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/policy/safe-browsing-protection-level

The policy is available for Browsers version 22.9.1 and higher.

Features

- It only works on Windows and macOS if it is set inside the domain or via the Management Console.

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled — files of formats that users have selected in the context menu of the downloaded file are automatically opened (for example, "More" → "Open JPG automatically").
- Enabled — the administrator sets a list of file formats that will be automatically opened after downloading. The file format is specified without a dot separator, for example, "txt".

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example of the value:

exe
txt</string>
      <string id="AutoOpenFileTypesDesc">Set a list of file formats that will open automatically after downloading</string>
      <string id="PromptForDownloadLocation">Configure the "Ask where to save each file before downloading" option</string>
      <string id="PromptForDownloadLocation_Explain">PromptForDownloadLocation

The policy controls the "Ask where to save each file before downloading" option.

Features

- This is a basic security policy. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support2/browser-corporate/ru/deployment/windows/setting-policy#basic

Values

- Not Configured: Users get a prompt for a file download location, which they can disable.
- Enabled: Users get a prompt for a file download location, which they can't disable.
- Disabled: Users don't get a prompt for a file download location, but they can enable it.

Safety recommendations

Value: Enabled. Enable prompt for file download location. This will prevent accidental downloads and protect against "drive-by download" attacks. For more information, see https://www.kaspersky.com/resource-center/definitions/drive-by-download</string>
      <string id="HTTPAuthentication_group">Proxy server and authentication settings</string>
      <string id="AllowCrossOriginAuthPrompt">Allow showing authorization windows via images</string>
      <string id="AllowCrossOriginAuthPrompt_Explain">AllowCrossOriginAuthPrompt

The policy allows or restricts showing authorization windows via images.

Features

- This is a basic security policy. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/deployment/windows/setting-policy#basic

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: Windows are disabled.
- Enabled: Windows are allowed.

Safety recommendations

Value: Disabled. Restrict images from showing authorization windows to protect against phishing.</string>
      <string id="AuthNegotiateDelegateAllowlist">Allow delegation of rights over the Kerberos Protocol on servers</string>
      <string id="AuthNegotiateDelegateAllowlist_Explain">AuthNegotiateDelegateAllowlist

The policy sets the list of Kerberos servers to transfer credentials to.

Features

- Available in the mobile version of Yandex Browser for organizations. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: This list can't be set. Yandex Browser doesn't transmit user credentials to servers, including on the intranet. 
- Enabled: The administrator sets the list of servers that can delegate credentials over the Kerberos protocol. You can use the wildcard "*".

Example value:

*.example.com,example.com</string>
      <string id="AuthSchemes">Set authentication schemas</string>
      <string id="AuthSchemes_Explain">AuthSchemes

The policy specifies which HTTP authentication schemas Yandex Browser supports.

Features

- This is an increased security policy. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/deployment/windows/setting-policy#advanced
- Available in the mobile version of Yandex Browser for organizations. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: All four schemas are used.
- Enabled: The administrator lists schemas separated by commas.

Available schemas:
- Basic.
- Digest.
- NTLM.
- Negotiate.

Example values: basic,digest,ntlm,negotiate

Safety recommendations

Value: Enabled. Choose the "ntlm" and "negotiate" values because they support built-in authentication. The "basic" and "digest" values don't provide sufficient protection. For example, sites can send passwords in plain text, unencrypted.

Possible problems. Outdated web applications or sites that use unsafe schemas may not work correctly.</string>
      <string id="AuthServerAllowlist">Allow SSO authentication on servers from the list</string>
      <string id="AuthServerAllowlist_Explain">AuthServerAllowlist

The policy sets a list of servers (including proxy servers) for which Single sign-on (SSO) authentication is enabled.

The list of exceptions can be set by the AuthServerBlocklist policy.

Property

- Available in the mobile version of the Browser for organizations. Most likely: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html

Meaning

- Not Configured, Disabled-do not make a list. The browser responds to authentication requests only after it is determined whether the server is found on the intranet. If the server is on the Internet, the Browser ignores incoming requests from it.
- Enabled-the administrator sets the list of servers where SSO is enabled. You can use the wildcard "*".

Example of a value:

*.example.com,example.com</string>
      <string id="AuthServerBlocklist">Disable SSO authentication on servers from the list</string>
      <string id="AuthServerBlocklist_Explain">AuthServerBlocklist

The policy sets a list of servers (including proxy servers) for which single sign-on (SSO) authentication is disabled.
The policy sets the list of exceptions for the Auth Server Allow list policy.

Property

- Available in the mobile version of the Browser for organizations. Most likely: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html

Meaning

- Not Configured, Disabled-do not make a list. The browser responds to authentication requests only after it is determined that the server has been found on the intranet. If the server is on the Internet, the Browser ignores incoming requests from it.
- Enabled-the administrator sets the list of servers where SSO is disabled. You can use the URL template.

Learn more about URL templates: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/policy/url-patterns.html

Convert URLs without the Latin alphabet (for example, yandex.RF) via punycode: https://www.reg.ru/web-tools/punycode

Example of a value:

*.example.com,example.com</string>
      <string id="BasicAuthOverHttpEnabled">Allow Basic authentication when connecting via HTTP</string>
      <string id="BasicAuthOverHttpEnabled_Explain">BasicAuthOverHttpEnabled

The policy allows Basic authentication when connecting via HTTP.

It doesn't work if the AuthSchemes policy restricts the use of Basic authentication.

Values

- Not Configured, Enabled: Basic authentication requests are allowed to be received over the insecure HTTP protocol.
- Disabled: Basic authentication requests can only be received over the secure HTTPS protocol.</string>
      <string id="DisableAuthNegotiateCnameLookup">Disable CNAME record search when querying for Kerberos authentication</string>
      <string id="DisableAuthNegotiateCnameLookup_Explain">DisableAuthNegotiateCnameLookup

The policy disables CNAME record search when querying for Kerberos authentication.

Features

- Available in the mobile version of Yandex Browser for organizations. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: Searching for a CNAME record determines the canonical server name when creating a Kerberos SPN.
- Enabled: CNAME record search is not performed. The server name entered when creating the Kerberos SPN is used.</string>
      <string id="UserAgentSpoofing">Substitute User-Agent</string>
      <string id="UserAgentSpoofing_Explain">UserAgentSpoofing

The policy substitutes the User-Agent for the specified sites.

  Substitution modes:
   - default: The product name is substituted in the User-Agent line.
   - full: The User-Agent string is completely replaced.

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: Yandex Browser doesn't substitute the User-Agent.
- Enabled: The administrator sets the User-Agent substitution mode.

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example value:

{
  "full": {
    "Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64)": [
      "domain-only.com",
      ".domain-and-subdomains.com"
    ]
  },
  "default": {
    "": [
      ".remove-product-name.com"
    ],
    "OPR/34.0.2036.50": [
      ".replace-product-name.com"
    ]
  }
}</string>
      <string id="MaxConnectionsPerProxy">Set the maximal number of simultaneous connections to the proxy server</string>
      <string id="MaxConnectionsPerProxy_Explain">MaxConnectionsPerProxy

The policy sets the maximal number of concurrent connections to the proxy server.

By default, 32 concurrent connections to the proxy server are used. If the proxy server can't handle a high number of concurrent connections per client, this value should be reduced. This value should be increased if, for example, web applications use several connections for GET requests.

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: The value is set to 32.
- Enabled: The administrator sets the value in the range from 6 to 100. After changing the value, Yandex Browser should be restarted.

Example value:

7</string>
      <string id="ProxySettings">Configure a proxy server</string>
      <string id="ProxySettings_Explain">ProxySettings

The policy sets the proxy server settings for Yandex Browser and ignores all proxy settings from the command line.

Features

- This is a basic security policy. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support2/browser-corporate/ru/deployment/windows/setting-policy#basic
- On Windows and macOS only works within the domain.
- Available in the mobile version of Yandex Browser for organizations. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: Users can configure the proxy server.
- Enabled: The administrator fills in the following fields:
- ProxyMode: Sets the proxy server configuration mode and restricts changing it. Possible values:
     - direct: The proxy server is not used, and the values of other fields are ignored.
     - system: The system settings of the proxy server are used, the values of other fields are ignored.
     - auto_detect: The values of other fields are ignored.
     - fixed_servers: ProxyServer and ProxyBypassList fields are used.
     - pac_script: ProxyPacUrl, ProxyPacMandatory, and ProxyBypassList fields are used.
- ProxyPacUrl field: Sets the URL of the proxy server's PAC file.
- ProxyPacMandatory field: Prevents the network stack from returning to direct connections with an invalid or unavailable PAC script.
- ProxyServer field: Sets the proxy server URL.
- ProxyBypassList field: Sets the list of hosts for which the proxy server is ignored.

Convert non-Latin URLs (for example, яндекс.рф) via punycode: https://www.reg.ru/web-tools/punycode

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example value:

{
  "ProxyMode": "fixed_servers",
  "ProxyServer": "123.123.123.123:8080",
  "ProxyBypassList": "https://www.example1.com,https://www.example2.com,https://internalsite/"
}

Safety recommendations

Enable the policy, don't set the ProxyMode parameter to "auto_detect". Attackers can use the WPAD (Web Proxy Auto-Discovery Protocol) auto-configuration feature to provide computers with a PAC file that specifies a fake web proxy under their control.

Possible problems.	The proxy server configuration will no longer be detected using WPAD.</string>
      <string id="Import_group">Import</string>
      <string id="ImportCookies">Configure importing of cookies from another browser</string>
      <string id="ImportCookies_Explain">ImportCookies

This policy allows or restricts importing cookies from another browser.

Features

- Can be configured as a recommendation. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/deployment/setting-policy.html#recommend-policy

Values

- Not Configured: Cookies are imported upon the first launch of Yandex Browser from the default browser (if it has any cookies). Users can import cookies from another browser.
- Enabled: Cookies are automatically imported when importing any data. Users can't disable this setting.
- Disabled: Cookies are not imported when Yandex Browser is first launched. Users can't import cookies.</string>
      <string id="ImportExtensions">Configure import of extensions from another browser</string>
      <string id="ImportExtensions_Explain">ImportExtensions

The policy allows or restricts importing extensions from another browser.

Features

- Can be configured as a recommendation. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/deployment/setting-policy.html#recommend-policy

Values

- Not Configured: Extensions are imported when you first launch Yandex Browser from the default browser (if it has any extensions). Users can import extensions from another browser.
- Enabled: Extensions are automatically imported when importing any data. Users can't disable this setting.
- Disabled: Extensions are not imported when Yandex Browser is first launched. Users can't import extensions.</string>
      <string id="ImportFrom">Set the browser for data import when first launching Yandex Browser</string>
      <string id="ImportFrom_Explain">ImportFrom

The policy sets the browser for importing data when Yandex Browser is launched for the first time.

If the ImportOnFirstRun policy is:
- disabled, a conflict will occur and the data will not be imported;
- enabled, the data is imported from Yandex Browser specified by the importFrom policy.

The following policies take precedence over the importFrom policy:
- ImportBookmarks;
- ImportSavedPasswords;
- ImportLastSession;
- ImportExtensions;
- ImportHistory;
- ImportCookies;
- ImportSearchEngine.

The composition of imported data depends on the operating system and the browser from which it is downloaded. For more information, see https://browser.yandex.ru/help/ru/about/import

The policy is available for Browsers version 26.6.4 and higher.

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: when Yandex Browser is launched for the first time, the user can optionally select any Browser for importing data.
- Enabled: the administrator sets the browser from which data is imported when Yandex Browser is launched for the first time. Available values:
     - «0» — Mozilla Firefox (passwords and the added search engine are not imported);
     - «1» — Google Chrome;
     - «2» — Opera (the added search engine is not imported);
     - «3» — Microsoft Edge (open tabs and cookies are not imported);
     - «4» — Opera GX;
     - «5» — Safari.</string>
      <string id="ImportFrom_Firefox">Mozilla Firefox</string>
      <string id="ImportFrom_Chrome">Google Chrome</string>
      <string id="ImportFrom_Opera">Opera</string>
      <string id="ImportFrom_Edge">Microsoft Edge</string>
      <string id="ImportFrom_OperaGX">Opera GX</string>
      <string id="ImportFrom_Safari">Safari</string>
      <string id="ImportLastSession">Configure import of open tabs from another browser</string>
      <string id="ImportLastSession_Explain">ImportLastSession

The policy allows or restricts importing open tabs from another browser.

Features

- Can be configured as a recommendation. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/deployment/setting-policy.html#recommend-policy

Values

- Not Configured: Open tabs are imported when you first launch Yandex Browser from the default browser (if it has any open tabs). Users can import open tabs from another browser.
- Enabled: Open tabs are automatically imported when importing any data. Users can't disable this setting.
- Disabled: Open tabs are not imported at the first launch of Yandex Browser. Users can't import open tabs.</string>
      <string id="ImportOnFirstRun">Configure automatic import when the Browser is first started</string>
      <string id="ImportOnFirstRun_Explain">ImportOnFirstRun

The policy allows or restricts importing data from the default browser when you first start Yandex Browser.

Values

- Not Configured, Enabled: Data is imported when Yandex Browser is first started (if possible).
- Disabled: Data is not imported when Yandex Browser is first started.

Import data:
- History.
- Bookmarks.
- Passwords.
- Search engines.
- Cookies.
- Last open tabs.

For more information about importing from other browsers, see Help: https://yandex.ru/support/browser/about/import.html#automatic</string>
      <string id="ImportOther">Configure importing system settings from another browser</string>
      <string id="ImportOther_Explain">ImportOther

The policy allows or restricts importing system settings from another browser.

Features

- Can be configured as a recommendation. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/deployment/setting-policy.html#recommend-policy

Values

- Not Configured: System settings are imported when you first launch Yandex Browser from the default browser (if it has any system settings). Users can import system settings from another browser.
- Enabled: System settings are automatically imported when importing any data. Users can't disable this setting.
- Disabled: System settings are not imported at the first launch of Yandex Browser. Users can't import system settings.</string>
      <string id="YandexImportBookmarksPath">Configure import of bookmarks from Chromium-based browsers at launch</string>
      <string id="YandexImportBookmarksPath_Explain">YandexImportBookmarksPath

The policy configures a one-time importing bookmarks from Chromium-based browsers at launch and sets the path to the folder with the file \"Bookmarks\".

In Yandex Browser, this file is located at C:\\Users\\User name\\AppData\\Local\\Yandex\\YandexBrowser\\User Data\\Default\\Bookmarks.

The policy takes precedence over the EditBookmarksEnabled policy.

Features

- Works only in the extended version of Yandex Browser for organizations. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: Bookmark import is disabled.
- Enabled: The administrator sets the path to the folder with bookmarks which are then imported once at Yandex Browser launch.

Example value:

C:\bookmarks_folder\</string>
      <string id="ImportBookmarks">Configure import of bookmarks from another browser</string>
      <string id="ImportBookmarks_Explain">ImportBookmarks

The policy allows or restricts importing bookmarks from another browser.

The policy takes precedence over the EditBookmarksEnabled policy.

Features

- Can be configured as a recommendation. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/deployment/setting-policy.html#recommend-policy

Values

- Not Configured: Bookmarks are imported when you first launch Yandex Browser from the default browser (if it has any bookmarks). Users can import bookmarks from another browser.
- Enabled: Bookmarks are automatically imported when importing any data. Users can't disable this option.
- Disabled: Bookmarks are not imported when Yandex Browser is first launched. Users can't import bookmarks.</string>
      <string id="ImportHistory">Configure importing of browsing history from another browser</string>
      <string id="ImportHistory_Explain">ImportHistory

The policy allows or restricts importing browsing history from another browser.

Features

- Can be configured as a recommendation. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/deployment/setting-policy.html#recommend-policy

Values

- Not Configured: The browsing history is imported when you first launch Yandex Browser from the default browser (if it has any history). Users can import their browsing history from another browser.
- Enabled: Browsing history is automatically imported when importing any data. Users can't disable this setting.
- Disabled: Browsing history is not imported when Yandex Browser is first launched. Users can't import browsing history.</string>
      <string id="ImportSavedPasswords">Configure importing saved passwords from another browser</string>
      <string id="ImportSavedPasswords_Explain">ImportSavedPasswords

The policy allows or prohibits importing saved passwords from another browser.

Features

- This is a basic security policy. For more information, see: https://yandex.ru/support2/browser-corporate/ru/deployment/windows/setting-policy#basic
- Can be configured as a recommendation. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/deployment/setting-policy.html#recommend-policy

Values

- Not Configured: Saved passwords are imported when you first launch Yandex Browser from the default browser (if it has any passwords). Users can import saved passwords from another browser.
- Enabled: Saved passwords are automatically imported when importing any data. Users can't disable this setting.
- Disabled: Saved passwords are not imported at the first launch of Yandex Browser. Users can't import saved passwords.

Safety recommendations

Value: Disabled. Disable password import. They may be compromised or unsafe.</string>
      <string id="ImportSearchEngine">Configure default search import from another browser</string>
      <string id="ImportSearchEngine_Explain">ImportSearchEngine

The policy allows or restricts importing the default search engine from another browser.

Features

- This is a basic security policy. For more information, see: https://yandex.ru/support2/browser-corporate/ru/deployment/windows/setting-policy#basic
- Can be configured as a recommendation. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/deployment/setting-policy.html#recommend-policy

Values

- Not Configured: Search engine settings are imported when you first launch Yandex Browser from the default browser (if it has any search engine settings). Users can import search engine settings from another browser.
- Enabled: Search engine settings are automatically imported when importing any data. Users can't disable this setting.
- Disabled: Search engine settings are not imported at the first launch of Yandex Browser. Users can't import search engine settings from another browser.

Safety recommendations

Value: Disabled. Disable importing search engine settings. This can lead to the installation of a malicious search engine.</string>
      <string id="Interface_group">Interface</string>
      <string id="YandexBrowserThemeColor">Set the color scheme</string>
      <string id="YandexBrowserThemeColor_Explain">YandexBrowserThemeColor

The policy sets Yandex Browser's color scheme.

The policy controls the Color Scheme setting. To go to the settings, in the Browser, click "Main Menu" → "Settings" → "Interface" → "Color Scheme" and select it.

The policy is available for Browsers version 23.9.5 and higher.

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: users control the setting and can change the color scheme.
- Enabled: the administrator sets the color scheme. The setting is disabled, users cannot enable it.

Color schemes and their values:

- As in system: System
- Transparent: Transparent
- Light: Light
- Dark: Dark
- Turquoise: Aqua,Color
- Dark turquoise: Aqua,Full
- Light turquoise: Aqua,Half
- Transparent turquoise: Aqua,Light
- Yellow: Yellow,Color
- Dark yellow: Yellow,Full
- Light yellow: Yellow,Half
- Transparent yellow: Yellow,Light
- Green: Green,Color
- Dark green: Green,Full
- Light green: Green,Half
- Transparent green: Green,Light
- Red: Red,Color
- Dark red: Red,Full
- Light red: Red,Half
- Transparent red: Red,Light
- Orange: Orange,Color
- Dark orange: Orange,Full
- Light orange: Orange,Half
- Transparent orange: Orange,Light
- Purple: Purple,Color
- Dark purple: Purple,Full
- Light purple: Purple,Half
- Transparent purple: Purple,Light
- Blue: Blue,Color
- Dark blue: Blue,Full
- Light blue: Blue,Half
- Transparent blue: Blue,Light

Example value: 

System</string>
