      <string id="DeniedFluteBrowserButtons">Disable toolbar buttons on the sidebar</string>
      <string id="DeniedFluteBrowserButtons_Explain">DeniedFluteBrowserButtons

The policy manages the available tool buttons in the sidebar.

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: All buttons are available to users.
- Enabled: The administrator sets the buttons that are not available in the sidebar: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/policy/denied-flute-browser-buttons#sidebar

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example value:

portal_login
history
notes
music
tab_manager
screenshot</string>
      <string id="DeniedFluteBrowserButtonsDesc">Disable toolbar buttons on the sidebar</string>
      <string id="EnableBackgroundAnimationHighResolution">Enable high-resolution animated background</string>
      <string id="EnableBackgroundAnimationHighResolution_Explain">EnableBackgroundAnimationHighResolution

The policy includes a high-resolution animated background.

The policy controls the "High-resolution animated bakgrounds" setting. To proceed to the setting, in the Browser, click "Main Menu" → "Settings" → "Interface" → "New tab page view" and select it.

The policy is available for Browsers version 23.7.1 and higher.

Values

- Not Configured — Animated bakgrounds are displayed in standard resolution. Users manage the settings.
- Enabled — Animated bakgrounds are displayed in high resolution. The setting is enabled, users cannot disable it.
- Disabled — Animated bakgrounds are displayed in standard resolution. The setting is disabled, users cannot enable it.</string>
      <string id="EnableSearchByImageInSystemMenu">Enable search for similar images in the Windows system menu</string>
      <string id="EnableSearchByImageInSystemMenu_Explain">EnableSearchByImageInSystemMenu

The policy includes searching for similar images in the Windows system menu.

The policy controls the "Suggest searching for similar images in the Windows system menu" setting. To go to the settings, in the Browser, click "Main Menu" → "Settings" → "Tools" → "Image Search" and select it.

Values

- Not Configured — in Windows Explorer, the "Image Search" action is displayed in the file menu. Users manage the settings.
- Enabled — in Windows Explorer, the "Image Search" action is displayed in the file menu. The setting is enabled, users cannot disable it.
- Disabled — in Windows Explorer, the "Image Search" action is not displayed in the file menu. The setting is disabled, users cannot enable it.</string>
      <string id="InstaserpDisabled">Disable context menu for selected text</string>
      <string id="InstaserpDisabled_Explain">InstaserpDisabled

The policy disables the context menu that pops up when text is highlighted on a page.

Values

- Not Configured: The context menu is shown, users can disable it in the settings.
- Enabled: The context menu is not shown, users can't enable it in the settings (the option "Show Search and Copy buttons when text is selected" is inactive).
- Disabled: The context menu is displayed, users can't disable it in the settings.</string>
      <string id="NeuroNtpTools">Set up neural tools on the new tab screen</string>
      <string id="NeuroNtpTools_Explain">NeuroNtpTools

The policy adjusts the display of the "Editor", "Translator" and "Summarization" buttons on the new tab screen. It also adjusts neural tools in the pop-up menu and in the right-click context menu.

The policy controls the settings:

- "Neural tools"
- "Show the "Editor", "Translate", "Summarize" buttons on a new tab"

To proceed to the setting, in the Browser, click "Main Menu" → "Settings" → "Interface" → "New tab page view" and select it.

To proceed to the settings, in the Browser, click "Main Menu" → "Settings" → "Tools" → "Neural Tools" and select it.

The policy is available for Browsers version 24.12.4 and higher.

Features

- Available in the mobile Browser version for organizations. Learn more: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html

Values

- Not Configured: the buttons are disabled. Users can't turn them on.
- Enabled: the buttons are enabled. The settings are enabled, users cannot turn them off.
- Disabled: the buttons are disabled. The settings are disabled, users cannot enable them.</string>
      <string id="NeuroQuestionEnabled">Enable the "Ask Alice AI" button in the SmartBox</string>
      <string id="NeuroQuestionEnabled_Explain">NeuroQuestionEnabled

The policy enables a "Ask Alice AI" button in the in the SmartBox.

The policy controls the "Show the "Ask Alice AI" button on the page" setting. To go to the settings, in the Browser, click "Main Menu" → "Settings" → "Tools" → "Neural Tools" and select it.

To disable Alice AI completely, enable the policy [YandexAliceMsgDisable](https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/policy/yandex-alice-msg-disable).

The policy is available for Browsers version 25.12.4 and higher.

Values

- Not Configured, Enabled — the button is enabled, users control the setting.
- Disabled — the button is disabled, users cannot turn it on.</string>
      <string id="NtpCustomWallpaperSelectDisable">Prohibit the installation of a custom background on the screen of a new tab</string>
      <string id="NtpCustomWallpaperSelectDisable_Explain">NtpCustomWallpaperSelectDisable

The policy prohibits setting a custom background on the new tab screen.

The policy controls the "Upload background" setting. 
To set your background:
1. Open a new tab in the Browser.
2. In the lower right corner, click "Settings" → "Upload background".
3. Select the image and click "Open".

The policy is available for Browsers version 25.2.1 and higher.

Features

- Available in the mobile Browser version for organizations. Learn more: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: setting a custom background is allowed.
- Enabled: setting a custom background is prohibited.</string>
      <string id="NtpWallpaper">Set the background of the new tab page</string>
      <string id="NtpWallpaper_Explain">NtpWallpaper

The policy sets the background of the new tab screen. You can specify a URL, local, or network path to an image.

The policy controls the "Change the background daily" setting. To access the setting, open a new tab in the Browser, click "Settings" in the bottom-right corner, and select it.

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: the new tab screen uses the default background. Users can change the background. The "Change the background daily" setting is disabled, and users can enable it.
- Enabled: the administrator sets the path to the image for the background of the new tab screen. Users can change the background. The "Change the background daily" setting is disabled, and users cannot enable it.

 Convert non-Latin URL (for example, яндекс.рф) using punycode: https://www.reg.ru/web-tools/punycode

Example value: 

https://domain.example/path/to/image/wallpaper.png
C:\folder\file.jpg
file:\\desktop-ab12345z\1\1.jpg</string>
      <string id="NtpWallpaperSelectDisable">Disable Backgrounds gallery</string>
      <string id="NtpWallpaperSelectDisable_Explain">NtpWallpaperSelectDisable

The policy disables Yandex Background Gallery.

Background Gallery opens via the internet. If your computer runs in a closed loop with limited internet, you can disable the gallery. 

Features

- On Windows and macOS only works within the domain.
- Can be configured as a recommendation. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/deployment/setting-policy.html#recommend-policy

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: Gallery is available.
- Enabled: Gallery is disabled on a new tab page and in the Tableau settings. The "Change the background daily" setting is disabled.
The option "Settings" → "Interface" → "Color scheme" → "Only use dark backgrounds when the dark theme is enabled" is disabled and blocked.</string>
      <string id="SidePanelMode">Display sidebar</string>
      <string id="SidePanelMode_Explain">SidePanelMode

The policy sets the sidebar display mode and restricts users from changing it.

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: Users can select the sidebar display mode in the settings.
- Enabled: The sidebar settings are disabled, the administrator selects the display mode.

Sidebar display modes:
- Pin on sites.
- Pin only to a new tab.
- Hide.</string>
      <string id="SidePanelMode_Pinned">Pin on sites.</string>
      <string id="SidePanelMode_PinnedOnNTP">Pin only to a new tab.</string>
      <string id="SidePanelMode_Hidden">Don't show</string>
      <string id="TabloPreset">Set Up a Corporate Tableau</string>
      <string id="TabloPreset_Explain">TabloPreset

The policy sets the tiles on the Corporate Tableau. Users cannot edit it, but they can minimize it. 

Up to 24 tiles can be placed on the Tableau. It is not displayed in Incognito mode and when setting the minimum page view.

You can create local icons on the Tableau. To do this, set the favicon_path parameter, which is the path to the local icon.

Specify the path to the local icon in a shielded form, otherwise it will not be recognized by the policy. You can't set a base64-encoded icon.

Learn more about the Corporate Board: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/corp-tablo

Features

- Available in the mobile version of the Browser for organizations. More details: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: The Corporate Tableau is disabled, users can change, move or delete any tiles on the user's Tableau.
- Enabled: The administrator sets the parameters of the Corporate Tableau, users can change, move or delete any tiles on the user's Tableau. List of parameters:
     - title: tile name. Required parameter.
     - url: The URL of the tile indicating the scheme, for example https://. Required parameter.
     - background_color: the background color of the tile. Required parameter.
     - text_color: the color of the tile text. An optional parameter.
     - favicon_path: the path to the local icon in the escaped form. An optional parameter.

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example value:

[
  {
    "title": "Main corp site",
    "url": "https://home.corp.org",
    "background_color": "FF00FF",
    "text_color": "00BB44"
  },
  {
    "title": "Example site 1",
    "url": "https://example1.com",
    "background_color": "FF0000",
    "favicon_path": "C:\\Users\\AliceCarrol\\Downloads\\file.webp"
  }
]</string>
      <string id="UseTabGroups">Enable tab groups</string>
      <string id="UseTabGroups_Explain">UseTabGroups

The policy enables or disables tab groups in Yandex Browser. 

After changing the policy value, Yandex Bowser should be restarted: press Ctrl + Shift + Q or the Main Menu icon → "Close browser" and open it again.

Values

- Not Configured, Enabled: Tab groups are enabled.
- Disabled: Tab groups are disabled.</string>
      <string id="WebGalleryRotation">Configure daily rotation of backgrounds from the gallery in the new tab page</string>
      <string id="WebGalleryRotation_Explain">WebGalleryRotation

The policy enables or disables daily rotation of backgrounds on the new tab page from the background gallery. Users can change this parameter.

The policy controls the "Change the background daily" setting. To access it, go to the "New tab view" menu in the Browser on the new tab screen and select it.

Features

- Can be configured as a recommendation. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/deployment/setting-policy.html#recommend-policy

Values

- Not Configured: Background rotation is enabled. Users manage the settings.
- Enabled: Background rotation is enabled. The setting is enabled, users cannot disable it.
- Disabled: Background rotation is disabled. The setting is disabled, users cannot enable it.</string>
      <string id="YandexEcomEnabled">Enable shopping tools in the Browser</string>
      <string id="YandexEcomEnabled_Explain">YandexEcomEnabled

The policy includes tools for in-browser purchases for organizations:

- cashback;
- promo codes;
- Split.

These buttons are displayed on the pages of marketplaces, for example on [Yandex Market](https://market .yandex.ru). They are disabled by default in the Browser for organizations.

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled — shopping tools are not displayed in the Smart Bar and in the page menu.
- Enabled — Shopping tools are displayed in the Smart Bar and in the page menu.</string>
      <string id="YandexImageDescriberButtonEnabled">Enable the "Get a description of the image" button</string>
      <string id="YandexImageDescriberButtonEnabled_Explain">YandexImageDescriberButtonEnabled

The policy enables the "Get a description of the image" button.

The policy controls all ways to include a picture description:
- the "Describe picture" button on the picture panel;
- the "Describe picture" item in the context menu.

The policy controls the "Show image description button" setting. To access the setting, in the Browser, click "Main menu" → "Settings" → "Tools" section → "Accessibility" and select it.

The policy is available for Browsers version 26.6.4 and higher.

Features

- Works only in the extended version of the Browser for organizations. More details: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html

Values

- Not Configured: The button is enabled. Users manage the settings.
- Enabled: The button is enabled. Users cannot disable it.
- Disabled: The button is disabled. Users can't turn it on.</string>
      <string id="YandexNeuroEdit">Configure the editor</string>
      <string id="YandexNeuroEdit_Explain">Yandex Neuro Edit

The policy configures the editor functions in the Browser:
- «Editor» and «Translate» buttons on the new tab page;  
- the «Edit» button in the SmartBox;  
- the «Open in editor» item in the context menu.

The policy controls the setting «Show the «Edit» button when text is selected». To access this setting, in the Browser click «Main menu» → «Settings» → the «Tools» section → «Neuro tools» and select it.

The policy is available for Browsers version 24.4.3 and higher.

Values

- Not Configured: editor is enabled. Users manage the setting.
- Enabled: editor is enabled. The setting is enabled; users cannot disable it.
- Disabled: editor is disabled. The setting is disabled; users cannot enable it.

Security recommendations

Value: Disabled. Disable the policy to prevent the transfer of data used during editing and translation.</string>
      <string id="YandexNeuroLawyer">Configure NeuroLawyer</string>
      <string id="YandexNeuroLawyer_Explain">This policy configures the NeuroLawyer settings:

- the text on the NeuroLawyer button;
- the page that opens in the right-side panel when the button is clicked.

The application loaded from the specified URL gains access to the Browser API, as well as to the address and content of the page where the NeuroLawyer panel is open.

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: The NeuroLawyer button and panel are disabled.
- Enabled: The administrator specifies the following parameters:
     - url — the URL of the NeuroLawyer application. Only secure HTTP and HTTPS addresses are allowed;
     - button_text — the text on the NeuroLawyer button. The text length must be between 1 and 40 characters.

If the policy contains invalid parameter values, the NeuroLawyer button is not displayed.

Convert non-Latin URLs (for example, яндекс.рф) via punycode: https://www.reg.ru/web-tools/punycode

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example of a value:

{
  "url": "https://neuro-lawyer.example.com/",
  "button_text": "Open NeuroLawyer"
}</string>
      <string id="YandexNtpClockEnabled">Enable the clock on the new tab screen</string>
      <string id="YandexNtpClockEnabled_Explain">YandexNtpClockEnabled

The policy configures the clock on the new tab page.

The policy manages the clock settings. To access the settings, use one of the following methods:
- On the new tab screen, click «Settings» and select «Clock and date».  
- In the browser, click «Main Menu» → «Settings» → section «Interface» → «New tab page view», and select «Clock».

The policy is available for Browsers version 24.6.4 and higher.

Values

- Not Configured — the clock is off. Users manage the settings.
- Enabled — the clock is on. The setting is enabled, users cannot disable it.
- Disabled — the clock is disabled. The setting is disabled, users cannot enable it.</string>
      <string id="YandexNtpSmartboxEnabled">Set up a Smartbox on the new tab screen</string>
      <string id="YandexNtpSmartboxEnabled_Explain">YandexNtpSmartboxEnabled

The policy enables or disables the Smartbox on the new tab page.

The policy controls the "Search Bar" setting. To proceed to the settings, in the Browser settings, click "Interface" → "New Tab screen View" and select it.

The policy is available for Browsers version 24.6.4 and higher.

Values

- Not Configured: the Smartbox is enabled, users can disable it.
- Enabled: the Smartbox is enabled, users cannot disable it.
- Disabled: the Smartbox is disabled, users cannot enable it.</string>
      <string id="YandexNtpWidgets">Customize widgets on the new tab screen</string>
      <string id="YandexNtpWidgets_Explain">YandexNtpWidgets

The policy sets the widgets on the new tab screen and their settings.

Features

- Works only in the extended version of Yandex Browser for organizations. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled — widgets are not configured.

- Enabled — the administrator sets the parameters:

     - For text widgets:
          - type — widget type: "text". Required parameter.
          - column — the number of the column in the grid. Acceptable values are 1–6. The length of the entire row should be no more than 6 columns. Required parameter.
          - row — row number in the grid. Required parameter.
          - width — the width of the widget. Required parameter.
          - height — the height of the widget. Required parameter.
          - content — an object containing the "text" field. Required parameter.
          - the URL of the link with the scheme, for example, `https://`. Optional parameter.

     - For graphic widgets:
          - type — widget type: "image". Required parameter.
          - column — the number of the column in the grid. Acceptable values are 1–6. The length of the entire row should be no more than 6 columns. Required parameter.
          - row — row number in the grid. Required parameter.
          - width — the width of the widget. Required parameter.
          - height — the height of the widget. Required parameter.
          - image — the path to the image file as a URL ("http:"/"https:") or in Base64 format ("data:image/png;base64,&lt;base64_code&gt;"). Required parameter.
          - imageFittingMode — image insertion mode. Optional parameter. Values:
               - original — the image is centered, retains its size and proportions, and the excess is cropped.
               - contain — the image is centered, keeps the proportions and scaled so that it fits completely into the widget. Used by default.
          - replacementText — text that replaces the image if it is not available. Required parameter.
          - the URL of the link. An optional parameter.

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example of a value:

{
  "widgets": [
    {
      "type": "image",
      "column": 1,
      "row": 1,
      "width": 1,
      "height": 1,
      "image": "https://example.com/images/sample-image.png",
      "imageFittingMode": "original",
      "replacementText": "Текст для картинки",
      "url": "https://example.com"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "column": 1,
      "row": 2,
      "width": 1,
      "height": 1,
      "content": {
        "text": "Текст виджета"
      },
      "url": "https://example.org"
    }
  ]
}</string>
      <string id="YandexSearchImagesButton">Configure the display of the image search button</string>
      <string id="YandexSearchImagesButton_Explain">YandexSearchImagesButton

The policy adjusts the image search button.

Features

- Works only in the extended version of the Browser for organizations. More details: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html

Values:

- Not Configured: the button is displayed, users can disable its display.
- Enabled: the button is displayed, users cannot disable its display.
- Disabled: the button is not displayed, users cannot enable its display.</string>
      <string id="YandexShowWebReviews">Set up the display of site reviews</string>
      <string id="YandexShowWebReviews_Explain">YandexShowWebReviews

The policy controls the review button on the Neuroprotect panel. To access the button, click the connection status icon in the SmartBox on the left in the Browser. The Neuroprotect panel opens with a review button.

The policy is available for Browsers version 23.1.2 and higher.

Values

- Not Configured: The review button on the Neuroprotect panel is enabled.
- Enabled: The review button on the Neuroprotect panel is enabled.
- Disabled: The review button on the Neuroprotect panel is disabled.</string>
      <string id="YandexSubtitlesButton">Customize the display of the subtitle button and the Subtitles section on the video panel</string>
      <string id="YandexSubtitlesButton_Explain">YandexSubtitlesButton

The policy configures the display of the subtitles button and the "Subtitles" section on the video panel.

To switch to the subtitles button, turn on the video and hover the cursor over it. A video panel will appear with a subtitle button. To go to the "Subtitles" section, click "Video Menu" on the video panel.

The policy controls the "Show the subtitles button on videos" setting. To go to the setting, in the Browser click  "Main Menu" → "Settings" → "Tools" → "Translate" and select it.

The policy is available for Browsers version 23.1.2 and higher.

Values

- Not Configured:The "Subtitles" button and section on the video panel are enabled. The setting is enabled, users can disable it.
- Enabled: The "Subtitles" button and section on the video panel are enabled. The setting is enabled, users cannot disable it.
- Disabled: The "Subtitles" button and section on the video panel are disabled. The setting is disabled, users cannot enable it.</string>
      <string id="YandexVideoQR">Set up QR code recognition on video</string>
      <string id="YandexVideoQR_Explain">YandexVideoQR

The policy sets up QR code recognition on video.

The policy controls the "Automatically recognize QR codes on video" setting. To go to the setting, in the Browser click  "Main Menu" → "Settings" → "Tools" → "QR code recognition" and select it.

The policy is available for Browsers version 24.4.3 and higher.

Values

- Not Configured: QR code recognition on video is enabled. Users manage the settings.
- Enabled: QR code recognition on video is enabled. The setting is enabled, users cannot disable it.
- Disabled: QR code recognition on video is disabled. The setting is disabled, users cannot enable it.</string>
      <string id="YandexVideoSummarization">Set up the summarize button on a video</string>
      <string id="YandexVideoSummarization_Explain">Yandex Video Summarization

The policy sets up the Summarize button on the video.

The policy controls the "Show the "Summarize" button on the video" setting. To go to the settings, in the Browser, click "Main Menu" → "Settings" → "Tools" → "Neural Tools" and select it.

The policy is available for Browsers version 24.4.3 and higher.

Features

- Available in the mobile version of the Browser for organizations. More details: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html

Values

- Not Configured: the button is enabled. Users manage the settings.
- Enabled: the button is enabled. The setting is enabled, users cannot disable it.
- Disabled: the button is disabled. The setting is disabled, users cannot enable it.</string>
      <string id="AlternateErrorPagesEnabled">Enable alternative pages with errors</string>
      <string id="AlternateErrorPagesEnabled_Explain">AlternateErrorPagesEnabled

The policy uses alternative error pages in the Browser, for example, "Page not found".

The policy controls the "Offer corrections for typos in site addresses" setting. To go to the setting, in the Browser click  "Main Menu" → "Settings" → "General Settings" → "Search" and select it.


Features

- Refers to the basic security level. Learn more: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/deployment/windows/setting-policy#basic

Values

- Not Configured — alternative pages are being used. Users manage the settings. 
- Enabled — alternative pages are being used. The setting is enabled, users cannot disable it. 
- Disabled — alternative pages are not used. The setting is disabled, users cannot enable it.

Safety recommendations

Value: Disabled. Disable alternative error pages. Their use may lead to leakage of information about the visited site.

Possible problems. The browser will not be able to use alternative error pages.</string>
      <string id="ApplicationLocaleValue">Set the interface language</string>
      <string id="ApplicationLocaleValue_Explain">ApplicationLocaleValue

The policy sets the interface language in the Browser.

The policy controls the "Interface language" setting. To go to the setting, in the Browser click  "Main Menu" → "Settings" → "System" → "Language and region settings" and select it.

Features

- Can be configured as a recommendation page. Learn more: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/deployment/setting-policy.html#recommend-policy

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled — the OS language is used. Users can change the language in the settings. After changing the language, you need to restart the Browser.
- Enabled — the administrator sets the interface language. Users cannot change the language in the settings.

Example of a value:

en</string>
      <string id="BrowserSwitcher_group">Browser Switcher</string>
      <string id="AlternativeBrowserParameters">Set command line parameters for another browser</string>
      <string id="AlternativeBrowserParameters_Explain">AlternativeBrowserParameters

The policy sets command-line parameters for another browser.

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: Only the URL is passed as a command-line parameter.
- Enabled: The administrator sets a list of strings, each of them is passed to another browser as a separate command-line parameter. In Windows, parameters are combined using spaces. In macOS and Linux, a parameter itself can contain spaces and still be treated as a whole.

When using environment variables, their values are substituted. In Windows, the expression %ABC% is replaced with the value of the environment variable ABC. In macOS and Linux, the expression ${ABC} is replaced by the value of the environment variable ABC.

If a parameter contains the ${url} variable, the URL of the page to be opened is substituted for ${url}. If there is no ${url} variable in any parameter, the desired URL is added at the end of the command line.

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example value:

-foreground
-new-window
${url}
-profile
%HOME%\browser_profile</string>
      <string id="AlternativeBrowserParametersDesc">Set command line parameters for another browser</string>
      <string id="AlternativeBrowserPath">Specify a different browser</string>
      <string id="AlternativeBrowserPath_Explain">AlternativeBrowserPath

The policy specifies another browser in which URLs from the BrowserSwitcherUrlList and BrowserSwitcherExternalSitelistUrl policy lists should be opened.

You can set command-line parameters for another browser in the AlternativeBrowserParameters policy.

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: No other browser is specified.
- Enabled: The administrator sets a different browser. You can specify:
     - The path to the browser executable file.
     - A value: ${ie}, ${chrome}, ${firefox}, ${safari}, ${opera}, ${edge}.

Examples of values:

${opera}

C:\Program Files\Opera\launcher.exe</string>
      <string id="BrowserSwitcherDelay">Set a delay before launching another browser</string>
      <string id="BrowserSwitcherDelay_Explain">BrowserSwitcherDelay

The policy sets an interval in milliseconds during which Yandex Browser displays a warning about launching another browser.

On Windows, the policy only works when the BrowserSwitcherEnabled policy is enabled and any of the BrowserSwitcherUrlList, BrowserSwitcherExternalSitelistUrl, or both are enabled at once.

The policy is available for Browsers version 23.9.1 and higher.

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: Sites open in another browser without delay.
- Enabled: The administrator sets the delay. The value "0" means the policy is disabled.

Example value: 

300</string>
      <string id="BrowserSwitcherEnabled">Open the URL from the list in another browser</string>
      <string id="BrowserSwitcherEnabled_Explain">BrowserSwitcherEnabled

The policy allows you to open URLs from the BrowserSwitcherUrlList and BrowserSwitcherExternalSitelistUrl policy lists in another browser.

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: Yandex Browser doesn't open URLs from the BrowserSwitcherUrlList policy in another browser.
- Enabled: Yandex Browser opens URLs from the BrowserSwitcherUrlList and BrowserSwitcherExternalSitelistUrl policies in another browser, unless prohibited by other policies. The policies of the "Different browser" group are used to configure the function:
     - BrowserSwitcherUrlList: Defines a list of URLs that should be opened in a different browser.
     - AlternativeBrowserPath: Defines the browser in which URLs from this list should be opened.
     - AlternativeBrowserParameters: Defines the launch parameters of a different browser.</string>
      <string id="BrowserSwitcherExternalGreylistUrl">Set the URL of an XML file with a list of URLs that won't open in another browser</string>
      <string id="BrowserSwitcherExternalGreylistUrl_Explain">BrowserSwitcherExternalGreylistUrl

The policy sets the URL of an XML file with a list of URLs that won't open in another browser. 

On Windows, the policy only works when the BrowserSwitcherEnabled policy is enabled and any of the BrowserSwitcherUrlList, BrowserSwitcherExternalSitelistUrl, or both are enabled at once.

The BrowserSwitcherExternalSitelistUrl policy takes precedence over the BrowserSwitcherExternalGreylistUrl policy.

The policy is available for Browsers version 23.9.1 and higher.

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: The file URL is not set.
- Enabled: The administrator sets the file URL.

For more information about the XML file format with a list of URLs, see https://learn.microsoft.com/ru-ru/internet-explorer/ie11-deploy-guide/what-is-enterprise-mode#site-list-xml-file

Convert non-Latin URLs (for example, яндекс.рф) via punycode: https://www.reg.ru/web-tools/punycode

Example value: 

http://example.com/greylist.xml</string>
      <string id="BrowserSwitcherExternalSitelistUrl">Set the URL of an XML file with a list of URLs that will open in another browser</string>
      <string id="BrowserSwitcherExternalSitelistUrl_Explain">BrowserSwitcherExternalSitelistUrl

The policy sets the URL of an XML file with a list of URLs that will open in a different browser. The policy works like the BrowserSwitcherUrlList policy, but the list of URLs is set in a file.

The policy only works when the BrowserSwitcherEnabled and AlternativeBrowserPath policies are enabled.

The policy takes precedence over the BrowserSwitcherExternalGreylistUrl policy.

The policy is available for Browsers version 23.9.1 and higher.

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: The file URL is not set.
- Enabled: The administrator sets the URL of the file.

For more information about the XML file format with a list of URLs, see https://learn.microsoft.com/ru-ru/internet-explorer/ie11-deploy-guide/what-is-enterprise-mode#site-list-xml-file

Convert non-Latin URLs (for example, яндекс.рф) via punycode: https://www.reg.ru/web-tools/punycode

Example value: 

http://example.com/sitelist.xml</string>
      <string id="BrowserSwitcherParsingMode">Set the URL list analysis mode for another browser</string>
      <string id="BrowserSwitcherParsingMode_Explain">BrowserSwitcherParsingMode

The policy sets the analysis mode for URL lists in the "Different browser" category policies:

- BrowserSwitcherUrlList
- BrowserSwitcherUrlGreylist
- BrowserSwitcherExternalSitelistUrl
- BrowserSwitcherExternalGreylistUrl

The policy only works when the BrowserSwitcherEnabled and AlternativeBrowserPath policies are enabled.

The policy is available for Browsers version 23.9.1 and higher.

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: Less strict URL matching conditions apply. For values without the "/" character, the substring can be anywhere in the URL host name. Case-sensitive.
- Enabled: The administrator selects the analysis mode.
     - Default mode: Less strict URL matching conditions apply. For values without the "/" character, the substring can be anywhere in the URL host name. Case-sensitive.
     - Enhanced compatibility mode: Stricter URL matching conditions apply. For values without the "/" character, the substring can be only at the end of the URL host name. The substring should be at a domain name boundary. Case-insensitive.

For example, if substrings are specified in policies with URL lists example.com and acme.com/abc:
- Addresses http://example.com/, http://subdomain.example.com/, and http://acme.com/abc are considered appropriate regardless of the analysis mode.
- Addresses http://notexample.com/, http://example.com.invalid.com/, and http://example.comabc/ are considered appropriate only in default mode.
- Address http://acme.com/ABC is considered appropriate only in enhanced compatibility mode.</string>
      <string id="BrowserSwitcherParsingMode_Default">Default mode</string>
      <string id="BrowserSwitcherParsingMode_IESiteListMode">Enhanced compatibility mode</string>
      <string id="BrowserSwitcherUrlGreylist">Set a list of URLs that will not open in another browser</string>
      <string id="BrowserSwitcherUrlGreylist_Explain">BrowserSwitcherExternalGreylistUrl

The policy sets a list of URLs that won't open in another browser. Unlike the BrowserSwitcherUrlList policy, the URLs specified in the list apply to both browsers.

On Windows, the policy only works when the BrowserSwitcherEnabled policy is enabled and any of the BrowserSwitcherUrlList, BrowserSwitcherExternalSitelistUrl, or both are enabled at once.

To add more URLs to the list, you can use the BrowserSwitcherExternalGreylistUrl policy.

The BrowserSwitcherUrlList policy takes precedence over the BrowserSwitcherUrlGreylist policy.

The policy is available for Browsers version 23.9.1 and higher.

Applying the policy:

- Each URL from the list is processed separately.
- The exclamation mark before the URL inverts the rule: addresses set with «!» will open in another browser.
- If the link matches several URLs from the list, the most specific value applies. For example, the list contains the ie.com and !open-in-browser.ie.com addresses:
     - If users open the http://open-in-browser.ie.com address, then a more specific !open-in-browser.ie.com URL value is applied. There is the inversion sign «!», so the page will open in another browser.
     - If users open the http://ie.com address, the first rule applies and the site opens in Yandex Browser.
- You can see the sites set in the policy on the browser://browser-switch/internals page.

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: The list of URLs is not set.
- Enabled: The administrator sets the list of URLs.

Convert non-Latin URLs (for example, яндекс.рф) via punycode: https://www.reg.ru/web-tools/punycode

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example value:

ie.com
!open-in-chrome.ie.com
foobar.com/ie-only/</string>
      <string id="BrowserSwitcherUrlGreylistDesc">Set a list of URLs that will not open in another browser</string>
      <string id="BrowserSwitcherUrlList">Set URLs that will open in another browser</string>
      <string id="BrowserSwitcherUrlList_Explain">BrowserSwitcherUrlList

The policy sets a list of URLs to open in a different browser.

The policy only works when the BrowserSwitcherEnabled and AlternativeBrowserPath policies are enabled.

To add more URLs to the list, you can use the BrowserSwitcherExternalSitelistUrl policy.

The policy takes precedence over the BrowserSwitcherUrlGreylist policy.

Applying the policy:

- Each URL from the list is processed separately.
- The exclamation mark before the URL inverts the rule: addresses set with «!» won't open in a different browser.
- If the link matches multiple URLs from the list, the most specific value is applied. For example, the list contains the ie.com and !open-in-browser.ie.com addresses:
     - If users open the http://open-in-browser.ie.com address, then a more specific !open-in-browser.ie.com URL value is applied. It has the inversion sign «!», so the page will open in Yandex Browser.
     - If users open the http://ie.com address, the first rule applies and the site opens in a different browser.
- The sites specified in the policy are displayed on the browser://browser-switch/internals page.

The following keywords can be used:

- internal_urls: All single-level domains that can only be located on a local network (for example, http://ya or https://domain), local files (for example, C:\folder\file.pdf), and shared files (for example, \\desktop-1\folder\file.pdf).

- ie_proxy_urls (Windows only): List of URLs specified in the system registry at the following addresses:

- HKEY_CURRENT_USER\SOFTWARE\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\Internet Settings\ProxyOverride: For the current user.

- 
HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\Internet Settings\ProxyOverride: For all users.
- HKEY_CURRENT_USER\SOFTWARE\Policies\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\Internet Settings\ProxyOverride: For the current user.
- HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Policies\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\Internet Settings\ProxyOverride: For all users.

You can also set the ProxyOverride parameter in Internet Explorer settings: «Connections» → «LAN Settings» → «Advanced» → «Exceptions». Specify the list of URLs in the "Do not use proxy server for addresses beginning with:" field.

When the sites specified in the policy open in Internet Explorer, the Yandex Browser policies cease to apply to them and the Internet Explorer rules begin to apply.

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: The list of URLs is not set.
- Enabled: The administrator sets the list of URLs.

Convert non-Latin URLs (for example, яндекс.рф) via punycode: https://www.reg.ru/web-tools/punycode

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example value:

ie.com
!open-in-browser.ie.com
foobar.com/ie-only
internal_urls
ie_proxy_urls</string>
      <string id="BrowserSwitcherUrlListDesc">Set URLS to open in another browser</string>
      <string id="BrowserSwitcherUseIeSitelist">Use the SiteList parameter from Internet Explorer for another browser</string>
      <string id="BrowserSwitcherUseIeSitelist_Explain">BrowserSwitcherUseIeSitelist

The policy configures the use of the SiteList parameter from Internet Explorer for another browser. The policy handles the list of sites in the same way as BrowserSwitcherUrlList.

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: The SiteList parameter from Internet Explorer is not used.
- Enabled: The SiteList parameter from Internet Explorer is used.</string>
      <string id="RenderInInternetExplorerEnabled">Enable opening sites in a new window on the Internet Explorer engine</string>
      <string id="RenderInInternetExplorerEnabled_Explain">RenderInInternetExplorerEnabled

The policy extends the BrowserSwitcherEnabled policy and enables opening sites in a separate window on the Internet Explorer engine.

The policy does not support dynamic updates, so enable it before launching the browser.

The policy is available for browsers version 23.11.1 and higher.

Features

- Works only in the extended version of Yandex Browser for organizations. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: The policy is not set.
- Enabled: URLs from the BrowserSwitcherUrlList policy open in a new window on the Internet Explorer engine.</string>
      <string id="RenderInInternetExplorerException">Set exceptions to the RenderInInternetExplorerEnabled policy</string>
      <string id="RenderInInternetExplorerException_Explain">RenderInInternetExplorerException

The policy sets a list of exceptions to the RenderInInInternetExplorerEnabled policy.

The analysis mode for URL lists is set by the BrowserSwitcherParsingMode policy.

The policy only works in 32-bit Yandex Browser and with the BrowserSwitcherEnabled and RenderInInInternetExplorerEnabled policies enabled.

Features

- Only works in the extended version of Yandex Browser for organizations. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html

Applying the policy

- Each URL from the list is processed separately.
- The exclamation mark before the URL inverts the rule: addresses set with "!" won't open in another browser.
- If the link matches multiple URLs from the list, the most specific value applies. For example, the list contains addresses "ie.com" and "!open-in-browser.ie.com":
     - If users open the address "http://open-in-browser.ie.com", a more specific URL value is applied: !open-in-browser.ie.com. It has the inversion sign "!", so the page will open in another browser.
     - If users open the http://ie.com address, the first rule applies and the site opens in Internet Explorer.
- The sites specified in the policy are displayed on the browser://browser-switch/internals page.

You can use the following keywords:

- internal_urls: All single-level domains that can only be located on a local network (for example, http://ya or https://domain), local files (for example, C:\folder\file. pdf), and shared files (for example, \\desktop-1\folder\file.pdf).

- ie_proxy_urls (Windows only): List of URLs specified in the system registry at the following addresses:

- HKEY_CURRENT_USER\SOFTWARE\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\Internet Settings\ProxyOverride — for the current user
- HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\Internet Settings\ProxyOverride — for all users
- HKEY_CURRENT_USER\SOFTWARE\Policies\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\Internet Settings\ProxyOverride — for the current user
- HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Policies\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\Internet Settings\ProxyOverride — for all users

You can also set the ProxyOverride parameter in Internet Explorer settings: "Connections" → "LAN Settings" → "Advanced" → "Exceptions". Specify the list of URLs in the "Do not use proxy server for addresses beginning with:" field.

When the sites specified in the policy open in another browser, the Yandex Browser policies cease to apply to them and the other browser rules begin to apply.

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: The policy is not set.
- Enabled: The administrator sets the list of URLs. They open in the browser specified in the AlternativeBrowserPath policy.

Convert non-Latin URLs (for example, яндекс.рф) via punycode: https://www.reg.ru/web-tools/punycode

Example value:

ie.com
!open-in-chrome.ie.com
foobar.com/ie-only/
internal_urls
ie_proxy_urls</string>
      <string id="RenderInInternetExplorerExceptionDesc">Set exceptions to the RenderInInternetExplorerEnabled policy</string>
      <string id="NotificationsTrainingAdvertising_group">Notifications, training, and advertising</string>
      <string id="Education">Enable training</string>
      <string id="Education_Explain">Education

The policy enables training in Yandex Browser.

Values

- Not Configured, Enabled: Training is enabled.
- Disabled: Training is disabled.</string>
      <string id="FastSignup">Set up a reminder to enable syncing</string>
      <string id="FastSignup_Explain">FastSignup

The policy manages the reminder to enable syncing in Yandex Browser.

Values

- Not Configured, Enabled: The reminder is shown after 3 Yandex Browser launches without syncing.
- Disabled: The reminder is not shown.</string>
      <string id="NtpNotificationsDisable">Disable notifications on the new tab screen</string>
      <string id="NtpNotificationsDisable_Explain">NtpNotificationsDisable

The policy disables notifications on the new tab screen.

The policy controls the settings on the browser page://settings/ntpNotifications.

To proceed to the settings, in the Browser, click "Main Menu" → "Settings" → "Interface" → "Informer and notification settings".

The policy is available for Browsers version 23.1.2 and higher.

Values

- Not Configured: notifications and informers are enabled. Users manage the settings.
- Enabled: notifications and informers are disabled. Users can't turn them on.
- Disabled: notifications and informers are enabled. Users cannot disable them.</string>
      <string id="WelcomeExperiments">Set up the display of training pages for experiments</string>
      <string id="WelcomeExperiments_Explain">WelcomeExperiments

The policy enables or disables the display of training pages for experiments when Yandex Browser is started.

Values

- Not Configured, Enabled: The display of training pages is enabled.
- Disabled: The display of training pages is disabled.</string>
      <string id="Optimization_group">Optimization</string>
      <string id="SitePerProcess">Run tabs in separate processes</string>
      <string id="SitePerProcess_Explain">SitePerProcess

The policy manages the launch of tabs in separate processes.

Features

- This is a basic security policy. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support2/browser-corporate/ru/deployment/windows/setting-policy#basic

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: Tabs run in separate processes, frames do not.
- Enabled: Each tab and each frame runs in a separate process.

Safety recommendations

Value: Enabled. Enable the policy to increase security. Even if a site bypasses protection, it won't be able to steal data from another site.

Possible problems. Running each site in a separate process requires more RAM for Yandex Browser, which can degrade system performance.</string>
      <string id="TabDiscardingExceptions">Set a list of URLs that are not unloaded from memory on inactive tabs</string>
      <string id="TabDiscardingExceptions_Explain">TabDiscardingExceptions

The policy sets a list of URL exceptions — these pages are not unloaded from memory on inactive tabs.

If there is a lack of RAM, Yandex Browser unloads inactive tabs from it. When you switch to such a tab, it loads again.

The TotalMemoryLimitMb policy sets the RAM limit for a single Yandex Browser instance. When this limit is exceeded, inactive tabs get unloaded from RAM.

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: Pages on inactive tabs are unloaded when there's not enough RAM.
- Enabled: The administrator sets the list of URLs. You can use URL templates. You can use the "internal_urls" keyword to designate all single-domain sites. For example, the rule will apply to "https://example" but not to "https://example.com".

For more information about URL templates, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/policy/url-patterns.html

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example value:

example.com
https://*
*</string>
      <string id="TabDiscardingExceptionsDesc">Set URL exceptions that are loaded on inactive tabs when there is a lack of RAM and power saving mode is enabled</string>
      <string id="TotalMemoryLimitMb">Set the amount of memory for a single browser instance</string>
      <string id="TotalMemoryLimitMb_Explain">TotalMemoryLimitMb

The policy sets the amount of memory that a single Yandex Browser instance can use. If this amount is exceeded, Yandex Browser unloads inactive tabs from memory. The memory allocated for them is freed, and when you open them, the page will load again.

Browser instance — each open window of Incognito mode or different profiles.

You can set the list of URL exceptions that will not be unloaded from memory even if there's not enough memory in the TabDiscardingExceptions policy.

Features

- It works only on Windows and macOS.

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: Yandex Browser will start saving memory when the amount of available physical memory on the computer may not be enough for new tabs.
- Enabled: The administrator sets the memory limit in megabytes. Minimum value: 1024 MB. A value less than 1024 is rounded to 1024.

Example value: 

2048</string>
      <string id="YandexDisableBackgroundVideos">Disable video phone animation when the battery is low</string>
      <string id="YandexDisableBackgroundVideos_Explain">YandexDisableBackgroundVideos

The policy disables video background animation when the battery is low.

 The policy controls the setting "Disable video background animation when the battery is low". To go to the setting, in the Browser, click "Main menu" → "Settings" → "Tools" section → "Power saving mode" and select it.

 The policy is available for Browsers version 23.1.2 and higher.

Values

- Not Configured: The video phone animation turns off when the battery is low. Users control the setting.
- Enabled: The video phone animation turns off when the battery is low. The setting is enabled, and users cannot disable it.
- Disabled: The video phone animation does not turn off when the battery is low. The setting is disabled, and users cannot enable it.</string>
      <string id="YandexDiscardUnusedTabs">Configure loading unused tabs from memory</string>
      <string id="YandexDiscardUnusedTabs_Explain">YandexDiscardUnusedTabs

The policy sets up the unloading of unused tabs from memory.

The policy controls the "Free up memory with sleeping tabs" setting. To go to the setting, in the Browser click  "Main Menu" → "Settings" → "System" → "Performance" and select it.

The policy is available for Browsers version 23.1.2 and higher.

Values

- Not Configured: Unused tabs are unloaded from memory. Users manage the settings.
- Enabled: Unused tabs are unloaded from memory. The setting is enabled, users cannot disable it.
- Disabled: Unused tabs are not unloaded from memory. The setting is disabled, users cannot enable it.</string>
      <string id="YandexPowerSavingEnableAuto">Configure automatic power saving mode</string>
      <string id="YandexPowerSavingEnableAuto_Explain">YandexPowerSavingEnableAuto

The policy controls the "Enable automatically" power saving mode setting. To go to the setting, in the Browser click  "Main Menu" → "Settings" → "Tools" → "Power saving mode" and select it.

The condition for automatically enabling the power saving mode is set by the YandexPowerSavingMode policy.

Values

- Not Configured: The setting is enabled, users can disable it.
- Enabled: The setting is enabled, users can't disable it.
- Disabled: The setting is disabled, users can't enable it.</string>
      <string id="YandexPowerSavingMode">Set the percentage of battery power at which the browser will switch to power saving mode</string>
      <string id="YandexPowerSavingMode_Explain">YandexPowerSavingMode

The policy sets the condition for Yandex Browser to switch to power saving mode.

The policy only works if the YandexPowerSavingEnableAuto policy is not set or enabled.

The policy controls the value of the "Enable automatically" setting. To go to the setting in the Browser, click "Main Menu" → "Settings" → "Tools" → "Power Saving mode" and select the desired value:

- when device is unplugged;
- when device is less than 80% charged;
- when device is less than 50% charged;
- when device is less than 20% charged.

The policy is available for Browsers version 23.1.2 and higher.

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: The condition is set, users can change it.
- Enabled: The administrator selects a condition (battery charge percentage or unplugging from power), users can't change it.

Example value:

When device is less than 20%.
When device is less than 50%.
When device is less than 80%.
When device is unplugged.</string>
      <string id="YandexPowerSavingMode_WhenUnplagged">When disconnecting the device from the network</string>
      <string id="YandexPowerSavingMode_Battery_80">When charge is less than 80%</string>
      <string id="YandexPowerSavingMode_Battery_50">When charge is less than 50%</string>
      <string id="YandexPowerSavingMode_Battery_20">When charge is less than 20%</string>
      <string id="Other_group">Other</string>
      <string id="YandexBrowserAPISettings">Set the availability of the corporate JS API for extensions and pages</string>
      <string id="YandexBrowserAPISettings_Explain">YandexBrowserAPISettings

The policy sets a list of extensions and pages that can use the corporate JS API.

Features

- It only works in the extended version of the Browser for organizations. Learn more: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled — extensions and pages are not specified.
- Enabled — the administrator sets lists of extensions and pages that can use the corporate JS API.
     - extensions — a list of extension IDs. Optional parameter.
     - pages — a list of page URLs. Optional parameter.

Convert URLs without Latin letters (for example, яндекс.рф) via punycode: https://www.reg.ru/web-tools/punycode

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example of the value:

{
  "extensions": [
    "lgomcfbcdhebpjppbpcjpemgdbiiknnf"
  ],
  "pages": [
    "https://example.com/"
  ]
}</string>
      <string id="EnableMediaRouter">Enable Google Cast</string>
      <string id="EnableMediaRouter_Explain">EnableMediaRouter

The policy enables or disables Google Cast. You can activate this feature via the app menu, the page context menu, media controls on Google Cast-enabled sites, and using the broadcast icon on the toolbar (if shown).

Features

- This is a basic security policy. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support2/browser-corporate/ru/deployment/windows/setting-policy#basic

Values

- Not Configured, Enabled: Google Cast is enabled.
- Disabled: Google Cast is disabled.

Safety recommendations

Value: Disabled. Disable Google Cast to prevent sending tab or desktop content to untrusted devices in your local network.</string>
      <string id="MediaRouterCastAllowAllIPs">Allow connection to Google Cast devices on all IP addresses</string>
      <string id="MediaRouterCastAllowAllIPs_Explain">MediaRouterCastAllowAllIPs

The policy allows or restricts connecting to Google Cast devices on all IP addresses, not just private addresses of the RFC1918/RFC4193 standard.

Features

- This is a basic security policy. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support2/browser-corporate/ru/deployment/windows/setting-policy#basic

Values

- Not Configured: Connection is restricted if the CastAllowAllIPs option is not activated.
- Enabled: Connection is allowed.
- Disabled: Connection is restricted.

Safety recommendations

Value: Disabled. Disable the policy to ensure that you only connect to private addresses. Connecting Google Cast to public IP addresses threatens the security of confidential data.</string>
      <string id="YandexHideItemsInAppMenu">Hide the license status in the Browser interface</string>
      <string id="YandexHideItemsInAppMenu_Explain">YandexHideItemsInAppMenu

The policy hides all license-related statuses in the Browser interface (including violations, errors, etc.).

If there is no license or it is blocked, the policy does not apply.

The policy does not affect the display:

- license status on the "browser://help" and "browser://corp-internals" pages;
- other types of messages, for example, about using the Browser in a closed loop.

Features

- Works only in the extended version of Yandex Browser for organizations. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled — the license status is displayed.
- Enabled — the license status is not displayed.</string>
      <string id="BackgroundModeEnabled">Enable background operation mode</string>
      <string id="BackgroundModeEnabled_Explain">BackgroundModeEnabled

The policy enables the Browser's background mode.

The policy controls the "Enable background mode" setting. To go to the setting, in the Browser click "Main menu" → "Settings" → "System" → "Autorun and Background mode" and select it.

In the background, processes, applications, and the current Browser session remain active after the last Browser window is closed. All cookies saved during the session also remain active.

The background process icon is displayed in the notification area.

Features

- Refers to the basic security level. Learn more: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/deployment/windows/setting-policy#basic
- Can be configured as a recommendation page. Learn more: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/deployment/setting-policy.html#recommend-policy

Values

- Not Configured — background mode is enabled, users control the setting.
- Enabled — background mode is enabled. The setting is enabled, users cannot disable it.
- Disabled — the background mode is disabled. The setting is disabled, users cannot enable it.

Safety recommendations

Value: Disabled. Turn off the background mode. Vulnerable or malicious plugins, applications, and processes may continue to run even after the Browser is closed.</string>
      <string id="ChromeVariations">Configure Yandex Browser modifications</string>
      <string id="ChromeVariations_Explain">ChromeVariations

This policy controls Yandex Browser modifications that allow you to enable or disable browser features without installing a new version of the app.

Modifications allow you to try out security updates and new features before official release. If you encounter errors, roll back functions by restarting the computer.

Features

- This is a basic security policy. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support2/browser-corporate/ru/deployment/windows/setting-policy#basic

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: All modifications are available.
- Enabled: The administrator determines the type of available modifications:
     - All.
     - Only with critical fixes.
     - Prohibited.

Safety recommendations

Value: Enabled → All. Enable access to all modifications. Other options don't increase Yandex Browser security.</string>
      <string id="ChromeVariations_VariationsEnabled">All</string>
      <string id="ChromeVariations_CriticalFixesOnly">Only with critical fixes</string>
      <string id="ChromeVariations_VariationsDisabled">Not allowed</string>
      <string id="DeveloperToolsAvailability">Restrict developer tools</string>
      <string id="DeveloperToolsAvailability_Explain">DeveloperToolsAvailability

The policy restricts the use of developer tools.

The DeveloperToolsAvailabilityURLs policy takes precedence over the DeveloperToolsAvailability policy.

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: Developer tools and the JavaScript console are only restricted for extensions restricted by the corporate policy.
- Enabled: The administrator specifies one of the parameters: 
- "Disable the use of developer tools";
 - "Disable for extensions installed in accordance with corporate policy, and allow in all other cases";
 - "Allow the use of developer tools".

Security recommendations

Value: Enabled ("Disable the use of developer tools"). Prevent uploading files to websites to protect against data breaches.</string>
      <string id="DeveloperToolsAvailability_DeveloperToolsDisallowedForForceInstalledExtensions">Block for extensions installed in accordance with the corporate policy and allow in all other cases</string>
      <string id="DeveloperToolsAvailability_DeveloperToolsAllowed">Allow</string>
      <string id="DeveloperToolsAvailability_DeveloperToolsDisallowed">Don't allow</string>
      <string id="DeveloperToolsAvailabilityUrls">Set the availability of developer tools for the specified sites</string>
      <string id="DeveloperToolsAvailabilityUrls_Explain">DeveloperToolsAvailabilityUrls

The policy sets lists of URLs for which developer tools are forcibly allowed or prohibited. 

The policy takes precedence over the DeveloperToolsAvailability policy.

If the URL is not included in any of the lists, then the availability of developer tools is set by the DeveloperToolsAvailability policy.

Features

- It only works in the extended version of the Browser for organizations. Learn more: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled — the availability of developer tools is set by the DeveloperToolsAvailability policy.
- Enabled — the administrator sets the URL lists. You can use URL templates.
     - allow — a list of URLs for which developer tools are allowed.
     - block — a list of URLs for which developer tools are prohibited.

Learn more about URL templates: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/policy/url-patterns.html

Convert URLs without Latin letters (for example, яндекс.рф) via punycode: https://www.reg.ru/web-tools/punycode

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example of the value:

{
  "allow": [
    "example.com",
    "example.net"
  ],
  "block": [
    "[*.]example.org"
  ]
}

Security recommendations

Value: Enabled

{
 "allow": [
 "example.com",
 "example.net"
 ],
 "block": [
 "*"
 ]
}

Enable the policy and block the use of developer tools for all URLs to protect against security policy bypassing. Set exceptions for the URLs you want to allow.

Potential issues. Reduces the performance of web developers who use debugging tools.</string>
      <string id="Disable3DAPIs">Disable the three-dimensional graphics API</string>
      <string id="Disable3DAPIs_Explain">Disable3DAPIs

The policy restricts using the three-dimensional graphics API in Yandex Browser.

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: To access the 3D graphics API, you need to pass command-line arguments.
- Enabled: Pages can't use the WebGL API, plugins can't use the Pepper 3D API.</string>
      <string id="DisableScreenshots">Prohibit taking screenshots in Yandex Browser</string>
      <string id="DisableScreenshots_Explain">DisableScreenshots

The policy restricts users from taking screenshots using Yandex Browser and extensions.

The policy controls the "Allow browser to take screenshots" setting. To go to the settings, in the Browser click "Main Menu" → "Settings" → "Tools" → "Screenshots" and select it.

The policy is available for Browsers version 22.7.0 and higher.

Features

- Available in the mobile version of Yandex Browser for organizations. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html

Values

- Not Configured — the creation of screenshots using the Browser and API extensions is allowed, users control the settings.
- Enabled — the creation of screenshots using the Browser and API extensions is prohibited. The setting is disabled, users cannot enable it.
- Disabled — the creation of screenshots using the Browser and API extensions is allowed. The setting is enabled, users cannot disable it.</string>
      <string id="DownloadDirectory">Set a folder for downloads</string>
      <string id="DownloadDirectory_Explain">DownloadDirectory

The policy sets the folder where Yandex Browser saves downloaded files.

The policy controls the settings:

- "Always ask where to save files"
- "Save to: &lt;folder path&gt;" 

To go to the "Always ask where to save files" setting, in the Browser click "Main Menu" → "Settings" → "Tools" → "Downloaded files" and select it. 

To specify a folder to save files to, in the "Downloaded Files" section to the right of "Save to: &lt;folder path&gt;", click "Edit" and select the folder.

The policy is available for Browsers version 22.11.0 and higher.

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: Yandex Browser downloads files to the default folder. Users manage the settings.
- Enabled: The administrator sets the folder for downloading files. The setting "Always ask where to save files" is disabled. Users cannot change the settings.

Example value: 

C:\Users\${user_name}\Downloads</string>
      <string id="DownloadRestrictions">Limit downloads</string>
      <string id="DownloadRestrictions_Explain">DownloadRestrictions

The policy restricts file downloads.

Restrictions don't apply to loading the currently open page and saving in PDF format from the print window. 

The policy is available for Browsers version 22.11.0 and higher.

Features

- This is a basic security policy. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/deployment/windows/setting-policy#basic
- Can be configured as a recommendation. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/deployment/setting-policy.html#recommend-policy

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: Yandex Browser uses the default settings to download files.
- Enabled: The administrator sets restrictions for downloads that users can't change:
     - Unlimited (default).
     - Block all downloads: We recommend using this mode in special cases only.
     - Block malicious file downloads (recommended): Blocks known malicious files, doesn't block potentially dangerous file types.

Safety recommendations

Value: Enabled → Block malicious file downloads (recommended). Enable the "Block malicious file downloads (recommended)" mode to increase security.

Possible problems.	The system may erroneously block safe downloads.

For more information about how Protect checks downloaded files, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser/security/file-checking.html</string>
      <string id="DownloadRestrictions_DefaultDownloadSecurity">Unlimited (default)</string>
      <string id="DownloadRestrictions_BlockDangerousDownloads">Block downloads of malware and dangerous files</string>
      <string id="DownloadRestrictions_BlockAllDownloads">Block all downloads</string>
      <string id="DownloadRestrictions_BlockMaliciousDownloads">Block malicious file downloads (recommended)</string>
      <string id="HardwareAccelerationModeEnabled">Enable hardware acceleration</string>
      <string id="HardwareAccelerationModeEnabled_Explain">HardwareAccelerationModeEnabled

The policy enables hardware acceleration in Yandex Browser.

The policy controls the "Use hardware acceleration if possible" setting. To go to the setting, click "Main Menu" → "Settings" → "System" → "Performance" in the Browser and select it.

Values

- Not Configured: hardware acceleration is used if it is supported by the device configuration. Users manage the settings.
- Enabled: hardware acceleration is used if it is supported by the device configuration. The setting is enabled, users cannot disable it.
- Disabled: hardware acceleration is disabled. The setting is disabled, users cannot enable it.</string>
      <string id="IntensiveWakeUpThrottlingEnabled">Control the IntensiveWakeUpThrottling feature</string>
      <string id="IntensiveWakeUpThrottlingEnabled_Explain">IntensiveWakeUpThrottlingEnabled

The policy controls the IntensiveWakeUpThrottling feature.

When the IntensiveWakeUpThrottling feature is enabled, JavaScript timers on tabs running in the background are limited and synchronized. If the page is not used for at least 5 minutes, no more than one timer per minute is started.

The function complies with web standards, but its use may delay the execution of certain actions on some sites by up to one minute. At the same time, the function allows you to significantly reduce the load on the processor and reduce battery consumption. More details: https://bit.ly/30b1XR4

The rule is applied to each rendering process that starts with the latest policy value. To have the same value applied to all tabs, restart the Browser.

Values

- Not Configured: the feature is controlled by the Browser, users can change the settings.
- Disabled: the feature is disabled, users cannot enable it.
- Enabled: the feature is enabled, users cannot disable it.</string>
      <string id="NetworkPredictionOptions">Configure sites preloading</string>
      <string id="NetworkPredictionOptions_Explain">NetworkPredictionOptions

The policy configures the preloading of regularly visited sites: DNS, TCP and SSL connection, and page display.

Features

- This is a basic security policy. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support2/browser-corporate/ru/deployment/windows/setting-policy#basic
- Can be configured as a recommendation. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/deployment/setting-policy.html#recommend-policy

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: Preloading is enabled.
- Enabled: The administrator determines the preloading mode:
     - Enabled.
     - Wi-Fi only (not supported since version 16.9.0).
     - Disabled.

Safety recommendations

Value: Enabled → Disabled. Disable site preloading. This will reduce the number of connections that can be used for hacker attacks. There will also be no interaction with sites that users didn't intend to open.</string>
      <string id="NetworkPredictionOptions_NetworkPredictionAlways">Enabled</string>
      <string id="NetworkPredictionOptions_NetworkPredictionWifiOnly">Wi-Fi only (not supported since version 16.9.0)</string>
      <string id="NetworkPredictionOptions_NetworkPredictionNever">Disabled</string>
      <string id="WebRtcLocalIpsAllowedUrls">Set a list of URLs that can be shown a private IP via WebRTC</string>
      <string id="WebRtcLocalIpsAllowedUrls_Explain">WebRtcLocalIpsAllowedUrls

The policy sets a list of URLs that can see a private IP via WebRTC.

The policy only works if the WebRtcIPHandling policy is not set or enabled with the value "By default (only public IP is transmitted)".

In the extended version of Yandex Browser for organizations, the policy only works if the WebRtcIPHandling policy is set to "By default (only public IP is transmitted)". For more information about the extended version, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html

Features

- This is a basic security policy. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support2/browser-corporate/ru/deployment/windows/setting-policy#basic

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: Private IP addresses are hidden using mDNS host names.
- Enabled: The administrator sets the list of URLs including the protocol. You can use URL patterns. This weakens the protection of private IP addresses.

For more information about URL templates, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/policy/url-patterns.html 

Convert non-Latin URLs (for example, яндекс.рф) via punycode: https://www.reg.ru/web-tools/punycode

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example value:

https://www.example.com
*example.com*

Safety recommendations

Value: Disabled. Disable this policy. Access to IP addresses makes it possible to collect information about the internal network. Attackers can use it to hack and bypass the network.</string>
      <string id="WebRtcLocalIpsAllowedUrlsDesc">Set a list of URLs that can be shown a private IP via WebRTC</string>
      <string id="WebRtcUdpPortRange">Restrict the range of local UDP ports used by WebRTC</string>
      <string id="WebRtcUdpPortRange_Explain">WebRtcUdpPortRange

The policy limits the UDP port range for WebRTC.

In the extended version of the browser for organizations, IP is not transmitted via WebRTC and the policy is not applied.

- Not Configured, Disabled: WebRTC uses any available UDP port.
- Enabled: The administrator sets the range, including endpoints. If an empty string or invalid range is specified, WebRTC uses any available UDP port.

Example value: 10000-11999</string>
      <string id="YandexPolicyInFileConfig">Set the frequency of re-reading configuration files with policy values</string>
      <string id="YandexPolicyInFileConfig_Explain">YandexPolicyInFileConfig

The policy sets the frequency of re-reading configuration files with policy values. You can specify how often to re-read files when a successful or unsuccessful attempt is made.

Value format:
- for objects (DICT): you need to specify the path as a field: ""_FILE_": { "name": "path to file" }"
- for objects of the array (LIST) type: you need to specify the path as an object: "[ { "_FILE_": { "name": "path to file" } } ]"

Files with policy values can be accessed:

- locally (for example, "C:/folder/file.txt ");
- through a network folder (for example, "//computer/file.txt `");
- by URL (for example, "http://192.168.0.1/file.txt ").

Examples of policy values:

- For the object: let the policy have a string value in the policy editor (in the registry) in the form "{ "extension": { "id": "12345" , … }, … }». To replace the value with a file, you need to replace this value in the policy editor (or registry) with "{ "_FILE_": { "name": "path to the file" } }". The file itself must exist at the specified path and contain the value "{ "extension": { "id": "12345" , … }, … }».

- For an array type object: let the URLBlocklist policy have a value in the policy editor (registry) in the form of "["example.com "]". To replace the value with a configuration file, you need to create a file, for example "C:\broconfigs\policy.txt " and write the value of "[" into itexample.com "]". Then, in the policy itself, you can specify the path to the file in the form of "[{"_FILE_": {"name":"C:\\broconfigs\\policy.txt "}}]".

Spaces, tabs, and line feeds can be used in the file for better readability, but there should be no attached files.

Rules for specifying file paths:
- on Linux and macOS, you need to use a unix slash on the way, for example "/home/user/broconfigs/test.json";
- on Windows, you can use any slash, but the backslash in windows paths must be escaped, for example, you can specify "c:\\broconfigs\\test .json" or "c:/broconfigs/test .json".

In the extended version of the Browser for organizations:
- You can use Policy.InFileLoader histograms to evaluate performance.filesCount and Policy.InFileLoader.LoadTime at browser://histograms;
- upon successful or unsuccessful reading of files, a FileInPolicy security event is sent, which contains the md5 hash of the file and the path to the file.

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled — the contents of files with policy values are not rechecked at startup. If the file does not open the first time, access to it is rechecked after 2 minutes, then this interval increases quadratically.
- Enabled — the administrator sets time intervals for rechecking the contents of files containing the values of other policies and access to these files:
    - refresh — the maximum interval (in minutes) between automatic file checks. By default, 120.
    - retry is the minimum interval (in minutes) for automatic rechecking of a file that could not be read. For a file that could not be read again, this interval increases exponentially until the Browser is restarted or the result is successful. The default value is 1.

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example of a value:

{
  "refresh": 120,
  "retry": 2
}</string>
      <string id="RefererEnabledOnFaviconRequests">Pass the Referer URL when requesting a site favicon</string>
      <string id="RefererEnabledOnFaviconRequests_Explain">RefererEnabledOnFaviconRequests

The policy allows or restricts passing a Referer URL when requesting a site favicon.

Values

- Not Configured, Enabled: When requesting a site favicon, the Referer URL is passed.
- Disabled: The Referer URL is not passed.</string>
      <string id="YandexAliceMsgDisable">Disable Alice</string>
      <string id="YandexAliceMsgDisable_Explain">YandexAliceMsgDisable

The policy disables voice activation of Alice in Yandex Browser and prohibits users from enabling it.

How to enable voice activation of Alice:

- In the current version of Yandex Browser:
     - On a new tab in the Smart Bar, click the “Chat with Alice AI and voice search” icon.
- In the previous version of Yandex Browser:
     - Right‑click the sidebar and go to the Tools section.
     - Enable or disable Alice (the “Enable Alice” option).

In the browser version for computers, the policy:

- disables the buttons:
     - “Chat with Alice AI” on the new tab screen;
     - “Ask Alice AI” to the right of the Smart Search bar;
     - “Solve with Alice AI” on educational sites.
- disables the chat history in the Alice AI window on the right side of the screen;
- manages the settings:
     - “Set a keyword for voice activation”. To access the settings, in the Browser, click “Main menu” → “Settings” → the “Tools” section → “Alice — virtual assistant”.
     - “Show Alice AI chat history along with search history”. To access the settings, in the Browser, click “Main menu” → “Settings” → the “General settings” section and select it.
     - “Show the ‘Understand the problem with Alice AI’ button on educational sites”. To access the settings, in the Browser, click “Main Menu” → “Settings” → the “Tools” section → “Neural tools” and select it.

The policy is available for Browsers version 25.10.1 and above.

Features

- Available in the mobile version of the Browser for organizations. More details: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled — enabled:
     - voice activation of Alice AI;
     - buttons:
          - “Chat with Alice AI” on the new tab screen.
          - “Ask Alice AI” to the right of the Smart Search bar.
          - “Solve with Alice AI” on educational sites.
     - chat history in the Alice AI window on the right side of the screen;
     - settings:
          - “Set a keyword for voice activation”.
          - “Show Alice AI chat history along with search history”.
          - “Show the ‘Understand the problem with Alice AI’ button on educational sites”.
    - Users can disable them.
- Enabled — disabled:
     - voice activation of Alice AI;
     - buttons:
          - “Chat with Alice AI” on the new tab screen.
          - “Ask Alice AI” to the right of the Smart Search bar.
          - “Solve with Alice AI” on educational sites.
     - chat history in the Alice AI window on the right side of the screen;
     - settings:
          - “Set a keyword for voice activation”.
          - “Show Alice AI chat history along with search history”.
          - “Show the ‘Understand the problem with Alice AI’ button on educational sites”.
- Users cannot enable them.

Security recommendations

Value: Enabled. Enable the policy to disable the ability to send data to Alice and prevent the leakage of confidential information.

Possible issues. There may be a decrease in the productivity of employees who use this feature.</string>
      <string id="YandexCustomHeader">Add a custom header to all browser requests</string>
      <string id="YandexCustomHeader_Explain">YandexCustomHeader

The policy sets the X-Yandex-CustomHeader header and adds it to all Yandex Browser requests. You can use this header to filter requests from Yandex Browsers in your organization's network.

Features

- Available in the mobile version of the Browser for organizations. More details: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html
- Works only in the extended version of Yandex Browser for organizations. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: The header is not added.
- Enabled: The administrator sets their own header which is added to all Yandex Browser requests.

Example value: Example Custom Header</string>
      <string id="YandexCustomHeaderExt">Set the encrypted value of the X-Yandex-CustomHeader header</string>
      <string id="YandexCustomHeaderExt_Explain">YandexCustomHeaderExt

The mobile version is only available on iOS. Learn more: https://yandex.ru/support2/browser-corporate/ru/mobile-ios

The policy sets the encrypted value of the X-Yandex-CustomHeader header. The browser decrypts it when processing the policy and adds it to all HTTP requests. You can use this header to filter requests from Browsers on the organization's network.

The title is hidden — it is not displayed when using DevTools, as well as on the browser://policy page.

Only one of the YandexCustomHeader or YandexCustomHeaderExt policies can be set at a time, otherwise both policies will be disabled.

Features

- Available in the mobile version of the Browser for organizations. More details: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html
- Works only in the extended version of the Browser for organizations. More details: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html

Header Encryption

For the YandexCustomHeaderExt policy:

1. Get in the Support Service (https://yandex.ru/support2/browser-corporate/ru/support/support ) the encrypt_value_for_yandex_custom_header utility.

2. Generate the encryption key using the utility. To do this, run the command line:

encrypt_value_for_yandex_custom_header.exe --key
  
A key will appear in the terminal (for example, dxG15e9yR+A1Dt3MuInx1vOTbK15oxB+4ta/wtGkcHw=).

3. In the Management Console (https://browser .yandex.ru/corp/builds/create) → Browser Builder configure the extended Browser build.

4. In the Advanced Browser Settings → Encryption Keys section, click Create Encryption Keys. Specify the name of the key set and enter the key you received in step 2.

5. Download and install the configured Browser build. The generated keys will be integrated into it.

6. Using the utility and the key obtained in step 2, encrypt the header value of the header. To do this, run the command line:

encrypt_value_for_yandex_custom_header.exe --key="key obtained in step 2" --encrypt="encrypted value`

An encrypted header will appear in the terminal. For example, for the key dxG15e9yR+A1Dt3MuInx1vOTbK15oxB+4ta/wtGkcHw= and the test header, the encrypted value will be ql9EdhT2BeqRkyzYX3WIQdBZT6RZOyXtahO019c/nGTdtACPOn15.

7. Enable the YandexCustomHeaderExt policy and set the value {"value":"policy_value","key_index":key_index}. Fields:

     * "value" is the encrypted header received in step 6;

     * "key_index" is the sequence number of the key in the list specified in step 4.

8. Launch The Browser.
  
After these settings, all requests to sites will contain the specified header `X-Yandex-CustomHeader` in decrypted form.

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled — the header is not added.
- Enabled — The administrator sets the encrypted header value, which is decrypted and added to all Browser requests.

Example of a value:

{
  "value": "base64 string"
}</string>
      <string id="YandexCustomHeaderSettings">Set lists of URLs to which additional header transmission is allowed or prohibited</string>
      <string id="YandexCustomHeaderSettings_Explain">YandexCustomHeaderSettings

The policy sets lists of URLs to which the transmission of an additional header is allowed or prohibited. It works when the YandexCustomHeader or YandexCustomHeaderExt policy is enabled — these policies configure the header.

Features

- It only works in the extended version of the Browser for organizations. Learn more: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: URL listsThe 's are not set. An additional header is always passed if it is set by the YandexCustomHeader or YandexCustomHeaderExt policies.
- Enabled: the administrator sets the parameters in JSON format:
     - allow: a list of URLs to which additional header transmission is allowed. If the list is empty, transmission is allowed to all URLs except the prohibited ones.
     - deny: a list of URLs to which the transmission of an additional header is prohibited. If the list is empty, transmission is allowed to all URLs.
     - If the URL is not included in the allow and deny lists, the transmission of an additional header is allowed.
     - If the URL is included in the allow and deny lists at the same time (for example, the ""allow" lists are set: ["example.com "]" and ""deny": ["example.com "])" — the policy will cause an error.
     - If the link matches several URLs from the list, the most specific rule applies. For example, if the lists ""deny": ["*"]" and ""allow": ["example.com "]", then when opening the address example.com the transmission of an additional header is allowed.
     - You can use URL templates. Learn more about URL templates: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/policy/url-patterns.html
     - You can use the wildcard "*".

Convert URLs without Latin letters (for example, яндекс.рф) via punycode: https://www.reg.ru/web-tools/punycode

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example of a value:

{
  "allow": [
    "example.com",
    "[*.]example.org"
  ],
  "deny": [
    "*"
  ]
}</string>
      <string id="YandexExtCorpBrowserHeader">Add the header of the extended version of Yandex Browser to all requests</string>
      <string id="YandexExtCorpBrowserHeader_Explain">YandexExtCorpBrowserHeader

The policy adds the "X-Yandex-Extcorpbrowser: X" header to all Yandex Browser requests except CONNECT requests. You can use this header to filter requests from the extended version of Yandex Browser for organizations.

Features

- Available in the mobile version of the Browser for organizations. More details: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html
- Works only in the extended version of Yandex Browser for organizations. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: The header is not added.
- Enabled: The header is added to all Yandex Browser requests except CONNECT requests.</string>
      <string id="YandexLoginAllowedDomains">Set the list of allowed domains for accounts in the organization</string>
      <string id="YandexLoginAllowedDomains_Explain">YandexLoginAllowedDomains

The policy sets a list of the organization's domains you can use to log in to Yandex ID (using an account from these domains). The account should match the format "username@example.com" where example.com is one of the allowed domains of the organization.

Features

- Available in the mobile version of the Browser for organizations. More details: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html
- Works only in the extended version of Yandex Browser for organizations. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: You can log in with any Yandex ID.
- Enabled: The administrator sets the list of the organization's domains.

Example value: 

testserver.example.com;ya.org</string>
      <string id="YandexLoginAllowedDomainsForceLogout">Enable force logout from Yandex ID</string>
      <string id="YandexLoginAllowedDomainsForceLogout_Explain">YandexLoginAllowedDomainsForceLogout

The policy enables the force logout of users from Yandex ID when the list of allowed domains in the YandexLoginAllowedDomains policy changes.

When the policy is enabled, there is no force logout from Yandex ID. It will be triggered when you change the list in YandexLoginAllowedDomains, except when the list becomes empty.

You can set the maximum delay in minutes for the force logout from Yandex ID in the YandexLoginAllowedDomainsForceLogoutMaxDelay policy.

Features

- Available in the mobile version of the Browser for organizations. More details: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html
- Works only in the extended version of Yandex Browser for organizations. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: Force logout is disabled.
- Enabled: Force logout is enabled. If the YandexLoginAllowedDomainsForceLogoutMaxDelay policy is not set, the force logout occurs within 5 minutes.</string>
      <string id="YandexLoginAllowedDomainsForceLogoutMaxDelay">Set a delay for the force logout from Yandex ID</string>
      <string id="YandexLoginAllowedDomainsForceLogoutMaxDelay_Explain">YandexLoginAllowedDomainsForceLogoutMaxDelay

The policy sets the maximum delay in minutes to force logout users from Yandex ID when changing the list of domains in the YandexLoginAllowedDomains policy. 

The delay for different users will be a random number from 0 to the set value. The maximum value is 1440 minutes (24 hours). If the value is 0, the force logout is triggered immediately.

The policy only works when the YandexLoginAllowedDomainsForceLogout policy is enabled.

Features

- Available in the mobile version of the Browser for organizations. More details: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html
- Works only in the extended version of Yandex Browser for organizations. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: The delay time is not set. If the YandexLoginAllowedDomainsForceLogout policy is enabled, then the forced exit occurs within 5 minutes.
- Enabled: The administrator sets the delay time.

Example value:

10</string>
      <string id="YandexNoRefererSettings">Configure the transfer of the Referer header</string>
      <string id="YandexNoRefererSettings_Explain">YandexNoRefererSettings

The policy aims to switch to the referrer search at any time on the internal and external network.

The policy sends out user capabilities via email using the Yandex Link policy setting YandexNoRefererSettingAllowlistExt.

Features

- Works only in the extended version of Yandex Browser for organizations. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html

Values

- Not configured, Disabled: the link header is displayed on all sites.
- Enabled: the administrator downloads the parameters in JSON format:
     - allow: search for URLs where the link is not blocked.
     - deny_to: a link to the URLs that the user is referring to.
     - allow_from_deny_to_deny: change to click on a link to request a link to another address:
          - true: allowed;
          - false: prohibited.

You can use the wildcard "*" and template URLs.

For more information about URL templates, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/policy/url-patterns.html

Convert non-Latin URLs (for example, яндекс.рф) via punycode: https://www.reg.ru/web-tools/punycode

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example value:

Block access to information about internal links to external sites through a Referrer:

{
  "allow": [
    "internal_urls"
  ],
  "deny_to": [
    "*"
  ],
  "allow_from_deny_to_deny": true
}

Dissemination of the YandexNoRefererSettingAllowlistExt policy:

{
  "allow": [
    &lt;содержимое политики YandexNoRefererSettingAllowlistExt&gt;
  ],
  "deny_to": [
    "*"
  ],
  "allow_from_deny_to_deny": false
}</string>
      <string id="YandexUrlPatternsAliases">Set aliases for a list of URL templates</string>
      <string id="YandexUrlPatternsAliases_Explain">YandexUrlPatternsAliases

The policy sets aliases for the list of URL templates and IP address masks. These aliases will be applied to all policies that contain alias names in the format `$(alias_name)'.

The policy is available for Browsers version 24.6.4 and higher.

Features

- Available in the mobile Browser version for organizations. Learn more: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html
- Works only in the extended version of the Browser for organizations. More details: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled — the aliases of the template list are not set.
- Enabled — the administrator sets aliases for the list of URL templates. You can use URL templates. The wildcard "*" must not specify other aliases.

Learn more about URL templates: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/policy/url-patterns.html

Convert URLs without the Latin alphabet (for example, яндекс.рф) via punycode: https://www.reg.ru/web-tools/punycode

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example of a value:

{
  "aliases": {
    "foo": "ya.ru; ya.com",
    "bar": "*; [*.]com; [*.]net",
    "baz": "internal_urls"
  }
}</string>
      <string id="YandexLicenseCheckInterval">Set an emergency license verification interval on the server</string>
      <string id="YandexLicenseCheckInterval_Explain">YandexLicenseCheckInterval

The policy sets the license verification interval on the server, which is used in emergency mode — when the Browser has received the 425 error code from the server. In this case, the Browser will use the specified interval instead of the standard one.

Features

- It only works in the extended version of the Browser for organizations. Learn more: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html
- Available in the mobile version of Yandex Browser for organizations. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled — the standard value is used.
- Enabled — the administrator sets the interval in minutes, from 1 to 1440.

Example of the value:

10</string>
      <string id="WebRtcIPHandling">Set the WebRTC IP handling policy</string>
      <string id="WebRtcIPHandling_Explain">WebRtcIPHandling

The policy determines which IP addresses WebRTC uses when attempting to find the best available connection. For more information, see https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc8828.html#section-5.2

Features

- This is a basic security policy. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support2/browser-corporate/ru/deployment/windows/setting-policy#basic

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: Only the public IP is transmitted. In the extended version of Yandex Browser for organizations, IP is not transmitted. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html
- Enabled: The administrator selects one of the modes:
     - By default (only public IP is transmitted).
     - Public and private IP.
     - Public IP.
     - No IP is transmitted.

Safety recommendations

Value: Enabled → Public IP. Restrict transmitting private IPs. Access to IP addresses makes it possible to collect information about the internal network. Attackers can use it to hack and bypass the network.</string>
      <string id="WebRtcIPHandling_default">By default (only public IP is transmitted)</string>
      <string id="WebRtcIPHandling_default_public_and_private_interfaces">Public and private IP</string>
      <string id="WebRtcIPHandling_default_public_interface_only">Public IP</string>
      <string id="WebRtcIPHandling_disable_non_proxied_udp">No IP is transmitted</string>
      <string id="PersonalData_group">Personal Data</string>
      <string id="AllowDeletingBrowserHistory">Allow to delete your browsing and download history</string>
      <string id="AllowDeletingBrowserHistory_Explain">AllowDeletingBrowserHistory

The policy allows you to delete your browsing and download history.

The policy controls the "Views" and "Downloads" options in the history cleanup settings. To go to the settings, click on "Main Menu" → "History" → "Clear history" in the Browser.

Features

- Refers to the basic security level. Learn more: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/deployment/windows/setting-policy#basic
- Available in the mobile Browser version for organizations. Learn more: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html

Values

- Not Configured, Enabled: Users can delete their browsing and download history. Users manage the options.
- Disabled: Users cannot delete their browsing and download history. The options are disabled, users cannot enable them.

Safety recommendations

Value: Disabled. Prohibit users from deleting their browsing and download history. This way they won't be able to hide browsing banned or malicious sites.</string>
      <string id="AutofillAddressEnabled">Enable address autocomplete</string>
      <string id="AutofillAddressEnabled_Explain">AutofillAddressEnabled

The policy enables auto-completion of addresses.

The policy controls the "Suggest form autofill" setting. To go to the setting, in the Browser click "Main Menu" → "Settings" → "Tools" → "Autofill" and select it.


Features

- Refers to the basic security level. Learn more: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/deployment/windows/setting-policy#basic
- Can be configured as a recommendation page. Learn more: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/deployment/setting-policy.html#recommend-policy

Values

- Not Configured, Enabled — auto-completion of addresses is enabled. Users manage the settings.
- Disabled — auto-completion of addresses is disabled. The entered addresses are not saved. The setting is disabled, users cannot enable it.

Safety recommendations

Value: Disabled. Disable auto-completion of addresses. Attackers can steal this data if they gain access to the user's computer.

Possible problems. Auto-completion will not be available to users.</string>
      <string id="AutofillCreditCardEnabled">Enable credit card autofill</string>
      <string id="AutofillCreditCardEnabled_Explain">AutofillCreditCardEnabled

The policy includes auto-completion of bank card details.

The policy controls the activation and deactivation of the map manager (https://browser .yandex.ru/help/ru/security/payment-card). If the policy is disabled, the card manager is automatically blocked — users cannot add or manage new cards.

Features

- Refers to the basic security level. Learn more: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/deployment/windows/setting-policy#basic
- Can be configured as a recommendation page. Learn more: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/deployment/setting-policy.html#recommend-policy

Values

- Not Configured — auto-completion of bank card details is enabled.
- Enabled — auto-completion of bank card details is enabled. The card manager is enabled.
- Disabled — auto-completion of bank card details is disabled, the entered data is not saved. The card manager is blocked.

Safety recommendations

Value: Disabled. Disable auto-completion of bank card details. Attackers can steal this data if they gain access to the user's computer.

Possible problems. Auto-completion will not be available to users.</string>
      <string id="BlockThirdPartyCookies">Restrict third-party cookies</string>
      <string id="BlockThirdPartyCookies_Explain">BlockThirdPartyCookies

The policy restricts third-party cookies and prohibits users from changing their settings.

The policy controls the settings "Restrict third-party cookies" and "Block third-party cookies". To proceed to the settings, in the Browser, click "Main Menu" → "Settings" → "Websites" → "Advanced site settings" → "Cookies" and select one of the settings options.

The policy is available for Browsers version 23.3.1 and higher.

Features

- Refers to the basic security level. Learn more: https://yandex.ru/support2/browser-corporate/ru/deployment/windows/setting-policy#basic
- Can be configured as a recommendation page. Learn more: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/deployment/setting-policy.html#recommend-policy

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: the "Restrict third-party cookies" setting is enabled. In Incognito mode, third-party cookies are blocked. Third-party cookies can only be used by sites that the user has visited. Users manage the settings.
- Enabled: the "Block third-party cookies" setting is disabled, users cannot enable it.

Safety recommendations

Value: Enabled. Restrict third-party cookies. Third-party cookies can violate privacy and track user activity.

Possible problems. Office applications and other products that use cookies may stop working. In this case, disable the policy.</string>
      <string id="BrowsingDataLifetime">Configure automatic deletion of user data</string>
      <string id="BrowsingDataLifetime_Explain">BrowsingDataLifetime

The policy sets up the automatic deletion of user data. 

In the desktop version, it only works when the SyncDisabled policy is enabled.

15 seconds after launch, the Browser automatically deletes the data specified by the administrator if it is stored for longer than the specified period.

Features

- Available in the mobile Browser version for organizations. Learn more: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled — user data is not automatically deleted.
- Enabled — the administrator sets the parameters:
     - time_to_live_in_hours — the data storage period in hours. The minimum value is 1 hour.
     - data_types — the types of data that will be deleted.

Types of data to delete:

- browsing_history
- download_history
- cookies_and_other_site_data
- cached_images_and_files
- autofill
- password_signin 
- site_settings
- hosted_app_data

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example of a value:

[
  {
    "time_to_live_in_hours": 24,
    "data_types": [
      "browsing_history"
    ]
  },
  {
    "time_to_live_in_hours": 12,
    "data_types": [
      "password_signin",
      "autofill"
    ]
  }
]</string>
      <string id="ClearBrowsingDataOnExitList">Delete work data when you log out of the Browser</string>
      <string id="ClearBrowsingDataOnExitList_Explain">ClearBrowsingDataOnExitList

The policy sets a list of user data that is deleted after all Browser windows are closed: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/policy/clear-browsing-data-on-exit-list#user-data

If the policy is configured at the platform level, you must disable synchronization for the entire platform. If the policy is configured at the user level, it works if synchronization is disabled for them.

If the Browser closes unexpectedly (for example, due to a malfunction), the user data is deleted the next time the profile is loaded.

The policy is available for Browsers version 22.11.0 and higher.

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: User data is not deleted after closing all Browser windows.
- Enabled: The administrator sets which user data is deleted after closing all Browser windows.

Types of data to delete:

- history (browsing_history); 
- downloads (download_history);
- cookies and other website data (cookies_and_other_site_data); 
- cache (cached_images_and_files); 
- autofill data; 
- passwords (password_signin); 
- site settings (site_settings);
- application data (hosted_app_data).

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example of a value:

browsing_history
download_history
cookies_and_other_site_data
cached_images_and_files
password_signin
autofill
site_settings
hosted_app_data</string>
      <string id="ClearBrowsingDataOnExitListDesc">Set data to delete after closing the browser</string>
      <string id="ForceEphemeralProfiles">Enable temporary profiles</string>
      <string id="ForceEphemeralProfiles_Explain">ForceEphemeralProfiles

The policy enables temporary profiles. 

When the policy is enabled, profile data is stored on the device only during the session. When Yandex Browser closes, the browsing history, extensions and their data, as well as cookies, databases, and other site data is deleted. A new profile opens when launching Yandex Browser. 

Features

- This is a basic security policy. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/deployment/windows/setting-policy#basic

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: Normal profile is used.
- Enabled: If the policy is enabled on the device, all profiles on it become temporary. If the policy is enabled on the local network, active user profiles become temporary. If users enable syncing, all data will be saved in the synced profile.

Safety recommendations

Value: Disabled. Disable temporary profiles. It's difficult to investigate cybercrimes when data is deleted after each session.</string>
      <string id="IncognitoModeAvailability">Set up Incognito mode</string>
      <string id="IncognitoModeAvailability_Explain">IncognitoModeAvailability

The policy determines whether users can enable
Incognito mode.

Features

- This is an increased security policy. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support2/browser-corporate/ru/deployment/windows/setting-policy#advanced
- Available in the mobile version of Yandex Browser for organizations. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html

Values

- Not Configured: Users can open pages in Incognito mode.
- Disabled: Users can open pages in Incognito mode.
- Enabled: The administrator sets the policy application mode:
     - Forced use of Incognito mode: Incognito mode is always on.
     - Incognito mode is available: Users can view pages in both normal mode and Incognito mode.
     - Incognito mode disabled: Users can only view pages in normal mode.


Safety recommendations

Value: Enabled → "Incognito mode is disabled". Enable "Incognito mode is disabled". Incognito mode allows users to hide signs of malicious behavior and doesn't save files that are important for investigating cybercrimes.</string>
      <string id="IncognitoModeAvailability_Enabled">Incognito mode is available</string>
      <string id="IncognitoModeAvailability_Disabled">Incognito mode is disabled</string>
      <string id="IncognitoModeAvailability_Forced">Forced use of Incognito mode</string>
      <string id="SavingBrowserHistoryDisabled">Prohibit saving browsing history</string>
      <string id="SavingBrowserHistoryDisabled_Explain">SavingBrowserHistoryDisabled

The policy restricts saving browsing history and syncing open tabs.

Features

- This is a basic security policy. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support2/browser-corporate/ru/deployment/windows/setting-policy#basic
- Available in the mobile version of the Browser for organizations. More details: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: Browsing history is saved. When syncing is enabled, tabs and the Tableau are synced with the Yandex server, and users can import history from other browsers.
- Enabled: Browsing history is not saved, users can't disable this option and import history from other browsers. 
Only the Tableau can sync with the Yandex server.

Safety recommendations

Value: Disabled. Disable the policy to save your browsing history. This can be useful in investigating cybercrimes.</string>
      <string id="UserDataDir">Set a folder for storing user data</string>
      <string id="UserDataDir_Explain">UserDataDir

The policy sets the folder where Yandex Browser stores user data. If there is no folder at the specified location, it will be created.

Data from the current storage folder is not transferred to the folder specified by the policy. If there is data in the folder, it is applied to the profile in the Browser. If there is no data in the folder, a new profile is created with default settings.

To avoid losing data, don't specify a root folder or a folder that's used for other purposes in the policy.

Yandex Browser profiles aren't backward compatible. If you use a roaming profile and access it from different versions of Yandex Browser, this may cause crashes and data loss. To avoid this, we recommend using variables or synchronization.

Features

- Only works in Windows and macOS.

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: Yandex Browser uses the default profile folder. Users can change it with the command-line parameter --user-data-dir.
- Enabled: The administrator sets a folder for storing user data. Yandex Browser uses the specified folder regardless of the --user-data-dir parameter. You can use supported variables.

Example value:

C:\yandex_user_data</string>
      <string id="YandexSyncEnabled">Enable user synchronization</string>
      <string id="YandexSyncEnabled_Explain">YandexSyncEnabled

The policy enables synchronization with the user.

The policy controls the settings section "Sync settings". To go to the section, in the Browser click "Main Menu" → "Settings" → "General Settings" → "Sync settings".

The policy is available for Browsers version 24.6.1 and higher.

Do not enable the policy when the SyncDisabled policy is active — it contains the functionality of the YandexSyncEnabled policy.

Features

- Works only in the extended version of the Browser for organizations. More details: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html
- Available in the mobile version of the Browser for organizations. More details: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html

Values

- Not Configured — Synchronization settings depend on other policies.
- Disabled — disable synchronization for the users. The users will not be able to enable it.
- Enabled — enable synchronization for the users.</string>
      <string id="MasterPasswordDisabled">Disable the use of the master password</string>
      <string id="MasterPasswordDisabled_Explain">MasterPasswordDisabled

The policy disables the use of the master password by users.

The policy takes precedence over the YandexMasterPassword policy.

The policy is available for Browsers version 22.9.1 and higher.

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: Users can use a master password.
- Enabled: Master password is disabled.</string>
      <string id="YandexAntiTracking">Set up anti tracking</string>
      <string id="YandexAntiTracking_Explain">YandexAntiTracking

The policy allows filtering requests and their individual parameters to protect user data.

For example, when opening example.com, a request with user data is sent to spy-site.com, a third-party site. Using the policy, the administrator removes parameters with user data from requests or blocks sending data to spy-site.com. The example.com site will still open.

The policy filters requests but doesn't block URLs. The URLBlocklist policy takes priority over YandexAntiTracking. The YandexAntiTracking policy takes priority over URLAllowlist. If requests to a page are blocked by the YandexAntiTracking policy, the page won't open even if it is specified in the URLAllowlist policy. If requests to a page are enabled by the YandexAntiTracking policy, the page won't open if it is specified in the URLBlocklist policy.

General syntax rules

- ; — Rule separator. Not used if the rules are set in the file.
- * — Wildcard symbol, represents any number of characters of any kind, including no characters.
- ^ — Separates the address and modifier.
- ,domain=[...]|[...] — Parameter for limiting the modifier action to a list of domains to whose requests the rule will be applied. Domains are separated by «|».
- ! — Comment. Placed at the beginning of a line. Acts as a separate rule and should be separated by ";" or a line break in the file.

Request filters

- || — Replaces the beginning of the address without specifying the http:// or https:// scheme.
- | — Indicates the beginning or end of the address.
- @@ — Exception for the entire rule. Placed at the beginning of the rule.

Request parameter filters

- $removeparam — Modifier, removes parameters from URL requests, sets parameter names. Can be used separately from the address. If the list is not set, then all (any) request parameters are deleted. Can be used together with request filters.
- ~ — Exception for the parameter.

You can find examples of rules in Help: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/policy/yandex-anti-tracking.html

Features

- Available in the mobile version of Yandex Browser for organizations. For more information, see: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html
- Works only in the extended version of Yandex Browser for organizations. For more information, see: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: Antitracking is disabled.
- Enabled: The "referer" header is removed from all Yandex Browser requests. The administrator sets the rules for blocking requests and iframe requests with ";" or uses "$file-rules=" to set the path to the rules file located on the computer or the local network. For example: "$file-rules=C:\rules.txt" or "$file-rules=\\shared-folder\rules.txt". In the file, each rule is placed on a separate line. Using one of the methods for setting rules excludes the use of another.

Convert non-Latin URLs (for example, яндекс.рф) using Punycode: https://www.reg.ru/web-tools/punycode

Example of a policy value: 

!Removing parameters of requests to example.com;||example.com^$removeparam

Example file:

!Blocking example.com
||example.com
!Blocking of subdomains example.com
||*.example.com</string>
      <string id="YandexDisableID">Disable Yandex ID support</string>
      <string id="YandexDisableID_Explain">YandexDisableID

The policy disables support for Yandex ID in the Browser.

The YandexDisableID policy contains the functionality of the SyncDisabled policy. Do not turn them on at the same time.

The policy is available for Browser versions:

- 23.3.1 and higher (for Windows, Linux and macOS);
- 25.3.0 and higher (for Android);
- 25.4.2 and higher (for iOS).

Renamed in the interface:

- The "Syncing" section — to the "Autocomplete" section (browser://settings page). To go to the section, in the Browser click "Main Menu" → "Settings" → "General Settings" section and select it.

- The "Yandex ID" section — to the "Autocomplete" section (browser://personal page). To go to the section, in the Browser  click "Main Menu" → "Settings" and select it from the top menu.

Disabled in the interface:

- Profile widget in the main menu. To go to the widget, in the Browser click "Main Menu".

- The reminder "Save data" in the profile widget in the main menu. To go to the reminder, in the Browser click "Main Menu".

- Sections "Sync settings" and "Restore Tableau" (browser://settings page). To go to the sections, in the Browser click "Main Menu" → "Settings" → "General Settings" section and select them.

- The option "Save to Yandex Pay" in the "Wallet and cards" section (browser://personal/cards page). To go to the option, in the Browser click "Main Menu" → "Wallet and Cards" and hover the mouse pointer over the desired card.

- The side menu item "Account" in the profile settings (browser page://personal). To go to the menu item, in the Browser click "Main Menu" → "Settings" → "Yandex ID" and select it from the side menu.

- The "Sync and backup" section in the profile settings (browser://personal/settings page). To go to the section, in the Browser click "Main Menu" → "Settings" → "Yandex ID" → "Settings" and select it.

- The option "Disable option to reset the master password" in the profile settings (browser://personal/settings page). To go to the option, in the Browser click "Main Menu" → "Settings" → "Yandex ID" → "Settings" → "Passwords and cards are encrypted" and select it.

- The "Sync" extension (browser page://tune). To go to the extension, in the Browser click "Main Menu" → "Extensions" → "Data management" section.

Features

- Available in the mobile version of the Browser for organizations. More details: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: Yandex ID-related functions are available.
- Enabled: The functions associated with Yandex ID are disabled.</string>
      <string id="YandexMasterPassword">Configure the master password usage mode</string>
      <string id="YandexMasterPassword_Explain">YandexMasterPassword

The policy sets up the master password usage mode.

The MasterPasswordDisabled policy takes precedence over the YandexMasterPassword policy.

The policy is available for Browsers version 25.4.1 and higher.

Features

- Works only in the extended version of the Browser for organizations. More details: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: Users can enable or disable the master password.
- Enabled: the administrator sets the mode of using the master password:
    - mode: the mode of using the master password. Required parameter. Meanings:
        - soft: when using or saving a password, a notification is displayed about the need to set a master password. Users can cancel the setting of the master password in the current Browser session.
        - hard: when the Browser starts, a notification is displayed about the need to set a master password. Passwords are not saved until the master password is set. By default, all previously saved passwords will be deleted after 14 days.
    - custom_message: notification text. To set a link, use the replacement symbol "${url}". An optional parameter.
    - delete_after_days: the number of days until all saved passwords are deleted if the master password is not set. To disable password deletion, set the value to "delete_after_days: -1". An optional parameter. Default value: 14. Works only for "mode": "hard".

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example of a value:

{
  "mode": "hard",
  "custom_message": "Set a master password to save your passwords. After 7 days, the passwords will be deleted.",
  "delete_after_days": 7
}</string>
      <string id="Safety_group">Security</string>
      <string id="LocalNetworkAccessAllowedForUrls">Allow sites to make network requests to local devices and local network endpoints.</string>
      <string id="LocalNetworkAccessAllowedForUrls_Explain">LocalNetworkAccessAllowedForUrls

The policy allows the specified sites to send network requests to local devices and endpoints on the local network.

For sources not specified in the policy, the user settings are applied.

If a source is subject to multiple policies, priority is determined in the following order:
- LocalNetworkBlockedForUrls
- LocalNetworkAllowedForUrls
- LoopbackNetworkAccessBlockedForUrls
- LoopbackNetworkAccessAllowedForUrls
- LocalNetworkAccessBlockedForUrls
- LocalNetworkAccessAllowedForUrls

The policy is available for Browsers version 26.6.4 and higher.

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled — user settings are applied.
- Enabled — the administrator sets a list of URLs.

You can use URL templates. Learn more about URL templates: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/policy/url-patterns.html

Convert URLs without Latin letters (for example, yandex.Russian Federation) via punycode: https://www.reg.ru/web-tools/punycode

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example of a value:

http://www.example.com:8080
[*.]example.edu</string>
      <string id="LocalNetworkAccessAllowedForUrlsDesc">Allow sites to make network requests to local devices and local network endpoints.</string>
      <string id="LocalNetworkAccessBlockedForUrls">Block sites from making network requests to local devices and local network endpoints</string>
      <string id="LocalNetworkAccessBlockedForUrls_Explain">LocalNetworkAccessBlockedForUrls

The policy prohibits these sites from sending network requests to local devices and endpoints on the local network.

For sources not specified in the policy, the user settings are applied.

If a source is subject to multiple policies, priority is determined in the following order:
- LocalNetworkBlockedForUrls
- LocalNetworkAllowedForUrls
- LoopbackNetworkAccessBlockedForUrls
- LoopbackNetworkAccessAllowedForUrls
- LocalNetworkAccessBlockedForUrls
- LocalNetworkAccessAllowedForUrls

The policy is available for Browsers version 26.6.4 and higher.

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled — user settings are applied.
- Enabled — the administrator sets a list of URLs.

You can use URL templates. Learn more about URL templates: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/policy/url-patterns.html

Convert URLs without Latin letters (for example, yandex.Russian Federation) via punycode: https://www.reg.ru/web-tools/punycode

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example of a value:

http://www.example.com:8080
[*.]example.edu</string>
      <string id="LocalNetworkAccessBlockedForUrlsDesc">Block sites from making network requests to local devices and local network endpoints.</string>
      <string id="LocalNetworkAccessIpAddressSpaceOverrides">Override IP address space mappings</string>
      <string id="LocalNetworkAccessIpAddressSpaceOverrides_Explain">LocalNetworkAccessIpAddressSpaceOverrides

The policy overrides IP address mappings. Redefinition specifies which type of address space a particular IP address or address range belongs to, for more precise control of access to the local network.

The policy is set as a list, where the key is an IP address or a range of addresses, and the value is one of the supported address spaces.:

- "local" — local addresses;
- "public" — public addresses;
- "loopback" is a local host.

The key supports two formats:

- CIDR range (applies to all ports): 192.168.0.0/16=local.
- Specific IP address and port: 192.168.1.50:8080=public.

Common key format: 
[ip-address]:[port]=[public|local|loopback], where the part 
:[port] is optional. If no port is specified, the override is applied to all ports of the specified address or range.

IPv6 addresses must be specified in a URL-compatible format — in square brackets. Example: [2001:db8::1]=local.

The policy is available for Browsers version 26.6.4 and higher.

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled — redefinitions of address spaces are not set.
- Enabled — the administrator sets a list of redefinitions of IP address spaces.

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example of a value:

192.168.0.0/16=local
100.64.0.0/10=public</string>
      <string id="LocalNetworkAccessIpAddressSpaceOverridesDesc">Override IP address space mappings</string>
      <string id="LocalNetworkAccessPermissionsPolicyDefaultEnabled">Allow Local Area Network (LNA) access requests in subframes without explicit delegation</string>
      <string id="LocalNetworkAccessPermissionsPolicyDefaultEnabled_Explain">LocalNetworkAccessPermissionsPolicyDefaultEnabled

The policy controls the mechanism for inheriting local network access rights for subframes (iframes).

If no policy is set, the Browser requires the parent page to explicitly transfer rights to the subframe via the "Permissions-Policy" header. Without this, the subframe will not be able to initiate requests to the local network.

If the policy is enabled, the explicit delegation requirement is removed: by default, subframes inherit access rights to the local network from the parent (unless the parent explicitly forbade it). This makes it easier for legitimate widgets and iframes to work on the internal network.

The policy applies to the following "Permissions Polic" functions: "local-network-access", "local-network", "loopback-network".

To make the policy work, restart the Browser.

The Enabled mode allows scripts in embedded frames to access the local network without additional coordination, which reduces the level of security. For more information about the mechanism for delegating rights, see the documentation: https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Guides/Permissions_Policy .

The policy is available for Browsers version 26.6.4 and higher.

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled — default behavior.
- Enabled — subframes get the right to request access to the local network without having to register special "Permissions-Policy" headers on the parent's side.

The policy removes the ban at the frame level, but requesting permission from the user may be required according to other security settings.</string>
      <string id="LocalNetworkAllowedForUrls">Allow sites to make network requests to local network endpoints</string>
      <string id="LocalNetworkAllowedForUrls_Explain">LocalNetworkAllowedForUrls

The policy allows the specified sites to send network requests to the endpoints of the local network.

For sources not specified in the policy, the user settings are applied.

If a source is subject to multiple policies, priority is determined in the following order:
- LocalNetworkBlockedForUrls
- LocalNetworkAllowedForUrls
- LocalNetworkAccessBlockedForUrls
- LocalNetworkAccessAllowedForUrls

The policy is available for Browsers version 26.6.4 and higher.

Values

- Not configured, disabled — user settings are accepted.
- Enabled — the administrator sets a list of URLs.

You can use URL templates. Learn more about URL templates: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/policy/url-patterns.html

Convert URLs without Latin letters (for example, yandex.Russian Federation) via punycode: https://www.reg.ru/web-tools/punycode

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example of a value:

http://www.example.com:8080
[*.]example.edu</string>
