      <string id="LoopbackNetworkBlockedForUrlsDesc">Block sites from making network requests to the local device</string>
      <string id="CommandLineFlagSecurityWarningsEnabled">Enable warnings about dangerous command line parameters</string>
      <string id="CommandLineFlagSecurityWarningsEnabled_Explain">CommandLineFlagSecurityWarningsEnabled

The policy enables or disables warnings about the use of potentially dangerous command-line parameters at the Yandex Browser startup.

Features

- This is a basic security policy. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support2/browser-corporate/ru/deployment/windows/setting-policy#basic
- On Windows and macOS only works within the domain.

Values

- Not Configured, Enabled: Warnings are enabled.
- Disabled: Warnings are disabled. 

Safety recommendations

Value: Enabled. Enable warnings about dangerous command-line parameters. If users launch Yandex Browser with potentially dangerous parameters, they should see a warning about a possible security problem.</string>
      <string id="DNSInterceptionChecksEnabled">Enable DNS interception check</string>
      <string id="DNSInterceptionChecksEnabled_Explain">DNSInterceptionChecksEnabled

This policy enables or disables DNS interception checks. These checks determine if Yandex Browser uses a proxy server that redirects requests to unknown hosts.

If the DNS on the network is configured by the administrator, these checks may be unnecessary, since they create DNS and HTTP traffic at startup and each time the DNS settings are changed.

Features

- This is a basic security policy. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support2/browser-corporate/ru/deployment/windows/setting-policy#basic

Values

- Not Configured, Enabled: Checks are enabled.
- Disabled: Checks are disabled.

Safety recommendations

Value: Enabled. Disabling the checks may cause DNS requests to be intercepted. Always enable the checks if the network configuration is unknown.</string>
      <string id="DisableSafeBrowsingProceedAnyway">Prevent access from the Secure browsing warning page</string>
      <string id="DisableSafeBrowsingProceedAnyway_Explain">DisableSafeBrowsingProceedAnyway

The policy enables or disables the "Ignore warning" button on the warning page about a site threatening the computer's security. If the button is disabled, users can't go to the dangerous page.

When a user opens a page, Yandex Browser checks it against its database of malicious resources and blocks it in case of a match. At this point, the user will be shown a page with a warning that the site may threaten the security of the computer.

By default, users can ignore the warning by tapping the "Ignore warning" button at the bottom of the page. The policy controls the display of this button in the warning window.

Features

- This is a basic security policy. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support2/browser-corporate/ru/deployment/windows/setting-policy#basic
- Available in the mobile version of Yandex Browser for organizations. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: There is an "Ignore warning" button on the warning page.
- Enabled: There is no "Ignore warning" button on the warning page.

Safety recommendations

Value: Enabled. Disable the "Ignore warning" button. Users shouldn't go to pages with potentially malicious content.

Possible problems.	Some safe and important sites may be blocked.</string>
      <string id="DnsOverHttpsMode">Configure the DNS over HTTPS mode</string>
      <string id="DnsOverHttpsMode_Explain">DnsOverHttpsMode

The policy defines the default DNS converter mode over HTTPS for each request and restricts users from changing the settings in the "Secure connection" section.

The mode can be overridden for special types of requests, such as requests for hostname conversion for a server of the "DNS over HTTPS" type.

Features

- This is an increased security policy. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support2/browser-corporate/ru/deployment/windows/setting-policy#advanced

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: Yandex Browser can send requests over the "DNS over HTTPS" protocol to the converter, which is connected to the system converter configured by the user.
- Enabled: The administrator specifies the converter mode:
     - off: The "DNS over HTTPS" protocol is disabled;
     - automatic: The "DNS over HTTPS" protocol is used primarily to send requests (if a "DNS over HTTPS" server is available), but unsecured requests can be sent in case of an error.
     - secure: Requests are sent only via the "DNS over HTTPS" protocol and the conversion is not performed if errors occur. In this case, the DnsOverHttpsTemplates policy should be configured.

Example value: 

off

Safety recommendations

Value: Enabled → secure. 

Select secure mode to get the benefits of using the "DNS over HTTPS" protocol:

- DNS name encryption helps hide your online activities.
- The protocol helps prevent DNS spoofing and man-in-the-middle (MitM) attacks.

Possible problems. Not all providers support the "DNS over HTTPS" protocol. Organizations also sometimes monitor DNS requests to block access to malicious sites.

Sometimes DNS monitoring is used to detect malware that is trying to "call home". Since the "DNS over HTTPS" protocol encrypts name resolution requests, this can create a blind spot for security monitoring.</string>
      <string id="DnsOverHttpsMode_off">off</string>
      <string id="DnsOverHttpsMode_automatic">automatic</string>
      <string id="DnsOverHttpsMode_secure">secure</string>
      <string id="DnsOverHttpsTemplates">Set the URI template of the DNS converter over HTTPS</string>
      <string id="DnsOverHttpsTemplates_Explain">DnsOverHttpsTemplates

The policy sets the URI template of the DNS converter over HTTPS. Works in conjunction with the DnsOverHttpsMode policy. For example, if the DnsOverHttpsMode policy is set to "secure", the template can't be left empty.

If the URI template contains a "dns" variable, then the GET method will be used to send requests to the converter. Otherwise, the POST method will be used.

Templates with incorrect formatting are ignored.

Features

- This is an increased security policy. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support2/browser-corporate/ru/deployment/windows/setting-policy#advanced

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: Mappings specified directly in the program are used to try to update the current DNS converter to the DoH converter of the same provider.
- Enabled: The administrator sets the URI templates of the desired "DNS over HTTPS" converter separated by spaces.

Example value: 

https://dns.example.net/dns-query{?dns}

Safety recommendations

Value: Enabled → secure. 

In the DnsOverHttpsMode policy, select secure mode to get the benefits of using the "DNS over HTTPS" protocol:

- DNS name encryption helps hide your online activities.
- The protocol helps prevent DNS spoofing and man-in-the-middle (MitM) attacks.

Possible problems. Not all providers support the "DNS over HTTPS" protocol. Organizations also sometimes monitor DNS queries to block access to malicious sites.

Sometimes DNS monitoring is used to detect malware that is trying to "call home". Since the "DNS over HTTPS" protocol encrypts name resolution requests, this can create a blind spot for security monitoring.</string>
      <string id="EnableOnlineRevocationChecks">Enable OCSP and CRL online checks</string>
      <string id="EnableOnlineRevocationChecks_Explain">EnableOnlineRevocationChecks

The policy enables or disables OCSP and CRL online certificate checks.

Features

- This is a basic security policy. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support2/browser-corporate/ru/deployment/windows/setting-policy#basic

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: Checks are disabled.
- Enabled: Checks are enabled.

Safety recommendations

Value: Disabled. Disable these checks. They are already performed by the OS, regardless of Yandex Browser settings.

Attackers can block traffic over OCSP to provoke soft-fail behavior. This way, information about visited sites and request sources can also be transmitted to the certification centers.</string>
      <string id="GloballyScopeHTTPAuthCacheEnabled">Enable global cache usage on HTTP servers</string>
      <string id="GloballyScopeHTTPAuthCacheEnabled_Explain">GloballyScopeHTTPAuthCacheEnabled

The policy allows or restricts the use of cache from one HTTP server for authorization on other HTTP servers.

Global cache usage on HTTP servers:
- Makes sites more vulnerable to cross-site attacks.
- Makes it possible to track user transitions between sites without using cookies.
- Can lead to leakage of confidential information.

Features

- This is a basic security policy. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support2/browser-corporate/ru/deployment/windows/setting-policy#basic

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: Cache usage is restricted.
- Enabled: Cache usage is allowed.

Safety recommendations

Value: Disabled. Disable the policy to ensure connection security.</string>
      <string id="HttpsOnlyMode">Set up a warning about the absence of the HTTPS version of the site</string>
      <string id="HttpsOnlyMode_Explain">HttpsOnlyMode

The policy sets up a warning about the absence of the HTTPS version of the site.

In the computer version of the Browser, the policy controls the "Warn if a site should have an HTTPS version, but it doesn't" setting. To go to the settings, in the Browser, click "Main Menu" → "Settings" → "System" → "Network" and select it.

In the mobile version, the policy determines whether a warning will be displayed if the site does not support HTTPS.

The HttpsUpgradesEnabled policy takes precedence over the HttpsOnlyMode policy.

Features

- Can be configured as a recommendation page. Learn more: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/deployment/setting-policy.html#recommend-policy
- Available in the mobile version of the Browser for organizations. More details: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html

Values

- Not Configured — Users can enable or disable the setting.
- Disabled — Users can enable or disable the setting.
- Enabled — The administrator sets the mode:
    - "allowed" — users can enable or disable the setting.
    - "disallowed" — the setting is disabled, users cannot enable it. The browser does not show the warning.
    - "force_enabled" — the setting is enabled, users cannot disable it. The browser shows a warning.

Example of a value: 

force_enabled</string>
      <string id="HttpsOnlyMode_allowed">Allow users to enable or disable the setting</string>
      <string id="HttpsOnlyMode_disallowed">Disable the setting and prohibit users from enabling it</string>
      <string id="HttpsOnlyMode_force_enabled">Enable the setting and prohibit users from disabling it</string>
      <string id="HttpsOnlyMode_force_balanced_enabled">The mode does not work</string>
      <string id="HttpsUpgradesEnabled">Allow websites to be opened automatically over HTTPS</string>
      <string id="HttpsUpgradesEnabled_Explain">HttpsUpgradesEnabled

The policy allows websites to be opened automatically over HTTPS.

In the computer version of the Browser, the policy controls the setting "Automatically open sites over HTTPS if they support it". To go to the settings, in the Browser, click "Main Menu" → "Settings" → "System" → "Network" and select it.

In the mobile version, the policy allows you to automatically update the site protocol to HTTPS protocol.

Features

- Refers to the basic security level. Learn more: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/deployment/windows/setting-policy#basic
- Available in the mobile version of the Browser for organizations. More details: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html

Values

- Not Configured — the setting is enabled, users can disable it.
- Enabled — the setting is enabled, users cannot disable it.
- Disabled — the setting is disabled, users cannot enable it.

Safety recommendations

Value: Enabled. Enable the policy so that sites open automatically over HTTPS.</string>
      <string id="IntranetRedirectBehavior">Set up the redirection mode for internal resources</string>
      <string id="IntranetRedirectBehavior_Explain">IntranetRedirectBehavior

The policy sets up a redirection mode for internal resources. This policy enables or disables DNS interception checks and redirection messages to the internal resources. These checks determine if Yandex Browser uses a proxy server that redirects requests to unknown hosts.

The policy is related to the DNSInterceptionChecksEnabled policy. DNS interception checks are disabled if they are disabled in at least one of the policies.

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled — default behavior. DNS query interception checks is enabled. The message about redirection to internal resources is not displayed.
- Enabled — the administrator selects the redirection mode to the internal resources:
     - "Default behavior"— DNS query interception checks is enabled. The message about redirection to internal resources is not displayed.
     - "Сhecks and the message are disabled" — DNS query interception checks is disabled. The message about redirection to internal resources is not displayed.
     - "Сhecks is disabled, the message is enabled"— the DNS request interception is disabled. The message about redirection to internal resources is displayed.
     - "Сhecks and the message are enabled"— DNS query interception checks is enabled. The message about redirection to internal resources is displayed.</string>
      <string id="IntranetRedirectBehavior_Default">Default behavior</string>
      <string id="IntranetRedirectBehavior_DisableInterceptionChecksDisableInfobar">Checks and message are disabled</string>
      <string id="IntranetRedirectBehavior_DisableInterceptionChecksEnableInfobar">Сhecks is disabled, the message is enabled</string>
      <string id="IntranetRedirectBehavior_EnableInterceptionChecksEnableInfobar">Сhecks and the message are enabled</string>
      <string id="OverrideSecurityRestrictionsOnInsecureOrigin">Set a list of URL exceptions for TLS</string>
      <string id="OverrideSecurityRestrictionsOnInsecureOrigin_Explain">OverrideSecurityRestrictionsOnInsecureOrigin

The policy sets a list of URL exceptions for TLS. These URLs won't be marked as insecure in SmartBox.

For example, you can specify a source list of legacy applications that can't use TLS or set up an auxiliary server for internal web development and test features that require a secure context without deploying TLS.

The policy supersedes the unsafely-treat-insecure-origin-as-secure command line parameter with a comma-separated list of URLs and changes the UnsafelyTreatInsecureOriginAsSecure parameter.

Features

- This is a basic security policy. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/deployment/windows/setting-policy#basic

Values

- Not Configured: Default settings are used.
- Disabled: The value is treated as Not Configured.
- Enabled: The administrator sets a list of URL exceptions for TLS. You can use URL templates.

Learn more about the secure context: https://www.w3.org/TR/secure-contexts.

For more information about URL templates, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/policy/url-patterns.html

Convert non-Latin URLs (for example, яндекс.рф) via punycode: https://www.reg.ru/web-tools/punycode

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example of a value:

http://testserver.example.com/
*.example.org

Safety recommendations

Value: Disabled. Disable or don't set the OverrideSecurityRestrictionsOnInsecureOrigin policy. Users should always be informed about insecure URLs.</string>
      <string id="OverrideSecurityRestrictionsOnInsecureOriginDesc">Set exceptions for TLS</string>
      <string id="RemoteDebuggingAllowed">Allow remote debugging</string>
      <string id="RemoteDebuggingAllowed_Explain">RemoteDebuggingAllowed

The policy allows or prohibits remote debugging and automation of the Browser using a web driver (for example, YandexWebDriver or ChromeDriver).

For remote debugging, you need to specify the command-line switches "--remote-debugging-port" and "remote-debugging-pipe".

Values

- Not Configured, Enabled: Users can perform remote debugging using the web driver.
- Disabled: remote debugging of the Browser is prohibited.</string>
      <string id="RendererCodeIntegrityEnabled">Enable Renderer Code Integrity</string>
      <string id="RendererCodeIntegrityEnabled_Explain">RendererCodeIntegrityEnabled

The policy enables Renderer Code Integrity, which prevents loading unknown and potentially dangerous code when rendering pages.

After disabling the policy, it will be possible to load unknown and potentially malicious code. Disable it only if you have compatibility issues with third-party software that you want to run inside rendering processes. For more information, see https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/HEAD/docs/design/sandbox.md#Process-mitigation-policies

Features

- This is a basic security policy. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support2/browser-corporate/ru/deployment/windows/setting-policy#basic

Values

- Not Configured, Enabled: Renderer Code Integrity is enabled.
- Disabled: Renderer Code Integrity is disabled.

Safety recommendations

Value: Enabled. Disabling the policy carries the risk of loading potentially dangerous code. Disable it only if Renderer Code Integrity conflicts with software (for example, with an antivirus) during the rendering process.</string>
      <string id="RequireOnlineRevocationChecksForLocalAnchors">Check the server certificate</string>
      <string id="RequireOnlineRevocationChecksForLocalAnchors_Explain">RequireOnlineRevocationChecksForLocalAnchors

The policy configures server certificate verification. The certificate should be signed by the local certificate authority.

Features

- This is an increased security policy. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support2/browser-corporate/ru/deployment/windows/setting-policy#advanced

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: The check is not performed.
- Enabled: If Yandex Browser can't get information about the certificate, it will be considered revoked, and access to the server will be restricted.

Safety recommendations

Value: Enabled. Enable certificate verification. They should always be verified.

Possible problems. If the local certificate authority is not available, the pages whose certificates are signed by this center will no longer open.</string>
      <string id="SSLErrorOverrideAllowed">Allow access to sites with SSL errors</string>
      <string id="SSLErrorOverrideAllowed_Explain">SSLErrorOverrideAllowed

The policy allows or restricts skipping SSL error warnings.

Features

- This is an increased security policy. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support2/browser-corporate/ru/deployment/windows/setting-policy#advanced
- The mobile version only works on Android.
- Available in the mobile version of the Browser for organizations. More details: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html

Values

- Not Configured, Enabled: Users can skip warnings and go to sites with SSL errors.
- Disabled: Users can't skip warnings and go to sites with SSL errors.

Safety recommendations

Value: Disabled. Disable the option to skip warnings and go to sites with SSL errors. The security protocol should work correctly. Otherwise, users can visit sites with malicious content.

Possible problems. Sites with SSL errors will stop opening.</string>
      <string id="SafeBrowsingExtendedReportingEnabled">Configure the transfer of advanced reports for Secure viewing</string>
      <string id="SafeBrowsingExtendedReportingEnabled_Explain">SafeBrowsingExtendedReportingEnabled

The policy enables or disables the transmission of advanced Safe Browsing reports.

Safe Browsing is a Yandex Browser mode in which the sites you open are checked for malware.

Advanced reports include system information and page content so that Yandex can recognize dangerous applications and sites. 

You can enable or disable sending advanced reports in Yandex Browser settings: Main menu icon → Settings → Security → Threat security → Send Yandex information about suspicious files and sites.

Values

- Not Configured: Users choose in the settings whether to send reports or not.
- Enabled: Reports are sent, users can't disable this setting.
- Disabled: Reports aren't sent, users can't enable this setting.</string>
      <string id="SafeBrowsingProtectionLevel">Select Secure browsing protection mode</string>
      <string id="SafeBrowsingProtectionLevel_Explain">SafeBrowsingProtectionLevel

The policy manages the Safe Browsing mode in Yandex Browser.

Safe Browsing is a Yandex Browser mode in which the sites you open are checked for malware.

Features

- This is a basic security policy. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support2/browser-corporate/ru/deployment/windows/setting-policy#basic
- Can be configured as a recommendation. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/deployment/setting-policy.html#recommend-policy

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: Safe Browsing works in standard protection mode, users can change this setting.
- Enabled: The administrator selects the Safe Browsing protection mode, users can't change this setting.

Protection modes:

- Disabled (the parameter doesn't work).
- Standard protection.
- Improved protection (more Browser data is sent to Yandex).

Safety recommendations

Value: Enabled → Standard protection. Enable the "Standard protection" or "Improved protection" mode. Safe Browsing protects users from malicious and fraudulent sites or downloading dangerous files.</string>
      <string id="SafeBrowsingProtectionLevel_NoProtection">Disabled (the parameter doesn't work)</string>
      <string id="SafeBrowsingProtectionLevel_StandardProtection">Standard protection</string>
      <string id="SafeBrowsingProtectionLevel_EnhancedProtection">Improved protection (more Browser data is sent to Yandex)</string>
      <string id="CaptureProtection">Prohibit screen capture</string>
      <string id="CaptureProtection_Explain">CaptureProtection

The policy restricts capturing the screen in Yandex Browser windows.

Features

- Available in the mobile version of the Browser for organizations. More details: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html
- Works only in the extended version of Yandex Browser for organizations. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled — Users can take screenshots and record videos in Browser windows.
- Enabled — Users cannot take screenshots or record videos in Browser windows.</string>
      <string id="CaptureProtectionRestrictionsByUrl">Set a lists of URLs for which screen capture protection is enabled or disabled</string>
      <string id="CaptureProtectionRestrictionsByUrl_Explain">CaptureProtectionRestrictionsByUrl

The policy sets a lists of URLs for which screen capture protection is enabled or disabled in Browser windows.

Screen capture protection will be enabled not only on the site URL, but also on any frame with this URL.

The policy only works in conjunction with the CaptureProtection policy:
- if the CaptureProtection policy is enabled, then all URLs are protected from screen capture, except those specified in the CaptureProtectionRestrictionsByUrl policy in the block parameter.
- if the CaptureProtection policy is disabled, then the screen can be captured on all URLs, except those specified in the CaptureProtectionRestrictionsByUrl policy in the allow parameter.

Features

- It only works in the extended version of the Browser for organizations. Learn more: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: the CaptureProtection policy is used, if it is set.
- Enabled: the administrator sets the parameters:
     - allow: a list of URLs for which screen capture protection is enabled;
     - block: a list of URLs for which screen capture protection is disabled.
You can use URL templates. You can use the "internal_urls" keyword to designate all single-domain sites. For example, the rule will apply to "https://example" but not to "https://example.com".

For more information about URL templates, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/policy/url-patterns.html

Convert non-Latin URLs (for example, яндекс.рф) via punycode: https://www.reg.ru/web-tools/punycode

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example of a value:

{
  "allow": [
    "*",
    "en.example.org"
  ],
  "block": [
    "testserver.example.com",
    "[*.]example.org",
    "internal_urls"
  ]
}</string>
      <string id="Integrity">Check the integrity of Browser modules</string>
      <string id="Integrity_Explain">Integrity

The policy sets up a regular search for Browser modules and checks their integrity.

Features

- It works only on Windows and Linux.
- Works only in the extended version of the Browser for organizations. More details: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: integrity check is disabled.
- Enabled: Integrity check is enabled. If an integrity violation is detected, an Integrity security event is sent. All parameters are required:
     - enabled: the value is «true».
     - modules_collection_frequency: the period in seconds after which the module files are searched.
     - verification_frequency: the period in seconds after which signatures are verified.

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example of a value:

{
  "enabled": true,
  "modules_collection_frequency": 60,
  "verification_frequency": 600
}</string>
      <string id="ProtectedStorageHosts">Set a list of URLs for protected storage</string>
      <string id="ProtectedStorageHosts_Explain">ProtectedStorageHosts

The policy sets a list of URLs for protected storage. Downloaded files from these sites are stored on the user's device in encrypted form.

Files are decrypted only when used in the Browser. For example, when opening files of supported formats for viewing or editing, as well as when uploading to secure sites.

Features

- Available in the mobile version of the Browser for organizations. More details: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html
- Works only in the extended version of the Browser for organizations. More details: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: protected storage is disabled.
- Enabled: the administrator sets a list of URLs for the protected storage. You can use URL templates. The wildcard "*" is used only for subdomains in this form: "[*.]".

Learn more about URL templates: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/policy/url-patterns.html

Convert URLs without the Latin alphabet (for example, яндекс.рф) via punycode: https://www.reg.ru/web-tools/punycode

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example of a value:

support.company.ru
[*.]example.com</string>
      <string id="ProtectedStorageHostsDesc">Set a list of URLs for protected storage</string>
      <string id="Telemetry">Set the settings for collecting statistics</string>
      <string id="Telemetry_Explain">Telemetry

The policy sets the settings for collecting statistics and the interval at which the Browser will collect and send them.

If the Telemetry policy is enabled and the Telemetry security event is enabled, then Browser usage statistics will be collected and sent in it.

When the Browser is first launched, statistics are collected and transmitted with a delay of 10 minutes. Subsequent statistics are sent with a delay, which the administrator specified in the interval parameter.

Features

- It only works in the extended version of the Browser for organizations. Learn more: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: statistics collection and transmission are disabled.
- Enabled: the administrator sets the parameters for transmitting statistics:
- interval: the interval for transmitting statistics in seconds. If no parameter is specified, the report is sent once every 24 hours.
    - config: settings for data types. The administrator can enable or disable data transfer, as well as limit the amount of data transfer. Values:
        - common: common parameters.
            - max_reg_string_size : the maximum length of values in the registry.
            - max_reg_bin_size : the maximum size of binary data in the registry.
            - max_gzip_size : the maximum size of the archive with all the data.
            - parse_cmd_line : whether to pass the path to the file with the full file parameters (true/false).
            - version: the version.
        - browser_files: collecting and transferring Browser files with extensions .exe, .dll, .pak.
            - enable: enable or disable data transmission (true/false).
            - max_entries: the maximum number of values.
        - hosts: collection and transfer of host files.
            - enable: enable or disable data transmission (true/false).
            - max_file_size: the maximum file size.
        - links: collecting and transmitting links and URLs.
            - enable: enable or disable data transmission (true/false).
            - max_entries: the maximum number of values.            
            - max_contents_count: the maximum amount of content.
            - max_content_size: the maximum size of the content.
            - browser_lnk_masks: valid link masks.
        - reg_programs: collecting and transferring applications from the registry.
            - enable: enable or disable data transmission (true/false).
            - max_entries: the maximum number of values.
        - fs_programs: collecting and transferring installed applications from the file system.
            - enable: enable or disable data transmission (true/false).
            - max_entries: the maximum number of values.
        - network_settings: collecting and transmitting network settings.
            - enable: enable or disable data transmission (true/false).
            - max_entries: the maximum number of values.
        - registry_autorun: collecting and transferring applications for autorun from the registry.
            - enable: enable or disable data transmission (true/false).
            - max_entries: the maximum number of values.
        - registry_startup: collecting and transferring applications for autorun from the Startup directory.
            - enable: enable or disable data transmission (true/false).
            - max_entries: the maximum number of values.
        - tasks: collecting and transferring scheduled tasks from the Task Scheduler service.
            - enable: enable or disable data transmission (true/false).
            - max_entries: the maximum number of values.
            - extract_xml: extract xml files (true/false)
- network_filters: collecting and transmitting network filters from the register.
            - enable: enable or disable data transmission (true/false).
            - max_entries: the maximum number of values.
        - services: collecting and transferring drivers and services from the registry.
            - enable: enable or disable data transmission (true/false).
            - max_entries: the maximum number of values.
        - processes: collection and transfer of running processes.
            - enable: enable or disable data transmission (true/false).
            - max_entries: the maximum number of values.
            - max_cmd_line_size is the maximum line length that can be used in the command line.
            - use_wmi: use the WMI technology (true/false).
        - rootcerts: collection and transfer of root certificates.
            - enable: enable or disable data transmission (true/false).
            - max_entries: the maximum number of values.
        - auto_updates: collecting and transmitting Windows update settings.
            - enable: enable or disable data transmission (true/false).
            - max_entries: the maximum number of values.
        - enrolled_to_domain: collecting and transmitting information about whether a computer belongs to a domain.
            - enable: enable or disable data transmission (true/false).
        - winusers_count: collecting and transmitting information about the number of users in the system.
            - enable: enable or disable data transmission (true/false).
        - security_center: collecting and transmitting information about Browser security components.
            - enable: enable or disable data transmission (true/false).
            - max_entries: the maximum number of values.
        - os_info: collecting and transmitting information about the operating system.
            - enable: enable or disable data transmission (true/false).
        - installed_browsers: collecting and transmitting information about installed browsers.
            - enable: enable or disable data transmission (true/false).
        - net_adapters: collecting and transmitting information about network adapters from the registry.
            - enable: enable or disable data transmission (true/false).
            - max_entries: the maximum number of values.
        - file_features: collecting and transmitting information about file features.
            - enable: enable or disable data transmission (true/false).
            - max_file_size: the maximum file size.
            - max_catalogue_file_size: the maximum size of the directory file.
            - file_extract_flags: flag for notification of file extraction.
            - trusted_signers: a list of trusted signatories.
            - pe_extract_flags: flag for notification of the extraction of the PE file.
            - max_pe_entries: the maximum number of PE files.
            - max_pe_import_entries: the maximum number of incoming PE files.
            - max_pe_section_headers: the maximum number of section headers of PE files.
            - max_pe_debug_headers: the maximum number of debugging headers of PE files.
            - max_pe_imports: the maximum number of imported PE files.
            - pe_hash_import_size: the maximum size of the imported hash of PE files.
            - non_pe_dump_size: the size of the PE file without dump.
            - max_neighbor_entries: the maximum number of neighboring entries.
            - max_neighbors_nearby: the maximum number of nearby data points.
        - theme: collecting and transmitting information about the current Windows theme.
            - enable: enable or disable data transmission (true/false).

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example of a value:

{
  "interval": 60,
  "config": {
    "common": {
      "max_reg_string_size": 256,
      "max_reg_bin_size": 2048,
      "max_gzip_size": 1048576,
      "parse_cmd_line": true,
      "version": 0
    },
    "browser_files": {
      "enable": true,
      "max_entries": 100
    },
    "hosts": {
      "enable": true,
      "max_file_size": 2048
    },
    "links": {
      "enable": true,
      "max_entries": 200,
      "max_contents_count": 100,
      "max_content_size": 2048,
      "browser_lnk_masks": [
        "Yandex\\.lnk",
        "Yandex \\(\\d+\\)\\.lnk"
      ]
    },
    "reg_programs": {
      "enable": true,
      "max_entries": 500
    },
    "fs_programs": {
      "enable": true,
      "max_entries": 200
    },
    "network_settings": {
      "enable": true,
      "max_entries": 100
    },
    "registry_autorun": {
      "enable": true,
      "max_entries": 100
    },
    "registry_startup": {
      "enable": true,
      "max_entries": 100
    },
    "tasks": {
      "enable": true,
      "max_entries": 500,
      "extract_xml": false
    },
    "network_filters": {
      "enable": true,
      "max_entries": 100
    },
    "services": {
      "enable": true,
      "max_entries": 1000
    },
    "processes": {
      "enable": true,
      "max_entries": 1000,
      "max_cmd_line_size": 256,
      "use_wmi": true
    },
    "rootcerts": {
      "enable": true,
      "max_entries": 200
    },
    "auto_updates": {
      "enable": true,
      "max_entries": 200
    },
    "enrolled_to_domain": {
      "enable": true
    },
    "winusers_count": {
      "enable": true
    },
    "security_center": {
      "enable": true,
      "max_entries": 100
    },
    "os_info": {
      "enable": true
    },
    "installed_browsers": {
      "enable": true
    },
    "net_adapters": {
      "enable": true,
      "max_entries": 3
    },
    "file_features": {
      "enable": true,
      "max_file_size": 52428800,
      "max_catalogue_file_size": 10485760,
      "file_extract_flags": "ALL",
      "trusted_signers": [
        "Microsoft Corporation",
        "Microsoft Windows"
      ],
      "pe_extract_flags": "NONE",
      "max_pe_entries": 300,
      "max_pe_import_entries": 100,
      "max_pe_section_headers": 10,
      "max_pe_debug_headers": 10,
      "max_pe_imports": 1000,
      "pe_hash_import_size": 6,
      "non_pe_dump_size": 10,
      "max_neighbor_entries": 100,
      "max_neighbors_nearby": 5
    },
    "theme": {
      "enable": true
    }
  }
}</string>
      <string id="TelemetrySelective">Set the settings for collecting selective statistics</string>
      <string id="TelemetrySelective_Explain">TelemetrySelective

Set the settings for collecting sample statistics

The policy sets the settings for collecting sample statistics in JSON format compatible with osquery configurations.

If the TelemetrySelective policy is enabled and the TelemetrySelective security event is enabled, statistics will be collected and sent in it.

The policy supports:
- Direct scheduled requests ("schedule"). They are executed at a specified interval.
- Query groups ("pack"). They are executed under the conditions specified in the "discovery" requests.
- Filtering requests by platform.
- Setting execution intervals from 1 second to 1 week.

The policy is available for Browsers version 25.10.3 and higher.

Features

- Available in the mobile Browser version for organizations. Learn more: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html
- It only works in the extended version of the Browser for organizations. Learn more: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html

Policy format

The policy configuration is set in a JSON object consisting of three sections:

{
"options": { /* global settings */ },
  "schedule": { /* direct requests */ },
"packs": { /* request groups */ }
}

Configuration requirements:
- at least one of the "schedule" or "packs" sections must be specified;
- both sections can be set at the same time;
- an empty configuration "{}" disables the policy.

The "options" section

Contains global policy settings. Format:

"options": {
  "pack_refresh_interval": 3600
}

Where:

- pack_refresh_interval — the interval for checking discovery requests to activate the request group ("pack"). It is specified in seconds, the range is from 60 to 604800 (from 1 minute to 1 week). The default value is 3600 (1 hour).

The "schedule" section

Contains a dictionary of queries that are executed on a schedule. Format:

"schedule": {
"query_name": { // name of a specific query
"query": "SQL query",
"interval": number,
"platform": "platform" // optional
}
}

Where:

- query_name — the unique name of the query (within the "schedule" section). Required field. Contains a JSON object with request parameters.
- query — SQL query to execute. Required field.
- interval — the query execution interval in seconds. The range is from 1 to 604800 (1 week). Required field. Examples:
- platform — string, the target platform for execution. Optional field. It runs on all platforms by default. Possible values:
    - windows — Windows only;
    - darwin — macOS only;
    - linux — Linux only;
    - posix — Unix-like systems (Linux and macOS).


The "packs" section

It contains a group of logically related queries with the possibility of conditional activation via "discovery" queries.
A query group is enabled only if all of its "discovery" queries returned at least one row. If at least one "discovery" query returns an empty result, the entire "pack" is disabled and its queries are not executed.
Discovery requests are executed immediately when the policy is applied and are periodically repeated to verify the conditions.
Configuring the "packs" section allows you to activate statistics collection only when certain conditions are met (for example, the Browser is running,
the software is installed, and the file is present).

Format:

"packs": {
"pack_name": {
"platform": "platform", // optional
    "discovery": ["SQL query"], // optional
    "queries": {
"query_name": {
"query": "SQL query",
"interval": number,
        "platform": "platform" // optional
      }
    }
  }
}

Where:
- pack_name is the unique name of the query group (within the "packs" section). Required field. Contains a JSON object with query group parameters.
- platform — string, the target platform for executing a group of requests. Optional field. It runs on all platforms by default. Queries inherit the "platform" value from "pack", but it can be redefined in the "query_name" query itself. Possible values:
    - windows — Windows only;
    - darwin — macOS only;
    - linux — Linux only;
    - posix — Unix-like systems (Linux and macOS).
- discovery — SQL queries that act as a trigger for activating a query group (a specific "pack_name"). This "pack_name" is activated only if all "discovery" requests return at least one string. Optional field. It is checked periodically with the interval "pack_refresh_interval" from the "options" section (by default, 1 hour).
- queries — dictionary of queries in this `pack_name'. Required field.
- query_name — the unique name of the query (within the "packs" section). Required field. Contains a JSON object with request parameters. The format is described in the "schedule" section.


Values

- Not Configured, Disabled — statistics collection and transmission are disabled.
- Enabled — the administrator sets the parameters for transmitting statistics.

Example of a value:

{
  "options": {
    "pack_refresh_interval": 1800
  },
  "schedule": {
    "running_processes": {
      "query": "SELECT pid, name, path, cmdline FROM processes WHERE name LIKE '%browser%';",
      "interval": 3600
    },
    "installed_apps": {
      "query": "SELECT name, version FROM installed_applications WHERE name LIKE '%Yandex%';",
      "interval": 86400
    }
  },
  "packs": {
    "browser_monitoring": {
      "discovery": [
        "SELECT 1 FROM processes WHERE name IN ('chrome.exe', 'yandex_browser.exe', 'browser.exe');"
      ],
      "queries": {
        "browser_processes": {
          "query": "SELECT pid, parent, name, path, resident_size_bytes FROM processes WHERE name IN ('chrome.exe', 'yandex_browser.exe', 'browser.exe');",
          "interval": 300
        },
        "browser_memory": {
          "query": "SELECT name, resident_size_bytes, start_time FROM processes WHERE resident_size_bytes &gt; 100000000;",
          "interval": 600,
          "platform": "windows"
        }
      }
    },
    "applications_monitoring": {
      "platform": "windows",
      "queries": {
        "security_apps": {
          "query": "SELECT name, version FROM installed_applications WHERE name LIKE '%antivirus%' OR name LIKE '%security%';",
          "interval": 3600
        },
        "yandex_apps": {
          "query": "SELECT name, version FROM installed_applications WHERE name LIKE '%Yandex%';",
          "interval": 1800
        }
      }
    }
  }
}</string>
      <string id="UnknownRootCerts">Allow unknown root certificates with the given sha256-hashes</string>
      <string id="UnknownRootCerts_Explain">UnknownRootCerts
Allow unknown root certificates with the given sha256-hashess

Пример значения:

cert_sha256_1
cert_sha256_2
cert_sha256_3</string>
      <string id="UnknownRootCertsDesc">Allow unknown root certificates with the given sha256-hashes</string>
      <string id="YandexBrowserRestart">Set the Browser restart time when an update appears</string>
      <string id="YandexBrowserRestart_Explain">Yandex Browser Restart

The policy sets up the time interval before the Browser is restarted or the exact restart time when the update appears.

Features

- It works on Windows and macOS.
- It only works in the extended version of the Browser for organizations. Learn more: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: The browser does not restart automatically.
- Enabled: The browser automatically restarts at the set time. Parameters:
     - period: the period of time after which the Browser restarts after the update. It is set in hours, from 1 to 24.
     - time: the exact time of Browser restart in the "hh:mm" format.

Both parameters are optional, but at least one must be set. If both parameters are set, the value of the "period" parameter is used.

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example of the value:

{
  "period": 2,
  "time": "01:00"
}</string>
      <string id="YandexBrowserRules">Enable dynamic device verification</string>
      <string id="YandexBrowserRules_Explain">YandexBrowserRules

The policy enables dynamic device verification and sets a set of triggers and responses.

 If the YandexSecurityEventConnectorUrl policy is enabled and the YandexBrowserRulesReport security event is allowed, it will send information about the device and violations of access rules to websites during device verification.

Features

- Refers to the advanced security level. More details: https://yandex.ru/support2/browser-corporate/ru/deployment/windows/setting-policy#advanced
- Available in the mobile version of the Browser for organizations. More details: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html
- Works only in the advanced version of the Browser for organizations. More details: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html

Policy format

The administrator sets access rules for the specified URLs in JSON format with three dictionaries:
- conditions — conditions for granting access. Optional parameter;
- actions — actions when the access rules for the specified URLs are violated. Optional parameter;
- rules — rules for using the specified conditions for URLs. Required parameter.

Dictionary "conditions"

Contains the conditions for granting access.

Parameters:

- "/* custom condition name */" — custom condition name;
- {"type": "/* condition type */"} — condition types;
- update_period_sec — condition check interval in seconds. Optional parameter. The minimum value is 1 second. If the parameter is set for several types of conditions, then all access rules are checked, and not only the condition for which this parameter is configured. To start the checks, the minimum of the intervals specified in the policy is taken.
- contacts — the administrator's contacts that will be displayed to the user on the page if the URL access conditions are violated. An optional parameter.

For more information about the supported types of conditions for each OS: https://browser.yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/policy/yandex-browser-rules

 Example value:

"conditions": {
  "app_not_running": {
    "type": "processes",
    "required_processes": [
      "*app*"
    ],
    "update_period_sec": 10,
    "contacts": [
      "Иванов Иван Иванович",
      "Телефон: +7 999 999 99-99",
      "usermail@example.ru"
    ]
  }
}

Dictionary "actions"

Contains actions when the rules of access to the specified URLs are violated, for example, warning, blocking.

 Parameters:

- block - blocking the page. Values:
     - mode - mode of policy operation. Required parameter. Values:
          - silent — information about the device is collected;
          - weak — access rules for the specified URLs are checked. Access rules and URLs are specified in the rules dictionary. If the conditions are violated, access to the URL is restricted. You can repeat the check or continue working on the website;
          - strict — access rules for the specified URLs are checked. Access rules and URLs are specified in the rules dictionary. If the conditions are violated, access to the URL is blocked. You can only repeat the check;
     - type — the type of action. Has the value "block_page".
- clear — clearing all Browser data, such as passwords, cookies, cache, history. Values:
     - type — action type. Has the value "clear_browser_data".

Example value:

"actions": {
  "block": {
    "mode": "strict",
    "type": "block_page"
  },
  "clear": {
    "type": "clear_browser_data"
  }
}

Dictionary "rules"

Contains rules for using specified conditions for URL.

 It is set in the format "/* custom rule name */": {scope, conditions, actions}.

 Parameters:

- scope - URL or device parameters to which the rule is applied or not applied. Optional parameter. Values:
     - url_patterns - URL patterns. Parameters:
          - allow — a list of URLs for which the action specified in "actions" is applied if the URL does not match the conditions specified in "conditions";
          - deny — a list of URLs for which the action specified in "actions" is not applied if the URL does not match the conditions specified in "conditions".
- device_posture — the device parameters to which the rule applies.
- conditions — the conditions for granting access. You can use a list of condition names from the "conditions" dictionary or specify a condition directly within the rule in dictionary format.
- actions — actions when the rules for accessing the specified URLs are violated, such as blocking. You can use a list of condition names from the "actions" dictionary or set a condition directly inside the rule in dictionary format.

 Example value:

"rules": {
  "main_rule": {
    "actions": [
      "clear"
    ],
    "conditions": [
    "working_time"
    ],
    "scope": {
      "url_patterns": {
        "allow": [
          "example.com"
        ]
      }
    }
  }
}

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: device verification is disabled, and no access rules are set for the specified URLs.
- Enabled: device verification is enabled. The administrator sets access rules for the specified URLs. URL patterns can be used.

More information about URL patterns: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/policy/url-patterns.html

 Convert URLs without Latin characters (for example, yandex.rf) using punycode: https://www.reg.ru/web-tools/punycode

 You can configure it using a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

 Example value:

{
  "actions": {
    "block": {
      "mode": "strict",
      "type": "block_page"
    }
  },
  "conditions": {
    "app_not_running": {
      "blocking_processes": [
        "*app*"
      ],
      "type": "processes",
      "update_period_sec": 10
    }
  },
  "rules": {
    "main_rule": {
      "actions": [
        "block"
      ],
      "conditions": [
        "app_not_running"
      ],
      "scope": {
        "url_patterns": {
          "allow": [
            "example.com"
          ]
        }
      }
    }
  }
}

Security recommendations

Value: Enabled

"actions": {
  "block": {
    "type": "block_page",
    "mode": "strict"
  },
  "clear": {
    "type": "clear_browser_data"
  }
}

 Enable the policy to collect device information and check site access rules. Block URL access in "strict" mode or clear data.</string>
      <string id="YandexDLPDialogs">Configure messages for DLP events</string>
      <string id="YandexDLPDialogs_Explain">YandexDLPDialogs

The policy sets up custom messages for different types of DLP events.

The policy is available for Browsers version 25.8.1 and higher.

Features

- Available in the mobile version of the Browser for organizations. More details: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html
- It only works in the extended version of the Browser for organizations. Learn more: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled$: user messages are not configured. The default message from the Browser is used.
- Enabled: the administrator sets the parameters:
     - messages: a list of user messages.
          - dialog_types: a list of types of DLP events at which the message appears. Required field. Supported DLP events:
               - audio_video_capture_denied: prohibition of audio and video recording;
               - copy_denied: copy prohibition;
               - copy_denied_max_size_exceeded: maximum copy size;
               - drag_denied: prohibition of dragging;
               - drop_denied: prohibition of deletion;
               - paste_denied: forbidding insertion;
               - paste_denied_max_size_exceeded: maximum insertion size;
               - print_denied: print ban;
               - save_denied: forbidding file saving;
               - screenshoter_is_running — launching or detecting a program for taking screenshots;
               - screenshot_warning: taking a screenshot;
               - upload_denied: prohibits uploading files.
          - message: a custom message. An optional parameter. If the value is empty or unset, standard Browser messages are used.
              - title: the title of the message window. An optional parameter.
              - button: the text on the button in the window with the user message. An optional parameter. It is specified together with the "href".
              - href: URL for clicking the button. An optional parameter. It is specified together with the "button".

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example of a value:

{
  "messages": [
    {
      "dialog_types": [
        "drag_denied",
        "drop_denied",
        "copy_denied",
        "paste_denied"
      ],
      "message": "Операция с буфером обмена заблокирована политикой безопасности",
      "title": "Ограничение",
      "button": "Подробнее о копировании",
      "href": "https://example.local?q=Переход+после+клика",
      "display_time": 30
    },
    {
      "dialog_types": [
        "upload_denied",
        "save_denied"
      ],
      "message": "Действие заблокировано системой предотвращения утечки данных",
      "title": "Внимание!"
    },
    {
      "dialog_types": [
        "*"
      ],
      "message": "Действие заблокировано",
      "title": "Внимание!"
    }
  ]
}</string>
      <string id="YandexDisableSafeBrowsingLookup">Disable requests for checking suspicious links</string>
      <string id="YandexDisableSafeBrowsingLookup_Explain">YandexDisableSafeBrowsingLookup

The policy disables requests to check suspicious links.

The policy is available for Browsers version 23.3.1 and higher.

Features

- On Windows and macOS only works within the domain.

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: Requests are being sent.
- Enabled: Requests are not sent.</string>
      <string id="YandexExternalDLPConfig">Configure integration with an external DLP system</string>
      <string id="YandexExternalDLPConfig_Explain">YandexExternalDLPConfig

The policy sets the parameters for integration with an external DLP system. The browser sends the content of the actions for analysis:
- paste from clipboard (text, pictures, files);
- drag and drop of files, text, and other objects;
- opening files for download via the standard file dialog.

You can specify one or more URLs of the external DLP system.

In case of an error (for example, code 502 or 404):
- a DataLeakProtection security event is sent;
- if multiple URLs are specified, the request is sent to another URL.

During the specified time, the Browser waits for a response from the external DLP system, after which it performs or blocks the action. If no response is received, the action is blocked.

Features

- Available in the mobile Browser version for organizations. Learn more: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html
- It only works in the extended version of the Browser for organizations. Learn more: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: integration is not configured.
- Enabled: the administrator adjusts the integration parameters. The list of parameters is:
    - endpoint/endpoints — the URL of the external DLP system/the list of URLs of the external DLP system. One of the options must be used. Required parameter.
    - websocket_port — the number of the WebSocket port for establishing a WS connection. An optional parameter.
    - token — a token for Browser authorization in the DLP system. Required parameter.
    - bypass_ssl_errors — whether to ignore non-critical errors with certificates. Critical errors are not ignored (for example, HSTS is enabled). With any value, a Data Leak Protection security event is sent. Optional parameter.
        - true — ignore;
        - false — do not ignore (by default).
    - timeout — the time in seconds during which the Browser sends requests to the DLP system. Optional parameter. The default value is 60.

The administrator can additionally configure the verification of various types of data transmission channels.
  List of parameters:
    - sources — type of data or data actions for the templates specified in `enable` and `disable'.
        - Text — any text (pasted from the clipboard or moved to web forms using Drag-and-drop), while only pasting is prohibited, copying from the page is allowed.;
        - File — any files to be uploaded (specified via the "Select File" form or using Drag-and-drop);
        - Print — print a web page.
        - PageContent — sending the contents of tabs to an external DLP system on initial load and on every change:
             - text_format — the format of the sent contents:
                  - text — send the page innerText (default);
                  - html — send the page with tags/hypertext, but without the &lt;script&gt; tag.
             - minimum_data_size — the minimum page data size in bytes at which the contents of tabs are sent to the DLP system.
    - enable — a list of URL templates for which you need to do DLP verification of the data or actions specified in sources.
    - disable — a list of URL templates for which you do not need to do DLP verification of the data or actions specified in sources. You can use the "internal_urls" keyword to designate all single-domain sites. For example, the rule will apply to "https://example" but not to "https://example.com".
    - block_large_files — whether to block files exceeding the specified size:
        - true — block (default);
        - false — do not block.
    - max_file_size_kb — the maximum file size in kilobytes, if exceeded, it will not be sent to the DLP system. In this case, the block_large_files parameter is responsible for blocking the file. Default: 0 (unlimited size).
    - ignore_block_large_files — a list of URL templates for which the maximum file size is unlimited.
    - allow_if_endpoints_unavailable — action when all DLP servers are unavailable:
        - true - allow file operations;
        - false — block operations with files (by default).
    - block_until_verdict — verdict of the DLP system
        - true — expect;
        - false — do not expect.
    - ignore_block_until_verdict — a list of URL templates for which you do not need to expect the verdict of the DLP system.
    - block_password_protected — whether to block an encrypted archive:
        - true — block, do not send to the DLP system (by default);
        - false — send the encrypted archive to the DLP system and use its verdict.
    - custom_messages — configure messages displayed during DLP events.
        - event_type — the type of DLP event at which the message appears. Required field. Supported types:
           - file_too_large — exceeding the maximum file size;
           - cert_error — certificate error;
           - network_error — network error;
           - clipboard_paste_access_denied — prohibits pasting from the clipboard;
           - drag_and_drop_denied — prohibits dragging data using drag-and-drop;
           - file_picker_dialog_denied — forbidding the file selection dialog;
           - print_preview_print_denied — prohibiting the print dialog in the Browser;
           - system_dialog_print_denied — disallowing the system print dialog.
        - message — a custom message. Required field.
        - learn_more_url — the address of the page with additional information for the user. Optional field.

The block_until_verdict parameter is optional and enabled by default. If this parameter is not specified, the browser is waiting for a response from the DLP system.

The block_large_files and max_file_size_kb parameters are optional and apply only to File type actions.

If the data_sources section is missing, DLP checks the data for all URLs, and a DLP system verdict is always expected to continue the operation. 
  
You cannot specify multiple rules for the same sources in the data_sources section.

You can use URL templates. For more information: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/policy/url-patterns.html

Convert non-Latin URLs (for example, яндекс.рф) via punycode: https://www.reg.ru/web-tools/punycode

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example of a value for a single URL:

{
  "infowatch": {
    "endpoint": "https://iw.localdomain/xapi",
    "token": "sometokenstring",
    "bypass_ssl_errors": true,
    "timeout": 30,
    "data_sources": [
      {
        "sources": [
          "File",
          "Text"
        ],
        "enable": [
          ".mail.example.com",
          "paste.example.com"
        ],
        "block_large_files": true,
        "max_file_size_kb": 5000,
        "allow_if_endpoints_unavailable": false,
        "block_until_verdict": true,
        "custom_messages": [
          {
            "message": "Ошибка сети",
            "event_type": "network_error",
            "learn_more_url": "https://example.com"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "sources": [
          "Print"
        ],
        "enable": [
          "*"
        ],
        "disable": [
          "http://*"
        ],
        "block_until_verdict": false
      },
      {
        "sources": [
          "PageContent"
        ],
        "enable": [
          "*"
        ],
        "disable": [
          "http://*"
        ],
        "text_format": "text",
        "minimum_data_size": 1024
      }
    ]
  }
}

Example of a value for a list of URLs:

{
  "infowatch": {
    "endpoints": [
      "https://10.1.35.101/xapi/",
      "https://10.1.35.102:9106/xapi/"
    ],
    "token": "sometokenstring",
    "timeout": 30,
    "data_sources": [
      {
        "sources": [
          "File",
          "Text"
        ],
        "enable": [
          ".mail.example.com",
          "paste.example.com"
        ],
        "block_large_files": true,
        "max_file_size_kb": 5000,
        "allow_if_endpoints_unavailable": false,
        "block_until_verdict": true,
        "custom_messages": [
          {
            "message": "Ошибка сети",
            "event_type": "network_error",
            "learn_more_url": "https://example.com"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "sources": [
          "Print"
        ],
        "enable": [
          "*"
        ],
        "disable": [
          "http://*"
        ],
        "block_until_verdict": false
      },
      {
        "sources": [
          "PageContent"
        ],
        "enable": [
          "*"
        ],
        "disable": [
          "http://*"
        ],
        "text_format": "text",
        "minimum_data_size": 1024
      }
    ]
  }
}</string>
      <string id="YandexIpReputation">Enable IP address verification</string>
      <string id="YandexIpReputation_Explain">YandexIpReputation
При включении политики браузер проверяет репутацию IP-адресов посещаемых
ресурсов по базе Safe Browsing.

Чтобы включить проверку, задайте поле enabled со значением true. Если политика
не задана или enabled имеет значение false, проверка репутации IP-адресов не
выполняется.

В поле categories можно задать действие для каждой категории угроз: allow —
разрешить переход, block — заблокировать переход, warn — показать
предупреждение с возможностью продолжить. Если для категории действие не
задано, переход блокируется (block). Если вердикт Safe Browsing относится к
нескольким категориям, применяется самое строгое из назначенных им действий.

Значение политики считывается при запуске браузера, поэтому изменения
вступают в силу только после его перезапуска.
Чтобы узнать больше о наборе атрибутов и форматировании, перейдите по ссылке https://chromeenterprise.google/policies/?policy=YandexIpReputation.


Пример значения:

{
  "enabled": true,
  "categories": {
    "c2": "block",
    "malware": "block",
    "phishing": "warn"
  }
}</string>
      <string id="YandexLockBrowserByPin">Configure Browser lock</string>
      <string id="YandexLockBrowserByPin_Explain">YandexLockBrowserByPin

The policy includes Yandex Browser protection by password. The password is invented by the user himself when the Browser is launched for the first time with the policy activated.

The policy manages the "Additional Security" section with settings:

- "Enable password lock";
- "Change login password";
- "Disable password lock";
- "Block automatically after".

To proceed with the configuration, in Yandex Browser, click "Main Menu" → "Settings" → "Security" tab → "Advanced Security" section and select it.

 The password is set as an alphanumeric combination. On mobile devices, biometric login to Yandex Browser is supported.

 A password is required if:
- the user launches the Browser for the first time during a working session;
- the user closes the Browser manually or by force stop method and then reopens it;
- the automatic lock time set in the settings has expired;
- the user returned to the Browser after it was minimized, and the automatic lock was triggered.

 The policy is available for Browsers version 24.7.6 and higher.

Features

- Refers to the advanced security level. More details: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/deployment/windows/setting-policy.html#advanced
- Available in the mobile version of the Browser for organizations. More details: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/mobile.html
- Only works in the advanced version of the Browser for organizations. More information: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/paid.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: no password is required to log in to the Browser. Users manage the settings.
- Enabled: the administrator sets the parameters:
    - required — requires a password to log in to the Browser, a mandatory setting:
        - true:
            - A password is required. After three consecutive failed attempts, the password is locked for 30 seconds.
            - The browser is automatically locked after the specified time in the settings. The lock time is counted from the last user activity.
            - The settings are enabled and users can manage them.
            - Users cannot disable the password.
        - false:
            - A password is not required.
            - The settings are disabled and users cannot manage them.
    - autolock_interval_sec is the time in seconds for auto-locking. Users do not manage the "Lock automatically after" setting. When the value is "0", auto-locking is disabled.
    - min_pin_length — the minimum length of the password. The range of values is from "1" to "32".
    - learn_more_text — an arbitrary hint text.
    - pin_history_count — how many previous PIN codes are not allowed to be reused.

 You can configure it through the file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example of value:

{
  "required": true,
  "autolock_interval_sec": 30,
"min_pin_length": 6,
"learn_more_text": "enter password",
  "pin_history_count": 6
}

Safety recommendations

Value: Enabled

{
  "required": true,
  "autolock_interval_sec": 30,
  "min_pin_length": 6,
  "learn_more_text": "enter your password",
  "pin_history_count": 6
}

Enable the policy to protect your Browser data from unauthorized access.</string>
      <string id="YandexPhishingProtection">Set up anti-phishing credit cards</string>
      <string id="YandexPhishingProtection_Explain">YandexPhishingProtection

The policy controls the "Phishing protection for banks cards" setting. To proceed to the setting, click «Security» in the Browser settings and select it.

The policy is available for Browsers version 23.1.2 and higher.

Values

- Not Configured — anti-phishing of bank cards is enabled, users can disable it.
- Enabled — anti-phishing of bank cards is enabled, users cannot disable it.
- Disabled — anti-phishing of bank cards is disabled, users cannot enable it.</string>
      <string id="YandexProtectedMode">Set up opening pages of online banks and payment systems in Protected mode</string>
      <string id="YandexProtectedMode_Explain">YandexProtectedMode

The policy sets up the opening of online banking and payment system pages in secure mode.

The policy controls the "Open online banking and payment system sites in Protected mode" setting. To go to the settings, click on "Security" in the Browser settings and select it.

Values

- Not Configured — the pages of online banks and payment systems open in secure mode, users can disable the setting.
- Enabled — the pages of online banks and payment systems open in secure mode, users cannot disable the setting.
- Disabled — the pages of online banks and payment systems open normally, users cannot enable the setting.

Security recommendations

Value: Enabled. Enable the policy to protect against untrusted extensions by restricting their access to the site's execution context.</string>
      <string id="YandexProtectedModeAllowList">Enable protected mode on URLs from the list</string>
      <string id="YandexProtectedModeAllowList_Explain">YandexProtectedModeAllowList

The policy sets a list of URLs where Protected mode is force enabled.

If a domain is specified in the list, Protected mode also applies to all subdomains. For example, if "example.com" is specified in the list, the policy also applies to "sub.example.com". If a specific subdomain is specified in the list, the policy will only apply to it. Other subdomains and the top-level domain won't be affected. For example, if "sub.example.net" is set, the policy doesn't apply to "under.example.net" and "example.net".

The policy supersedes YandexProtectedModeDenyList. 

Features

- Works only in the extended version of Yandex Browser for organizations. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: Only online banking and payment system pages open in Protected mode.
- Enabled: The administrator uses a semicolon to list URLs including the scheme, such as https://. Invalid URLs are ignored. Protected mode doesn't turn on if the option "Open online banking and payment system sites in Protected mode" is disabled in Yandex Browser settings.

Convert non-Latin URLs (for example, яндекс.рф) via punycode: https://www.reg.ru/web-tools/punycode

Example value: 

http://example.org;https://example.net

Security Recommendations

Value: Enabled

http://example.org;https://example.net

Set a list of URLs that enable secure mode to protect against untrusted extensions.</string>
      <string id="YandexProtectedModeDenyList">Disable protected mode on URLs from the list</string>
      <string id="YandexProtectedModeDenyList_Explain">YandexProtectedModeDenyList

The policy sets a list of URLs where Protected mode is force disabled.

If a domain is specified in the list, Protected mode is also disabled for all subdomains. For example, if "example.com" is specified in the list, the policy also applies to "sub.example.com". If a specific subdomain is specified in the list, the policy will only apply to it. Other subdomains and the top-level domain won't be affected. For example, if "sub.example.net" is set, the policy doesn't apply to "under.example.net" and "example.net".

The YandexProtectedModeAllowList policy supersedes YandexProtectedModeDenyList.

Features

- Works only in the extended version of Yandex Browser for organizations. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: Only online banking and payment system pages open in Protected mode.
- Enabled: The administrator uses a semicolon to list URLs including the scheme, such as https://. Invalid URLs are ignored.

Convert non-Latin URLs (for example, яндекс.рф) via punycode: https://www.reg.ru/web-tools/punycode

Example value: http://example.org;https://example.net

Security recommendations

Value: Disabled. Disable the policy to protect against untrusted extensions by restricting their access to the site's execution context.</string>
      <string id="YandexRemoteBrowserIsolation">Configure Remote Browser Isolation (RBI)</string>
      <string id="YandexRemoteBrowserIsolation_Explain">YandexRemoteBrowserIsolation

The policy sets the configuration of the remote isolation server and the list of sites that need to be opened in the remote isolation mode of the Browser.

Remote Browser Isolation (RBI) prevents Internet traffic from entering the user's system. In remote isolation mode, filtering, threat analysis, and sandbox startup are performed on a specified server. The user's device does not participate in online activity: the session takes place on a remote server and is broadcast from there in real time, simulating local viewing.

Features

- Works only in the extended version of the Browser for organizations. More details: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html

Values:

- Not Configured, Disabled: Remote Browser isolation is disabled.
- Enabled: Remote Browser isolation is enabled. The administrator sets the following values:
     - host_url: the address of the RBI server;
     - allow: a list of URL templates that are opened in remote isolation mode (on the RBI server). You can use the wildcard "*" to open all sites in RBI mode, except for internal pages and sites from the block list.;
     - block: a list of URL templates that open normally (in the local Browser);
    - open_when_incognito: whether all sites are opened in remote isolation mode when the Browser is in Incognito mode. Values:
        - true: n RBI mode, all sites are opened except for sites from the block list, and values from the allow list are ignored;
        - false: in RBI mode, only sites from the allow list are opened.
    - auto_redirect_interstitial — open error description pages in RBI mode (true/false).

Example of a value:

{
  "host_url": "https://rbi.ya.ru/corp/rbi/?rbi_url=$Url",
  "allow": [
    "topleveldomain.ru",
    "*.partial.com/register"
  ],
  "block": [
    "norbi.partial.com/register"
  ],
  "open_when_incognito": true,
  "auto_redirect_interstitial": true 
}</string>
      <string id="YandexSecurityEventAllowlist">Set a list of events that are allowed to be exported</string>
      <string id="YandexSecurityEventAllowlist_Explain">YandexSecurityEventAllowlist

The policy specifies a list of security events that are allowed to be exported to an external system. Other events are not exported.

To view the event name, monitoring status, filter string and the current status of each event, open the page in the Browser browser://corp-secevents

Only one policy can be set at a time: YandexSecurityEventAllowlist or YandexSecurityEventBlocklist. If
both are set, they don't work.

Features

- Available in the mobile version of the Browser for organizations. More details: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html
- Works only in the extended version of the Browser for organizations. More details: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: all events are exported if the YandexSecurityEventBlocklist policy is not set.
- Enabled: the administrator sets the list of events separated by commas.

Example value: ClipboardRestrictionViolation,PrintingDisabled</string>
      <string id="YandexSecurityEventBlocklist">Set a list of events that can't be exported</string>
      <string id="YandexSecurityEventBlocklist_Explain">YandexSecurityEventBlocklist

The policy sets a list of security events that are prohibited from being exported to an external system. The rest of the events are exported.

To view the event name, monitoring status, filter string and the current status of each event, open the page in the Browser browser://corp-secevents

Only one policy can be set at a time: YandexSecurityEventAllowlist or YandexSecurityEventBlocklist. If
both are set, they don't work.

Features

- Available in the mobile version of the Browser for organizations. More details: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html
- Works only in the extended version of the Browser for organizations. More details: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: all events are exported if the YandexSecurityEventAllowlist policy is not set.
- Enabled: the administrator sets the list of events separated by commas.

Example value: ClipboardRestrictionViolation,PrintingDisabled</string>
      <string id="YandexSecurityEventConnectorUrl">Set a URL for exporting security events</string>
      <string id="YandexSecurityEventConnectorUrl_Explain">YandexSecurityEventConnectorUrl

The policy sets the URL for exporting security events from Yandex Browser to an external SIEM system. If the URL is empty, the policy doesn't work. 

The YandexSecurityEventConnectors policy takes precedence over the YandexSecurityEventConnectorUrl policy.

Export features:
- You can specify an IPv4/IPv6 address and port, as well as an http or https scheme.
- TLS/mTLS connection is supported.
- You can add a client certificate by specifying it in the AutoSelectCertificateForUrls policy filters.
- Events are exported each time the site is opened and at any transition on the site.
- If the server is unavailable, Yandex Browser repeats sending, each time increasing the interval between attempts.
- When the server becomes available, unsent events will be sent on the next attempt.
- If Yandex Browser was closed, unsent events will be sent upon Yandex Browser launch.
- If there are more than 11,000 unsent requests, the first 1000 of them are deleted.

Features

- Available in the mobile version of the Browser for organizations. More details: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html
- Works only in the extended version of Yandex Browser for organizations. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: Security events are not exported.
- Enabled: The administrator sets the URL for exporting security events.

Convert non-Latin URLs (for example, яндекс.рф) via punycode: https://www.reg.ru/web-tools/punycode

Example value: https://example.com/event-collector</string>
      <string id="YandexSecurityEventConnectors">Set a list of URLs for exporting security events</string>
      <string id="YandexSecurityEventConnectors_Explain">YandexSecurityEventConnectors

The policy sets a list of URLs for exporting security events from the Browser to an external SIEM system.

The policy takes precedence over the YandexSecurityEventConnectorUrl policy.

Export Features:
- you can specify an IPv4/IPv6 address and port, as well as an http or https scheme;
- TLS/mTLS connection is supported;
- you can add a client certificate by specifying it in the AutoSelectCertificateForUrls policy filters;
- events are exported every time the site is opened and any click is made on the site;
- if the server is unavailable, the Browser repeats sending, increasing the interval between attempts each time;
- when the server becomes available, unsent events will be sent on the next attempt;
- if the Browser was closed, unsent events will be sent after the Browser is started;
- if there are more than 11,000 unsent requests, the first 1,000 of them are deleted.

Features

- Available in the mobile Browser version for organizations. Learn more: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html
- It only works in the extended version of the Browser for organizations. Learn more: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: security events are not exported.
- Enabled: the administrator sets an array consisting of dictionaries of URLs for exporting security events:
    - connectors — an array of URLs.
        - url — The URL for exporting security events. 

Convert URLs without Latin letters (for example, яндекс.рф) via punycode: https://www.reg.ru/web-tools/punycode


Example of the value:

"YandexSecurityEventConnectors": {
  "connectors": [
    {
      "url": "https://example.com"
    },
    {
      "url": "https://example2.com"
    }
  ]
}</string>
      <string id="YandexSecurityEventStorageLimits">Set storage size for security events</string>
      <string id="YandexSecurityEventStorageLimits_Explain">YandexSecurityEventStorageLimits

The policy sets the storage size and cleanup period for security event records if there is no connection to the SIEM system.

Features

- The mobile version only works on iOS.
- Available in the mobile Browser version for organizations. Learn more: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html
- It only works in the extended version of the Browser for organizations. Learn more: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled — the default size of 5000 records is used. If the maximum size is exceeded, the 100 oldest records will be deleted. The storage will be cleaned every 30 days.
- Enabled — the administrator sets the storage settings in JSON format through the parameters:
     - max_event_count — the maximum number of records in the storage. Maximum: 50,000, default: 5,000.
     - excess_max_count_by — the number of records above the maximum, upon reaching which the excess_max_count_by of the oldest records will be deleted. Maximum: 1000, default: 100.
     - vacuum_db_period_days — the period of cleaning the security event repository, in days. Maximum: 365, by default: 30. A value of 0 disables cleaning.

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example of a value:

{
  "max_event_count": 50000,
  "excess_max_count_by": 1000,
  "vacuum_db_period_days": 30
}</string>
      <string id="YandexUserActivityEventReporter">Configure sending events based on activity in Yandex Browser</string>
      <string id="YandexUserActivityEventReporter_Explain">YandexUserActivityEventReporter

The policy sets up sending events based on activity in Yandex Browser via POST requests. Activity refers to mouse movements or clicks, keyboard events, etc.

Features

- Works only in the extended version of Yandex Browser for organizations. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: Browser activity events are not sent.
- Enabled: The administrator configures the parameters for sending events based on activity in Browser. List of parameters:
     - connector_url: URL for sending events. Required parameter.
     - max_event_count: The maximum number of POST requests in the queue in case of problems with sending. The range of values is from 1 to 1440. The default is 180.
     - collecting_interval: The time in seconds for which the activity is counted. The range of values is from 1 to 3600. The default is 1.
     - sending_interval: The interval in seconds between sending POST requests. The range of values is from 60 to 10,800. The default is 60.

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example value:

{
  "connector_url": "https://example.com/user-activity-collector",
  "max_event_count": 180,
  "collecting_interval": 1,
  "sending_interval": 60
}</string>
      <string id="YandexSearchOnPageReporting">Set URL lists for sending security events during searching on a page</string>
      <string id="YandexSearchOnPageReporting_Explain">YandexSearchOnPageReporting

The policy sets URL lists for sending security events during searching on a page.

The SearchOnPage event is sent when searching on the page using one of the following methods:

- in the page menu using the "Find on page" option;
- in the context menu using the "Search by page" option;
- using the keyboard shortcuts Ctrl + F (on Windows and Linux) and ⌘ + S (on macOS);
- using the F3 hotkey.

The policy is available for Browsers version 26.3.1 and higher.

Features

- It only works in the extended version of the Browser for organizations. Learn more: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled — the security event is not sent.
- Enabled — the administrator sets lists of URLs:
     - allow — URLs for which the security event is enabled;
     - deny — URLs for which the security event is disabled.

You can use the "internal_urls" keyword to designate all single-domain sites. For example, the rule will apply to "https://example" but not to "https://example.com".

You can use URL templates. Learn more about URL templates: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/policy/url-patterns.html

Convert URLs without Latin letters (for example, яндекс.рф) via punycode: https://www.reg.ru/web-tools/punycode

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example of a value:

{
  "allow": [
    "[*.]yandex.ru"
  ],
  "deny": [
    "[*.]passwords.example.com"
  ]
}</string>
      <string id="Smartbox_group">SmartBox</string>
      <string id="YandexSummarizationDisable">Disable the summarize button in the SmartBox and page menu</string>
      <string id="YandexSummarizationDisable_Explain">YandexSummarizationDisable

The policy disables the Summarize button in the SmartBar and the page menu.

The policy is available for Browsers version 23.9.1 and higher.

Features

- Available in the mobile version of the Browser for organizations. More details: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: the button is displayed.
- Enabled: the button is not displayed, users can't enable it.</string>
      <string id="SearchSuggestEnabled">Enable search suggestions</string>
      <string id="SearchSuggestEnabled_Explain">SearchSuggestEnabled

The policy controls the "Show suggestions while entering addresses and queries" setting and prevents users from changing this parameter. The policy doesn't affect the display of bookmarks and sites from history in the SmartBox.

Features

- This is an increased security policy. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support2/browser-corporate/ru/deployment/windows/setting-policy#advanced
- Can be configured as a recommendation. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/deployment/setting-policy.html#recommend-policy

Values

- Not Configured: Suggestions are enabled, users can disable them.
- Enabled: Suggestions are enabled, users can't disable them.
- Disabled: Suggestions are disabled, users can't enable them.

Safety recommendations

Value: Disabled. If the user enters confidential information in the SmartBox and search suggestions are enabled, a leak may occur. If security requirements are high, it's better to disable search suggestions.</string>
      <string id="YandexButtonDisable">Configure the Yandex button in the SmartBox</string>
      <string id="YandexButtonDisable_Explain">YandexButtonDisable

The policy configures the Yandex button in the SmartBox.

Features

- On Windows and macOS only works within the domain.

Values

- Not Configured: The button is displayed. Users can hide it.
- Enabled: The button is not displayed. Users can't enable it.
- Disabled: The button is displayed. Users can't hide it.</string>
      <string id="YandexCopyShareButton">Set up the "Copy" button in the SmartBox</string>
      <string id="YandexCopyShareButton_Explain">YandexCopyShareButton

The policy enables or disables the display of the "Copy" button in the SmartBox.

 The policy controls the "Suggest copying the page address when it's selected" setting. To access the setting, click on the "Main Menu" → "Settings" → "Interface" section → "SmartBox" and select it.

The policy is available for browsers version 23.1.2 and above.

Values

- Not Configured: The "Copy" button in the Smart Bar is enabled. Users control the setting.
- Enabled: The "Copy" button in the Smart Bar is enabled. The setting is enabled, and users cannot disable it.
- Disabled: The "Copy" button in the Smart Bar is disabled. The setting is disabled, and users cannot enable it.</string>
      <string id="YandexDomainTitleClickOpensHomePage">Open the main page of the site by clicking on its domain in the Smart line</string>
      <string id="YandexDomainTitleClickOpensHomePage_Explain">YandexDomainTitleClickOpensHomePage

The policy allows or disallows opening the website's main page by clicking on its domain in the Smart Bar.

The policy controls the "Open a site's main page by clicking on its domain in the SmartBox" setting. To go to the setting, in the Browser click  "Main Menu" → "Settings" → "Interface" → "SmartBox" and select it.

The policy is available for Browsers version 23.1.2 and higher.

Values

- Not Configured: The site's main page opens when you click on its domain, users can manage the setting.
- Enabled: The site's main page opens when you click on its domain, and the setting is enabled, users cannot disable it.
- Disabled: The site's main page does not open when you click on its domain, and the setting is disabled, users cannot enable it.</string>
      <string id="YandexDomainTitleFormat">Set the page address format in the SmartBox</string>
      <string id="YandexDomainTitleFormat_Explain">YandexDomainTitleFormat

The policy sets the format of the page address in the SmartBox as "domain &gt; title" or as a URL.

The policy controls the "Display page adresses in the "domain &gt; title format" setting. To go to the setting, in the Browser click  "Main Menu" → "Settings" → "Interface" → "SmartBox" and select it.

The policy is available for Browsers version 23.1.2 and higher.

Values

- Not Configured: The page address in the SmartBox is displayed as "domain → header". For example "example.com Example page 123". Users manage the settings.
- Enabled: The page address in the SmartBox is displayed as "domain → header". For example, "example.com Example page 123". The setting is enabled, users cannot disable it.
- Disabled: The page address in the SmartBox is displayed as a URL. For example, "https://sample.com/example/p?=123". The setting is disabled, users cannot enable it.</string>
      <string id="YandexPowerSavingModeIcon">Configure the power saving icon display</string>
      <string id="YandexPowerSavingModeIcon_Explain">YandexPowerSavingModeIcon

The policy controls the display of the energy saving icon in the SmartBox.

The policy controls the "Show power saving icon" setting. To go to the setting, in the Browser click  "Main Menu" → "Settings" → "Tools" → "Power saving mode" and select it.

The policy is available for Browsers version 23.1.2 and higher.

Values

- Not Configured: The icon is shown, users can hidethe icon.
- Enabled: The icon is shown, the setting is enabled, users cannot hide the icon.
- Disabled: The icon is hidden, the setting is disabled, users can't restore the icon.</string>
      <string id="YandexReaderModeButton">Configure the read mode button in the Smart bar</string>
      <string id="YandexReaderModeButton_Explain">YandexReaderModeButton

The policy configures the read mode button in the SmartBox. To go to the button, click "Page Menu" → "Enable Reader mode" in the Browser on the right in the SmartBox.

The policy is available for Browsers version 23.1.2 and higher.

Values

- Not Configured: The button is enabled.
- Enabled: The button is enabled.
- Disabled: The button is disabled.</string>
      <string id="YandexTextToSpeechButton">Configure the read aloud button in the Smart bar</string>
      <string id="YandexTextToSpeechButton_Explain">YandexTextToSpeechButton

The policy controls the text-to-speech button in the SmartBox.

The policy is available for Browsers version 23.1.2 and higher.

Values

- Not Configured: The "Voice the page" button is enabled.
- Enabled: The "Voice the page" button is enabled.
- Disabled: The "Voice the page" button is disabled.</string>
      <string id="YandexTrackingProtectionButton">Configure the tracking protection button in the Smart bar</string>
      <string id="YandexTrackingProtectionButton_Explain">YandexTrackingProtectionButton

The description is outdated, and the policy is currently being updated.

The policy configures the tracking protection button in the SmartBox.

The policy is available for Browsers version 23.1.2 and higher.

Values

- Not Configured: The button is enabled. Users can disable it.
- Enabled: The button is enabled. Users can't disable it.
- Disabled: The button is disabled. Users can't enable it.</string>
      <string id="YandexWebAppInstallButton">Configure the web app install button in the Smart bar</string>
      <string id="YandexWebAppInstallButton_Explain">YandexWebAppInstallButton

The description is outdated, and the policy is currently being updated.

The policy configures the web application installation button in the SmartBox.

The policy is available for Browsers version 23.1.2 and higher.

Values

- Not Configured: The button is enabled, users can disable it.
- Enabled: The button is enabled, users can't disable it.
- Disabled: The button is disabled, users can't enable it.

A web application is a website that you can open in a separate window and work with it as a program. Viewing a site as a web application is convenient for messengers, email services, and video conferences. For more information, see Help: https://yandex.ru/support/browser/personalization/web-app.html .</string>
      <string id="Translator_group">Translate</string>
      <string id="TranslateEnabled">Enable page-by-page translator</string>
      <string id="TranslateEnabled_Explain">TranslateEnabled

The policy enables or disables page translation in Yandex Browser and restricts users from changing this setting.

Features

- This is an increased security policy. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support2/browser-corporate/ru/deployment/windows/setting-policy#advanced
- Can be configured as a recommendation. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/deployment/setting-policy.html#recommend-policy
- The mobile version only works on iOS.
- Available in the mobile version of the Browser for organizations. More details: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html

Values

- Not Configured: Users decide whether to enable page translation.
- Enabled: Yandex Browser offers to translate pages, the translation icon in the SmartBox and the context menu item are displayed.
- Disabled: Page translation is disabled.

Safety recommendations

Value: Disabled. Disable page translation. The content of the pages is sent to the translation service, which can lead to data leakage.</string>
      <string id="YandexTranslateRestrictions">Set up lists of URLs for automatic translation</string>
      <string id="YandexTranslateRestrictions_Explain">YandexTranslateRestrictions

The policy sets a list of URLs for automatic translation.

Features

- It only works in the extended version of the Browser for organizations. Learn more: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled — automatic text translation is enabled on all sites.
- Enabled — the administrator sets two lists of URLs:
 - `allowed` — sites for which automatic translation is allowed;
 - `denied` — sites for which automatic translation is prohibited.

You can use URL templates. After disabling the policy, the previously set list of URLs is not saved.

Learn more about URL templates: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/policy/url-patterns.html 

Convert URLs without Latin letters (for example, яндекс.рф) via punycode: https://www.reg.ru/web-tools/punycode

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example of a value:

{
 "allowed": [
 "*",
 "en.example.org"
 ],
 "denied": [
 "testserver.example.com",
 "[*.]example.org",
 "internal_urls"
 ]
}</string>
      <string id="WordTranslatorDisabled">Disable word translator</string>
      <string id="WordTranslatorDisabled_Explain">WordTranslatorDisabled

The policy disables word translator in Yandex Browser.

The policy manages the settings:

- "Translate selected words and phrases"
- "Translate a word by pointing the cursor at it and pressing the Shift key"

To go to the settings, in the Browser click  "Main Menu" → "Settings" → "Tools" → "Translate" and select them.

The WordTranslatorDisabled policy is incompatible with the InstaserpDisabled policy.

Values

- Not Configured: The word translator is enabled. Users manage the settings.
- Enabled: The word translator is enabled. The settings are enabled, users cannot disable them.
- Disabled: The word translator is disabled. The settings are disabled, users cannot enable them.</string>
      <string id="YandexCloudLanguageDetectEnabled">Enable sending text fragments to Yandex to improve the quality of translation</string>
      <string id="YandexCloudLanguageDetectEnabled_Explain">YandexCloudLanguageDetectEnabled

The policy enables or disables the sending of text fragments to Yandex to improve the quality of translation.

 The policy controls the setting "Send text fragments to Yandex to improve the quality of translation." To access the setting, click on the "Main Menu" → "Settings" → "Tools" section → "Translate" and select it.

 By default, the Browser automatically detects the language of the loaded page and opens a translation dialog box for foreign-language pages. The language is determined either only locally or simultaneously locally and on the Yandex server. The second method is more accurate, but it sends part of the page text to the server.

Values

- Not Configured: Text fragments are sent to Yandex. Users manage the setting.
- Enabled: Text fragments are sent to Yandex. The setting is enabled, and users cannot disable it.
- Disabled: Text fragments are not sent to Yandex. The setting is disabled, and users cannot enable it.</string>
      <string id="YandexDisplayOriginalTxt">Customize the display of pop-ups with the original text</string>
      <string id="YandexDisplayOriginalTxt_Explain">YandexDisplayOriginalTxt

The policy customizes the display of pop-ups with the original text.

The policy controls the "Display pop-ups with original text" setting. To go to the setting, in the Browser click  "Main Menu" → "Settings" → "Tools" → "Translate" and select it.

The policy is available for Browsers version 23.1.2 and higher.

Values

- Not Configured: Pop-ups with the original text are displayed, users can manage the setting.
- Enabled: Pop-ups with the original text are displayed, the setting is enabled, users cannot disable it.
- Disabled: Pop-ups with the original text are not displayed, the setting is disabled, users cannot enable it.</string>
      <string id="YandexTranslateCursor">Set up translation of words by hovering the cursor and pressing Shift</string>
      <string id="YandexTranslateCursor_Explain">YandexTranslateCursor

The policy configures the translation of words by hovering the cursor and pressing Shift.

The policy controls the "Translate words by hovering the cursor and pressing Shift" setting. To go to the setting, in the Browser click  "Main Menu" → "Settings" → "Tools" → "Translator" and select it.

The policy is available for Browsers version 23.1.2 and higher.

Values

- Not Configured: The translation of words by hovering the cursor + Shift is enabled. Users manage the settings.
- Enabled: The translation of words by hovering the cursor + Shift is enabled. The setting is enabled, users cannot disable it.
- Disabled: The translation of words by hovering the cursor + Shift is disabled. The setting is disabled, users cannot enable it.

Security recommendations

Value: Disabled. Disable translation to prevent data leakage through the use of cursor translation.</string>
      <string id="YandexTranslateImagesButton">Set up the image translation button</string>
      <string id="YandexTranslateImagesButton_Explain">YandexTranslateImagesButton

The policy sets up the image translation button.

The policy controls the "Show the image translation button" setting. To go to the setting, in the Browser click  "Main Menu" → "Settings" → "Tools" → "Translator" and select it.

The policy is available for Browsers version 23.1.2 and higher.

Values

- Not Configured: The button is displayed. Users manage the settings.
- Enabled: The button is displayed. The setting is enabled, users cannot disable it.
- Disabled: The button is not displayed, users can't enable it. The setting is disabled, users cannot enable it.</string>
      <string id="YandexTranslateSelected">Set up translation of selected words and phrases</string>
      <string id="YandexTranslateSelected_Explain">YandexTranslateSelected

The policy adjusts the translation of selected words and phrases in the context menu.

The policy controls the "Translate selected words and phrases" setting. To go to the setting, in the Browser click  "Main Menu" → "Settings" → "Tools" → "Translate" and select it.

The policy is available for Browsers version 23.1.2 and higher.

Features

- The mobile version only works on iOS.
- Available in the mobile version of the Browser for organizations. More details: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html

Values

- Not Configured: translation of selected words and phrases in the context menu is enabled. Users manage the settings.
- Enabled: translation of selected words and phrases in the context menu is enabled. The setting is enabled, users cannot disable it.
- Disabled: translation of selected words and phrases in the context menu is disabled. The setting is disabled, users cannot enable it.</string>
      <string id="YandexTranslateVideosButton">Configure the display of the video translation button</string>
      <string id="YandexTranslateVideosButton_Explain">YandexTranslateVideosButton

The policy configures the «Translate and dub» video translation button.

The policy controls the "Show the "Translate video" button" setting. To go to the setting, in the Browser click  "Main Menu" → "Settings" → "Tools" → "Translate" and select it.

The policy is available for Browsers version 23.1.2 and higher.

Features

- The mobile version only works on iOS.
- Available in the mobile version of the Browser for organizations. More details: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html

Values

- Not Configured: the button is displayed, users control the setting.
- Enabled: the button is displayed, the setting is enabled, users cannot disable it.
- Disabled: the button is not displayed, the setting is disabled, users cannot enable it.</string>
      <string id="PasswordManager_group">Passwords</string>
      <string id="PasswordManagerBlockedURLs">Set a list of URLS for which Password Manager is disabled</string>
      <string id="PasswordManagerBlockedURLs_Explain">PasswordManagerBlockedURLs

The policy sets a list of sites for which the password manager is disabled.

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: The password manager can be used on any sites.
- Enabled: The administrator sets a list of URL templates for which the password manager is disabled. You can use the "internal_urls" keyword to designate all single-domain sites. For example, the rule will apply to "https://example" but not to "https://example.com". You can use URL templates.

For more information about URL templates, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/policy/url-patterns.html

Convert non-Latin URLs (for example, яндекс.рф) via punycode: https://www.reg.ru/web-tools/punycode

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example value:

example.com
*.com
*.acme.com
*</string>
      <string id="PasswordManagerBlockedURLsDesc">Set sites where Password Manager is disabled</string>
      <string id="PasswordManagerEnabled">Allow automatic saving of passwords</string>
      <string id="PasswordManagerEnabled_Explain">PasswordManagerEnabled

The policy allows passwords to be automatically saved in the Browser and substituted when logging in on websites.

Features

- This is a basic security policy. For more information, see: https://yandex.ru/support2/browser-corporate/ru/deployment/windows/setting-policy#basic
- Can be configured as a recommendation. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/deployment/setting-policy.html#recommend-policy
- Available in the mobile version of Yandex Browser for organizations. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html

Values

- Not Configured: Yandex browser automatically saves passwords. Users can enable and disable this option.
- Enabled: Yandex browser automatically saves passwords. Users cannot disable this option.
- Disabled: Yandex browser does not automatically save passwords. Users cannot enable password saving. Users can add passwords to the password manager manually, but such passwords are also not automatically substituted on websites. Passwords saved before disabling the policy are available on the browser://password page.

Safety recommendations

If your organization has its own solution for storing passwords, disable the policy. Otherwise, enable the policy.</string>
      <string id="PasswordProtectionChangePasswordURL">Set the URL of the page for changing the protected password</string>
      <string id="PasswordProtectionChangePasswordURL_Explain">PasswordProtectionChangePasswordURL

The policy sets the URL for the "Reset password" button on the browser://reset-password page.

If users enter a protected password on another site, the Browser redirects to the browser://reset-password page and offers to change the password. On it, users click "Reset password", and a page opens for changing the password.

The list of URLs where passwords are considered protected from entering on another site is set by the PasswordProtectionLoginURLs policy. 

The condition under which Yandex Browser warns about entering a protected password is determined by the PasswordProtectionWarningTrigger policy.

Features

- In Windows and macOS only works within the domain.
- The mobile version only works on Android.
- Available in the mobile version of the Browser for organizations. More details: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: Passwords are changed on the default https://id.yandex.ru/.
- Enabled: The administrator sets the URL of the page for changing the protected password.

Convert non-Latin URLs (for example, яндекс.рф) via punycode: https://www.reg.ru/web-tools/punycode

Example value:

https://mydomain.com/change_password.html</string>
      <string id="PasswordProtectionLoginURLs">Set a list of URLs where passwords will be considered protected</string>
      <string id="PasswordProtectionLoginURLs_Explain">PasswordProtectionLoginURLs

The policy sets a list of URLs where passwords will be considered secure.

On these URLs, the Browser remembers password hashes with salt. If the same password is entered on another site, the browser will show a warning and prompt users to change their password.

The condition under which the Browser warns about entering a protected password is determined by the PasswordProtectionWarningTrigger policy. 

The URL of the page for changing the protected password is set by the PasswordProtectionChangePasswordURL policy.

Features

- It only works on Windows and macOS if it is set inside the domain or via the Management Console.
- Available in the mobile Browser version for organizations. Learn more: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled — the control of protected passwords is disabled.
- Enabled — the administrator sets a list of URLs where passwords will be considered protected.

Convert URLs without Latin letters (for example, яндекс.рф) via punycode: https://www.reg.ru/web-tools/punycode

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example of the value:

https://mydomain.com/login.html
https://login.mydomain.com</string>
      <string id="PasswordProtectionLoginURLsDesc">Configure a list of corporate account login URLs where the password protection service should record hashes with salt for passwords</string>
      <string id="PasswordProtectionWarningTrigger">Set a password protection warning trigger</string>
      <string id="PasswordProtectionWarningTrigger_Explain">PasswordProtectionWarningTrigger

The policy defines a condition under which Yandex Browser warns about entering a protected password on another site and prompts users to change their password.

The list of URLs where passwords are considered protected from entering on another site is set by the PasswordProtectionLoginURLs policy. 

The URL of the page for changing the protected password is set by the PasswordProtectionChangePasswordURL policy.

Features

- On Windows and macOS, it only works within the domain.

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: Warnings are disabled.
- Enabled: The administrator sets the alert display mode:
     - Warnings disabled.
     - Entering on another site.
     - Entering on a dangerous site. For more information about how Yandex Browser detects dangerous sites, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser/security/virus-protection.html#how-working</string>
      <string id="PasswordProtectionWarningTrigger_PasswordProtectionWarningOff">Warnings disabled</string>
      <string id="PasswordProtectionWarningTrigger_PasswordProtectionWarningOnPasswordReuse">Entering on another site</string>
      <string id="PasswordProtectionWarningTrigger_PasswordProtectionWarningOnPhishingReuse">Entering on a dangerous site</string>
      <string id="ContentSettings_group">Content settings</string>
      <string id="AutoSelectCertificateForUrls">Set a list of URLs for which the Browser can automatically select the client certificate</string>
      <string id="AutoSelectCertificateForUrls_Explain">AutoSelectCertificateForUrls

The policy sets a list of URLs for which Yandex Browser can automatically select the client certificate.

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: Automatic certificate selection is restricted on all sites.
- Enabled: The administrator sets the list of URL templates and client certificate filters.

The value is an array of JSON dictionaries converted to strings. Each dictionary should have the form { "pattern": "$URL_PATTERN", "filter" : $FILTER }, where $URL_PATTERN is a template for content settings. $FILTER defines a set of client certificates from which Yandex Browser automatically selects the necessary one. Regardless of the filter settings, only certificates that match the server request are selected.

Examples of using the $FILTER fragment:

- If $FILTER has the form { "ISSUER": { "CN": "$ISSUER_CN" } }, only client certificates issued by the publisher with the common name $ISSUER_CN are selected.
- If $FILTER contains both "ISSUER" and "SUBJECT" fragments, only client certificates that meet both conditions are selected.
- If $FILTER contains a "SUBJECT" fragment with the value "O", only the certificate with at least one organization name corresponding to the specified value is selected.
- If $FILTER contains a "SUBJECT" fragment with the value "OU", only the certificate with at least one organization unit name corresponding to the specified value is selected.
- If $FILTER contains empty brackets {}, the choice of certificates is not limited by any other factor. However, the web server filters are still applied.

For more information about URL templates, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/policy/url-patterns.html

Convert non-Latin URLs (for example, яндекс.рф) via punycode: https://www.reg.ru/web-tools/punycode

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example value:

[
  {
    "pattern": "https://www.example.com",
    "filter": {
      "ISSUER": {
        "CN": "certificate issuer name",
        "L": "certificate issuer location",
        "O": "certificate issuer org",
        "OU": "certificate issuer org unit"
      },
      "SUBJECT": {
        "CN": "certificate subject name",
        "L": "certificate subject location",
        "O": "certificate subject org",
        "OU": "certificate subject org unit"
      }
    }
  }
]</string>
      <string id="AutoSelectCertificateForUrlsDesc">Automatically select client certificates for sites</string>
      <string id="ClipboardAllowedForUrls">Allow access to the clipboard for URLs from the list</string>
      <string id="ClipboardAllowedForUrls_Explain">ClipboardAllowedForUrls

The policy sets a list of URLs that can use the clipboard. 

The policy blocks access to the clipboard only through the JavaScript API. It does not apply to clipboard actions for other sources. For example, users will still be able to insert text with a keyboard shortcut or a long press on a mobile device, since this feature is not limited to the clipboard access option.

The policy supersedes DefaultClipboardSetting. The ClipboardBlockedForUrls policy supersedes ClipboardAllowedForUrls.

The policy is disabled if the YandexPasteAllowlist policy is set.

Features

- This is a basic security policy. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/deployment/windows/setting-policy#basic
- Available in the mobile version of the Browser for organizations. More details: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: The value of the DefaultClipboardSetting policy is used (if it is set). 
- Enabled: The administrator sets the list of URLs that can use the clipboard. You can use URL templates.

For more information about URL templates, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/policy/url-patterns.html

Convert non-Latin URLs (for example, яндекс.рф) via punycode: https://www.reg.ru/web-tools/punycode

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example value:

["ya.ru", "[*.]badssl.com"]</string>
      <string id="ClipboardAllowedForUrlsDesc">Allow clipboard for URLs from the list</string>
      <string id="ClipboardBlockedForUrls">Prohibit access to the clipboard for URLs from the list</string>
      <string id="ClipboardBlockedForUrls_Explain">ClipboardBlockedForUrls

The policy sets a list of URLs that can't use the clipboard. 

The policy blocks access to the clipboard only through the JavaScript API. It does not apply to clipboard actions for other sources. For example, users will still be able to insert text with a keyboard shortcut or a long press on a mobile device, since this feature is not limited to the clipboard access option.

The policy supersedes ClipboardAllowedForUrls and DefaultClipboardSetting.

The policy is disabled if the YandexPasteBlocklist policy is set.

Features

- This is a basic security policy. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/deployment/windows/setting-policy#basic
- Available in the mobile version of the Browser for organizations. More details: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: The value of the DefaultClipboardSetting policy is used (if it is set).
- Enabled: The administrator sets the list of URLs that can't use the clipboard. You can use URL patterns. 

For more information about URL templates, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/policy/url-patterns.html

Convert non-Latin URLs (for example, яндекс.рф) via punycode: https://www.reg.ru/web-tools/punycode

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example value:

["ya.ru", "[*.]badssl.com"]</string>
      <string id="ClipboardBlockedForUrlsDesc">Block clipboard for URLs from the list</string>
      <string id="CookiesAllowedForUrls">Allow cookies for URLS from the list</string>
      <string id="CookiesAllowedForUrls_Explain">CookiesAllowedForUrls

The policy sets a list of URLs that are allowed to save cookies.

The policy supersedes DefaultCookiesSetting. The policies CookiesBlockedForUrls and CookiesSessionOnlyForUrls supersede CookiesAllowedForUrls.

Features

- Available in the mobile version of Yandex Browser for organizations. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: The value of the DefaultCookiesSetting policy is used (if it is set).
- Enabled: The administrator sets a list of URLs. Users can't change this list. You can use URL patterns. The "*" wildcard is only used for subdomains in this form: "[*.]". 

For more information about URL patterns, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/policy/url-patterns.html

Convert non-Latin URLs (for example, яндекс.рф) to punycode: https://www.reg.ru/web-tools/punycode

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example value:

https://www.example.com
[*.]example.edu</string>
      <string id="CookiesAllowedForUrlsDesc">Allow cookies on these sites</string>
      <string id="CookiesBlockedForUrls">Block cookies for URLS from the list</string>
      <string id="CookiesBlockedForUrls_Explain">CookiesBlockedForUrls

The policy sets a list of URLs that are not allowed to save cookies.

The policy supersedes DefaultCookiesSetting and CookiesAllowedForUrls. The CookiesSessionOnlyForUrls policy supersedes CookiesBlockedForUrls.

Features

- Available in the mobile version of Yandex Browser for organizations. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: The DefaultCookiesSetting policy value is used (if it is set).
- Enabled: The administrator sets a list of URLs. Users can't change this list. You can use URL patterns. The "*" wildcard is only used for subdomains in this form: "[*.]".

For more information about URL patterns, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/policy/url-patterns.html

Convert non-Latin URLs (for example, яндекс.рф) to punycode: https://www.reg.ru/web-tools/punycode

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example value:

https://www.example.com
[*.]example.edu</string>
      <string id="CookiesBlockedForUrlsDesc">Block cookies on these sites</string>
      <string id="CookiesSessionOnlyForUrls">Store cookies for a URL from the list for the duration of the session and delete it after it ends</string>
      <string id="CookiesSessionOnlyForUrls_Explain">CookiesSessionOnlyForUrls

The policy sets a list of sites that are allowed to store cookies during a session.

The policy supersedes DefaultCookiesSetting, CookiesBlockedForUrls, and CookiesAllowedForUrls.

Features

- Available in the mobile version of Yandex Browser for organizations. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: The value of the DefaultCookiesSetting policy is used (if it is set).
- Enabled: The administrator sets a list of URLs. Websites on the list will only be allowed to store cookies for the duration of the session. Users can't change this list. You can use URL patterns. The "*" wildcard is only used for subdomains in this form: "[*.]". 

For more information about URL patterns, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/policy/url-patterns.html

Convert non-Latin URLs (for example, яндекс.рф) to punycode: https://www.reg.ru/web-tools/punycode

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example value:

https://www.example.com
[*.]example.edu</string>
      <string id="CookiesSessionOnlyForUrlsDesc">Cookies saved by sites with URLS from the list are deleted after the session ends</string>
      <string id="DefaultClipboardSetting">Configure clipboard access</string>
      <string id="DefaultClipboardSetting_Explain">DefaultClipboardSetting

The policy allows or restricts sites access to the clipboard.

The policy blocks access to the clipboard only through the JavaScript API. It does not apply to clipboard actions for other sources. For example, users will still be able to insert text with a keyboard shortcut or a long press on a mobile device, since this feature is not limited to the clipboard access option.

The YandexPasteBlocklist, ClipboardAllowedForUrls, and ClipboardBlockedForUrls policies supersede DefaultClipboardSetting.

Features

- This is a basic security policy. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/deployment/windows/setting-policy#basic
- Available in the mobile version of the Browser for organizations. More details: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: Sites can request permission to access the clipboard.
- Enabled: The administrator determines the clipboard access mode:
     - Allowed.
     - Prohibited.</string>
      <string id="DefaultClipboardSetting_BlockClipboard">Prohibited</string>
      <string id="DefaultClipboardSetting_AskClipboard">Allowed</string>
      <string id="DefaultCookiesSetting">Configure cookies</string>
      <string id="DefaultCookiesSetting_Explain">DefaultCookiesSetting

The policy manages cookie settings and restricts users from changing them.

Cookies are used for authorization. If they are disabled, Yandex Browser syncing won't work. This policy applies to all sites.

The CookiesSessionOnlyForUrls, CookiesBlockedForUrls, and CookiesAllowedForUrls policies supersede DefaultCookiesSetting.

Features

- This is an increased security policy. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support2/browser-corporate/ru/deployment/windows/setting-policy#advanced
- Available in the mobile version of Yandex Browser for organizations. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: Cookies are allowed, users can change their settings.
- Enabled: The administrator sets the mode for applying the policy:
     - Prohibit saving cookies.
     - Allow saving cookies.
     - Store cookies until the end of the session. When Yandex Browser runs in the background, the session doesn't end even after all windows are closed.

Safety recommendations

Value: Enabled → "Store cookies until the end of the session". Enable "Store cookies until the end of the session" mode. Attackers can use permanently stored cookies.

Possible problems. If the "Restore the last session" value is set in the RestoreOnStartup policy, cookies are permanently saved for these sites.</string>
      <string id="DefaultCookiesSetting_AllowCookies">Allow saving cookies</string>
      <string id="DefaultCookiesSetting_BlockCookies">Prohibit saving cookies</string>
      <string id="DefaultCookiesSetting_SessionOnly">Store cookies until the end of the session</string>
      <string id="DefaultFileSystemReadGuardSetting">Configure sites' access to reading files on the device</string>
      <string id="DefaultFileSystemReadGuardSetting_Explain">DefaultFileSystemReadGuardSetting

The policy configures sites' access to reading files on the device via the File System API.

The FileSystemReadAskForUrls and FileSystemReadBlockedForUrls policies supersede DefaultFileSystemReadGuardSetting.

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: Access is requested.
- Enabled: The administrator selects the access mode for reading files on the device:
     - Ask.
     - Prohibit.</string>
      <string id="DefaultFileSystemReadGuardSetting_BlockFileSystemRead">Don't allow</string>
      <string id="DefaultFileSystemReadGuardSetting_AskFileSystemRead">Ask</string>
      <string id="DefaultFileSystemWriteGuardSetting">Configure sites' access to changing files on the device</string>
      <string id="DefaultFileSystemWriteGuardSetting_Explain">DefaultFileSystemWriteGuardSetting

The policy configures sites' access to changing files on the device via the File System API.

The FileSystemWriteAskForUrls and FileSystemWriteBlockedForUrls policies supersede DefaultFileSystemWriteGuardSetting.

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: Access is requested.
- Enabled: The administrator selects the access mode for changing files on the device:
     - Ask.
     - Prohibit.</string>
      <string id="DefaultFileSystemWriteGuardSetting_BlockFileSystemWrite">Don't allow</string>
      <string id="DefaultFileSystemWriteGuardSetting_AskFileSystemWrite">Ask</string>
      <string id="DefaultGeolocationSetting">Configure location detection</string>
      <string id="DefaultGeolocationSetting_Explain">DefaultGeolocationSetting

The policy allows or restricts sites from tracking the user's location.

The policy controls the "Location Access" setting. To go to settings:

1. In the Browser click "Main Menu" → "Settings" → "Sites" → "Advanced Site Settings".
2. In the "Location Access" section enable the desired option.

Features

- This is a basic security policy. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/deployment/windows/setting-policy#basic
- Available in the mobile version of Yandex Browser for organizations. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: Sites can request permission to track the user's location. Users manage the settings.
- Enabled: The administrator specifies one of the values that users can't change:
     - "Disable location detection".
     - "Allow location detection".
     - "Ask if the site wants to see the user's location".

Safety recommendations

Value: Enabled → "Disable location detection". Activate the "Disable location detection" mode. Location sharing may violate the user's privacy and cause leakage of data about network infrastructure around the device.

Possible problems.	Yandex Browser will stop sharing the computer's IP address and data about nearby Wi-Fi hotspots and cellular communication nodes (even if they are not used).</string>
      <string id="DefaultGeolocationSetting_AllowGeolocation">Allow location detection</string>
      <string id="DefaultGeolocationSetting_BlockGeolocation">Disable location detection</string>
      <string id="DefaultGeolocationSetting_AskGeolocation">Ask if the site wants to see the user's location</string>
      <string id="DefaultImagesSetting">Configure the display of images on sites</string>
      <string id="DefaultImagesSetting_Explain">DefaultImagesSetting

The policy controls the display of images on sites.

The ImagesAllowedForUrls and ImagesBlockedForUrls policies take priority over DefaultImagesSetting.

- Not Configured, Disabled: Images are displayed, users can hide them.
- Enabled: The administrator sets the mode for displaying images on sites:
     - Allowed
     - Prohibited</string>
      <string id="DefaultImagesSetting_AllowImages">Allowed</string>
      <string id="DefaultImagesSetting_BlockImages">Forbidden</string>
      <string id="DefaultJavaScriptJitSetting">Select JavaScript JIT compiler mode</string>
      <string id="DefaultJavaScriptJitSetting_Explain">DefaultJavaScriptJitSetting

The policy enables or disables the JIT compiler in the v8 JavaScript engine.

The JavaScriptJitAllowedForSites and JavaScriptJitBlockedForSites policies supercede DefaultJavaScriptJitSetting.

If the JIT compiler is disabled, the page content may render more slowly, and some JavaScript elements like WebAssembly may be disabled. This allows Yandex Browser to render page content more securely.

After changing the policy value, restart Yandex Browser: press Ctrl + Shift + Q or the Main menu icon → "Close browser" and open it again.

Features

- The mobile version only works on Android.
- Available in the mobile version of the Browser for organizations. More details: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: JIT compiler is enabled.
- Enabled: The administrator sets the JIT compiler mode:
     - Allowed.
     - Prohibited.</string>
      <string id="DefaultJavaScriptJitSetting_AllowJavaScriptJit">Allowed</string>
      <string id="DefaultJavaScriptJitSetting_BlockJavaScriptJit">Prohibited</string>
      <string id="DefaultJavaScriptSetting">Configure JavaScript launch by sites</string>
      <string id="DefaultJavaScriptSetting_Explain">DefaultJavaScriptSetting

The policy allows or restricts sites from executing JavaScript.

Features

- The mobile version only works on Android.
- Available in the mobile version of the Browser for organizations. More details: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html

Values

- Not Configured: Sites execute JavaScript, users can change this parameter.
- Enabled: The administrator allows or restricts sites to execute JavaScript, users can't change this parameter.</string>
      <string id="DefaultJavaScriptSetting_AllowJavaScript">Allow sites to execute JavaScript</string>
      <string id="DefaultJavaScriptSetting_BlockJavaScript">Prohibit sites from executing JavaScript</string>
      <string id="DefaultLocalFontsSetting">Configure sites' access to fonts on the device</string>
      <string id="DefaultLocalFontsSetting_Explain">DefaultLocalFontsSetting

The policy controls sites' access to fonts on a device.

The LocalFontsAllowedForUrls and LocalFontsBlockedForUrls policies supersede DefaultLocalFontsSetting.

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: Sites request access.
- Enabled: The administrator determines how sites access fonts on a device:
     - "Ask when a site requests access to fonts on the device".
     - "Prohibit access to fonts on the device".</string>
      <string id="DefaultLocalFontsSetting_BlockLocalFonts">Prohibit access to fonts on the device</string>
      <string id="DefaultLocalFontsSetting_AskLocalFonts">Ask when a site requests access to fonts on the device</string>
      <string id="DefaultNotificationsSetting">Configure site notifications</string>
      <string id="DefaultNotificationsSetting_Explain">DefaultNotificationsSetting

The policy configures notifications from sites and restricts users from changing this setting.

Once restricted, the sites won't offer sending notifications. Sites that users already allowed to send notifications will still send them. You need to block such notifications separately for each site.

NotificationsAllowedForUrls and NotificationsBlockedForUrls policies supersede DefaultNotificationsSetting.

Features

- This is an increased security policy. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support2/browser-corporate/ru/deployment/windows/setting-policy#advanced

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: Users allow or restrict each site from showing notifications.
- Enabled: The administrator sets the notification display mode:
     - Allow requests to send notifications.
     - Prohibit requests to send notifications.
     - Ask if the site is going to show a notification.

Safety recommendations

Value: Enabled → "Prohibit requests to send notifications". Prohibit requests to send notifications because they may contain false messages with links to malicious sites.

Disable or don't set the NotificationsAllowedForUrls and NotificationsBlockedForUrls policies.</string>
      <string id="DefaultNotificationsSetting_AllowNotifications">Allow requests to send notifications</string>
      <string id="DefaultNotificationsSetting_BlockNotifications">Prohibit requests to send notifications</string>
      <string id="DefaultNotificationsSetting_AskNotifications">Ask if the site is going to show a notification</string>
      <string id="DefaultPopupsSetting">Configure pop-up display</string>
      <string id="DefaultPopupsSetting_Explain">DefaultPopupsSetting

The policy allows or restricts popup windows on all sites.

The PopupsAllowedForUrls and PopupsBlockedForUrls policies supersede DefaultPopupsSetting.

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: Popup windows are blocked on all sites, users can allow or block popup windows in Yandex Browser settings.
- Enabled: The administrator determines the policy application mode:
     - Do not allow any site to show pop-ups.
     - Allow all sites to show pop-ups.
Users can't allow or block popup windows in Yandex Browser settings.</string>
      <string id="DefaultPopupsSetting_AllowPopups">Allow on all sites</string>
      <string id="DefaultPopupsSetting_BlockPopups">Block on all sites</string>
      <string id="DefaultSensorsSetting">Configure access to sensors</string>
      <string id="DefaultSensorsSetting_Explain">DefaultSensorsSetting

The policy sets up site access to device sensors, such as an accelerometer or light sensor.

Features

- This is an increased security policy. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support2/browser-corporate/ru/deployment/windows/setting-policy#advanced

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: Access is allowed.
- Enabled: The administrator sets the access mode for sites to sensors:
     - Allowed.
     - Prohibited.

Safety recommendations

Value: Enabled → Prohibited. Prohibit access to sensors. Malicious sites can identify the device through them.

Possible problems. Sites that use sensors won't work correctly.</string>
      <string id="DefaultSensorsSetting_AllowSensors">Allowed</string>
      <string id="DefaultSensorsSetting_BlockSensors">Prohibited</string>
      <string id="DefaultSerialGuardSetting">Configure sites' access to the Web Serial API</string>
      <string id="DefaultSerialGuardSetting_Explain">DefaultSerialGuardSetting

The policy configures site access to serial ports via the Web Serial API.

The SerialAllowUsbDevicesForUrls, SerialAllowAllPortsForUrls, SerialAskForUrls, and SerialBlockedForUrls policies supersede DefaultSerialGuardSetting.

Features

- This is an increased security policy. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support2/browser-corporate/ru/deployment/windows/setting-policy#advanced

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: Requests are not allowed.
- Enabled: The administrator determines site requests for access to serial ports:
     - Allowed.
     - Prohibited.

Safety recommendations

Value: Enabled → Prohibited. Prohibit requests for access to serial ports. Malicious sites can use them to access connected devices.

Possible problems. Sites that use serial ports may not work correctly.</string>
      <string id="DefaultSerialGuardSetting_BlockSerial">Not allowed</string>
      <string id="DefaultSerialGuardSetting_AskSerial">Allowed</string>
      <string id="DefaultWebBluetoothGuardSetting">Configure sites' access to the Web Bluetooth API</string>
      <string id="DefaultWebBluetoothGuardSetting_Explain">DefaultWebBluetoothGuardSetting

The policy allows or prohibits site requests to access Bluetooth devices via the Web Bluetooth API.

Features

- This is an increased security policy. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support2/browser-corporate/ru/deployment/windows/setting-policy#advanced

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: Requests are allowed.
- Enabled: The administrator determines site requests for access to Bluetooth devices:
     - Allowed.
     - Prohibited.

Safety recommendations

Value: Enabled → Prohibited. Prohibit requests for access to Bluetooth devices. Malicious sites can access devices through them.

Possible problems. Sites won't be able to use connected Bluetooth devices like headphones or webcams.</string>
      <string id="DefaultWebBluetoothGuardSetting_BlockWebBluetooth">Not allowed</string>
      <string id="DefaultWebBluetoothGuardSetting_AskWebBluetooth">Allowed</string>
      <string id="DefaultWebHidGuardSetting">Configure access to HID devices</string>
      <string id="DefaultWebHidGuardSetting_Explain">DefaultWebHidGuardSetting

The policy configures site requests to access HID devices via the WebHID API and restricts users from changing this parameter.

HID (human interface device) is a class of USB devices for interacting with a person, such as a keyboard, mouse, or game controller.

The WebHidAllowAllDevicesForUrls, WebHidAllowDevicesForUrls, WebHidAskForUrls, and WebHidBlockedForUrls policies supersede DefaultWebHidGuardSetting.

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: Requests are allowed.
- Enabled: The administrator defines access requests to HID devices:
     - Allowed.
     - Prohibited.</string>
      <string id="DefaultWebHidGuardSetting_BlockWebHid">Disabled</string>
      <string id="DefaultWebHidGuardSetting_AskWebHid">Enabled</string>
      <string id="DefaultWebUsbGuardSetting">Configure sites' access requests to USB devices</string>
      <string id="DefaultWebUsbGuardSetting_Explain">DefaultWebUsbGuardSetting

The policy allows or restricts sites to request access to USB devices via the WebUSB API and restricts users from changing access parameters.

The policy controls the "Access to your USB devices" setting. To go to the settings, in the Browser, click "Main Menu" → "Settings" → "Websites" → "Advanced site settings" and select it.

WebUsbAskForUrls and WebUsbBlockedForUrls policies supersede DefaultWebUsbGuardSetting.

The policy is available for Browsers version 23.3.1 and higher.

Features

- This is an increased security policy. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support2/browser-corporate/ru/deployment/windows/setting-policy#advanced

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: Requests for website access to USB devices are allowed, users control the configuration.
- Enabled:
     - The administrator defines access requests to USB devices:
          - "Allowed"
          - "Prohibited"
     - Users cannot change the setting.

Safety recommendations

Value: Enabled → Prohibited. Assess the risks. If your organization doesn't need USB devices, block access to them. We also recommend to disable or not set the WebUsbAskForUrls and WebUsbBlockedForUrls policies.

WebUSB can be used for phishing attacks that can bypass two-factor authentication hardware devices.

Possible problems. Sites won't be able to use connected USB devices like tokens, headphones, and webcams.</string>
      <string id="DefaultWebUsbGuardSetting_BlockWebUsb">Not allowed</string>
      <string id="DefaultWebUsbGuardSetting_AskWebUsb">Allowed</string>
      <string id="DefaultWindowManagementSetting">Configure site access to window management</string>
      <string id="DefaultWindowManagementSetting_Explain">DefaultWindowManagementSetting

The policy configures site access to window management.

The WindowManagementAllowedForUrls and WindowManagementBlockedForUrls policies supersede DefaultWindowManagementSetting.

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: Access is requested.
- Enabled: The administrator selects the access mode for sites to manage windows:
     - Ask.
