      <string id="InsecureContentAllowedForUrls">Allow insecure content to be uploaded to a URL from the list</string>
      <string id="InsecureContentAllowedForUrls_Explain">InsecureContentAllowedForUrls

The policy allows URLs from the list to load insecure content.

The InsecureContentBlockedForUrls policy supersedes InsecureContentAllowedForUrls.

Features

- This is a basic security policy. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/deployment/windows/setting-policy#basic

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: Insecure content is blocked.
- Enabled: The administrator sets the list of URLs. You can use URL patterns. The «*» wildcard is only used for subdomains in this form: «[*.]».

For more information about URL templates, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/policy/url-patterns.html

Convert non-Latin URLs (for example, яндекс.рф) via punycode: https://www.reg.ru/web-tools/punycode

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example value:

https://www.example.com
[*.]example.edu

Safety recommendations

Sometimes a page may load over the secure HTTPS but still contain unencrypted elements, such as plugins, JavaScript scripts, or CSS styles. Attackers can intercept and use them to hack the user.

Value: Disabled. By default, insecure content is blocked. Disable or don't set the InsecureContentAllowedForUrls and InsecureContentBlockedForUrls policies.</string>
      <string id="InsecureContentAllowedForUrlsDesc">Allow insecure content to be uploaded to a URL from the list</string>
      <string id="InsecureContentBlockedForUrls">Prohibit uploading insecure content to a URL from the list</string>
      <string id="InsecureContentBlockedForUrls_Explain">InsecureContentBlockedForUrls

The policy restricts loading insecure content for URLs from the list.

The policy supersedes InsecureContentAllowedForUrls.

Features

- This is a basic security policy. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/deployment/windows/setting-policy#basic

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: Insecure content is blocked.
- Enabled: The administrator sets the list of URLs that can't download insecure content. You can use URL templates. The «*» wildcard is only used for subdomains in this form: «[*.]».

For more information about URL templates, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/policy/url-patterns.html

Convert non-Latin URLs (for example, яндекс.рф) via punycode: https://www.reg.ru/web-tools/punycode

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example value:

https://www.example.com
[*.]example.edu

Safety recommendations

Sometimes a page may load over the secure HTTPS but still contain unencrypted elements, such as plugins, JavaScript scripts, or CSS styles. Attackers can intercept and use them to hack the user.

Value: Disabled. By default, insecure content is blocked. Disable or don't set the InsecureContentAllowedForUrls and InsecureContentBlockedForUrls policies.</string>
      <string id="InsecureContentBlockedForUrlsDesc">Prohibit uploading insecure content to a URL from the list</string>
      <string id="JavaScriptAllowedForUrls">Allow JavaScript URLs from the list</string>
      <string id="JavaScriptAllowedForUrls_Explain">JavaScriptAllowedForUrls

The policy sets a list of URLs that are allowed to execute JavaScript.

The policy takes precedence over the DefaultJavaScriptSetting policy. The JavaScriptBlockedForUrls policy takes precedence over the JavaScriptAllowedForUrls policy.

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled — the value of the DefaultJavaScriptSetting policy is used, if it is set.
- Enabled — the administrator sets a list of URLs. Users cannot change this list. You can use URL templates. The wildcard «*» is used only for subdomains in this format: «[*.]». 

Learn more about URL templates: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/policy/url-patterns.html

Convert URLs without Latin letters (for example, яндекс.рф) via punycode: https://www.reg.ru/web-tools/punycode

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example of a value:

https://www.example.com
[*.]example.edu</string>
      <string id="JavaScriptAllowedForUrlsDesc">Allow JavaScript URLs from the list</string>
      <string id="JavaScriptBlockedForUrls">Ban JavaScript URLs from the list</string>
      <string id="JavaScriptBlockedForUrls_Explain">JavaScriptBlockedForUrls

The policy sets a list of URLs that are prohibited from executing JavaScript.

The policy takes precedence over the DefaultJavaScriptSetting and JavaScriptAllowedForUrls policies. 

The policy blocks JavaScript if the URL of the top-level page matches one of the specified templates. The policy does not protect against attacks when downloading JavaScript from other sites. For example:
- The policy has a template «https://[*.]foo.com/». On the website https://example.com JavaScript will not be blocked if it is downloaded from the website https://www.foo.com/example.js .
- The policy has a template  «https://example.com/». On the page https://example.com JavaScript will not be blocked if it is embedded as a frame on another site (for example, https://www.bar.com ).

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled — the value of the DefaultJavaScriptSetting policy is used, if it is set.
- Enabled — the administrator sets a list of URLs. Users cannot change this list. You can use URL templates. The wildcard «*» is used only for subdomains in this format: «[*.]».

Learn more about URL templates: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/policy/url-patterns.html

Convert URLs without Latin letters (for example, яндекс.рф) via punycode: https://www.reg.ru/web-tools/punycode

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example of the value:

https://www.example.com
[*.]example.edu</string>
      <string id="JavaScriptBlockedForUrlsDesc">Ban JavaScript URLs from the list</string>
      <string id="JavaScriptJitAllowedForSites">Allow using the JavaScript JIT compiler for a URL from the list</string>
      <string id="JavaScriptJitAllowedForSites_Explain">JavaScriptJitAllowedForSites

The policy sets a list of URLs that are allowed to run JavaScript code with the JIT compiler enabled.

The policy supersedes DefaultJavaScriptJitSetting. JavaScriptJitBlockedForSites supersedes JavaScriptJitAllowedForSites.

Enable the policy at the site level (second-level domain). For example, if only the subdomain.site.com subdomain is set in the policy, it will not work correctly for the site.com website or the subdomain1.site.com subdomain. As a result, the policy will not work correctly for the whole website.

The policy applies to individual frames. For example, if the policy specifies site-one.com that loads a frame with site-two.com, the JavaScript JIT compiler will only be enabled for site-one.com. The DefaultJavaScriptJitSetting policy (if it is set) will be applied to the frame with site-two.com, or the JavaScript JIT compiler will be enabled by default.

After changing the policy value, Yandex Browser should be restarted: press Ctrl + Shift + Q or the Main menu icon → «Close browser» and open it again.

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: The DefaultJavaScriptJitSetting policy is applied (if it is set).
- Enabled: The administrator sets the list of URLs where the JavaScript JIT compiler is enabled. You can use URL patterns. The «*» wildcard is only used for subdomains in this form: «[*.]».

For more information about URL templates, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/policy/url-patterns.html

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config
 
Example value:

[*.]example.edu</string>
      <string id="JavaScriptJitAllowedForSitesDesc">Allow using the JavaScript JIT compiler for a URL from the list</string>
      <string id="JavaScriptJitBlockedForSites">Prohibit using the JavaScript JIT compiler for a URL from the list</string>
      <string id="JavaScriptJitBlockedForSites_Explain">JavaScriptJitBlockedForSites

The policy sets a list of URLs that aren't allowed to run JavaScript code with the JIT compiler enabled.

The policy supersedes JavaScriptJitAllowedForSites and DefaultJavaScriptJitSetting.

By disabling the JIT compiler you improve the security of displaying web content. Still, such content can load slower and some JavaScript components may stop working.

Enable the policy at the site (second-level domain) level. For example, if only the subdomain.site.com subdomain is set in the policy, it will not work correctly for the site.com website or the subdomain1.site.com subdomain. As a result, the policy will not work correctly for the whole website.

The policy applies to individual frames. For example, if the policy specifies site-one.com that loads a frame with site-two.com, the JavaScript JIT compiler will only be enabled for site-one.com. The DefaultJavaScriptJitSetting policy (if it is set) will be applied to the frame with site-two.com, or the JavaScript JIT compiler will be enabled by default.

After changing the policy value, Yandex Browser should be restarted: press Ctrl + Shift + Q or the Main menu icon → «Close browser» and open it again.

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: The DefaultJavaScriptJitSetting policy is applied (if it is set).
- Enabled: The administrator sets the list of URLs where the JavaScript JIT compiler is disabled. You can use URL patterns. The «*» wildcard is only used for subdomains in this form: «[*.]».

For more information about URL templates, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/policy/url-patterns.html

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example value:

[*.]example.edu</string>
      <string id="JavaScriptJitBlockedForSitesDesc">Prohibit using the JavaScript JIT compiler for a URL from the list</string>
