      <string id="NotificationsAllowedForUrls">Allow notification requests for URLs from the list</string>
      <string id="NotificationsAllowedForUrls_Explain">NotificationsAllowedForUrls

The policy sets a list of URLs that are allowed to make requests to send notifications.

The NotificationsBlockedForUrls policy supersedes DefaultNotificationsSetting and NotificationsAllowedForUrls. The NotificationsAllowedForUrls policy supersedes DefaultNotificationsSetting.

Features

- This is an increased security policy. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/deployment/windows/setting-policy#advanced

Values

- Not Configured: The value of the DefaultNotificationsSetting policy is used (if it is set). Users can change notification settings if the DefaultNotificationsSetting policy isn't set.
- Disabled: The value is treated as Not Configured.
- Enabled: The administrator sets the list of URLs. Users can't change notification settings. You can use URL templates. The "*" wildcard is only used for subdomains in this form: "[*.]".

For more information about URL templates, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/policy/url-patterns.html

Convert non-Latin URLs (for example, яндекс.рф) via punycode: https://www.reg.ru/web-tools/punycode

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example value:

https://www.example.com
[*.]example.edu

Safety recommendations

Value: Disabled. Disable requests to send notifications in the DefaultNotificationsSetting policy because they may contain false messages with links to malicious sites.

Disable or don't set the NotificationsAllowedForUrls and NotificationsBlockedForUrls policies.</string>
      <string id="NotificationsAllowedForUrlsDesc">Allow notification requests for URLs from the list</string>
      <string id="NotificationsBlockedForUrls">Prohibit notification requests for URLs from the list</string>
      <string id="NotificationsBlockedForUrls_Explain">NotificationsBlockedForUrls

The policy sets a list of URLs that aren't allowed to make request to send notifications.

