Disable or don't set the NotificationsAllowedForUrls and NotificationsBlockedForUrls policies.</string>
      <string id="NotificationsBlockedForUrlsDesc">Prohibit notification requests for URLs from the list</string>
      <string id="PopupsAllowedForUrls">Allow pop-ups for URLs from the list</string>
      <string id="PopupsAllowedForUrls_Explain">PopupsAllowedForUrls

The policy sets up a list of URL patterns that are allowed to open pop-up windows.

The PopupsBlockedForUrls policy supersedes DefaultPopupsSetting and PopupsAllowedForUrls. The PopupsAllowedForUrls policy supersedes DefaultPopupsSetting.

- Not Configured, Disabled: Users allow or restrict pop-ups for each site. If the DefaultPopupsSetting policy is set, its settings are used.
- Enabled: The administrator sets the list of URL templates that can open pop-up windows. You can use URL templates. The "*" wildcard is only used for subdomains in this form: "[*.]".

For more information about URL templates, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/policy/url-patterns.html

