      <string id="SensorsAllowedForUrls">Allow access to sensors for URLs from the list</string>
      <string id="SensorsAllowedForUrls_Explain">SensorsAllowedForUrls

The policy sets a list of URLs that can request access to device sensors.

The policy supersedes DefaultSensorsSetting. The SensorsBlockedForUrls policy supersedes SensorsAllowedForUrls.

Features

- This is an increased security policy. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/deployment/windows/setting-policy#advanced

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: The value of the DefaultSensorsSetting policy is used (if it is set).
- Enabled: The administrator sets the list of URLs. You can use URL patterns. The "*" wildcard is not supported.

For more information about URL templates, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/policy/url-patterns.html

Convert non-Latin URLs (for example, яндекс.рф) via punycode: https://www.reg.ru/web-tools/punycode

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example value:

https://www.example.com
[*.]example.edu

Safety recommendations

Disable access to the sensors. Malicious sites can use them to identify the device. We recommend restricting access in the DefaultSensorsSetting policy. We also recommend disabling or not setting the SensorsAllowedForUrls and SensorsBlockedForUrls policies.

Possible problems. Sites that use sensors won't work correctly.</string>
