Possible problems. Sites that use sensors won't work correctly.</string>
      <string id="SensorsBlockedForUrlsDesc">Deny access to sensors for URLs from the list</string>
      <string id="SerialAllowAllPortsForUrls">Allow access to all serial ports for URLs from the list</string>
      <string id="SerialAllowAllPortsForUrls_Explain">SerialAllowAllPortsForUrls

The policy sets a list of URLs that are automatically granted access to all serial ports.

The policy supersedes DefaultSerialGuardSetting, SerialAskForUrls, and SerialBlockedForUrls.

Features

- This is an increased security policy. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/deployment/windows/setting-policy#advanced

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: The value of the DefaultSerialGuardSetting policy is used (if it is set).
- Enabled: The administrator sets the list of URLs. You can only use valid URLs.

Convert non-Latin URLs (for example, яндекс.рф) via punycode: https://www.reg.ru/web-tools/punycode

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example value:
https://www.example.com
https://server:8080/path

Safety recommendations

Value: Disabled. Restrict access requests to serial ports. Malicious sites can use them to access connected devices. We recommend disabling access to serial ports in the DefaultSerialGuardSetting policy. We also recommend disabling or not setting the SerialAskForUrls, SerialBlockedForUrls and SerialAllowAllPortsForUrls policies.

Possible problems. Sites that use serial ports may not work correctly.</string>
      <string id="SerialAllowAllPortsForUrlsDesc">Allow access to all serial ports for URLs from the list</string>
      <string id="SerialAllowUsbDevicesForUrls">Set a list of URLs and allowed USB devices with a serial interface</string>
      <string id="SerialAllowUsbDevicesForUrls_Explain">SerialAllowUsbDevicesForUrls

The policy sets a list of URLs that are allowed to access the specified USB devices with a serial interface.

Each list item should include the "devices" and "urls" fields. In the "devices" field, you can set the "vendor_id" and "product_id" IDs. If "vendor_id" is not set, the rule applies to all devices. If "product_id" is not set, the policy applies to all devices with the specified "vendor_id". The rule is ignored if only "product_id" is specified and "vendor_id" is missing.

The policy supersedes DefaultSerialGuardSetting, SerialAskForUrls, and SerialBlockedForUrls.

This policy only affects access to USB devices via the Web Serial API. To configure access to USB devices via the WebUSB API, use the WebUsbAllowDevicesForUrls policy.

- Not Configured, Disabled: The value of the DefaultSerialGuardSetting policy is used (if it is set).
- Enabled: The administrator sets the list of URLs and devices. 

Convert non-Latin URLs (for example, яндекс.рф) via punycode: https://www.reg.ru/web-tools/punycode

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example value:

[
    {
      "devices": [
        {
          "product_id": 5678,
          "vendor_id": 1234
        }
      ],
      "urls": [
        "https://example.com"
      ]
    },
    {
      "devices": [
        {
          "vendor_id": 1234
        }
      ],
      "urls": [
        "https://sample.net"
      ]
    }
  ]</string>
      <string id="SerialAskForUrls">Allow access to serial ports for URLs from the list</string>
      <string id="SerialAskForUrls_Explain">SerialAskForUrls

The policy sets a list of URLs that can request access to the device's serial ports.

The policy supersedes DefaultSerialGuardSetting. The SerialBlockedForUrls policy supersedes SerialAskForUrls policy.

Features

- This is an increased security policy. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support2/browser-corporate/ru/deployment/windows/setting-policy#advanced

Values

- Not Configured: The value of the DefaultSerialGuardSetting policy is used (if it is set).
- Disabled: The value is treated as Not Configured.
- Enabled: The administrator sets the list of URLs. You can use URL patterns. The "*" wildcard is only used for subdomains in this form: "[*.]".

For more information about URL templates, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/policy/url-patterns.html

Convert non-Latin URLs (for example, яндекс.рф) via punycode: https://www.reg.ru/web-tools/punycode

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example value:

https://www.example.com
[*.]example.edu

Safety recommendations

Value: Disabled. Restrict access requests to serial ports. Malicious sites can use them to access connected devices. We recommend disabling access to serial ports in the DefaultSerialGuardSetting policy. We also recommend disabling or not setting the SerialAskForUrls and SerialBlockedForUrls policies.

Possible problems. Sites that use serial ports may not work correctly.</string>
      <string id="SerialAskForUrlsDesc">Allow access to serial ports for URLs from the list</string>
      <string id="SerialBlockedForUrls">Prohibit serial port access requests for URLs from the list</string>
      <string id="SerialBlockedForUrls_Explain">SerialBlockedForUrls

The policy sets a list of URLs that can't request access to the device's serial ports. 

The policy supersedes DefaultSerialGuardSetting and SerialAskForUrls. 

Features

- This is an increased security policy. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/deployment/windows/setting-policy#advanced

Values

- Not Configured: The value of the DefaultSerialGuardSetting policy is used (if it is set).
- Disabled: The value is treated as Not Configured.
- Enabled: The administrator sets the list of URLs. You can use URL patterns. The "*" wildcard is only used for subdomains in this form: "[*.]".

For more information about URL templates, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/policy/url-patterns.html

Convert non-Latin URLs (for example, яндекс.рф) via punycode: https://www.reg.ru/web-tools/punycode

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example value:

https://www.example.com
[*.]example.edu

Safety recommendations

Value: Disabled. Restrict access requests to serial ports. Malicious sites can use them to access connected devices. We recommend disabling access to serial ports in the DefaultSerialGuardSetting policy. We also recommend disabling or not setting the SerialAskForUrls and SerialBlockedForUrls policies.

Possible problems. Sites that use serial ports may not work correctly.</string>
      <string id="SerialBlockedForUrlsDesc">Prohibit serial port access requests for URLs from the list</string>
      <string id="WebHidAllowAllDevicesForUrls">Set a list of URLs that automatically connect to HID devices</string>
      <string id="WebHidAllowAllDevicesForUrls_Explain">WebHidAllowAllDevicesForUrls

The policy sets a list of URLs that automatically connect to HID devices.

HID (human interface device) is a class of USB devices for interacting with a person, such as a keyboard, mouse, or game controller.

The policy supersedes DefaultWebHidGuardSetting, WebHidAskForUrls, and WebHidBlockedForUrls.

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: The value of the DefaultWebHidGuardSetting policy is used (if it is set).
- Enabled: The administrator sets the list of URLs. Only the scheme, host, and port are taken into account.

Convert non-Latin URLs (for example, яндекс.рф) via punycode: https://www.reg.ru/web-tools/punycode

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example value:

https://example.com
https://example.org:8080</string>
      <string id="WebHidAllowAllDevicesForUrlsDesc">Set a list of URLs that automatically connect to HID devices</string>
      <string id="WebHidAllowDevicesForUrls">Set a list of URLs and allowed HID devices</string>
      <string id="WebHidAllowDevicesForUrls_Explain">WebHidAllowDevicesForUrls

The policy sets a list of URLs that are allowed to access HID devices with the specified vendor and product IDs.

HID (human interface device) is a class of USB devices for interacting with a person, such as a keyboard, mouse, or game controller.

Each list item should include the "devices" and "urls" fields. In the "devices" field, the "vendor_id" is required, while the "product_id" is optional. If "product_id" is not set, the policy applies to all devices with the specified "vendor_id". The rule is ignored if only "product_id" is specified and "vendor_id" is missing.

The policy supersedes DefaultWebHidGuardSetting, WebHidAskForUrls, and WebHidBlockedForUrls.

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: The value of the DefaultWebHidGuardSetting policy is used (if it is set).
- Enabled: The administrator sets the list of URLs and devices.

Convert non-Latin URLs (for example, яндекс.рф) via punycode: https://www.reg.ru/web-tools/punycode

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example value:

[
  {
    "devices": [
      {
        "product_id": 5678,
        "vendor_id": 1234
      }
    ],
    "urls": [
      "https://example.com",
      "https://sample.net"
    ]
  }
]</string>
      <string id="WebHidAllowDevicesWithHidUsagesForUrls">Set a list of URLs and allowed HID devices from the HID collection</string>
      <string id="WebHidAllowDevicesWithHidUsagesForUrls_Explain">WebHidAllowDevicesWithHidUsagesForUrls

The policy sets a list of URLs that are allowed to access HID devices from the HID collection.

HID (human interface device) is a class of USB devices for interacting with a person, such as a keyboard, mouse, or game controller.

The HID collection groups HID devices by usage types.

For more information about HID collections, see https://learn.microsoft.com/ru-ru/windows-hardware/drivers/hid/top-level-collections

Each list item should include the "usages" and "urls" fields. In the "usages" field, the "usage_page" ID is required, while the "usage" ID is optional. If the "usage" field is not set, the rule applies to all devices contained by the HID collection for the specified "usage_page". The rule is ignored if only "usage" is specified and "usage_page" is missing.

The policy supersedes DefaultWebHidGuardSetting, WebHidAskForUrls, and WebHidBlockedForUrls.

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: The value of the DefaultWebHidGuardSetting policy is used (if it is set).
- Enabled: The administrator sets a list of URLs and devices.

Convert non-Latin URLs (for example, яндекс.рф) via punycode: https://www.reg.ru/web-tools/punycode

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example value:

[
  {
    "urls": [
      "https://example.com",
      "https://sample.net"
    ],
    "usages": [
      {
        "usage": 5678,
        "usage_page": 1234
      }
    ]
  }
]</string>
      <string id="WebHidAskForUrls">Set a list of URLs that are allowed to request access to HID devices</string>
      <string id="WebHidAskForUrls_Explain">WebHidAskForUrls

The policy sets a list of URLs that are allowed to request access to HID devices.

HID (human interface device) is a class of USB devices for interacting with a person, such as a keyboard, mouse, or game controller.

The policy supersedes DefaultWebHidGuardSetting. The WebHidAllowAllDevicesForUrls, WebHidAllowDevicesForUrls, WebHidAllowDevicesWithHidUsagesForUrls, and WebHidBlockedForUrls policies supersede WebHidAskForUrls.

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: The value of the DefaultWebHidGuardSetting policy is used (if it is set).
- Enabled: The administrator sets the list of URLs. You can use URL patterns. The "*" wildcard is not supported. 

For more information about URL templates, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/policy/url-patterns.html

Convert non-Latin URLs (for example, яндекс.рф) via punycode: https://www.reg.ru/web-tools/punycode

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example value:

https://example.com
https://sample.net</string>
      <string id="WebHidAskForUrlsDesc">Set a list of URLs that are allowed to request access to HID devices</string>
      <string id="WebHidBlockedForUrls">Set a list of URLs that cannot request access to HID devices</string>
      <string id="WebHidBlockedForUrls_Explain">WebHidBlockedForUrls

The policy sets a list of URLs that are not allowed to request access to HID devices.

HID (human interface device) is a class of USB devices for interacting with a person, such as a keyboard, mouse, or game controller.

The policy supersedes DefaultWebHidGuardSetting and WebHidAskForUrls. The WebHidAllowAllDevicesForUrls, WebHidAllowDevicesForUrls, and WebHidAllowDevicesWithHidUsagesForUrls policies supersede WebHidBlockedForUrls.

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: The value of the DefaultWebHidGuardSetting policy is used (if it is set).
- Enabled: The administrator sets the list of URLs. You can use URL patterns. The "*" wildcard is not supported. 

For more information about URL templates, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/policy/url-patterns.html

Convert non-Latin URLs (for example, яндекс.рф) via punycode: https://www.reg.ru/web-tools/punycode

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example value:

https://example.com
https://sample.net</string>
      <string id="WebHidBlockedForUrlsDesc">Set a list of URLs that cannot request access to HID devices</string>
      <string id="WebUsbAllowDevicesForUrls">Set a list of URLs and allowed USB devices</string>
      <string id="WebUsbAllowDevicesForUrls_Explain">WebUsbAllowDevicesForUrls

The policy sets a list of URLs that are allowed to access USB devices with the specified vendor and product IDs.

Each list item should include the "devices" and "urls" fields. In the "devices" field, you can set the "vendor_id" and "product_id" IDs. If "vendor_id" is not set, the rule applies to all devices. If "product_id" is not set, the policy applies to all devices with the specified "vendor_id". The rule is ignored if only "product_id" is specified and "vendor_id" is missing.

The policy supersedes DefaultWebUsbGuardSetting, WebUsbAskForUrls, and WebUsbBlockedForUrls.

The policy only affects access to USB devices via the WebUSB API. To configure access to USB devices via the Web Serial API, use the SerialAllowUsbDevicesForUrls policy.

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: The value of the DefaultWebUsbGuardSetting policy is used (if it is set).
- Enabled: The administrator sets the list of URLs and devices.

Convert non-Latin URLs (for example, яндекс.рф) via punycode: https://www.reg.ru/web-tools/punycode

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example value:

[
  {
    "devices": [
      {
        "product_id": 5678,
        "vendor_id": 1234
      }
    ],
    "urls": [
      "https://example.com"
    ]
  }
]</string>
      <string id="WebUsbAskForUrls">Allow USB access requests for URLs from the list</string>
      <string id="WebUsbAskForUrls_Explain">WebUsbAskForUrls

The policy allows requests to access USB devices to URLs from the list.

The policy takes precedence over the "Access to your USB devices" setting. The setting is not disabled, but its value is ignored for URLs from the list. To go to the settings, in the Browser, click "Main Menu" → "Settings" → "Websites" → "Advanced site settings" and select it.

The policy supersedes DefaultWebUsbGuardSetting policy. The WebUsbBlockedForUrls supersedes WebUsbAskForUrls.

Features

- This is an increased security policy. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/deployment/windows/setting-policy#advanced

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: The value of the DefaultWebUsbGuardSetting policy is used (if it is set). Users can change access settings if the DefaultWebUsbGuardSetting policy is not set.
- Enabled: The administrator sets a list of URLs for which USB access requests are allowed. Users can change the setting, but its value will be ignored. You can use URL patterns.

For more information about URL templates, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/policy/url-patterns.html

Convert non-Latin URLs (for example, яндекс.рф) via punycode: https://www.reg.ru/web-tools/punycode

Example value:

https://www.example.com
[*.]example.edu

Safety recommendations

Value: Disabled. Assess the risks. If your organization doesn't really need USB devices, we recommend restricting access to them in the DefaultWebUsbGuardSetting policy. We also recommend disabling or not setting the WebUsbAskForUrls and WebUsbBlockedForUrls policies.

WebUSB can be used for phishing attacks that can bypass two-factor authentication hardware devices.

Possible problems. Sites won't be able to use connected USB devices like tokens, headphones, and webcams.</string>
      <string id="WebUsbAskForUrlsDesc">Allow USB access requests for URLs from the list</string>
      <string id="WebUsbBlockedForUrls">Prohibit requests for access to USB devices for URLs from the list</string>
      <string id="WebUsbBlockedForUrls_Explain">WebUsbBlockedForUrls

The policy prohibits requests for access to USB devices by URLs from the list.

The policy supersedes over the "Access to your USB devices" setting. The setting is not disabled, but its value is ignored for URLs from the list. To go to the settings, in the Browser, click "Main Menu" → "Settings" → "Websites" → "Advanced site settings" and select it.

The policy supersedes DefaultWebUsbGuardSetting and WebUsbAskForUrls.

Features

- This is an increased security policy. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/deployment/windows/setting-policy#advanced

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: The value of the DefaultWebUsbGuardSetting policy is used (if it is set). Users can change access settings if the DefaultWebUsbGuardSetting policy is not set.
- Enabled: The administrator sets a list of URLs for which USB access requests are prohibited. Users can change the setting, but its value will be ignored. You can use URL patterns.

For more information about URL templates, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/policy/url-patterns.html

Convert non-Latin URLs (for example, яндекс.рф) via punycode: https://www.reg.ru/web-tools/punycode

Example value:

https://www.example.com
[*.]example.edu

Safety recommendations

Value: Disabled. Assess the risks. If your organization doesn't really need USB devices, we recommend restricting access to them in the DefaultWebUsbGuardSetting policy. We also recommend disabling or not setting the WebUsbAskForUrls and WebUsbBlockedForUrls policies.

WebUSB can be used for phishing attacks that can bypass two-factor authentication hardware devices.

Possible problems. Sites won't be able to use connected USB devices like tokens, headphones, and webcams.</string>
      <string id="WebUsbBlockedForUrlsDesc">Prohibit requests for access to USB devices for URLs from the list</string>
      <string id="WindowManagementAllowedForUrls">Allow URLs from the list to manage windows</string>
      <string id="WindowManagementAllowedForUrls_Explain">WindowManagementAllowedForUrls

The policy sets a list of URLs that are allowed to manage windows.

The policy supersedes DefaultWindowManagementSetting. The WindowManagementBlockedForUrls policy supersedes WindowManagementAllowedForUrls.

Values

