- Enabled: The administrator sets the list of URLs that are allowed to manage windows. You can use URL patterns. The "*" wildcard is only used for subdomains in this form: "[*.]".

For more information about URL templates, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/policy/url-patterns.html

Convert non-Latin URLs (for example, яндекс.рф) via punycode: https://www.reg.ru/web-tools/punycode

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example value:

https://www.example.com
[*.]example.edu</string>
      <string id="WindowManagementAllowedForUrlsDesc">Allow URLs from the list to manage windows</string>
      <string id="WindowManagementBlockedForUrls">Prevent URLs from the list from managing windows</string>
      <string id="WindowManagementBlockedForUrls_Explain">WindowManagementBlockedForUrls

The policy sets a list of URLs that are not allowed to manage windows. 

The policy supersedes DefaultWindowManagementSetting and WindowManagementAllowedForUrls.

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: The value of the DefaultWindowManagementSetting policy is used (if it is set).
- Enabled: The administrator sets the list of URLs that are not allowed to manage windows. You can use URL patterns. The "*" wildcard is only used for subdomains in this form: "[*.]".

For more information about URL templates, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/policy/url-patterns.html

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example value:

https://www.example.com
[*.]example.edu</string>
      <string id="WindowManagementBlockedForUrlsDesc">Prevent URLs from the list from managing windows</string>
      <string id="YandexRegisteredProtocolHandlers">Manage protocol handlers</string>
      <string id="YandexRegisteredProtocolHandlers_Explain">YandexRegisteredProtocolHandlers

The policy controls the settings of users' protocol handlers and can overwrite existing settings.

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled — the policy is not set.
- Enabled — the administrator sets a list of settings in JSON format:
- override_user — interaction with existing user settings:
- true — completely overwrite settings;
          - false — add settings to the list.
     - allowed — array of allowed protocols:
- default — whether to use by default:
               - true — yes;
               - false — no;
          - protocol — the name of the protocol;
          - url — The URL of the resource associated with the protocol, where "%s" is the content of the request.
     - ignored — array of ignored protocols:
- protocol — protocol name;
          - url — The URL of the resource associated with the protocol, where "%s" is the content of the request.

Convert URLs without Latin letters (for example, яндекс.рф) via punycode: https://www.reg.ru/web-tools/punycode

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example of a value:

{
  "override_user": true,
  "allowed": [
    {
      "default": true,
      "protocol": "mailto",
      "url": "https://example.com/%s"
    },
    {
      "default": true,
      "protocol": "tg",
      "url": "https://example.com/%s"
    }],
  "ignored": [
    {
      "protocol": "webcal",
      "url": "https://example.com/%s"
    }]
}</string>
      <string id="AutoLaunchProtocolsFromOrigins">Set a list of protocols for launching external applications without a request</string>
      <string id="AutoLaunchProtocolsFromOrigins_Explain">AutoLaunchProtocolsFromOrigins

The policy sets a list of protocols that can run an external application from the listed sources without sending a request to the user.

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled — no protocols can run external applications without sending a request to the user
- Enabled — the administrator sets a list of protocols in JSON format:
     - allowed_origins — an external application to be launched.
     - protocol — the protocol that runs the external application.

You can use the wildcard «*» and URL templates.

Learn more about URL templates: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/policy/url-patterns.html

Convert URLs without Latin letters (for example, yandex.Russian Federation) via punycode: https://www.reg.ru/web-tools/punycode

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example of a value:

[
  {
    "allowed_origins": [
      "example.com",
      "http://www.example.com:8080"
    ],
    "protocol": "spotify"
  },
  {
    "allowed_origins": [
      "https://example.com",
      "https://.mail.example.com"
    ],
    "protocol": "teams"
  },
  {
    "allowed_origins": [
      "*"
    ],
    "protocol": "outlook"
  }
]</string>
      <string id="Kiosk_group">Kiosk Mode Settings</string>
      <string id="RestrictedKioskModeHash">Set a password hash in SHA1 format to disable kiosk mode</string>
      <string id="RestrictedKioskModeHash_Explain">RestrictedKioskModeHash

The policy sets a password hash in SHA1 format to disable kiosk restricted mode. Users can move the mouse pointer to the upper-left corner of the screen and enter the specified password. After that, the browser will restart normally with an empty list of pages. The difference from the RestrictedKioskModePassword policy is that the password is checked using a hash.

The policy only works if the RestrictedKioskModeUrls policy is set.

Only one of the policies can be set at a time — RestrictedKioskModePassword or RestrictedKioskModeHash, otherwise both policies will be disabled.

Features

- It only works in the extended version of the Browser for organizations.

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: the password hash is not set, kiosk mode can be disabled only by the RestrictedKioskModeUrls policy, or by setting the RestrictedKioskModePassword policy.
- Enabled: the administrator sets the password hash to disable kiosk mode.

Example value: A9E23E621FF9CA8645174205B7247C1E393B2BB0</string>
      <string id="RestrictedKioskModePassword">Set a password to disable kiosk mode</string>
      <string id="RestrictedKioskModePassword_Explain">Restricted Kiosk Mode Password

The policy sets a password to disable the restricted kiosk mode. Users can point to the upper-left corner of the screen and enter the specified password, after which the browser will restart normally with an empty list of pages.

The policy only works when the RestrictedKioskModeUrls policy is enabled.

Only one of the policies can be set at a time — RestrictedKioskModePassword or RestrictedKioskModeHash, otherwise both policies will be disabled.

The policy is available for Browsers version 24.6.4 and higher.

Features

- Available in the mobile version of the Browser for organizations. More details: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html
- It only works in the extended version of the Browser for organizations. Learn more: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: no password is set, kiosk mode can be disabled only by the RestrictedKioskModeUrls policy, or by setting the RestrictedKioskModeHash policy.
- Enabled: the administrator sets a password to disable kiosk mode.

Example value: P@ssw0rd</string>
      <string id="RestrictedKioskModeUrls">Set URL for kiosk mode</string>
      <string id="RestrictedKioskModeUrls_Explain">RestrictedKioskModeUrls

The policy includes a limited kiosk mode, in which the Browser starts in full-screen mode with the opening of a given site. In kiosk mode, users have a number of restrictions enabled:
- navigation takes place on one page, new tabs or browser windows do not open.;
- The browser cannot be minimized or closed;
- login to Browser settings is disabled;
- internal pages are disabled (for example, "browser://policy");
- it is impossible to exit fullscreen mode;
- can't switch to another window;
- mouse gestures are disabled.

By specifying multiple URLs in the policy, you can also set up a multi-domain kiosk mode with additional restrictions.:
- a preset set of tabs is available, which is determined by policy; they cannot be closed, but they can be swapped and switched between them.;
- simplified interface for working with preset tabs:
     - there is no close button on the tabs;
     - there is no button to open a new tab, Browser menu, minimize and close window buttons.;
     - in the Smart Line, the input field is read—only;
- only the zoom and page search functions are available in the page menu.;
- only extensions pre-installed by the administrator are allowed.;
- there are no downloads if they are prohibited;
- the sidebar is missing;
- the bookmarks bar is only available if you enable it using the Bookmark Bar Enabled policy; bookmarks cannot be changed or opened in new tabs or windows.

To exit kiosk mode, you can set a password with the RestrictedKioskModePassword policy.

Attention: on Windows, the keyboard shortcut Ctrl+Alt+Del is available, which, if necessary, can be disabled using the operating system.

The policy is available for Browsers version 24.6.4 and higher.

Features

- Available in the mobile version of the Browser for organizations. More details: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html
- It only works in the extended version of the Browser for organizations. Learn more: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: Kiosk mode is disabled, the browser is running normally.
- Enabled: Kiosk mode is enabled, the administrator sets the URL (or URLs) that open when the Browser is started.

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example of a value:

https://example.com
or
["https://example.com ", "https://example.org "]</string>
      <string id="RestrictedKioskModeUrlsDesc">Set URL for kiosk mode</string>
      <string id="CertificateManagement_group">Certificate management</string>
      <string id="CACertificates">Set a list of trusted certificates</string>
      <string id="CACertificates_Explain">CACertificates

The policy sets a list of trusted certificates.

Only the root certificate can be added to the list of trusted certificates.

The CADistrustedCertificates policy takes precedence over the CACertificates policy.

The policy is available for Browsers version 26.4.4 and higher.

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: Yandex Browser uses a system set of trusted certificates. When you try to open a website with an untrusted certificate, a warning appears.
- Enabled: The administrator sets a list of trusted TLS certificates. Sites with certificates from the list open without warning if all other checks have been passed for them (expiration date, hostname match, etc.).

The value of the policy is X.509 certificate in Base64 format.

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Value example:

[
  "MIICCTCCAY...cRLInUue4X"
]</string>
      <string id="CACertificatesDesc">Set a list of trusted certificates</string>
      <string id="CADistrustedCertificates">Set a list of untrusted certificates</string>
      <string id="CADistrustedCertificates_Explain">CADistrustedCertificates

The policy sets a list of untrusted certificates.

Only the root certificate can be added to the list of untrusted certificates.

The CADistrustedCertificates policy takes precedence over the CACertificates policy.

The policy is available for Browsers version 26.4.4 and higher.

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: Yandex Browser uses a system set of trusted certificates. Sites with trusted certificates open without warning.
- Enabled: The administrator sets a list of untrusted TLS certificates. When you try to open a website with a certificate from the list, a warning appears.

The value of the policy is X.509 certificate in Base64 format. Certificates are compared by the SPKI value (SubjectPublicKeyInfo).

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example value:

[
  "MIIB/TCCAa...qokzUg0mAb"
]</string>
      <string id="CADistrustedCertificatesDesc">Set a list of untrusted certificates</string>
      <string id="CAHintCertificates">Set a list of Intermediate Certificates</string>
      <string id="CAHintCertificates_Explain">CAHintCertificates

The policy sets a list of Intermediate Certificates. Intermediate Certificates are not considered trusted, but can be used by Yandex Browser when building a TLS server certificate chain.

The policy is available for Browsers version 26.4.4 and higher.

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: Yandex Browser uses a system set of trusted certificates. When you try to open a website with an untrusted certificate, a warning appears.
- Enabled: The administrator sets a list of Intermediate Certificates. If they are used to obtain a complete chain up to a trusted root certificate, the site opens without warning.

The value of the policy is X.509 certificate in Base64 format.

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example value:

[
  "MIIFljCCA3.../FsRC6UfTd"
]</string>
      <string id="CAHintCertificatesDesc">Set a list of Intermediate Certificates</string>
      <string id="NativeMessaging_group">Native apps</string>
      <string id="NativeMessagingAllowlist">Allow hosts to exchange messages with native apps</string>
      <string id="NativeMessagingAllowlist_Explain">NativeMessagingAllowlist

The policy sets the list of hosts that are allowed to message with native applications.

The policy supersedes NativeMessagingBlocklist.

Features

- This is an increased security policy. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support2/browser-corporate/ru/deployment/windows/setting-policy#advanced

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: All hosts are allowed except those restricted by the NativeMessagingBlocklist policy.
- Enabled: The administrator sets the list of allowed hosts.

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example value:

com.native.messaging.host.name1
com.native.messaging.host.name2

Safety recommendations

Value: Enabled. Set the "*" value in the NativeMessagingBlocklist policy and specify the allowed hosts in the NativeMessagingAllowlistpolicy.

Possible problems. An enabled extension that can't interact with its internal code behaves unpredictably. The number of technical support requests may increase.</string>
      <string id="NativeMessagingAllowlistDesc">Allow hosts to exchange messages with native apps</string>
      <string id="NativeMessagingBlocklist">Prohibit hosts from exchanging messages with native apps</string>
      <string id="NativeMessagingBlocklist_Explain">NativeMessagingBlocklist

The policy sets the list of hosts that are blocked from messaging with native applications.

The NativeMessagingAllowlist policy supersedes NativeMessagingBlocklist.

Features

- This is an increased security policy. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support2/browser-corporate/ru/deployment/windows/setting-policy#advanced

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: All hosts are allowed.
- Enabled: The administrator sets the list of blocked hosts. "*" disables all hosts.

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example value:

com.native.messaging.host.name1
com.native.messaging.host.name2

Safety recommendations

Value: Enabled. Set the "*" value in the NativeMessagingBlocklist policy and specify the allowed hosts in the NativeMessagingAllowlist policy.

Possible problems. An enabled extension that can't interact with its internal code behaves unpredictably. The number of technical support requests may increase.</string>
      <string id="NativeMessagingBlocklistDesc">Block native messaging hosts</string>
      <string id="NativeMessagingUserLevelHosts">Allow native messaging hosts at the user level</string>
      <string id="NativeMessagingUserLevelHosts_Explain">NativeMessagingUserLevelHosts

The policy allows native messaging hosts at the user level. 

Native user-level applications are installed in the user profile (in Windows, for example, in %userprofile%/AppData). Native system-level applications are installed outside of user profiles and are available to everyone (in Windows, for example, in C:\Program Files).

Values

- Not Configured, Enabled: User-level hosts are allowed, system-level hosts are allowed.
- Disabled: User-level hosts are restricted, system-level hosts are allowed.</string>
      <string id="Printing_group">Print</string>
      <string id="YandexPrintRestrictions">Restrict printing to printers from the list</string>
      <string id="YandexPrintRestrictions_Explain">YandexPrintRestrictions

Restrict printing to printers from the list.

The policy sets a list of printers on which printing is allowed or prohibited.

Features

- Works only in the extended version of the Browser for organizations. More details: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: printing is allowed, the system print dialog is available.
- Enabled:  the system print dialog is blocked, printing is available only through the Browser print dialog. The administrator sets the parameters:
    - allow: list of allowed printers;
    - deny: list of prohibited printers.

You can use the wildcard "*" in printer names.

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example of a value:

{
  "printers": {
    "allow": [
      "*PDF*"
    ],
    "deny": [
      "*Microsoft Print to PDF*"
    ]
  }
}</string>
      <string id="DefaultPrintingSettings">Set print mode</string>
      <string id="DefaultPrintingSettings_Explain">DefaultPrintingSettings

The policy restricts or allows printing on all sites.

The PrintingAllowedForUrls and PrintingBlockedForUrls policies supersede DefaultPrintingSettings.

Features

- This is an increased security policy. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support2/browser-corporate/ru/deployment/windows/setting-policy#advanced
- Available in the mobile version of Yandex Browser for organizations. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html
- Works only in the extended version of Yandex Browser for organizations. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: Printing is allowed.
- Enabled: The administrator sets the print mode:
     - Allowed.
     - Prohibited.

Security recommendations

Value: Enabled (Prohibited). Prevent printing to protect against data leakage.</string>
      <string id="DefaultPrintingSettings_AllowPrintng">Allowed</string>
      <string id="DefaultPrintingSettings_BlockPrinting">Prohibited</string>
      <string id="PrintingAllowedForUrls">Allow printing for URLs from the list</string>
      <string id="PrintingAllowedForUrls_Explain">PrintingAllowedForUrls

The policy sets a list of URLs where printing is allowed.

The policy supersedes DefaultPrintingSettings and PrintingBlockedForUrls.

Features

- Available in the mobile version of Yandex Browser for organizations. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html
- Works only in the extended version of Yandex Browser for organizations. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: The value of the DefaultPrintingSetting policy is used (if it is set).
- Enabled: The administrator sets the list of URLs. You can use URL templates.

For more information about URL templates, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/policy/url-patterns.html

Convert non-Latin URLs (for example, яндекс.рф) via punycode: https://www.reg.ru/web-tools/punycode

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example value:

https://www.example.com
[*.]example.edu</string>
      <string id="PrintingAllowedForUrlsDesc">Allow printing for URLs from the list</string>
      <string id="PrintingBlockedForUrls">Prohibit printing for URLs from the list</string>
      <string id="PrintingBlockedForUrls_Explain">PrintingBlockedForUrls

The policy sets a list of URLs where printing is restricted.

The policy supersedes DefaultPrintingSettings. The PrintingAllowedForUrls policy supersedes PrintingBlockedForUrls.

Features

- Available in the mobile version of Yandex Browser for organizations. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html
- Works only in the extended version of Yandex Browser for organizations. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: The value of the DefaultPrintingSetting policy is used (if it is set).
- Enabled: The administrator sets the list of URLs. You can use URL templates.

For more information about URL templates, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/policy/url-patterns.html

Convert non-Latin URLs (for example, яндекс.рф) via punycode: https://www.reg.ru/web-tools/punycode

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example value:

https://www.example.com
[*.]example.edu</string>
      <string id="PrintingBlockedForUrlsDesc">Prohibit printing for URLs from the list</string>
      <string id="PrintingEnabled">Enable print mode</string>
      <string id="PrintingEnabled_Explain">PrintingEnabled

The policy enables print mode.

The policy governs printing methods:
- "Print" button in the page menu;
- "Print" button in the context menu;
- Ctrl + P and Ctrl + Shift + P keyboard shortcuts.

To go to the "Print" button in the page menu, in the Browser's Smart Bar, click "Page Menu" → "Print".

The PrintingEnabled policy takes precedence over the PrintingAllowedForUrls policy.

The PrintingBlockedForUrls policy takes precedence over the PrintingEnabled policy. 

Of the DefaultPrintingSettings and PrintingEnabled policies, the one that prohibits printing takes precedence. If the DefaultPrintingSettings policy takes precedence over the PrintingEnabled policy, then the PrintingAllowedForUrls policy has the highest priority.

Features

- Available in the mobile Browser version for organizations. Learn more: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html

Values

- Not Configured, Enabled — buttons are enabled, printing is allowed.
- Disabled — the buttons are disabled, printing is prohibited.</string>
      <string id="DefaultSearchProvider_group">The default search engine</string>
      <string id="DefaultSearchProviderAlternateURLs">Set a list of additional URLs for the default search engine</string>
      <string id="DefaultSearchProviderAlternateURLs_Explain">DefaultSearchProviderAlternateURLs

The policy sets a list of additional URLs for the default search engine. To extract queries from the search engine, the URL must contain the string '{searchTerms}'.

The policy only works when the DefaultSearchProviderEnabled policy is enabled.

Features

- It only works on Windows and macOS if it is set inside the domain or via the Management Console.
- It only works in the extended version of the Browser for organizations. Learn more: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled — additional URLsThe 's are not set.
- Enabled — the administrator sets a list of additional URLs that are used for search.

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example of the value:

https://example.com/suggest#q={searchTerms}
https://example.net/suggest/search#q={searchTerms}</string>
      <string id="DefaultSearchProviderAlternateURLsDesc">Set a list of additional URLs for the default search engine</string>
      <string id="DefaultSearchProviderEnabled">Enable the default search engine</string>
      <string id="DefaultSearchProviderEnabled_Explain">DefaultSearchProviderEnabled

The policy includes a search engine by default. You can set the default search engine using the DefaultSearchProviderSearchURL policy.

The list of search engines can be viewed on the settings page: browser://settings/searchEngines

Features

- In Windows and macOS, works only within the domain.
- It only works in the extended version of the Browser for organizations. Learn more: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html

Values

- Not Configured — users can set the default search engine themselves.
- Enabled — the administrator sets the default search engine. Users cannot change it.
- Disabled — the search engine is disabled by default. When you enter text in the Smart Bar, the search is not performed.</string>
      <string id="DefaultSearchProviderEncodings">Set default encodings for the search engine</string>
      <string id="DefaultSearchProviderEncodings_Explain">DefaultSearchProviderEncodings

The policy defines character encodings that are supported by the search engine by default, for example UTF-8, GB2312, ISO-8859-1. They are checked in the specified order.

The policy only works when the Default Search Provider Enabled policy is enabled.

Features

- In Windows and macOS, works only within the domain.
- It only works in the extended version of the Browser for organizations. Learn more: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: UTF-8 encoding is used.
- Enabled: the administrator sets the default character encoding for the search engine.

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example of the value:

UTF-8
UTF-16
GB2312
ISO-8859-1</string>
      <string id="DefaultSearchProviderEncodingsDesc">Set default encodings for the search engine</string>
      <string id="DefaultSearchProviderImageURL">Set the default URL of the search engine for images</string>
      <string id="DefaultSearchProviderImageURL_Explain">DefaultSearchProviderImageURL

The policy sets the default URL of the search engine for images. Image search is performed using the GET method. 

The policy only works when the DefaultSearchProviderEnabled policy is enabled.

To extract queries from a search engine, the URL can contain the following strings:
- «{example:imageURL}» — the URL of the image.
- «{example:imageOriginalHeight}» — the original height of the image in pixels.
- «{example:imageOriginalWidth}» — the original width of the image in pixels.
- «{example:processedImageDimensions}» — resized image (for example, the image was reduced).
- «{example:imageSearchSource}» — the site where the image is hosted.
- «{example:imageThumbnail}» — the URL of the thumbnail copy of the image.
- «{example:imageThumbnailBase64}» — a scaled—down copy of the image in Base64 format.

Features

- It only works on Windows and macOS if it is set inside the domain or via the Management Console.
- It only works in the extended version of the Browser for organizations. Learn more: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled — The URL of the image search engine is not set by default. The default search engine is used to search for images.
- Enabled — the administrator sets the default URL of the search engine for images. 

Example of the value: 

https://example.com/searchbyimage/upload</string>
      <string id="DefaultSearchProviderImageURLPostParams">Set parameters for POST requests when searching for images</string>
      <string id="DefaultSearchProviderImageURLPostParams_Explain">DefaultSearchProviderImageURLPostparams

The policy specifies a list of parameters used in POST queries when searching for images.

The policy only works when the DefaultSearchProviderEnabled policy is enabled.

Features

- On Windows and macOS, it only works if it is set inside the domain or through the management console.
- It only works in the extended version of the Browser for organizations. Learn more: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: the GET method is used for image search queries.
- Enabled: the administrator sets a list of POST request parameters. The list consists of name-value pairs separated by commas. If a template parameter is specified as the value (for example, "{imageThumbnail}"), it is replaced with the actual data. The image parameter in the URL must be specified using a valid combination of the following placeholders (their list depends on the search service provider):
     - {yandex:imageURL}
     - {yandex:imageOriginalHeight}
     - {yandex:imageOriginalWidth}
     - {yandex:processedImageDimensions}
     - {yandex:imageSearchSource}
     - {yandex:imageThumbnail}
     - {yandex:imageThumbnailBase64}

Example of a value:

content={yandex:imageThumbnail},url={yandex:imageURL},sbisrc={yandex:imageSearchSource}</string>
      <string id="DefaultSearchProviderKeyword">Set the default search engine keyword</string>
      <string id="DefaultSearchProviderKeyword_Explain">DefaultSearchProviderKeyword

The policy sets the default search engine keyword.

The policy only works when the DefaultSearchProviderEnabled policy is enabled.

Features

- In Windows and macOS, works only within the domain.
- It only works in the extended version of the Browser for organizations. Learn more: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled — the keyword is not set, the search engine is not activated using it.
- Enabled — the administrator sets a keyword, the search engine starts searching when it is entered into the Smart bar.

Example of a policy value: 

mis</string>
      <string id="DefaultSearchProviderName">Set the default name of the search engine</string>
      <string id="DefaultSearchProviderName_Explain">DefaultSearchProviderName

The policy sets the default name of the search engine.

The policy only works when the DefaultSearchProviderEnabled policy is enabled.

Features

- In Windows and macOS, works only within the domain.
- It only works in the extended version of the Browser for organizations. Learn more: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: the name of the search engine is not specified. The hostname specified in the search query URL is used.
- Enabled: the administrator sets the name of the search engine.

Example of a value:

My Intranet Search</string>
      <string id="DefaultSearchProviderSearchURL">Set the default search engine URL</string>
      <string id="DefaultSearchProviderSearchURL_Explain">DefaultSearchProviderSearchURL

The policy sets the default URL of the search engine. The URL must contain the string '{searchTerms}', which is replaced with the user's text when sending the request.

The policy only works when the DefaultSearchProviderEnabled policy is enabled.

The list of search engines can be viewed on the settings page: browser://settings/searchEngines

Features

- In Windows and macOS, works only within the domain.
- It only works in the extended version of the Browser for organizations. Learn more: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled — users can set the default search engine themselves.
- Enabled — the administrator sets the search engine, users cannot change it.



Example of a policy value: 

https://example.com/search?q={searchTerms}</string>
      <string id="DefaultSearchProviderSearchURLPostParams">Set the default parameters of POST requests to the search engine</string>
      <string id="DefaultSearchProviderSearchURLPostParams_Explain">DefaultSearchProviderSearchURLPostParams

The policy sets a list of parameters used in search POST requests.

The policy only works when the DefaultSearchProviderEnabled policy is enabled.

Features

- It works on Windows and macOS only if it is set inside the domain or via the Management Console.
- It only works in the extended version of the Browser for organizations. Learn more: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: the GET method is used for search queries.
- Enabled: the administrator sets a list of POST request parameters. The list consists of name-value pairs separated by commas. If a template parameter is specified as the value (for example, "{searchTerms}"), it is replaced with the actual data.

Example of the value:

q={searchTerms},ie=utf-8,oe=utf-8</string>
      <string id="DefaultSearchProviderSuggestURL">Set the default search engine URL for requesting suggestions</string>
      <string id="DefaultSearchProviderSuggestURL_Explain">DefaultSearchProviderSuggestURL

The policy sets the default URL of the search engine for requesting suggestions. The URL must contain the string "{searchTerms}", which is replaced with the user's text when sending the request.

The policy only works when the DefaultSearchProviderEnabled policy is enabled.

Features

- In Windows and macOS, works only within the domain.
- It only works in the extended version of the Browser for organizations. Learn more: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: the default search engine is used for suggestions.
- Enabled: the administrator sets the search engine to request suggestions.


Example of a value:

https://search.my.company/suggest?q={searchTerms}</string>
      <string id="DefaultSearchProviderSuggestURLPostParams">Set parameters for POST requests to the search engine for suggestions</string>
      <string id="DefaultSearchProviderSuggestURLPostParams_Explain">DefaultSearchProviderSuggestURLPostParams

The policy sets the parameters of POST requests when accessing the default search engine to search for suggestion options. 

The policy only works when the DefaultSearchProviderEnabled policy is enabled.

Features

- In Windows and macOS, works only within the domain.
- It only works in the extended version of the Browser for organizations. Learn more: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled — the GET method is used for search queries.
- Enabled — the administrator sets a list of POST request parameters. The list consists of name-value pairs separated by commas. If a template parameter is specified as the value (for example, "{searchTerms}"), it is replaced with the actual data.

Example of the value:

q={searchTerms},ie=utf-8,oe=utf-8</string>
      <string id="ScreenCapture_group">Screen capture</string>
      <string id="SameOriginTabCaptureAllowedByOrigins">Set a list of URLs that are allowed to cast tabs only to the same site</string>
      <string id="SameOriginTabCaptureAllowedByOrigins_Explain">SameOriginTabCaptureAllowedByOrigins

The policy sets a list of URLs that are allowed to cast tabs only to the same site. If a web application is open on the casted tab, it is also captured.

The policy supersedes TabCaptureAllowedByOrigins, WindowCaptureAllowedByOrigins, ScreenCaptureAllowedByOrigins, and ScreenCaptureAllowed.

The policy is available for Browsers version 23.9.1 and higher.

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: All tabs can be casted.
- Enabled: The administrator sets the list of URLs. You can use URL templates.

For more information about URL templates, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/policy/url-patterns.html

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example value:

https://www.example.com
[*.]example.edu</string>
      <string id="SameOriginTabCaptureAllowedByOriginsDesc">Set a list of URLs that can cast tabs to the same site only</string>
      <string id="ScreenCaptureAllowed">Allow Screen Capture</string>
      <string id="ScreenCaptureAllowed_Explain">ScreenCaptureAllowed

This policy controls screen capture. You can use a special API to display a tab, Yandex Browser window, or desktop.

The policy is available for Browsers version 23.9.1 and higher.

Features

- This is an increased security policy. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support2/browser-corporate/ru/deployment/windows/setting-policy#advanced

Values

- Not Configured, Enabled: Capture is allowed.
- Disabled: Capture is restricted.

Safety recommendations

Value: Disabled. Disable screen capture. This will prevent the transfer of confidential data that may be on the screen during capture.

Possible problems. Users won't be able to use video conferencing, video, and screen capture APIs.</string>
      <string id="ScreenCaptureAllowedByOrigins">Set a list of URLs that are allowed to capture the screen</string>
      <string id="ScreenCaptureAllowedByOrigins_Explain">ScreenCaptureAllowedByOrigins

The policy sets a list of URLs that can capture the screen.

The policy supersedes ScreenCaptureAllowed. The WindowCaptureAllowedByOrigins, TabCaptureAllowedByOrigins, and SameOriginTabCaptureAllowedByOrigins policies supersede ScreenCaptureAllowedByOrigins.

The policy is available for Browsers version 23.9.1 and higher.

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: Screen capture is allowed for all sites.
- Enabled: The administrator sets the list of URLs. You can use URL templates.

For more information about URL templates, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/policy/url-patterns.html

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example value:

https://www.example.com
[*.]example.edu</string>
      <string id="ScreenCaptureAllowedByOriginsDesc">Set a list of URLs that can capture the screen</string>
      <string id="ScreenshotTakenEventSettings">Set up a security event when taking a screenshot</string>
      <string id="ScreenshotTakenEventSettings_Explain">ScreenshotTakenEventSettings

The policy sets up sending ScreenshotTaken security event if at least one site from the "allow" list was open at the time of the screenshot and the user took a screenshot using programs or Yandex Browser tools.

The policy only works when the YandexSecurityEventConnectorUrl or YandexSecurityEventConnectors policy is enabled.

The policy is available for Browsers version 25.8.4 and higher.

Features

- It only works in the extended version of the Browser for organizations. Learn more: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: the security event is not created.
- Enabled: the administrator sets the parameters:
     - allow: a list of URLs for which the creation of a security event is enabled;
     - deny: a list of URLs for which the creation of a security event is disabled;
     - show_user_dialog: whether to show a screenshot warning. An optional parameter. Values:
          - true: the user is shown a standard warning that the organization has been notified about taking a screenshot. If in the policy YandexDLPDialogs the parameter "screenshot_warning" and a custom message are set, then the text of the custom message is displayed.
          - false: the warning is disabled. The default value.

You can use URL templates. You can use the keyword "internal_urls" to designate all single-domain sites. For example, then https://example it falls under the rule, but https://example.com —No. 

Learn more about URL templates: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/policy/url-patterns.html

Convert URLs without Latin letters (for example, yandex.Russian Federation) via punycode: https://www.reg.ru/web-tools/punycode

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config


Example of the value:

{
  "allow": [
    "[*.]example.org",
    "[*.]yandex.ru",
    "kinopoisk.ru"
  ],
  "deny": [
    "public.example.org"
  ],
  "show_user_dialog": true
}</string>
      <string id="TabCaptureAllowedByOrigins">Set a list of URLs that are allowed to capture tabs</string>
      <string id="TabCaptureAllowedByOrigins_Explain">TabCaptureAllowedByOrigins

The policy sets a list of URLs that are allowed to capture tabs. If a web application is open on the casted tab, it is also captured.

The policy supersedes WindowCaptureAllowedByOrigins, ScreenCaptureAllowedByOrigins, and ScreenCaptureAllowed. The SameOriginTabCaptureAllowedByOrigins policy supersede TabCaptureAllowedByOrigins.

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: Tab capture is allowed for all sites.
- Enabled: The administrator sets the list of URLs. You can use URL templates.

For more information about URL templates, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/policy/url-patterns.html

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example value:

https://www.example.com
[*.]example.edu</string>
      <string id="TabCaptureAllowedByOriginsDesc">Set a list of URLs that can capture tabs</string>
      <string id="WindowCaptureAllowedByOrigins">Set a list of URLs that are allowed to capture windows</string>
      <string id="WindowCaptureAllowedByOrigins_Explain">WindowCaptureAllowedByOrigins

The policy sets a list of URLs that are allowed to capture windows. If a web application is open in the casted window, it is also captured.

The policy supersedes ScreenCaptureAllowedByOrigins and ScreenCaptureAllowed. The TabCaptureAllowedByOrigins and SameOriginTabCaptureAllowedByOrigins policies supersede WindowCaptureAllowedByOrigins.

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: Window capture is allowed for all sites.
- Enabled: The administrator sets the list of URLs. You can use URL templates.

For more information about URL templates, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/policy/url-patterns.html

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example value:

https://www.example.com
[*.]example.edu</string>
      <string id="WindowCaptureAllowedByOriginsDesc">Set a list of URLs that are allowed to capture windows</string>
      <string id="RemovedPolicies_group">Removed Policies</string>
      <string id="DefaultPluginsSetting">Default plugin settings</string>
      <string id="DefaultPluginsSetting_Explain">DefaultPluginsSetting

Allows you to specify whether sites are allowed to run plugins automatically. Auto-launching of plugins can be enabled or disabled for all sites.
Click play allows plugins to start, but the user must click on the plugin.
If these rules are not set, the AllowPlugins parameter will be used and the user can change it.</string>
      <string id="DefaultPluginsSetting_AllowPlugins">Allow automatic launch of the Flash plugin on all sites</string>
      <string id="DefaultPluginsSetting_BlockPlugins">Block Flash plugin</string>
      <string id="DefaultPluginsSetting_ClickToPlay">Click to play</string>
      <string id="YandexNeuroAssistant">Set up the sidebar with Neuro Assistant</string>
      <string id="YandexNeuroAssistant_Explain">YandexNeuroAssistant

The policy sets up a sidebar with split-view Prompty. Before enabling the policy, disable the YandexNeuroEdit policy.

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: the sidebar is disabled.
- Enabled: the administrator sets the parameters in JSON format:
- url — the URL that will open in the sidebar with split-view Prompty. Required parameter.
     - restore_session — whether the session will be restored when the sidebar is opened. An optional parameter. The default value is false.

Example of a value:

{
  "url": "https://example.com",
  "restore_session": false
}</string>
      <string id="URLBlacklist">Blocking access to the URL list</string>
      <string id="URLBlacklist_Explain">URLBlacklist
Blocking access to the specified URL.
Blocks users from accessing web pages from the blacklist.
The list can contain URL templates and local file address templates. Templates for local files have the format "file: / / path", and the path must be absolute. All files whose path starts with the specified prefix are blocked.
URL template format- " scheme:// host: port / path".
If such a scheme exists, only it is blocked. If the scheme:// prefix is not set, all paths with all protocols (http, https, ftp, etc.) are blocked.
The host name or IP address must be specified. By default, all its subdomains are blocked. To avoid this, add a dot (.) before the host name. If there is a * symbol in the schema, all domains are blocked.
You can also specify the forbidden port number (from 1 to 65535). If no number is specified, all ports are blocked.
If a path is specified, only addresses with the appropriate prefix are blocked.
Exceptions can be set in the URLWhitelist policy. It must have no more than 1000 URLs, the other addresses will be ignored.
NOTE that blocking internal URLs with the browser:// and chrome:// * prefix is not recommended. This may cause unexpected errors.
If this policy is not set, the browser will not block any URLs.</string>
      <string id="URLBlacklistDesc">Blocking access to the URL list</string>
      <string id="URLWhitelist">Sets the list of exceptions for blocked URLs</string>
      <string id="URLWhitelist_Explain">URLWhitelist
Used to configure exceptions from the blacklist set by the URLBlacklist policy.
For example, if an asterisk ( * ) is specified in the blacklist, all addresses will be blocked. However, you can use the URLWhitelist policy to allow access to individual URLs by adding separate protocols, domains, subdomains, ports, or URLs to exceptions.
The white list takes priority over the black list.
The list can contain up to 1000 entries, all subsequent entries are ignored.
If the policy is not set, there will be no exceptions from the blacklist.
The record format is provided in the URLBlacklist policy description.</string>
      <string id="URLWhitelistDesc">Allows access to the list of URLs blocked by the URLBlacklist policy</string>
      <string id="RenderInInternetExplorer">Set a list of URLs that open on the Internet Explorer engine</string>
      <string id="RenderInInternetExplorer_Explain">RenderInInternetExplorer

Important! The performance of sites using the Internet Explorer engine is being tested — there may be failures.

The policy sets a list of URLs that open in a separate window using the Internet Explorer engine.

Features

- Works only in Windows.
- Works only in the extended version of Yandex Browser for organizations. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: Sites open on the Yandex Browser engine.
- Enabled: The administrator sets the list of URLs. You can use URL templates.

For more information about URL templates, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/policy/url-patterns.html

Convert non-Latin URLs (for example, яндекс.рф) via punycode: https://www.reg.ru/web-tools/punycode

Example value:

https://www.example.com
[*.]example.edu</string>
      <string id="RenderInInternetExplorerDesc">Set a list of URLs that open on the Internet Explorer engine</string>
      <string id="AllowOutdatedPlugins">Allow running outdated plugins</string>
      <string id="AllowOutdatedPlugins_Explain">If the policy is enabled, the browser runs outdated plugins as normal. If the policy is disabled, the browser does not use such plugins and does not request permission to run them. If the policy is not set, the browser asks the user if the deprecated plugin can be used each time.</string>
      <string id="DisabledPlugins">List of inactive plugins</string>
      <string id="DisabledPlugins_Explain">DisabledPlugins

Sets the list of plugins that must be disabled in Yandex Browser, and prohibits users from changing it.
To replace individual characters or their sequences, you can use wildcards: an asterisk ( * ) and a question mark (?). An asterisk replaces any number of characters, and a question mark corresponds to a single character or its absence. To enter an asterisk or question mark as such, add a backslash (\) before it.
If the policy is enabled, the specified plugins are blocked in Yandex Browser and marked on the about:plugins page as disabled. Users can't enable them.
Note that the DisabledPlugins and DisabledPluginsExceptions policies take precedence over this policy.
If the policy is not set, users can use any installed plugins, except for obviously incompatible, outdated, and malicious ones.</string>
      <string id="DisabledPluginsDesc">List of inactive plugins</string>
      <string id="ExtensionInstallBlacklist">Setting up a blacklist of extensions</string>
      <string id="ExtensionInstallBlacklist_Explain">ExtensionInstallBlacklist

Specifies which extensions users can't install. Extensions that are already installed will be deleted if you disable them with the policy. If you specify " * " in ExtensionInstallBlacklist, users can only install extensions listed in ExtensionInstallWhitelist. The ID of extensions must be separated by a comma.</string>
      <string id="ExtensionInstallBlacklistDesc">Setting up a blacklist of extensions</string>
      <string id="ExtensionInstallWhitelist">Setting up a whitelist of extensions</string>
      <string id="ExtensionInstallWhitelist_Explain">ExtensionInstallWhitelist

Specifies which extensions users can install. This policy applies if the black list (ExtensionInstallBlacklist) contains "*". The ID of extensions must be separated by a comma.</string>
      <string id="ExtensionInstallWhitelistDesc">Setting up a whitelist of extensions</string>
      <string id="SSLVersionMin">Set the minimum SSL version</string>
      <string id="SSLVersionMin_Explain">SSLVersionMin

The policy controls the use of SSL and TLS technologies.

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: Sites with SSL and TLS support open without restrictions.
- Enabled: The administrator sets the TLS version, the Yandex Browser doesn't open sites that use protocols of earlier versions.

Support for tls1 and tls1.1 values is discontinued.

Example value:

tls1.3</string>
      <string id="SSLVersionMin_TLSv1">TLS 1.0</string>
      <string id="SSLVersionMin_TLSv1_1">TLS 1.1</string>
      <string id="SSLVersionMin_TLSv1_2">TLS 1.2</string>
      <string id="SyncTypesListDisabled">Set the types of data for which synchronization is prohibited</string>
      <string id="SyncTypesListDisabled_Explain">SyncTypesListDisabled

The policy defines the types of data for which synchronization is prohibited.

Features

- Refers to the basic security level. Learn more: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/deployment/windows/setting-policy#basic
- Available in the mobile Browser version for organizations. Learn more: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html
- It only works on iOS.
- It only works in the extended version of the Browser for organizations. Learn more: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: synchronization is allowed for all data types.
- Enabled: the administrator sets the types of data for which synchronization is prohibited.

Example of the value:

[
  "bookmarks",
  "passwords",
  "autofill"
]

Types of data to synchronize

- `passwords' — passwords and cards;
- `bookmarks`  — bookmarks;
- `autofill` — input forms;
- `typedUrls`  — history;
- `tabsAndGroups` — window tabs and tab groups;
- 'neuroeditData' — editor.

Safety recommendations

Value: Enabled. Disable data synchronization to avoid data leakage.</string>
      <string id="SyncTypesListDisabledDesc">Set the types of data for which synchronization is prohibited</string>
      <string id="WebRtcAllowLegacyTLSProtocols">Allow legacy TLS/DTLS protocols in WebRTC</string>
      <string id="WebRtcAllowLegacyTLSProtocols_Explain">WebRtcAllowLegacyTLSProtocols

The policy allows legacy TLS/DTLS protocols in WebRTC.

- Not Configured, Disabled: Legacy versions of TLS/DTLS protocols are prohibited.
- Enabled: WebRTC peer connections can use legacy TLS/DTLS protocols (DTLS 1.0, TLS 1.0, and TLS 1.1).</string>
      <string id="SecureWifiEnabled">Managing secure Wi-Fi functionality</string>
      <string id="SecureWifiEnabled_Explain">SecureWifiEnabled

If the policy is enabled or not, the user chooses whether to use secure Wi-Fi by clicking the icon in the Smart bar or the link in the browser notification. 
If the policy is disabled, the user does not see notifications, and traffic in open Wi-Fi networks is not proxied through Yandex servers.</string>
      <string id="YandexNeutralizeThreatsInBackground">Configure automatic removal of threats in the background</string>
      <string id="YandexNeutralizeThreatsInBackground_Explain">YandexNeutralizeThreatsInBackground

The policy controls the "Automatically neutralize threats in background mode" setting.

Values

- Not Configured: The setting is disabled, and users can enable it.
- Enabled: The setting is enabled, and users can't disable it.
- Disabled: The setting is disabled, and users can't enable it.</string>
      <string id="NtpAdsDisabled">Disable ads on a new tab page</string>
      <string id="NtpAdsDisabled_Explain">NtpAdsDisabled

The policy disables ads on the new tab page.

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: Ads are displayed.
- Enabled: Ads are not displayed.</string>
      <string id="DeprecatedPolicies_group">Deprecated Policies</string>
      <string id="YandexClipboardMaxImageSize">Set the maximum size of the image to paste</string>
      <string id="YandexClipboardMaxImageSize_Explain">Yandex Clipboard MaxImageSize

The policy is outdated. We recommend using the YandexClipboardSizeRestriction policy.

The policy sets the maximum amount of image in bytes for pasting on any sites, if exceeded, the operation is blocked.

Features

- Available in the mobile version of the Browser for organizations. More details: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html
- Works only in the extended version of the Browser for organizations. More details: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: the maximum volume is not set.
- Enabled: the administrator sets the maximum size of the image in bytes.

Example value: 5242880</string>
      <string id="YandexClipboardMaxSizePasteApplyUrls">Set a list of URLs where the clipboard size is limited</string>
      <string id="YandexClipboardMaxSizePasteApplyUrls_Explain">YandexClipboardMaxSizePasteApplyUrls

The policy is outdated. We recommend using the YandexClipboardSizeRestriction policy.

The policy sets a list of URLs on which clipboard restrictions will be applied when pasting, set by the YandexClipboardMaxTextSize and YandexClipboardMaxImageSize policies.

To set exceptions, use the YandexClipboardMaxSizePasteNotApplyUrls policy.

If the URL does not fall under any of the YandexClipboardMaxSizePasteApplyUrls or YandexClipboardMaxSizePasteNotApplyUrls policies, the clipboard size limits will apply.

Features

- Available in the mobile version of the Browser for organizations. More details: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html
- Works only in the extended version of the Browser for organizations. More details: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: the list of URLs is not set.
- Enabled: the administrator sets a list of URLs. You can use URL templates.

For more information about URL templates, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/policy/url-patterns.html

Convert non-Latin URLs (for example, яндекс.рф) via punycode: https://www.reg.ru/web-tools/punycode

Example of the value: testserver.example.com</string>
      <string id="YandexClipboardMaxSizePasteNotApplyUrls">Set a list of URLs where the clipboard size is not limited</string>
      <string id="YandexClipboardMaxSizePasteNotApplyUrls_Explain">YandexClipboardMaxSizePasteNotApplyUrls

The policy is outdated. We recommend using the YandexClipboardSizeRestriction policy.

The policy sets a list of URLs that will not be subject to clipboard restrictions when pasting, set by the YandexClipboardMaxTextSize and YandexClipboardMaxImageSize policies.

To set exceptions, use the YandexClipboardMaxSizePasteApplyUrls policy.

If the URL does not fall under any of the YandexClipboardMaxSizePasteApplyUrls or YandexClipboardMaxSizePasteNotApplyUrls policies, the clipboard size limits will apply.

Features

- Available in the mobile version of the Browser for organizations. More details: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html
- Works only in the extended version of the Browser for organizations. More details: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: the list of URLs is not set.
- Enabled: the administrator sets a list of URLs. You can use URL templates.

For more information about URL templates, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/policy/url-patterns.html

Convert non-Latin URLs (for example, яндекс.рф) via punycode: https://www.reg.ru/web-tools/punycode

Example of the value: testserver.example.com</string>
      <string id="YandexClipboardMaxTextSize">Set the maximum text size for pasting</string>
      <string id="YandexClipboardMaxTextSize_Explain">Yandex Clipboard MaxTextSize

The policy sets the maximum number of characters for pasting text on any sites, if exceeded, the operation is blocked.

Features

- Available in the mobile version of the Browser for organizations. More details: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html
- Works only in the extended version of the Browser for organizations. More details: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: the maximum number of characters is not set.
- Enabled: the administrator sets the maximum number of characters.

Example value: 1000</string>
      <string id="YandexPasteAllowlist">Allow pasting for URLs from the list</string>
      <string id="YandexPasteAllowlist_Explain">YandexPasteAllowlist

The policy sets a list of URLs where pasting from the clipboard is allowed.

The policy supersedes YandexPasteBlocklist.

The policy only works when the YandexClipboardAccessByPolicyEnabled policy is enabled.

Features

- Available in the mobile version of the Browser for organizations. More details: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html
- Works only in the extended version of Yandex Browser for organizations. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: The list is empty.
- Enabled: The administrator sets the list of URLs. You can specify domains. For example, if you specify "example.com", the policy will apply to https://example.com, https://subdomain.example.com, and https://example.com/index. To set a specific domain, put a period before the rule. For example ".example.com". You can use the "internal_urls" keyword to designate all single-domain sites. For example, the rule will apply to "https://example" but not to "https://example.com". You can't set the same rules in the YandexPasteAllowlist and YandexPasteBlocklist policies. The ClipboardAllowedForUrls policy is disabled.

Convert non-Latin URLs (for example, яндекс.рф) via punycode: https://www.reg.ru/web-tools/punycode

Example value:

example.com;.badssl.com

Security recommendations

Value: Enabled

test.ru;[*.]example.com;192.168.0.1;internal_urls;browser://policy/

Enable the YandexClipboardAccessByPolicyEnabled policy. Block copying and pasting on all URLs using the YandexCopyBlocklist and YandexPasteBlocklist policies to reduce the risk of data leakage through clipboard paste. Set exceptions for trusted URLs using the YandexCopyAllowlist and YandexPasteAllowlist policies.</string>
      <string id="YandexPasteBlocklist">Prohibit pasting for URLs from the list</string>
      <string id="YandexPasteBlocklist_Explain">YandexPasteBlocklist

The policy sets a list of URLs where pasting from the clipboard is restricted.

The YandexPasteAllowlist policy supersedes YandexPasteBlocklist.

The policy only works when the YandexClipboardAccessByPolicyEnabled policy is enabled.

Features

- Available in the mobile version of the Browser for organizations. More details: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html
- Works only in the extended version of Yandex Browser for organizations. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: The list is empty.
- Enabled: The administrator sets the list of URLs. You can specify domains. For example, if you specify "example.com", the policy will apply to https://example.com, https://subdomain.example.com, and https://example.com/index. To set a specific domain, put a period before the rule. For example ".example.com". You can use the "internal_urls" keyword to designate all single-domain sites. For example, the rule will apply to "https://example" but not to "https://example.com". An empty value or the "*" wildcard restrict pasting on all sites. You can't set the same rules in the YandexPasteAllowlist and YandexPasteBlocklist policies. The ClipboardBlockedForUrls policy is disabled.

Convert non-Latin URLs (for example, яндекс.рф) via punycode: https://www.reg.ru/web-tools/punycode

Example value:

example.com;.badssl.com

Security recommendations

Value: Enabled *

Enable the YandexClipboardAccessByPolicyEnabled policy. Block copying and pasting on all URLs using the YandexCopyBlocklist and YandexPasteBlocklist policies to reduce the risk of data leakage through clipboard paste. Set exceptions for trusted URLs using the YandexCopyAllowlist and YandexPasteAllowlist policies.</string>
      <string id="NeuroDocumentTranslate">Set up document translation</string>
      <string id="NeuroDocumentTranslate_Explain">NeuroDocumentTranslate

The policy is outdated. We recommend using the TranslateEnabled policy.

The policy sets up the translation of documents and controls the display of translation buttons.

Learn more about the translator: https://yandex.ru/support/browser/ru/search-and-browse/translators-settings

Features

- The mobile version only works on iOS.
- Available in the mobile version of the Browser for organizations. More details: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html

Values

- Not Configured — document translation is available, buttons are enabled. Users can enable or disable the buttons in the settings.
- Enabled — document translation is available, buttons are enabled. Users cannot disable them.
- Disabled — document translation is not available, the buttons are disabled. Users can't turn them on.

Security recommendations

Value: Disabled. Disable document translation and translation buttons to prevent data leakage through sending documents to external servers.</string>
      <string id="NtpContentDisabled">Disable infotainment content on a new tab page</string>
      <string id="NtpContentDisabled_Explain">NtpContentDisabled

The policy disables infotainment content on the new Yandex Browser tab page.

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: The display of content on the new tab page is controlled by Yandex Browser settings.
- Enabled: The infotainment content on the new tab page is disabled.</string>
      <string id="AutoFillEnabled">Enable Autofill</string>
      <string id="AutoFillEnabled_Explain">AutoFillEnabled
Connects an autofill function to Yandex Browser, enabling you to automatically fill out web forms with address fields or a credit card number. If the policy is disabled, the autofill feature is not available to users. If the policy is enabled or not, the user can use autofill, configure autofill profiles, and enable or disable autofill as they see fit.</string>
      <string id="DeveloperToolsDisabled">Disable developer tools</string>
      <string id="DeveloperToolsDisabled_Explain">DeveloperToolsDisabled

Disables the developer Tools and the JavaScript console. If the policy is enabled, Developer tools are not available, sites cannot be analyzed using them, and all shortcuts that control Developer tools and the JavaScript console are disabled. If the policy is disabled or not set, Developer tools and the JavaScript console can be used.</string>
      <string id="SigninAllowed">Allow login to Yandex Browser</string>
      <string id="SigninAllowed_Explain">SigninAllowed
The policy is outdated. SyncDisabled is recommended instead.
Allows you to disable or allow users to log in to Yandex Browser.
If the policy is enabled, authorization will be allowed. 
If the policy is disabled, authorization will be denied, but applications and extensions that use the chrome.identity API will not be able to work. Therefore, we recommend using SyncDisabled instead of SigninAllowed.

Do not enable this policy if the YandexDisableID policy is enabled. YandexDisableID disables the SigninAllowed ('False') policy.</string>
      <string id="DnscryptDisabled">Disable Dnsscrypt</string>
      <string id="DnscryptDisabled_Explain">DnscryptDisabled

The policy disables DNSCrypt. Yandex Browser uses DNSCrypt technology as part of the Protect security system, which protects users from DNS interception and spoofing.

Features

- Only works within the domain in Windows and macOS.

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: DNS encryption using DNSCrypt is disabled, and users can enable it in Yandex Browser settings.
- Enabled: DNS encryption using DNSCrypt is disabled, and users cannot enable it in Yandex Browser settings.</string>
      <string id="YandexNoRefererSettingAllowlist">Set a list of URLs for which the "Referer" header is allowed</string>
      <string id="YandexNoRefererSettingAllowlist_Explain">YandexNoRefererSettingAllowlist

The policy sets a list of URLs for which the "Referer" header is allowed in requests.

Features

- Works only in the extended version of Yandex Browser for organizations. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: The header is allowed on all sites.
- Enabled: The administrator sets the list of URLs for which the header is allowed. The "*" wildcard allows the header for all sites. You can use URL templates. Empty value restricts the header for all the sites.

For more information about URL templates, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/policy/url-patterns.html

Convert non-Latin URLs (for example, яндекс.рф) via punycode: https://www.reg.ru/web-tools/punycode

Example value:

http://example.com;ya.ru</string>
      <string id="YandexNoRefererSettingAllowlistExt">Set a list of URLs for which the "Referer" header is allowed</string>
      <string id="YandexNoRefererSettingAllowlistExt_Explain">YandexNoRefererSettingAllowlistExt

The policy sets a list of URLs for which the "Referer" header is allowed in requests.

Features

- Works only in the extended version of Yandex Browser for organizations. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled: The header is allowed on all sites.
- Enabled: The administrator sets the list of URLs for which the header is allowed. The "*" wildcard allows the header for all sites. You can use URL templates. An empty value in the "[]" format prohibits the header on all sites.

For more information about URL templates, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/policy/url-patterns.html

Convert non-Latin URLs (for example, яндекс.рф) via punycode: https://www.reg.ru/web-tools/punycode

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example value:

https://example.com
https://example.org</string>
      <string id="YandexNoRefererSettingAllowlistExtDesc">Set a list of URLs for which the "Referer" header is allowed</string>
      <string id="YandexBrowserEnforcement">Add special headers to HTTPS requests</string>
      <string id="YandexBrowserEnforcement_Explain">YandexBrowserEnforcement

The policy includes adding special dynamic headers to HTTPS requests.: 
- X-Ybe-Hmac is a cryptographic hash of HMAC. More details: RFC https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc2104
- X-Ybe-Timestamp — timestamp used in calculating HMAC, converted to a string.
- X-Ybe-Id is the session identifier (session_id) used in calculating HMAC, serialized in hex.

When JWT (JSON Web Token) mode is enabled, headers are added to requests:

- X-Ybe-Authorization — a string with the token data received by the Browser. It looks like "Bearer &lt;string&gt;".
- X-Ybe-DeviceID —device identifier (UUID in the form of a 32-character hex string).
- X-Ybe-Id — session identifier (UUID in the form of a 32-character hex string).

The policy sets up:
- the protection mode used;
- URLs of communication with the Enrollment Host service;
- lifetime of the data received from the Enrollment Host; 
- optional URL filters, in requests for which it is allowed to add additional headers.

The policy only works when the YandexDevicePosture policy is enabled.

The policy is available for Browsers version 24.7.6 and higher.

Features

- Available in the mobile version of the Browser for organizations. More details: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html
- It only works in the extended version of the Browser for organizations. Learn more: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled — adding headers is disabled.
- Enabled — the administrator adjusts the settings for adding headers. Supported parameters:

  Required:
     - scrollment_url — URL for receiving initialization tokens (upon first login or prolonged absence).
     - secret_url — The URL for getting up-to-date secrets. Required for HMAC protection mode.
     - access_url — The URL for receiving the token by the Browser. Required for JWT protection mode.

  The secret_url and access_url parameters are mutually exclusive, and only one of them should be set.

  Optional:
     - mode — Browser protection mode:
          - HMAC — the HMAC signature of the message is added to the header, formed using a secret obtained from the Enrollment Host. The default value.
          - JWT — the token received from the Enrollment Host is added to the header. The signature is not calculated.
     - expired_time_source — a method for choosing the time for a new token and secret request:
          - 0 — based on the expiredAt value from the server response.
          - 1 — based on the token_update_period and secret_update_period values from this policy.
          - 2 is the smaller of the two values above. The default value.
     - token_update_period — token lifetime in days. The default value is 30.
     - secret_update_period — secret's lifetime in hours. The default value is 24.
     - apply_urls — a list of allowed URL templates.
     - exclude_urls — a list of prohibited URL templates.

You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example of the value:

{
  "enrollment_url": "https://example.com/token",
  "secret_url": "https://example.com/secret",
  "mode": "HMAC",
  "expired_time_source": 1,
  "token_update_period": 30,
  "secret_update_period": 24,
  "apply_urls": [
    "*://example.com/*",
    "https://example2.com/path2"
  ],
  "exclude_urls": [
    "*://example.com/exclude1",
    "*://example.com/exclude2"
  ]
}</string>
      <string id="DomainReliabilityAllowed">Allow sending domain reliability data to Yandex</string>
      <string id="DomainReliabilityAllowed_Explain">DomainReliabilityAllowed

The policy is outdated.

The policy allows or restricts sending domain reliability data to Yandex.

After changing the policy value, Yandex Browser should be restarted: press Ctrl + Shift + Q or the Main menu icon → "Close browser" and open it again.

Features

- Can be configured as a recommendation. For more information, see https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/deployment/setting-policy.html#recommend-policy

Values

- Not Configured, Enabled: Data is transmitted.
- Disabled: Data is not transmitted.</string>
      <string id="TurboSettings">Turbo mode</string>
      <string id="TurboSettings_Explain">TurboSettings
Determines the operation of Turbo mode in Yandex Browser without the possibility of this setting being changed by users.
If the policy is disabled, Turbo mode is not available to the user in the settings and is not enabled in the browser under any conditions.
If the policy is not set, the Turbo mode settings are determined by users or initial settings.</string>
      <string id="TurboSettings_TurboSettingsOff">Turbo mode is always off</string>
      <string id="YandexDevicePosture">Enable device verification in the Browser</string>
      <string id="YandexDevicePosture_Explain">YandexDevicePosture

The policy includes checking the device in the Browser. 

If the YandexSecurityEventConnectorUrl policy is enabled and the DevicePostureReport security event is enabled, then device information will be sent in it.

To set the rules for accessing websites when checking the device, use the policyandexdeviceposturerules. If the YandexSecurityEventConnectorUrl policy is enabled and the DevicePostureViolation security event is enabled, it will send information about violations of these rules.

Features

- It only works in the extended version of the Browser for organizations. Learn more: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/paid.html
- Available in the mobile version of the Browser for organizations. More details: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/mobile.html

Values

- Not Configured, Disabled — device verification is disabled.
- Enabled — device verification is enabled. Supported parameters:
     - mode — the mode of operation of the policy. Required parameter. Meaning:
          - silent — Device information collection is enabled.
          - weak — verification of the access rules to the specified URLs is enabled. Access rules and URLs are set in the YandexDevicePostureRules policy. If the conditions are violated, access to URLs is restricted. You can repeat the check or continue working on the site.
          - strict — the verification of the access rules to the specified URLs is enabled. Access rules and URLs are set in the YandexDevicePostureRules policy. If the conditions are violated, access to URLs is blocked. You can only repeat the check.
     - notification_details — flag for notifying the user about verification issues. Required parameter. Values:
          - true — notifications are enabled;
          - false — notifications are disabled.
     - update_period_hrs — the period of updating device data in hours.  An optional parameter. The minimum value is 1 hour. The default value is 4 hours.
    - contacts — the administrator's contacts that will be displayed to the user on the page if the URL access conditions are violated. An optional parameter.
 
You can configure it via a file: https://yandex.ru/support/browser-corporate/ru/settings/policy-in-file-config

Example of the value:

{
  "mode": "silent",
  "notification_details": false,
  "update_period_hrs": 4,
  "contacts": [
"Ivanov Ivan Ivanovich",
      "Phone number: +7 999 999 99-99 ",
      "usermail@example.ru"
    ]
}

Security recommendations

Value: Enabled

{
  "mode": "strict",
  "notification_details": false,
  "update_period_hrs": 4,
  "contacts": [
    "Иванов Иван Иванович",
    "Телефон: +7 999 999 99-99",
    "usermail@example.ru"
  ]
}

Enable the policy to collect device information and check site access rules. Check URL access in strict mode.</string>
      <string id="YandexDevicePostureRules">Set device verification rules</string>
      <string id="YandexDevicePostureRules_Explain">Правило устарело. Его использование не рекомендуется. Подробную информацию можно найти на странице https://support.google.com/chrome/a/answer/7643500.
Чтобы узнать больше о наборе атрибутов и форматировании, перейдите по ссылке https://chromeenterprise.google/policies/?policy=YandexDevicePostureRules.


Пример значения:

{
  "conditions": {
    "MinOS": {
      "type": "os_version",
